France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,Gaza: overnight Israeli strikes kill at least 8,Gaza: overnight Israeli strikes kill at least 8,"Gaza: overnight Israeli strikes kill at least 8 Israel carried out overnight strikes in Gaza, killing at least eight people. This is a look at the Strip this Sunday morning. In one attack, an Israeli military helicopter struck an apartment, killing a husband and wife. In another, an elderly man and a child were killed. Earlier on Saturday, at least seven people were killed in strikes that also damaged medical supplies at a hospital. The attacks came after Hamas said it had agreed to the latest stage of a deal aimed at ending the war. Morgan Ayre reports. To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Issued on:02/08/2026 - 10:42 Israel carried out overnight strikes in Gaza, killing at least eight people. This is a look at the Strip this Sunday morning. In one attack, an Israeli military helicopter struck an apartment, killing a husband and wife. In another, an elderly man and a child were killed. Earlier on Saturday, at least seven people were killed in strikes that also damaged medical supplies at a hospital. The attacks came after Hamas said it had agreed to the latest stage of a deal aimed at ending the war. Morgan Ayre reports. The content you requested does not exist or is not available anymore.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:42:26 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-overnight-israeli-strikes-kill-at-least-8,2026-08-03 01:26:20
France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,Three people killed in Moscow bombing,Three people killed in Moscow bombing,"Three people killed in Moscow bombing A blast near the centre of Moscow has killed at least three people and injured 21 others. It happened at around 8pm local time, when a homemade explosive device detonated as a woman tried to enter a restaurant and was stopped by a security guard, according to Russia’s National Anti-Terrorist Committee. Both the woman and the security guard were killed, along with a visitor at the restaurant, which was hosting a private function. Authorities have not said who they believe was the target, but Russian independent media report it may have been a military official. The attack is also suspected of being linked to the war in Ukraine. In recent years, several senior Russian military figures have been assassinated in and around Moscow, with the Kremlin blaming Kyiv for those attacks. Morgan Ayre has this story. To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Issued on:02/08/2026 - 10:41 A blast near the centre of Moscow has killed at least three people and injured 21 others. It happened at around 8pm local time, when a homemade explosive device detonated as a woman tried to enter a restaurant and was stopped by a security guard, according to Russia’s National Anti-Terrorist Committee. Both the woman and the security guard were killed, along with a visitor at the restaurant, which was hosting a private function. Authorities have not said who they believe was the target, but Russian independent media report it may have been a military official. The attack is also suspected of being linked to the war in Ukraine. In recent years, several senior Russian military figures have been assassinated in and around Moscow, with the Kremlin blaming Kyiv for those attacks. Morgan Ayre has this story. The content you requested does not exist or is not avai","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:41:16 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/three-people-killed-in-moscow-bombing,2026-08-03 01:26:20
France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,"At least three killed in 'terrorist' bombing of Moscow restaurant, Russian officials say","At least three killed in 'terrorist' bombing of Moscow restaurant, Russian officials say","At least three killed in 'terrorist' bombing of Moscow restaurant, Russian officials say At least three people have been killed and 21 wounded after a homemade explosive device was detonated at a restaurant in Moscow, Russian officials said late Saturday. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin called the attack a “brutal terrorist act” but did not say who he thought was responsible. At least three people have been killed and 21 wounded after a homemade explosive device was detonated at a restaurant in Moscow, Russian officials said late Saturday. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin called the attack a “brutal terrorist act” but did not say who he thought was responsible. Issued on:02/08/2026 - 07:46Modified:02/08/2026 - 14:00 To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. An explosion Saturday at a Moscow restaurant that killed three people and wounded 21 others was a bombing,Russia's national anti-terrorismcommittee said, the Tass state news agency reported. ""A homemade explosive device blew up at a restaurant in Kudrinskaya Square in Moscow, killing three people,"" said the committee, quoted by the Tass state news agency. An unidentified woman who attempted to carry the explosive device into the restaurant died in the blast as did a security guard and a patron, the news agency said. Ria Novosti reported the woman attempted to smuggle the bomb into the establishment but the security guard refused to let her in before the bomb exploded. Moscow mayor Sergei Sobyanin called the bomb attack a “brutal terrorist act” on Sunday. “Yesterday, a brutal terrorist act was committed in Moscow that claimed human lives. The victims are currently in the city’s hospitals, where ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 05:46:20 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260802-at-least-three-killed-in-moscow-restaurant-bombing-russian-officials-say,2026-08-03 01:26:20
France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,"Trump holds off on striking Iran, calls for 'rapid' deal to end the conflict","Trump holds off on striking Iran, calls for 'rapid' deal to end the conflict","Trump holds off on striking Iran, calls for 'rapid' deal to end the conflict US President Donald Trump said Saturday that the United States and Israel had agreed to hold off on new strikes on Iran – provided a deal to end the months-long conflict is ""rapidly"" reached. Iran's acting defence minister said his country would ""neither ‌be caught off ​guard nor remain passive"" in the face of new US threats. Read our live blog to see how events unfolded. Issued on:02/08/2026 - 07:28Modified:02/08/2026 - 22:56 US President Donald Trump said Saturday that the United States and Israel had agreed to hold off on new strikes on Iran – provided a deal to end the months-long conflict is ""rapidly"" reached. Iran's acting defence minister said his country would ""neither ‌be caught off ​guard nor remain passive"" in the face of new US threats. Read our live blog to see how events unfolded. Israeli ​airstrikes hit Gaza for a second straight day, killing at least 18 Palestinians, medics said, despite US President Donald Trump's announcement of a breakthrough in efforts to implement last year's ceasefire agreement. From dawn, Israeli warplanes hit Gaza City in the north, the central city of Deir al-Balah and the southern area of Khan Younis, causing the biggest daily death toll in weeks, according to Palestinian health officials. The ​crew ​of an Iranian commercial ship that ​was ‌hit ⁠in ‌a Ukrainian attack ⁠and the body of ​a ‌sailor killed in the incident ‌have returned ​to Iran, according to Iran's semi-official ​ISNA ​news agency ​in a ​report on Sunday. Iran on Sunday said it was nearing a deal with Oman over a new route through the Strait of Hormuz, hours after the US called off major strikes to allow for diplomacy. US President Donald Trump said on Saturday that his country and Israel had agreed to hold off on new strikes on Iran, saying the ""perimeters"" of a deal were there. ""Throughout this conflict, the impact that the Gulf has fa","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 05:28:11 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260802-live-trump-says-us-to-stop-new-strikes-on-iran-calls-for-rapid-deal-on-hormuz,2026-08-03 01:26:21
