Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Russian and Ukrainian strikes kill 14 on both sides,Russian and Ukrainian strikes kill 14 on both sides,"Russian and Ukrainian strikes kill 14 on both sides Ukrainian strikes target Russian oil hubs and high-rises as Zelenskyy warns of critical Patriot interceptor shortages Save Share Russian and Ukrainian strikes have killed at least 14 people on both sides of the conflict, as Kyiv and Moscow escalate long-range attacks far beyond the front line. Swarms of drones launched overnight into Sunday by Ukraine towards targets in multiple Russian regions killed at least nine people, despite Russia saying it successfully shot down 635 drones. The deaths announced by regional governors included three killed by a drone strike on a car in the Udmurtia region, more than 1,300km (800 miles) beyond the Ukrainian front line. “This act is monstrous in its senselessness. These people were definitely not a military target,” acting Governor Olga Abramova said on Telegram. In the Saratov region, civilianinfrastructurewas hit in the cities of Saratov and Engels, and two people were killed when a residentialbuildingin Engels was struck,Governor Roman Busargin said. Both Saratov city, which hosts a major oil refinery, and Engels, home of a strategic bomber airbase, have come under repeated Ukrainian attack in recent years. Ukraine’s military said it had attacked ⁠the Saratov refinery and the Engels airbase, sparking fires at both facilities. It said its forces had also struck an oil ⁠depot in the western Kaluga region. In the Belgorod region bordering Ukraine, four people were killed, including a 13-year-old girl near a playground, the region’s acting Governor Alexander Shuvaev said. Ukrainian drones also attacked a Wildberries warehouse in the Samara region, around ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 18:37:23 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/2/ukrainian-drone-attacks-kill-eight-in-response-to-russian-missiles?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:23
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,‘Iron fist’ doesn’t work with Iran: Former US hostage in Tehran,‘Iron fist’ doesn’t work with Iran: Former US hostage in Tehran,"‘Iron fist’ doesn’t work with Iran: Former US hostage in Tehran Former US hostage John Limbert says Washington ‘can’t bomb and assassinate its way to a better relationship’ with Iran. Former US hostage John Limbert says Washington ‘can’t bomb and assassinate its way to a better relationship’ with Iran. “We can’t dictate to the Iranians, and the Iranians can’t dictate to us,” argues John Limbert, one of the American captives held in the US embassy in Tehran during the 1979 Iranian Revolution. Limbert, who went on to become US deputy assistant secretary of state for Iran, tells host Steve Clemons that US leaders believe that “all we have to do is drop more bombs and the Iranians will do what we want”. And Iranian leaders believe that “all we have to do is keep attacking ships in the Strait [of Hormuz], and the Americans eventually will do what we want”. Save Share","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 18:28:13 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/video/the-bottom-line/2026/8/2/iron-fist-doesnt-work-with-iran-former-us-hostage-in-tehran?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:23
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Republican senator says former son-in-law should resign from US Congress,Republican senator says former son-in-law should resign from US Congress,"Republican senator says former son-in-law should resign from US Congress Senator Bernie Moreno has broken silence around domestic abuse allegations involving Representative Max Miller. Save Share United States Senator Bernie Moreno has said that his former son-in-law, House of Representatives memberMax Miller, should not serve in Congress amid domestic abuse allegations involving Moreno’s daughter Emily Moreno. The Republican lawmaker said in a social media post on Sunday that Miller is not fit for his position and should “seek professional help”. The Ohio senator had largely declined to weigh in on allegations against Miller, who faces growing pressure to resign due to the accusations. “If there are any basic standards of character required to hold elected office, Max Miller fails them. He should not serve in the House of Representatives,” Bernie Moreno said. “I believe Max Miller needs to seek professional help to end the clear pattern of abuse he has left in his wake. I believe he should not be free to continue endangering others until he does.” Emily Moreno has said that Miller hit, threatened, and threw scalding water on her while they were married. The two finalised their divorce last year but have been in a protracted custody dispute. A recent article in the magazine Mother Jones revealed a new point of contention in their legal battle: a broken collarbone on their two-year-old daughter that led Emily Moreno to contact authorities. Miller and Emily Moreno presented different theories about how the injury occurred, according to court filings and police reports reviewed by the magazine. Last spring, a spokesperson for Miller provided documentation to T","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 18:27:41 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/2/republican-senator-says-former-son-in-law-should-resign-from-us-congress?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:23
