Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Suicide bomber kills 14 outside police station in Pakistan’s Swat,Suicide bomber kills 14 outside police station in Pakistan’s Swat,"Suicide bomber kills 14 outside police station in Pakistan’s Swat Explosion took place near crowd rallying against a surge in violence in northwestern Pakistan. Save Share A suicide bomber has killed at least 14 people and wounded others outside a police station inPakistan‘s Swat Valley, striking near a crowd that had gathered to protest. The bombing happened on Sunday evening in Kabal, a town in the valley in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province, near the border with Afghanistan. According to Swat District Police Officer (DPO) Umar Khan, the suicide bomber detonated explosives after police personnel attempted to stop and search him at the entrance of the police station. Swat Deputy Inspector General of Police Fida Hussain said at least 22 people were wounded. No group has claimed responsibility for the attack. The blast occurred near hundreds of people who had gathered at a nearby intersection to demand government action against the region’s escalating violence. It tore through the crowd as the final speaker was addressing the gathering, sending panicked residents fleeing the scene. The demonstrators had gathered specifically to condemn a resurgence of violent attacks in Swat – a valley that became a stronghold of the Pakistan Taliban, also known as the Tehreek-e-Taliban Pakistan (TTP), before a 2009 military offensive drove the group out. Speakers accused authorities of cracking down on peaceful residents while fighters operated openly in the surrounding mountains, circulating videos of their activities on social media. “We have witnessed years of bloodshed,” one speaker was quoted as saying by Pakistani outlet Dawn. “We do not want another","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:40:44 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/2/suicide-bomber-kills-14-outside-police-station-in-pakistans-swat?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:23
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Capital One cites anti-money laundering concerns in Trump Organization case,Capital One cites anti-money laundering concerns in Trump Organization case,"Capital One cites anti-money laundering concerns in Trump Organization case Capital One says Trump Organization account closures in 2021 followed review by anti-money laundering team. Save Share Capital One Financial has hit back against a US lawsuit over its decision to close more than 300 of theTrump Organization‘s bank accounts in 2021, stating that it did so after a review by its anti-money laundering team. The disclosure filed on Friday marks the first time a bank has formally tied money-laundering concerns to United States PresidentDonald Trump‘s family business, according to Reuters. Capital One is seeking to dismiss the case by casting doubt on claims of illegal debanking — or denial of services on religious or political grounds — against the Trump Organization. The Trump Organization and Capital One did not immediately respond to requests for comment. Capital One has never accused the Trump Organization of illegal money laundering. But Friday’s filing argues that “documents and Plaintiffs’ own allegations make clear that Capital One closed Plaintiffs’ accounts for anti-money laundering (‘AML’) reasons. The closures were the result of months of analysis and a careful review by Capital One’s AML team in accordance with bank policies and regulatory guidance.” Capital One gave notice in March 2021 of its plans to close more than 300 Trump-affiliated bank accounts. The Trump Organization and Eric Trump, the president’s son, filed a lawsuit in March 2025 in a US federal court in Florida, alleging the accounts were closed due to political reasons and Capital One’s desire to benefit from the political mood after the January 6, 2021, riot by Trump supporte","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:27:58 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/8/2/capital-one-cites-anti-money-laundering-concerns-in-trump-organization-case?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:23
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,حادث الحافلة في الجزائر.. ماذا كشفت التحقيقات؟,The bus accident in Algeria.. What did the investigations reveal?,"The bus accident in Algeria.. What did the investigations reveal? The Public Prosecution Office at the Boumerdes Judicial Council in Algeria said that preliminary investigations into the bus overturn accident - which left 28 dead and 36 injured - revealed that the driver was under the influence of narcotic substances during the accident. Save Share The Public Prosecution Office at the Boumerdes Judicial Council in Algeria said that preliminary investigations into the bus overturn accident - which left 28 dead and 36 injured - revealed that the driver was under the influence of narcotic substances during the accident. A statement by the Public Prosecution said that preliminary investigations revealed that the driver who died in the accident had taken “various types of narcotic substances,” noting that “two psychotropic pills were found on his clothes.” The bus was carrying 64 people, which exceeds the licensed number of 51 passengers, including the driver, according to the statement. Investigations also concluded that at the time of the accident, the bus was “passing at a speed of 121.63 kilometers per hour on a slope, despite the presence of a speed limit sign of 60 kilometers per hour.” The accident occurred - last Friday - on National Road No. 24, linking the municipality of Boumerdes and the municipality of Zemmouri, in the place called El Karma. Based on the Public Prosecution’s statement, the","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:48:34 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/3/%d9%85%d8%ae%d8%af%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d9%88%d8%b3%d8%b1%d8%b9%d8%a9-%d9%85%d9%81%d8%b1%d8%b7%d8%a9-%d9%88%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%a1-%d9%85%d8%a3%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%a9-%d8%ad%d8%a7%d9%81%d9%84%d8%a9?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:25
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,عاجل| زلزال بقوة 5.6 درجة شمال شرق شرم الشيخ بمصر,"Urgent| A 5.6 magnitude earthquake northeast of Sharm El Sheikh, Egypt","Urgent| A 5.6 magnitude earthquake northeast of Sharm El Sheikh, Egypt Details coming soon.. Save Share An earthquake with a magnitude of 5.4 struck Egypt, at dawn on Monday, according to what the Egyptian National Institute for Astronomical Research announced, noting that it occurred 61 kilometers northeast of Sharm El-Sheikh. In turn, the German Center for Earth Sciences Research said that an earthquake struck Egypt with a magnitude of 5.4, indicating that the epicenter of the tremor was at a depth of 10 kilometers below the surface of the earth. Egyptian media reported that residents of Greater Cairo felt the tremor. The Egyptian Red Crescent said that it had activated the emergency plan in the cities whose residents felt the earthquake, adding that it had not yet received any reports of injuries or damage to property. In its statement, the Red Crescent urged residents to “avoid approaching old buildings or those showing cracks,” and to follow official updates, while the authorities continue to evaluate the situation. The most devastating earthquake in modern Egyptian history occurred on October 12, 1992, with a magnitude of 5.8 and lasted for more than 30 days.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:46:19 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/3/%d8%b9%d8%a7%d8%ac%d9%84-%d8%b2%d9%84%d8%b2%d8%a7%d9%84-%d8%a8%d9%82%d9%88%d8%a9-5-6-%d8%af%d8%b1%d8%ac%d8%a9-%d8%b4%d9%85%d8%a7%d9%84-%d8%b4%d8%b1%d9%82-%d8%b4%d8%b1%d9%85?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:25
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,إعلام عبري: إسرائيل تصادق على عمليات هجومية واسعة بالضفة,Hebrew media: Israel approves large-scale offensive operations in the West Bank,"Hebrew media: Israel approves large-scale offensive operations in the West Bank Israel is preparing to expand its operations in the West Bank, amid an escalation in settler attacks and international and human rights warnings of forced displacement. Save Share The Israeli Channel 14 revealed - yesterday, Sunday, citing unnamed sources - that the political leadership has approved a series of large-scale offensive operations in several areas of the West Bank, and that the security services are preparing to expand the scope of their operations and move “from defense to attack.” The channel said that the decision comes against the backdrop of the escalation of attacks in recent weeks and the view that the West Bank is a potentially explosive front. She added that the West Bank has remained at the bottom of the priorities of the political and military leadership since the beginning of the war on Gaza, and that there are demands to allocate greater resources to it to enhance thwarting operations and securing settlements. At the same time, Israeli Defense Minister Yisrael Katz said that Israel would deal with the West Bank as it dealt with Gaza and Lebanon if they chose to confront it, citing the Shujaiya and Jabalia neighborhoods in the Gaza Strip, saying that they were “completely destroyed and no longer exist.” He added that he and Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu instructed the army","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:54:16 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/3/%d9%85%d9%86-%d8%a7%d8%b9%d8%aa%d8%af%d8%a7%d8%a1%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d8%b3%d8%aa%d9%88%d8%b7%d9%86%d9%8a%d9%86-%d8%a5%d9%84%d9%89-%d8%ad%d9%85%d9%84%d8%a9?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:27
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,في أول تعليق بعد الأزمة.. المغرب يعلن تدفق نحو 40 ألف شخص إلى سبتة,"In the first comment after the crisis.. Morocco announces the influx of about 40,000 people to Ceuta","In the first comment after the crisis.. Morocco announces the influx of about 40,000 people to Ceuta The Moroccan Ministry of the Interior announced - yesterday, Sunday - that about 40,000 people headed towards the city of Ceuta in attempts at irregular crossing, during events that resulted in the death of 11 people, in Rabat’s first official suspension. Save Share The Moroccan Ministry of the Interior announced - yesterday, Sunday - that about 40,000 people headed towards the city of Ceuta in attempts at irregular crossing, during events that resulted in the death of 11 people, in Rabat’s first official suspension. This came in a video statement by Ministry spokesman Rachid Al-Khalfi - on Sunday evening - regarding the recent events witnessed at the crossing points leading to the cities of Ceuta and Melilla, which are under Spanish administration. Al-Khalfi said: ""The actual number of migrants was about 40,000 people towards the city of Ceuta, and about 1,135 people towards the city of Melilla, where all the people who were able to reach Melilla were returned at the time."" According to Al-Khalfi, these events resulted in one accidental death due to a fall from a rocky area adjacent to the city of Ceuta, in addition to 10 deaths resulting from drowning. He said that the various data collected and analyzed showed that these events “were not the result of circumstantial or spontaneous factors.”","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:43:51 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/3/%d8%a3%d9%88%d9%84-%d8%aa%d8%b9%d9%84%d9%8a%d9%82-%d9%85%d9%86%d8%b0-%d8%a8%d8%af%d8%a1-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a3%d8%b2%d9%85%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d8%ba%d8%b1%d8%a8-%d9%8a%d9%83%d8%b4%d9%81?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:28
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,بـ 3 فرق.. أوميغا بول: ثورة رياضية جديدة تتحدى قواعد كرة القدم التقليدية,With 3 teams.. Omega Ball: a new sports revolution that challenges traditional football rules,"With 3 teams.. Omega Ball: a new sports revolution that challenges traditional football rules Learn about the sport of “Omega Ball” Completely new, and how it changes the rules of traditional football with three teams, fast games, and endless excitement. Discover the details of this game that ignites the enthusiasm of the fans. Save Share In a bold step that breaks the traditional rules of football, the “Omega Ball” game stands out as one of the most innovative and exciting derivative games, based on a revolutionary concept that brings together three teams in one confrontation on a unique circular stadium. This sport was launched for the first time in the United States in 2020, and since then it has witnessed a remarkable increase in public interest, which paved the way for the expansion of its championships regionally and globally to include a number of countries in Europe, Africa and Asia, breaking the usual binary pattern in football matches. Innovative rules and fast pace Omega Ball relies on an intense competitive format; Three teams play the match at the same time, and each team consists of five players (a goalkeeper and four field players). Competitions are held on a circular field with a diameter of about 55 meters, with three identical goals distributed around its perimeter. Each team faces a double challenge: defending a team","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:41:33 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/3/%d9%85%d8%a7-%d9%87%d9%8a-%d8%a3%d9%88%d9%85%d9%8a%d8%ba%d8%a7-%d8%a8%d9%88%d9%84-%d9%84%d8%b9%d8%a8%d8%a9-%d9%83%d8%b1%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%82%d8%af%d9%85?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:28
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,من نيجيريا إلى أيرلندا.. أمسية ملاكمة تنتهي بجدل تحكيمي وأخرى بضربة قاضية خطيرة,From Nigeria to Ireland...an evening of boxing ends in an arbitration controversy and another with a dangerous knockout,"From Nigeria to Ireland...an evening of boxing ends in an arbitration controversy and another with a dangerous knockout One evening of boxing witnessed exceptional events that sparked widespread reactions and reopened important discussions regarding the safety of fights and decisions inside the ring. Save Share The boxing confrontation between British super middleweight Samuel Antwi and Nigerian boxer Suleiman Jaafar ignited a wide wave of criticism, after the fight referee was accused of delaying in stopping the match despite Antwi being subjected to successive blows while he was in a state of clear loss of concentration. The fight was held at the Balmoral Conference Center in Lagos, where Antwi started the confrontation in a strong manner and controlled its course, before receiving a strong punch in the sixth round that knocked him to the ground. Although he was able to stand up before the count ended, the British boxer seemed unable to continue the fight normally, but wisdom allowed the fight to resume, and Jaafar continued to deliver a series of punches before finally intervening to stop the confrontation. During the fight, former European champion Dan Aziz called for the match to be stopped, and shouted: “Oh Wisdom...what is Wisdom doing?”, referring to the continuation of the fight despite the state Antwi was in. And","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:13:51 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/3/%d9%85%d9%86-%d9%86%d9%8a%d8%ac%d9%8a%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%a7-%d8%a5%d9%84%d9%89-%d8%a3%d9%8a%d8%b1%d9%84%d9%86%d8%af%d8%a7-%d8%a3%d9%85%d8%b3%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%85%d9%84%d8%a7%d9%83%d9%85%d8%a9?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:30
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,"انقسام عالمي بعد سقوط ""صفقة بيع المونديال"".. حصار غربي لإنفانتينو وتهدئة عربية",Global division after the collapse of the “World Cup deal”... Western siege of Infantino and Arab calm,"Global division after the collapse of the “World Cup deal”... Western siege of Infantino and Arab calm FIFA's retreat from privatizing the World Cup sparked a global division, as Europe and America demanded that FIFA President Gianni Infantino be held accountable, while Arab and Asian federations called for calm. Save Share Global reactions varied starkly after FIFA President Gianni Infantino announced that he was retracting his controversial plans to sell a stake in FIFA tournaments, most notably the World Cup, to private investors. While the Arab and Asian federations breathed a sigh of relief, considering the move a victory for the “football family unit,” the European and American federations launched a scathing attack on the Infantino administration, demanding investigations and radical reforms. The European Football Association (UEFA) led the opposition scene, stressing in a statement that withdrawing the proposal is a “victory for the game,” but it sent a strongly worded message to FIFA stating that the current administration has not only lost the confidence of the old continent, but also the confidence of many members, stressing that the task of rebuilding confidence has only just begun. Successive European strikes against Infantino quickly followed, as the Dutch Federation explicitly announced a “collapse of confidence.”","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:04:27 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/3/%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%82%d8%b3%d8%a7%d9%85-%d8%b9%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d9%8a-%d8%a8%d8%b9%d8%af-%d8%b3%d9%82%d9%88%d8%b7-%d8%b5%d9%81%d9%82%d8%a9-%d8%a8%d9%8a%d8%b9?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:31
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,ترمب: سنبدأ مفاوضات مع إيران بعد أن أوقفنا هجوما ضخما عليها,Trump: We will begin negotiations with Iran after we stopped a massive attack on it,"Trump: We will begin negotiations with Iran after we stopped a massive attack on it US President Donald Trump announced that new negotiations will begin with Iran - today, Monday - after he suspended strikes on Tehran, stipulating that a quick agreement be reached. Save Share US President Donald Trump said that Washington is talking with the Iranians regarding the form of negotiations and that they will begin Monday evening, stressing that there is an agreement regarding the Strait of Hormuz, and that there will also be an agreement regarding the Iranian nuclear program. Trump revealed that the United States was prepared to strike Iran, and that the strikes were going to continue, explaining that ""it was supposed to be a huge attack on Iran, the largest since World War II."" He pointed out that Saudi Arabia, the Emirates, Qatar and Iran asked him to cancel the strike, adding, ""We will see if we can achieve the denuclearization of the Iranians."" Trump's statements come two days after Washington announced the suspension of planned strikes against Iran, in a move that the US President said came in response to requests from Tehran and a number of countries in the region, and in order to pave the way for a quick agreement. Last Friday, Trump vowed to strike Iran “very forcefully.”","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:02:10 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/3/%d8%b9%d8%a7%d8%ac%d9%84-%d8%aa%d8%b1%d9%85%d8%a8-%d8%b3%d9%86%d8%a8%d8%af%d8%a3-%d9%85%d9%81%d8%a7%d9%88%d8%b6%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d9%85%d8%b9-%d8%a5%d9%8a%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a8%d8%b9%d8%af?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:32
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,الجزيرة ترصد المشهد في بارا بعد سيطرة الجيش السوداني عليها,Al Jazeera monitors the scene in Bara after the Sudanese army took control of it,"Al Jazeera monitors the scene in Bara after the Sudanese army took control of it Al Jazeera's camera monitored the situation in the city of Bara - the second largest city in North Kordofan state - after the Sudanese army announced complete control over it, where signs of widespread destruction and a state of complete desertion were revealed, with the neighborhoods turning into empty streets. Field coverage showed that the ""Bara Grand Market"", banking institutions and hospitals were subjected to comprehensive looting and vandalism, while only two elderly people remained inside the city who lived in harsh humanitarian conditions and documented vivid testimonies about the extent of violations and the seizure of property. On the field, Sudanese army soldiers continue deployment and combing operations to dismantle mines and unexploded ordnance in preparation for the return of the displaced to their homes, in parallel with preparations to move towards the western axes to pursue the withdrawing members of the Rapid Support Forces. Report: Waddah Al-Taher Save Share","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:00:41 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/video/2026/8/3/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d8%b2%d9%8a%d8%b1%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d8%b1%d8%b5%d8%af-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d8%b4%d9%87%d8%af-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%b1%d8%a7-%d8%a8%d8%b9%d8%af-%d8%b3%d9%8a%d8%b7%d8%b1%d8%a9?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:33
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,اليويفا يهدد إنفانتينو وكوشنر باللجوء إلى القضاء,UEFA threatens Infantino and Kouchner with legal recourse,"UEFA threatens Infantino and Kouchner with legal recourse UEFA is seriously considering taking legal action or filing a lawsuit against FIFA President Gianni Infantino and Joshua Kushner. Save Share The European Football Association (UEFA) threatened FIFA President Gianni Infantino with legal action over his plan to privatize some of the rights to the World Cup, and warned him against destroying any materials related to this project. The British newspaper The Telegraph confirmed that UEFA also contacted Joshua Kushner, Greg Maffei, JP Morgan Bank and Open Economics to inform them that UEFA is seriously considering taking legal action, or filing a lawsuit or regulatory complaints because of this failed project. Last Saturday, Infantino announced the cancellation of his proposal to sell a share of the commercial rights to major tournaments to private investors, after a wave of strong objections against the project, which includes people connected to US President Donald Trump. UEFA led the attack against Infantino, and the matter reached the point of threatening members of the federation","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:32:46 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/3/%d9%8a%d9%88%d9%8a%d9%81%d8%a7-%d9%8a%d9%87%d8%af%d8%af-%d8%a5%d9%86%d9%81%d8%a7%d9%86%d8%aa%d9%8a%d9%86%d9%88-%d9%88%d9%83%d9%88%d8%b4%d9%86%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%84%d8%ac%d9%88%d8%a1?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:35
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,حرب أوكرانيا.. هل اقتربت لحظة الحسم؟,The Ukraine war.. Is the moment of decisiveness approaching?,"The Ukraine war.. Is the moment of decisiveness approaching? The decline in interception rates for Russian attacks raises questions about the depletion of Ukraine's stock of Patriot missiles, while a military analyst believes that compensating for the shortage or producing missiles locally faces legal and logistical obstacles. Save Share Questions are increasing about the future of the war in Ukraine, in light of the escalation of Russian attacks and the decline in the rates of interception of missiles and drones, while attention is turning to the possibility of Kiev obtaining a license to produce American “Patriot” missiles, a step that the military analyst at King’s College London, Marina Meron, believes will not constitute a quick or practical solution to the worsening crisis. Meron told Al Jazeera that the increasing talk about Ukraine's manufacture of ""Patriot"" missiles coincides with a noticeable decline in the rates of interception of Russian attacks, after weeks during which the Ukrainian authorities confirmed their success in shooting down most of the air targets. She wonders whether this decline reflects a real depletion of the stock of interceptor missiles, or is it a political message aimed at convincing the Western allies of the necessity of accelerating the supply of weapons to Kiev and granting it the right to manufacture them. It believes that granting Ukraine a license to produce these missiles is not a decision that can be made","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:27:47 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/politics/2026/8/3/%d8%ad%d8%b1%d8%a8-%d8%a3%d9%88%d9%83%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%8a%d8%a7-%d9%87%d9%84-%d8%a7%d9%82%d8%aa%d8%b1%d8%a8%d8%aa-%d9%84%d8%ad%d8%b8%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ad%d8%b3%d9%85?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:37
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,ماذا لو أقيمت كأس العالم بدون منتخبات أوروبا؟,What if the World Cup was held without European teams?,"What if the World Cup was held without European teams? The European threat to boycott FIFA tournaments - especially the World Cup - raises interesting questions about what the World Cup would look like without European teams. Save Share FIFA's plan to allow private capital into the World Cup looked like a stunning ""backfire"" from its president, Gianni Infantino. The proposal was met with categorical rejection by the continental federations of Asia, North America, Central America and the Caribbean (CONCACAF). But the European Football Association (UEFA) took the lead in anger, threatening to boycott all FIFA tournaments if the proposal was passed. Although the plan was dashed and officially canceled with a statement from Infantino on Friday night, this European threat opens the door to an interesting thought experiment: What would a World Cup look like without Europe? The most prominent immediate result will be the absence of a group of the world's brightest stars, as the tournament will lose top scorers and resonant names such as Kylian Mbappe, Rodri, Erling Haaland, and Lamine Jamal. In terms of numbers, this would represent a devastating blow to the market value of the tournament. According to the Transfermarkt website:","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:18:35 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/3/%d9%85%d8%a7%d8%b0%d8%a7-%d9%84%d9%88-%d8%a3%d9%82%d9%8a%d9%85%d8%aa-%d9%83%d8%a3%d8%b3-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b9%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85-%d8%a8%d8%af%d9%88%d9%86-%d8%a3%d9%88%d8%b1%d9%88%d8%a8%d8%a7?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:38
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,إيران مباشر.. ترمب يعلن بدء محادثات مع إيران وطهران تقترب من اتفاق مع عُمان بشأن هرمز,Iran Live.. Trump announces the start of talks with Iran and Tehran is close to reaching an agreement with Oman regarding Hormuz,Iran Live.. Trump announces the start of talks with Iran and Tehran is close to reaching an agreement with Oman regarding Hormuz Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian announced that the memorandum of understanding with America will be the focus of Iran's foreign relations in the future. Tehran also spoke of talks being held with the Sultanate of Oman to open a new transit route in the Strait of Hormuz.,"Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/liveblog/2026/8/3/%d8%a5%d9%8a%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%86-%d9%85%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%b4%d8%b1-%d8%a8%d8%b2%d8%b4%d9%83%d9%8a%d8%a7%d9%86-%d9%8a%d8%b9%d9%8a%d8%af-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ad%d8%af%d9%8a%d8%ab-%d8%b9%d9%86?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:39
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,بالفيديو.. هجوم مفاجئ من ببغاء يربك أجواء مباراة في البرازيل,Video: A sudden attack by a parrot disrupts the atmosphere of a match in Brazil,"Video: A sudden attack by a parrot disrupts the atmosphere of a match in Brazil A funny scene occurred during the third-place match in the Brazilian Under-15 Cup, last Saturday. Save Share The match for third place in the Brazilian Under-15 Cup Championship - last Saturday - witnessed a funny situation, represented by a huge tropical parrot of the “Blue and Yellow Macaw” type storming the field in its first minutes. It began to fly low before boldly attacking the right-back of the Flamengo club, which prompted the player to lie down on the grass to avoid him, in a strange scene that reflects the bird’s curious desire for the players to closely share the atmosphere of the match, according to the report. The show did not end there, as the “parrot” returned again 15 minutes later, and landed quietly in the middle of the field, forcing the match referee to temporarily stop play, until a member of the technical staff was able to remove the bird outside the boundaries of the green rectangle. The match ended with the victory of the Ceara team with a score of (2-1), so that the followers wondered whether the winning team had obtained an exceptional ally from the world of birds to tip the balance in its favor! Fortunately, this has ended","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:48:53 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/2/%d8%a8%d8%a8%d8%ba%d8%a7%d8%a1-%d9%85%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a8%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%b2%d9%8a%d9%84?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:40
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,"مشروع ""إنسانيات عربية في الترجمة"".. نافذة فرنسية لتجسير الفجوة المعرفية مع الفكر العربي",“Arab Humanities in Translation” project...a French window to bridge the knowledge gap with Arab thought,"“Arab Humanities in Translation” project...a French window to bridge the knowledge gap with Arab thought The publication of the second volume of the catalog “Arab Humanities in Translation” by the Arab World Institute in Paris is a French step to break the hegemony of the novel and transmit Arab critical thought. Save Share The Arab World Institute in Paris announced the release of the second volume of the “Arab Humanities in Translation” catalogue, which includes a list of 53 titles selected from the latest Arabic literature in the fields of humanities and social sciences, which the research team recommends to French-speaking translators and publishers to translate into Molière’s language. This publication comes as an extension of a cultural and research project launched in 2024 in cooperation between the French Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Scientific Interest Group in the Middle East and the Islamic World of the National Center for Scientific Research (CNRS), and the French Institute in Tunisia, along with a number of French research institutes in the Arab world, and under the supervision of researchers: Saadia Aksous-Beinstein, Pierre Girard, Nisreen Al-Zahr, and Franck Mermier. The new volume covers a wide range of intellectual productions. It includes prominent works such as “The Arab Civil Wars as a Political System: Between State Fanaticism and the State of Fanaticism” by Waddah","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:46:38 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/culture/2026/8/2/%d9%85%d8%b4%d8%b1%d9%88%d8%b9-%d8%a5%d9%86%d8%b3%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d8%b9%d8%b1%d8%a8%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%aa%d8%b1%d8%ac%d9%85%d8%a9?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:41
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,"عملية تفتيش أوروبية جديدة تستهدف ""أسطول الظل"" الروسي","A new European inspection operation targets the Russian ""shadow fleet"".","A new European inspection operation targets the Russian ""shadow fleet"". The European Union inspected a sanctioned Russian oil tanker off the Italian coast, in the second operation in less than two weeks, as part of tightening supervision over the “shadow fleet.” Russian. Save Share The European Union escalated its measures against the so-called Russian ""shadow fleet"", after a European naval force led by Italy carried out - on Sunday - an inspection of a sanctioned oil tanker, in the second operation of its kind in less than two weeks. The Italian Ministry of Defense said that the tanker ""Toa Payoh"", which is on the European sanctions list, was intercepted west of the Sicilian island of Pantelleria while sailing from Benin to Istanbul. According to an informed source told Reuters, the tanker changed its registration to the Cameroonian flag last week, prompting the maritime authorities to carry out an inspection to verify the legality of flying the flag and the authenticity of its registration documents. The source explained that the European Union's ""Eonavor Med Irene"" mission does not have the authority to detain ships during inspections, so the tanker was not stopped, but the documents collected during the operation are still under review, and may be used by national authorities to take appropriate measures.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:40:15 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/ebusiness/2026/8/2/%d8%b9%d9%85%d9%84%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d9%81%d8%aa%d9%8a%d8%b4-%d8%a3%d9%88%d8%b1%d9%88%d8%a8%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d8%ac%d8%af%d9%8a%d8%af%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d8%b3%d8%aa%d9%87%d8%af%d9%81?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:42
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,"بعد التماس جمعية مهتمة بالحيوان.. محكمة توقف خطة بن غفير لإقامة ""سجن التماسيح""","After a petition from an animal association, a court stops Ben Gvir’s plan to establish a “crocodile prison”","After a petition from an animal association, a court stops Ben Gvir’s plan to establish a “crocodile prison” On Sunday evening, the Jerusalem District Court issued a decision to temporarily halt the plan to transfer Yaor’s crocodiles to Ketziot Prison, which is behind the far-right Israeli Minister of National Security, Itamar Ben Gvir. Save Share - On Sunday evening, the Jerusalem Criminal Court temporarily halted the plan of the far-right Israeli Minister of National Security, Itamar Ben Gvir, to establish what is known as a “crocodile prison,” following a lawsuit filed by an animal association against this approach. Judge Avraham Rubin issued a temporary order preventing the transfer of Yaor’s crocodiles to Ketziot Prison, based on Environmental Protection Minister Aidit Silman’s announcement that the crocodiles are “bred wild animals,” a legal definition that allows them to be transferred and held in the prison. The decision was issued just hours after the “Let the Animals Live” association submitted an administrative petition against Silman, Ben Gvir, and the Prison Service. The controversy centers on Minister Selman’s decision issued on July 15, which aims to allow the use of crocodiles as a means of deterrence and guarding in prisons that hold Palestinian prisoners, a step that the petition believes strips crocodiles of their status as protected wild animals, and removes them from oversight and control mechanisms.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:40:11 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/2/%d9%85%d8%ad%d9%83%d9%85%d8%a9-%d8%a5%d8%b3%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%a6%d9%8a%d9%84%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d8%aa%d9%88%d9%82%d9%81-%d9%85%d8%a4%d9%82%d8%aa%d8%a7-%d8%ae%d8%b7%d8%a9-%d9%84%d8%a5%d9%82%d8%a7%d9%85%d8%a9?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:43
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,قبل الإعلان الرسمي.. كواليس الانفصال بين الجزائر والمدرب بيتكوفيتش,Before the official announcement... behind the scenes of the separation between Algeria and coach Petkovic,"Before the official announcement... behind the scenes of the separation between Algeria and coach Petkovic While the arrangements were moving towards long-term stability, secret understandings within the corridors of the Algerian Federation created a decisive turning point in the fate of national team coach Vladimir Petkovic. Save Share Algerian national team coach Vladimir Petkovic reached an agreement with the Algerian Football Federation to terminate his contract by mutual consent, paving the way for confirming the end of his experience at the helm of the “Desert Warriors” technical crossbar, according to informed sources. The Competition website reported from the same source that the two parties preferred the option of amicably terminating the contract to avoid any financial or legal dispute, as they agreed to grant Petkovic financial compensation equivalent to three months’ salary of 480,000 euros (about 518,000 dollars). It is expected that the Algerian Federation will officially announce the decision as soon as the administrative procedures are completed. For his part, the Algerian sports commentator on the BeIN Sports channel, Hafid Darraghi, indicated - on his account on the “X” platform - that the career of the “Greens” coach has come to an end. He said, ""Vladimir Petkovic informed his assistants that his trip with the Algerian national team had ended, and that he would not continue to lead the 'Greens', after reaching a mutual agreement with them.""","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:36:32 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/2/%d9%82%d8%a8%d9%84-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a5%d8%b9%d9%84%d8%a7%d9%86-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b1%d8%b3%d9%85%d9%8a-%d9%83%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%8a%d8%b3-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%81%d8%b5%d8%a7%d9%84?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:44
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,نقص في الصواريخ أم تحضير للانسحاب.. تراجع ترمب يربك الحليف الإسرائيلي,Missile shortage or preparation for withdrawal... Trump's retreat confuses the Israeli ally,"Missile shortage or preparation for withdrawal... Trump's retreat confuses the Israeli ally The US President's decision to cancel a major attack on Iran for the second time within a week without prior coordination with Israel raises a state of confusion and fears among the Israeli government and army about the possibility of Washington withdrawing from the confrontation. Save Share Israeli security sources expressed their concern about the way US President Donald Trump is managing the military confrontation with Tehran, after his decision to cancel a major attack on Iran at the last minute without prior coordination, which, according to Israeli officials, directly threatens the operational readiness of the Israeli army and casts doubt on military and intelligence cooperation between the two allies. The Israeli newspaper ""Yedioth Ahronoth"" quoted sources in the Israeli security establishment as saying that the inability to predict Trump's decisions would harm, in the long run, the ability of the Israeli army to keep its various formations on high alert for extended periods, and could also lead to its exhaustion. A senior security official explained that although Iran tops Israeli priorities and all resources are directed to confronting it, there is a real difficulty in distributing tasks and resources when the White House’s decision is not clear. Charge sockets come","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:30:29 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/2/%d9%86%d9%82%d8%b5-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b5%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1%d9%8a%d8%ae-%d8%a3%d9%85-%d8%aa%d8%ad%d8%b6%d9%8a%d8%b1-%d9%84%d9%84%d8%a7%d9%86%d8%b3%d8%ad%d8%a7%d8%a8?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:46
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,الخطر محدق.. حين تصبح الدولة أبطأ من الذكاء الاصطناعي,The danger is imminent... when the state becomes slower than artificial intelligence,"The danger is imminent... when the state becomes slower than artificial intelligence The article warns that the acceleration of artificial intelligence is outpacing the ability of countries to modernize their laws and institutions, making institutional slowness a strategic threat. The real challenge for Arabs is to build flexible institutions that keep pace with the speed of innovation. Specialist in cyber policy. Save Share In a time when artificial intelligence is witnessing leaps similar to the speed of light, which poses a great danger to the security of countries and their future, security warnings continue in this context, and perhaps the most serious of them is the warning directed primarily to allies and decision-makers, issued by the “Five Eyes” coalition, which includes the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, and New Zealand. When this coalition asserts that “the time frame available for dealing with cyberattacks is not years, but months,” it is not only setting the date for a new wave, but it is sending a more profound strategic message: Artificial intelligence has become developing at a speed that exceeds the institutional adaptation cycle of the modern state, such that some laws and government strategies are being born later than the reality they were designed to regulate. The danger is not only that adversaries will use artificial intelligence to develop more sophisticated attacks, but that...","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:30:07 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/opinions/2026/8/2/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ae%d8%b7%d8%b1-%d9%85%d8%ad%d8%af%d9%82-%d8%ad%d9%8a%d9%86-%d8%aa%d8%b5%d8%a8%d8%ad-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%af%d9%88%d9%84%d8%a9-%d8%a3%d8%a8%d8%b7%d8%a3-%d9%85%d9%86?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:47
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,إسرائيل تصعّد وتناور.. ماذا بعد إقرار خريطة الطريق في غزة؟,Israel escalates and maneuvers... What happens after the approval of the road map in Gaza?,"Israel escalates and maneuvers... What happens after the approval of the road map in Gaza? Despite the Peace Council's announcement of the road map for the second phase of the Gaza Agreement and the Hamas movement's approval of it, Israel continues the field escalation and clings to conditions and objections that hinder implementation, amid growing skepticism about the chances of the agreement's success. Save Share A state of ambiguity and ambiguity has prevailed regarding the next steps in the road map for implementing the second phase of the agreement to stop the war in Gaza, since it was announced - last Friday - by US President Donald Trump and the peace council for Gaza, as there is no official position expressed by Israel regarding the map, while it continues to kill and continue its attacks on an escalating basis in the Strip. The Peace Council issued a 15-point road map document, in which it specified the principles and executive mechanisms to complete the implementation of the stages of the ceasefire agreement concluded in October 2025, including Israeli withdrawal and enabling an independent Palestinian administration for the Strip. Israeli Channel 13 concluded that the agreement has become threatened in light of the continued Israeli attacks on the Gaza Strip, noting that a source in the Peace Council considered these attacks a violation of the understandings, and revealed that the United States asked Israel to modify the scope of military operations so as not to","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:26:10 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2026/8/2/%d8%a5%d8%b3%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%a6%d9%8a%d9%84-%d8%aa%d8%b5%d8%b9%d8%af-%d9%88%d8%aa%d9%86%d8%a7%d9%88%d8%b1-%d9%85%d8%a7%d8%b0%d8%a7-%d8%a8%d8%b9%d8%af-%d8%a5%d9%82%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%b1?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:48
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,حين يصبح المؤثر شاهدا.. محمود زعيتر يوثق غزة بضحكة ودمعة,When the influencer becomes a witness... Mahmoud Zuaiter documents Gaza with laughter and tears,"When the influencer becomes a witness... Mahmoud Zuaiter documents Gaza with laughter and tears In Gaza, which used to test its children before giving them the opportunity to dream, the story of Mahmoud Khamis Abu Zuaiter began from a place far from the limelight. A young child carrying bags of fruit after long hours of work, returns at the end of the week to his mother carrying 20 shekels ($5.4), in which he sees a small treasure that he places in the hands of the woman who was his whole world. He did not know at the time that the child, who was working to help his family, would, years later, become a face known to millions of people, and that his voice, which began with laughter and comedic situations, would turn into a window through which the world would see the life of the Palestinians in Gaza. From the “Podcast from Gaza” broadcast on the “Atheer” platform today, Sunday (2/8/2026), Mahmoud Zuaiter recalls the details of a journey that was not easy. A journey that began with illness, poverty, and early work, through studying nursing and media, all the way to creating content that made him one of the most prominent Palestinian influencers. Zuaiter says that his mother was the first driver in his life. She was the one who gave him love and the motivation to continue, and she used to call him “Abu Jaber,” a name that became associated with him among his family and friends. It was family","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:16:50 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/video/uthir/2026/8/2/%d8%ad%d9%8a%d9%86-%d9%8a%d8%b5%d8%a8%d8%ad-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d8%a4%d8%ab%d8%b1-%d8%b4%d8%a7%d9%87%d8%af%d8%a7-%d9%85%d8%ad%d9%85%d9%88%d8%af-%d8%b2%d8%b9%d9%8a%d8%aa%d8%b1-%d9%8a%d9%88%d8%ab%d9%82?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:50
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,إغليسياس يندد بالتهديدات الخطيرة عقب موقفه من أزمة سبتة,Iglesias denounces the serious threats following his position on the Ceuta crisis,"Iglesias denounces the serious threats following his position on the Ceuta crisis Spanish striker Borja Iglesias - Celta Vigo player - posted on his Instagram account: Examples of death threat messages and insults he receives daily on social media sites. Save Share Spanish striker Borja Iglesias - a former Celta Vigo and international player - sparked widespread interaction on social media platforms after he published on his Instagram account public examples of death threats and harsh racist insults to which he was repeatedly exposed. This publication coincided with the state of political and social tension that Spain is witnessing due to the migration crisis and successive developments in the vicinity of the city of Ceuta, a crisis that ignited a heated debate between various political movements and public figures. Iglesias presented a strongly worded message that arrived on his account, which included harsh insults and an explicit death threat because of his opinions and positions. The author of the message attacked him, saying that he should have affirmed his patriotism and defended his country in the face of the Ceuta crisis instead of being preoccupied with side matters, questioning in an offensive tone about his silence on some issues. Iglesias commented on the photo with a brief phrase that summed up, ""This is how it is every day, every day.""","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:07:41 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/sport/2026/8/2/%d8%a8%d9%88%d8%b1%d8%ae%d8%a7-%d8%a5%d8%ba%d9%84%d9%8a%d8%b3%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%b3-%d8%b1%d8%b3%d8%a7%d8%a6%d9%84-%d9%83%d8%b1%d8%a7%d9%87%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d8%a5%d8%b3%d8%a8%d8%a7%d9%86%d9%8a%d8%a7?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:51
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,التطورات في إثيوبيا.. نذر حرب جديدة بين الجيش وجبهة تيغراي,Developments in Ethiopia... a harbinger of a new war between the army and the Tigray Front,"Developments in Ethiopia... a harbinger of a new war between the army and the Tigray Front Discuss the program “Beyond the News” In the episode (8/2/2026), the contexts and reasons that led to the outbreak of new armed clashes between the Ethiopian central government and the Tigray Liberation Front, and the challenges facing the peace agreement. The episode also discussed the strategic importance of the Tigray region adjacent to the border with Sudan, and the repercussions of the field escalation on the armed conflict there in light of accusations of the Rapid Support Forces of passing weapons and fighters across the border, in addition to the chances of success of the mediations led by the African Union and international envoys to contain the crisis and avoid its regional repercussions. The head of the Center for Strategic Studies in Addis Ababa, Nour El-Din Abda, the expert in African affairs, Mohamed Torshin, and the political researcher, Mohamed Hamid Juma, participated in the episode. Presented by: Ghanwa Ibrahim Save Share","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:05:28 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/video/behindthenews/2026/8/2/%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%aa%d8%b7%d9%88%d8%b1%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d9%81%d9%8a-%d8%a5%d8%ab%d9%8a%d9%88%d8%a8%d9%8a%d8%a7-%d9%86%d8%b0%d8%b1-%d8%ad%d8%b1%d8%a8-%d8%ac%d8%af%d9%8a%d8%af%d8%a9-%d8%a8%d9%8a%d9%86?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:52
Al Jazeera (AR),Middle East (Arabic),ar,كيف تؤثر ضبابية السياسة الأمريكية في الاقتصاد العالمي؟,How does the uncertainty of US policy affect the global economy?,"How does the uncertainty of US policy affect the global economy? The Bloomberg report highlighted that the decline in US policy predictability is no longer just a diplomatic issue, but has turned into an economic factor that pushes countries and companies to redraw their alliances and investments in the world. Save Share The controversy over US foreign policies is no longer limited to the balance of power or military alliances, but has extended to the global economy, as the degree of clarity in Washington’s decisions has become an influential factor in the movement of investment, trade, and market confidence. The British writer specializing in international affairs, Max Hastings, believes - in an opinion article published by Bloomberg - that many countries are reconsidering their political and economic calculations with the decline in the ability to predict American policy during the term of President Donald Trump. The writer points out that the issue is no longer related to the extent of the world’s admiration for the United States, but rather to the extent of confidence in its policies, pointing out that several opinion polls now show China as a more predictable partner than Washington, a development that he believes is gradually being reflected in the nature of economic relations and international alliances. Hastings believes that the lack of consistency in American policy does not have diplomatic dimensions","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:03:55 +0300",https://www.aljazeera.net/ebusiness/2026/8/2/%d9%83%d9%8a%d9%81-%d8%aa%d8%a4%d8%ab%d8%b1-%d8%b6%d8%a8%d8%a7%d8%a8%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b3%d9%8a%d8%a7%d8%b3%d8%a9-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a3%d9%85%d8%b1%d9%8a%d9%83%d9%8a%d8%a9-%d9%81%d9%8a?traffic_source=rss,2026-08-03 01:26:53
