Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Iran’s population exceeds 87 million, report shows","Iran’s population exceeds 87 million, report shows","Iran’s population exceeds 87 million, report shows TEHRAN – According to the Statistical Center of Iran, the current population of the country has surpassed 87 million, and the number is expected to rise to 87.134 million by the end of the current Iranian year, March 2027. TEHRAN – According to the Statistical Center of Iran, the current population of the country has surpassed 87 million, and the number is expected to rise to 87.134 million by the end of the current Iranian year, March 2027. Urban and rural populations will account for around 67 million and 20 million, respectively, IRNA reported. Furthermore, the average household size is less than 3.2 (3.19) members per household, the lowest level recorded since the 1950s. A total of 892,227 births and 459,984 deaths were registered in the country in the past Iranian calendar year (March 2025 – March 2026). The majority of births and deaths were recorded in summer and spring, respectively. According to the head of the Welfare Organization, the rate of aging in Iran is growing faster than the global average, so that the country will be among the oldest countries in the world in 25 years. Based on the World Health Organization (WHO) age classification in 2025, the elderly population constitutes those aged 60 and older. Accordingly, 14 percent of the country’s population is old now, ISNA quoted Seyed Javad Hosseini as saying in May. A population is considered to be young, with seven percent of people being 60 or older; when seven to 14 percent of people are over 60, the country is said to be aging. Countries with 14 to 21 percent and 21 to 27 percent of people aged 60 or over are aged and super-aged, respectively, the official said. In the Iranian year 1395 (2016 – 2017), only 9.5 percent of the","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:30:04 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/528789/Iran-s-population-exceeds-87-million-report-shows,2026-08-03 01:27:23
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Breastfeeding for a sustainable start in life: strengthen what works,Breastfeeding for a sustainable start in life: strengthen what works,"Breastfeeding for a sustainable start in life: strengthen what works TEHRAN – World Breastfeeding Day 2026 is commemorated from August 1 to 7 under the theme ‘Breastfeeding for a sustainable start in life: strengthen what works,’ focusing on tracking progress, evaluating impact, and scaling proven approaches that improve breastfeeding outcomes. TEHRAN – World Breastfeeding Day 2026 is commemorated from August 1 to 7 under the theme ‘Breastfeeding for a sustainable start in life: strengthen what works,’ focusing on tracking progress, evaluating impact, and scaling proven approaches that improve breastfeeding outcomes. In 2018, a World Health Assembly resolution endorsed World Breastfeeding Week as an important health promotion strategy. With a different theme each year, it aims to promote enabling environments that help women breastfeed – including support in the community and the workplace, with adequate protections in government policies and laws – as well as sharing information on breastfeeding benefits and strategies. This year’s theme calls on governments, health systems, workplaces, communities, civil society organizations, and families to build on successful experiences and strengthen the ‘Warm Chain of Support’ for breastfeeding. The health ministry is observing the week across the country; each day is centered on a specific topic, IRNA reported. Saturday, August 1, Breastfeeding for a sustainable start in life: mothers and children’s basic right to health Sunday, August 2, Breastfeeding in crisis and war: empowered mother, successful breastfeeding Monday, August 3, Youth population and breastfeeding, supportive families, successful breastfeeding, donating breast milk Tuesday, August 4, Baby-friendly centers: effective care for mother and baby Wednesday, August 5, Breastfeeding: a social responsibility; mothe","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:25:16 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/528787/Breastfeeding-for-a-sustainable-start-in-life-strengthen-what,2026-08-03 01:27:24
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"ISC to foster ties with Malaysian, Turkish universities","ISC to foster ties with Malaysian, Turkish universities","ISC to foster ties with Malaysian, Turkish universities TEHRAN – The Islamic World Science Citation Center (ISC) has highlighted the need to expand scientific research, exchange knowledge, and establish long-term strategic partnerships with Malaysian and Turkish universities. TEHRAN – The Islamic World Science Citation Center (ISC) has highlighted the need to expand scientific research, exchange knowledge, and establish long-term strategic partnerships with Malaysian and Turkish universities. The ISC head, Mohammad-Mehdi Alavianmehr, held online meetings with officials from the University of Malaya, National University of Malaysia, and Istanbul Okan University, saying that expanding science diplomacy, strengthening international academic networks, sharing knowledge, launching joint research projects, and establishing sustainable links between universities and scientific institutions are essential for enhancing scientific status on the global stage. Alavianmehr elaborated on the capacities and missions of the ISC over the past two decades, highlighting that the ISC has become one of the reference systems in ranking universities and institutions of the Islamic world. Developing cooperation among leading scientific institutions can contribute to enhancing research quality, fostering innovation, addressing global challenges, and realizing sustainable development goals, he added. By promoting collaborations with prestigious universities in Malaysia, Turkey, and other countries, the ISC Institute aims to strengthen its network of scientific cooperation across the Islamic world and Asia, paving the way for conducting joint projects, knowledge exchange, and the enhancement of the international standing of academic institutions. Exchanging experiences in s","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:09:13 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/528785/ISC-to-foster-ties-with-Malaysian-Turkish-universities,2026-08-03 01:27:25
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran Health Expo to kick off on August 8,Iran Health Expo to kick off on August 8,"Iran Health Expo to kick off on August 8 TEHRAN - The 27th Iran Health International Exhibition, the country's largest specialized event for the health industry, will be held from August 8 to 11 at the Tehran Permanent International Fairground. TEHRAN - The 27th Iran Health International Exhibition, the country's largest specialized event for the health industry, will be held from August 8 to 11 at the Tehran Permanent International Fairground. Bringing together leading companies and knowledge-based enterprises in the fields of medical, dental and laboratory equipment, pharmaceuticals, biotechnology and digital health, the exhibition will provide a platform to showcase the latest technological achievements and foster industry collaboration. Iran Health is recognized as the region's second-largest exhibition dedicated to medical, dental, laboratory and pharmaceutical equipment and services. Held annually, the event attracts a broad spectrum of industry stakeholders and serves as a professional venue for domestic and international companies to present cutting-edge technologies, products and innovations in the healthcare sector, ISNA reported. The exhibition also plays a key role in identifying market trends and assessing the future direction of the healthcare industry, contributing to the development of advanced medical technologies and services. Exhibits will span a wide range of sectors, including medical devices, healthcare solutions, diagnostic imaging, digital health technologies and medical tourism. The 27th edition of Iran Health is expected to provide opportunities for participants to showcase their capabilities, expand technological cooperation and strengthen connections across Iran's health innovation ecosys","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:01:19 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/528783/Iran-Health-Expo-to-kick-off-on-August-8,2026-08-03 01:27:25
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran to hold camp in Russia ahead of 2026 Asian Volleyball Championship,Iran to hold camp in Russia ahead of 2026 Asian Volleyball Championship,"Iran to hold camp in Russia ahead of 2026 Asian Volleyball Championship TEHRAN - Iran's national men's volleyball team will depart for a 10-day training camp in Russia on Aug. 20 as part of their final preparations for the 2026 Asian Men's Volleyball Championship, which will be held in Fukuoka, Japan, from Sept. 4 to 13. TEHRAN - Iran's national men's volleyball team will depart for a 10-day training camp in Russia on Aug. 20 as part of their final preparations for the 2026 Asian Men's Volleyball Championship, which will be held in Fukuoka, Japan, from Sept. 4 to 13. The Iranian squad will travel to Russia with a 14-player roster before heading directly to Japan for the continental championship. The team are currently holding their training camp in Tehran, with head coach Roberto Piazza's staff continuing preparations. The 2026 Asian Men's Volleyball Championship carries added significance, serving as the first qualifying stage for the Los Angeles 2028 Olympic Games. Under the competition regulations, the tournament champions will secure a direct berth at the 2028 Olympics. In addition to the Olympic qualification spot, the championship also offers places at the 2027 FIVB Volleyball Men's World Cup, with the top three finishers earning qualification for the global event. With Olympic qualification on the line, the tournament is expected to be one of the most competitive editions of the Asian Championship, as the continent's leading teams battle for both continental supremacy and a place on volleyball's biggest international stages.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 10:45:39 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/528780/Iran-to-hold-camp-in-Russia-ahead-of-2026-Asian-Volleyball-Championship,2026-08-03 01:27:26
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Израиль узнал об отмене ударов по Ирану из соцсетей,Israel learned about the cancellation of strikes on Iran from social networks,"Israel learned about the cancellation of strikes on Iran from social networks Advertising Israeli authorities, including Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, learned about the cancellation of joint strikes with the United States on Iran from the post of American leader Donald Trump on the Truth Social social network. This was reported by The Times of Israel. “We were left in the dark for several hours. President Trump has left us groping in the fog. ""Senior officials received information about what was happening from Trump's social networks,"" the Israeli official said. It is noted that the US Central Command also knew nothing about the cancellation of the strikes before Trump’s publication. Earlier, the American leader admitted that he had de-escalated and canceled the planned hard strike on Iran. Washington agreed not to attack their territory if both sides could “quickly conclude an agreement","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:23:40 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/izrail-uznal-ob-otmene-udarov-po-iranu-iz-sotssetey/,2026-08-03 01:27:30
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В России произвел фурор один праздник,One holiday caused a sensation in Russia,"One holiday caused a sensation in Russia Advertising VSuzdalev celebrated the Cucumber Festival for the 24th time. Izvestia reported this. As Alisa Biryukova, general director of the Vladimir-Suzdal Museum-Reserve, said, by mid-Saturday about 15 thousand people had visited the site. “I think we’ll set a new record this year,” she said. Cucumber Day, or Cucumber Festival, is a gastronomic festival that takes place every summer in Suzdal (Vladimir region). The holiday was invented by employees of the Vladimir-Suzdal Museum-Reserve in 2001. Zoomers brought it the greatest popularity, turning the holiday into a full-fledged Internet meme. In 2025, 35 thousand guests came to the holiday. This year the festival lasted two days.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:22:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/v-rossii-proizvel-furor-odin-prazdnik/,2026-08-03 01:27:33
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Раскрыта неожиданная причина не покупать дорогой смартфон,An unexpected reason not to buy an expensive smartphone has been revealed,"An unexpected reason not to buy an expensive smartphone has been revealed Advertising Overpaying for a smartphone with a large built-in storage may be irrational. This was reported by How-To Geek. The portal’s authors noted that the larger the storage capacity of a smartphone, the more expensive it is. Journalists revealed an unexpected reason to choose devices with a basic set of memory and told how best to store your data. According to experts, if you have a phone with a storage capacity of 512 gigabytes, 1 terabyte or more, it is wise to use this space to store large amounts of data - applications, photos and videos, documents. However, How-To Geek journalists called the built-in memory of a smartphone not the best place to keep valuable information on it, due to the risk of losing it forever. “If something happens to the phone, it could potentially be missing.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:15:25 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/less-storage/,2026-08-03 01:27:35
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Российские военнослужащие рисковали собой ради спасения сдавшихся солдат ВСУ,Russian servicemen risked themselves to save surrendered Ukrainian Armed Forces soldiers,"Russian servicemen risked themselves to save surrendered Ukrainian Armed Forces soldiers Advertising Russian military personnel shielded the surrendered soldiers of the Armed Forces of Ukraine (AFU) from attacks by Ukrainian drones in the Zaporozhye and Kherson directions. TASS writes about this with reference to the pro-Russian underground. “Russian fighters don’t just save the lives of those who laid down their arms, our guys risk themselves to save them,” the agency’s interlocutor noted. Stormtroopers and medics of the Russian army also share their own dressing bags and painkillers with prisoners before evacuation to the rear begins, in order to save them from blood loss and shock. “We know this information from the relatives of Ukrainian prisoners,” the underground explained. Among other things, the Russian military, at the first opportunity, allows those who surrender to contact their relatives and inform them that they are safe. A ro","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:05:37 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/rossiyskie-voennosluzhaschie-riskovali-soboy-radi-spaseniya-sdavshihsya-soldat-vsu/,2026-08-03 01:27:37
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Раскрыты серьезные последствия для Британии из-за закрытия Ормузского пролива,Serious consequences for Britain due to the closure of the Strait of Hormuz revealed,"Serious consequences for Britain due to the closure of the Strait of Hormuz revealed Advertising The UK economy could face a recession if the Strait of Hormuz does not open before 2027, the Independent writes, citing data from the consulting company EY. According to the publication, if the strait does not open by the beginning or at least by the middle of next year, Britain's GDP could grow by just 0.5 percent in 2026 and shrink by 0.2 percent in 2027. The company added that in this scenario, inflation could reach 6.4 percent by the end of this year due to a sharp rise in oil and energy prices. Earlier, UAE Minister of Foreign Trade Tanya Al Zeyoudi announced plans to get rid of dependence on the Strait of Hormuz. Local energy exporters, he noted, are already actively using ports on the east coast to ship raw materials to foreign buyers.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:02:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/raskryty-serieznye-posledstviya-dlya-britanii-iz-za-zakrytiya-ormuzskogo-proliva/,2026-08-03 01:27:39
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Мужчине разонравилось увлечение жены чтением по неожиданной причине,The man stopped liking his wife's hobby of reading for an unexpected reason,"The man stopped liking his wife's hobby of reading for an unexpected reason Advertising Reddit user with the nickname Best-Pirate5073 talked about a conversation with the husband of a friend from a book club. As Lenta.ru found out, he stopped liking his wife’s hobby of reading for an unexpected reason - because of the discussion of romance novels in the presence of another man. “I am a member of a neighborhood book club that has been meeting for about a year. They are mostly women aged 20 to 40, and I am the only man. Lately they have become interested in dark romantic stories. It wasn't my suggestion, but everyone voted for it. We devote most of our meetings to discussing the development of characters, plots and main characters of the books,” the author explained. However, after one of the club meetings, an unknown person approached him in the parking lot. He introduced himself as the husband of one of the participants and asked for social security.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:01:26 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/muzhchine-razonravilos-uvlechenie-zheny-chteniem-po-neozhidannoy-prichine/,2026-08-03 01:27:42
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Интимный момент экс-участницы Spice Girls с мужем попал на фото,The intimate moment of the former Spice Girls member with her husband was captured in the photo,"The intimate moment of the former Spice Girls member with her husband was captured in the photo Advertising British singer Melanie C was caught by the paparazzi while relaxing on the beach with her husband, fashion model Chris Dingwall. The photos are published by People. The couple, who got married on July 18, went on their honeymoon to Ibiza. Street photographers captured an intimate moment between the couple: the ex-Spice Girls member and Dingwall kissed while swimming in the sea. In February, Melanie Sea showed an archive photo of Victoria Beckham. In the published frame, the performer is captured inside a car with Beckham and Emma Bunton. “Too bad I don’t have this Tommy Hilfiger coat anymore, love Victoria Beckham and Emma Bunton,” she captioned the post.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:01:20 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/intimnyy-moment-eks-uchastnitsy-spice-girls-s-muzhem-popal-na-foto/,2026-08-03 01:27:45
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,«Самые серьезные последствия». Москва пригрозила Ирландии за присоединение к пиратским акциям по захвату российских судов,"""The most serious consequences."" Moscow has threatened Ireland for joining pirate attacks on Russian ships.","""The most serious consequences."" Moscow has threatened Ireland for joining pirate attacks on Russian ships. Advertising Moscow threatened Dublin with serious consequences for joining pirate actions against Russian ships. This was stated by the Ambassador of the Russian Federation to Ireland Yuri Filatov. Filatov emphasized that at the end of July, amendments to the law came into force in Ireland, which allow the Irish armed forces the “legal” ability to board sea vessels. We are talking about a demonstration on the part of Dublin that they are ready for such actions and, in theory, could join the pirate actions of their “senior comrades.” The Ambassador explained that the Irish have already been warned that attempts to implement such acts of piracy will have the most serious consequences for them. It is emphasized that the statements of the leadership in Dublin on this topic mainly copy the words of the British authorities. It is London that is the main supporter of detention","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:34:58 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/long-samye-serieznye-posledstviya-rossiya-prigrozila-irlandii-za-prisoedinenie-k-piratskim-aktsiyam-po-zahvatu-rossiyskih-sudov/,2026-08-03 01:27:48
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Сотрудника уволили из компании за оскорбление матери,An employee was fired from the company for insulting his mother,"An employee was fired from the company for insulting his mother Advertising in China The CEO of the company fired an employee for insulting his mother. This was reported by the South China Morning Post. The case was told by Cui Peijun, the founder of Henan Kuangshan Crane, known as “China's most generous boss” (he gave out bonuses worth 60 million yuan and donated more than 35 million yuan for scholarships). He admitted that he fired an employee who was embarrassed to invite his mother to his own wedding because, in his words, she “looked bad.” Later, according to Cui, the fired employee, unable to find a new job, returned to the office, knelt down and asked for forgiveness, but Cui refused to reinstate him. “I have no respect for you. I’m sorry, but you have to leave,” he allegedly replied. Instead, Cui offered a job at the same salary to his mother so that she could","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:32:16 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/sotrudnika-uvolili-iz-kompanii-za-oskorblenie-materi/,2026-08-03 01:27:50
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В ФРГ допустили отставку Мерца к Рождеству,Germany allowed Merz to resign by Christmas,"Germany allowed Merz to resign by Christmas Advertising The leadership of the Christian Democratic Union (CDU) is discussing the possibility of Friedrich Merz's resignation from the post of Chancellor of Germany. The magazine Der Spiegel became aware of this. According to the publication, Merz is rapidly losing authority among his colleagues, as evidenced by ridicule directed at him. It is expected that the resignation could happen by Christmas, which is celebrated on December 25 in Europe. At the same time, the author of the material noted that changing the head of government is currently not beneficial to anyone. Earlier, political scientist Vladimir Olenchenkov expressed the opinion that Friedrich Merz could be replaced in his post by the current Minister of Defense of the Federal Republic of Germany, Boris Pistorius.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:25:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/v-frg-dopustili-otstavku-mertsa-k-rozhdestvu/,2026-08-03 01:27:52
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,США и Евросоюз обвинили в желании использовать друг друга,The US and the European Union were accused of wanting to use each other,"The US and the European Union were accused of wanting to use each other Advertising Ambassador-at-Large of the Russian Foreign Ministry Rodion Miroshnik stated that the United States and the European Union (EU) want to use each other. TASS reports this. According to him, European countries hope to use military-technological capabilities to continue the conflict in Ukraine and the energy capabilities of the United States to supply the EU. Washington, in turn, expects to receive money. He added that the United States is not interested in European technological development. “They are interested in attracting brains and technologies from there, moving existing industries that should be concentrated in the United States,” Miroshnik said. Earlier it became known that there is an intensifying dispute within NATO about the goals of increasing defense spending and dependence on the United States. NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte advocates increasing defense","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:14:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/ssha-i-evrosoyuz-obvinili-v-zhelanii-ispolzovat-drug-druga/,2026-08-03 01:27:56
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,ВС России использовали для укрытия рвы ВСУ,The Russian Armed Forces used the ditches of the Ukrainian Armed Forces to cover them,"The Russian Armed Forces used the ditches of the Ukrainian Armed Forces to cover them Advertisement Soldiers of the Russian Armed Forces (AF) near the village of Svetloye in the Donetsk People's Republic (DPR) used the anti-tank ditches of the Ukrainian Armed Forces (AFU) for cover. The commander of the operational department with the call sign Pole spoke about this in an interview with TASS. “The offensive was carried out from east to west, and the enemy’s fortifications - these are anti-tank ditches - were just opened from west to east. And this partly made it possible to move along them, along anti-tank ditches,” said Pole. Earlier it was reported that the Russian Armed Forces took the village of Torskoye in the DPR thanks to the “fox holes” tactics.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:02:33 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/vs-rossii-ispolzovali-dlya-ukrytiya-rvy-vsu/,2026-08-03 01:27:58
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Воспитанные в строгих традициях люди рассказали о внушаемых им заблуждениях о сексе,People brought up in strict traditions spoke about the misconceptions instilled in them about sex,"People brought up in strict traditions spoke about the misconceptions instilled in them about sex Advertising Reddit forum users, brought up in strict traditions, spoke about the main misconceptions about sex that their relatives instilled in them. They shared their stories in the AskReddit section. Many people said that sex education classes in religious schools taught them little or no information about contraception. We were never taught about contraception in sex education because “we shouldn't have sex at all.” I didn't even know what birth control pills were until one of my friends started taking them in high school. I had a sex education class in school. Three girls from my class became pregnant because they did not know about contraception and sincerely believed the teachers’ words that only","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:02:32 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/vospitannye-v-strogih-traditsiyah-lyudi-rasskazali-o-vnushaemyh-im-zabluzhdeniyah-o-sekse/,2026-08-03 01:28:00
