Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Власти российского региона рассказали о моделях сбитых за выходные БПЛА,Authorities in the Russian region spoke about the models of UAVs shot down over the weekend,"Authorities in the Russian region spoke about the models of UAVs shot down over the weekend Advertising Acting Governor of the Belgorod Region Alexander Shuvaev in his official Telegram channel spoke about the models of unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) of the Armed Forces of Ukraine (AFU), which were shot down over the region from August 1 to 2. Shuvaev emphasized that air defense crews and the counter-unmanned systems battalion of the BARS-Belgorod brigade destroyed 54 enemy drones during this period. Namely: one reconnaissance UAV ""Gore"", ""Galka"", ""Domakha"", ""Falcon"" and a Fly-Eye drone. Darts, Backfire and R-15 attack drones were also shot down one at a time. In addition, the Russian military destroyed two Sith-X and RAM 2X loitering munitions, two Leleka-100 reconnaissance UAVs, two Baba Yagas, and two attack drones","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:30:47 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/08/03/vlasti-rossiyskogo-regiona-rasskazali-o-modelyah-sbityh-za-vyhodnye-bpla/,2026-08-03 01:29:11
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Two helicopters collide while battling wildfires (VIDEOS),Two helicopters collide while battling wildfires (VIDEOS),"Two helicopters collide while battling wildfires (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6fe42d2030271a0d70c4c0.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Two Bell firefighting helicopters collided near Athens, killing a Greek coordinator and a Danish pilot. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643785-firefighting-helicopter-crash-greece/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Two firefighting helicopters collided in midair in Greece, killing two crew members, as hundreds of personnel battled at least 220 wildfires recorded nationwide over the past week, according to the Greek Fire Service. Nearly 500 firefighters and 23 aircraft were deployed to the main front west of Athens alone, but gale-force winds drove flames through dry forests and hampered the response, preventing some aircraft from safely reaching the sea to collect water. Hundreds of people were evacuated from coastal communities by boat after flames and smoke cut off roads. The collision occurred on Sunday near Psatha, around 70km west of Athens, as the aircraft battled a major wildfire that broke out near Agios Vasileios on Friday before spreading toward Porto Germeno and the forested mountains west of the capital. BREAKING: Two firefighting helicopters collided Sunday while battling a wind-driven wildfire in the Porto Germeno area west of Athens. Video captured one of the aircraft crashing to the ground after the midair collision.pic.twitter.com/4kTHa7wR0V A Greek coordinator and a Danish pilot aboard one helicopter were killed, while the crew of the second aircraft – a Greek national and a British national – survived. No injuries were reported on the ground. 🚁 Battling the flames in Porto Germeno – Villia, Greece.Firefighters, supported by aerial firefighting operations, continue their efforts to contain the wildfire. Every minute counts in protecting lives, forests, and local commun","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 01:05:21 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643785-firefighting-helicopter-crash-greece/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:15
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump teases Iran talks as Truth Social starts selling fast access to his posts,Trump teases Iran talks as Truth Social starts selling fast access to his posts,"Trump teases Iran talks as Truth Social starts selling fast access to his posts <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6fde1e203027231f2ac0fd.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US President Donald Trump has teased new negotiations with Iran after abruptly calling off a major attack in a Truth Social post <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643786-trump-iran-truth-social/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has teased new negotiations with Iran after abruptly calling off a major attack in a Truth Social post published on the same day that his media company began selling Wall Street firms millisecond-fast access to the platform’s market-moving content. Speaking to reporters aboard Air Force One on Sunday, Trump claimed that talks would begin on Monday and said several Middle Eastern governments had urged him to give diplomacy another chance. “We’re just going to see whether or not we can make a deal,”Trump said, claiming that the canceled operation would have been the“biggest attack since World War II.” Last Monday, Trump claimed that“very friendly negotiations”with Tehran were already underway. Within days, however, the US had resumed bombing Iran, while Trump adopted increasingly aggressive rhetoric, promising to hit the country“very hard.” His administration declared US forces“locked and loaded”and prepared to unleash levels of military power not seen since World War II. US media reported on Friday that Washington and Israel were preparing anextensive campaignagainst Iranian power plants, refineries and other energy infrastructure. The threats, combined with continued disruption to shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, helped sustain fears of a wider energy shock and propelled crude prices toward $90 a barrel. On Saturday, Trump abruptly called off the strikes in aTruth Social post, claiming that Iran and several regional governments had ","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:13:14 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643786-trump-iran-truth-social/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:17
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Over 70,000 petition against NYC Mayor Mamdani attending 9/11 commemoration","Over 70,000 petition against NYC Mayor Mamdani attending 9/11 commemoration","Over 70,000 petition against NYC Mayor Mamdani attending 9/11 commemoration <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6fb3ba2030271f5546b59b.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> An online petition urging NYC Mayor Zohran Mamdani to stay away from the 9/11 celebrations, has gained over 70,000 backers <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643781-nyc-mayor-mamdani-petition/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A petition urging New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani to stay away from the commemoration of the 9/11 attacks has gained traction online, attracting more than 70,000 backers. This year marks the 25th anniversary of the attack, which resulted in nearly 3,000 fatalities and the destruction of the Twin Towers of the World Trade Center in New York City. The annual commemoration is customarily held at the monument built on the spot where the towers used to stand. It is frequented by senior local and federal officials. The upcoming anniversary sparked controversy well before the event, with a group of relatives of the victims launching a petition against Mamdani’s participation. According to the petitioners, the motion has nothing to do with the mayor’s religion, but with his controversial views and perceived connections to radicals. The petition, which was launched last month, reached 50,000 verified signatures earlier this week and over 70,000 as of Sunday. It calls out the Muslim mayor over what it described as“public positions, associations, and responses to rhetoric that many perceive as hostile to these shared values.” Among other things, it listed the mayor’s connections to radical Brooklyn Imam Siraj Wahhaj and the appointment of Ramzi Kassem, who previously represented a terrorist convicted in an al-Qaeda tanker bombing plot. The petition also called out his father, Mahmood Mamdani, over his 2004 book Good Muslim, Bad Muslim, in which the political scientist argued the","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:16:58 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643781-nyc-mayor-mamdani-petition/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:19
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Top stories that shaped the past week,Top stories that shaped the past week,"Top stories that shaped the past week <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f94e82030271fcc6a4cf6.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> RT looks back at the top stories of the week and the latest developments connected to the hottest topics <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643772-top-stories-rt-weekly/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> RT showcases its top five stories of the week and dives deeper into the topics that shaped the news over the past seven days. FIFA crisis as testament to US decline In an opinion piece, foreign policy expert and historian Aleksandr Bobrov reflected on the ongoing FIFA crisis triggered by its controversial handling of the World Cup in the US. The tournament was marred by a series of scandals, including harsh treatment of national teams by immigration authorities, and the lifting of a ban on a US player following a call between President Donald Trump and FIFA President Gianni Infantino. Bobrov views the debacle as a manifestation of a broader US decline and Washington’s weakening grip on global institutions it can no longer fully control. The FIFA scandal has been further aggravated by Infantino’s botched attempt to sell to private investors stakes in a $20 billion subsidiary to run the World Cup. The plan met with an overwhelmingly negative reaction and was opposed by UEFA’s national associations and other federations around the globe. Infantino eventually abandoned it. While the scandal might not finish off FIFA itself, it is expected to result in the early departure of its embattled boss. British AI drive runs into energy shortage UK energy regulator Ofgem has proposed a plan to introduce stricter rules and additional fees for AI data center developers, supposedly aimed at tackling“unviable, stalled, or speculative projects.”The regulator now wants to slap a refundable fee o","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:09:31 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643772-top-stories-rt-weekly/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:20
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,UEFA has built football’s apartheid system – now it wants to play savior,UEFA has built football’s apartheid system – now it wants to play savior,"UEFA has built football’s apartheid system – now it wants to play savior <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f5c2c2030271d65766614.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> UEFA forced FIFA to abandon its World Cup investment plan, but the boycott was really about money, Russia, Israel and control <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643771-uefa-has-built-footballs-apartheid/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByAlan Moore, a Vilnius-based sports journalist and host of Capital Sports 3.0. A former athlete, he has over 30 years of professional sports and higher education experience across the globe. ByAlan Moore, a Vilnius-based sports journalist and host of Capital Sports 3.0. A former athlete, he has over 30 years of professional sports and higher education experience across the globe. As I sat in the Olympic Stadium in Athens on Thursday night, I would like to say I felt the hand of history on my shoulder, but instead I felt a sick feeling in my stomach at how European football has been irreversibly damaged by the holier than thou brigade at UEFA. UEFA, the governing body for football in Europe and subordinate only to global overseer FIFA and to the richest clubs on the continent, has effectively created a full-on apartheid system that sees the rich get even richer and their power increasingly unchecked. And they showed their power in beating back FIFA’s bid to commercialize their biggest cash cow: the World Cup. In 1971, Panathinaikos made it to the final of the European Champions Cup, the previous name of the UEFA Champions League. The first and only Greek club to do so, they lost 2-0 to mighty Ajax of Amsterdam, who at the time were in their pomp with the late Johan Cruyff. The Greeks subsequently made two semifinals, in 1985 and 1996, but on Thursday played in the continent’s third tier competition, the UEFA Conference League. If the capital club go on to win thi","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 15:11:07 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643771-uefa-has-built-footballs-apartheid/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:21
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Sunken Nazi warships resurface in Europe amid record heatwave (PHOTOS),Sunken Nazi warships resurface in Europe amid record heatwave (PHOTOS),"Sunken Nazi warships resurface in Europe amid record heatwave (PHOTOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e5a1685f540353e379464.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Water levels in the Danube River have reached record lows, revealing relics of the past ranging from shipwrecks to mammoth bones <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643756-nazi-warships-europe-heatwave/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Several sunken World War II-era Nazi warships have resurfaced in the Danube River amid a major heatwave and prolonged drought. The vessels became visible as the water level in Europe’s second-longest river fell to record lows. Photos and videos posted on social media showed massive shipwrecks lying in the water and on a sand ridge in the middle of the waterway near the village of Prahovo in Serbia. Elsewhere, the wreck of a Hungarian cargo ship that sank in 1937 resurfaced near the Croatian village of Opatovac. Some 200 vessels could be lying on the bottom of the Danube River, according to the European Investment Bank. River transport has nearly come to a halt due to the low water levels, according to Hungary’s Transport Ministry. 🇷🇸🇭🇷 A sunken German flotilla has surfaced in Serbia due to the shallowing of the Danube, Reuters reports.The rusting hulks of the German flotilla, sunk in 1944 during the retreat before the Red Army, are reportedly posing a threat to shipping.pic.twitter.com/WwacLDGlgC Hungarian Prime Minister Peter Magyar also said that the Paks nuclear power plant, which covers nearly half of Hungary’s electricity needs, could be shut down for weeks because of insufficient water levels. Na Dunavu kod Prahova.Stari nacististički brodovi se vide zbog niskog vodostaja.📷Đorđe Kojadinovićpic.twitter.com/b44rZe2H4J In Budapest, a German WWII artillery shell was found near Margaret Bridge – one of the city’s major traffic arteries – last week. The discovery pro","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:45:27 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643756-nazi-warships-europe-heatwave/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:23
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US punished Colombia’s outgoing leader for calling Gaza war ‘genocide’ – FM to RT (VIDEO),US punished Colombia’s outgoing leader for calling Gaza war ‘genocide’ – FM to RT (VIDEO),"US punished Colombia’s outgoing leader for calling Gaza war ‘genocide’ – FM to RT (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f3428203027681706a019.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israel is to blame for the US’ long-running tensions with Colombia’s outgoing President Gustavo Petro, FM Rosa Yolanda Villavicencio told RT <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643770-colombia-trump-palestine-israel/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Israel is at the heart of Washington’s long-running tensions with Colombia and its outgoing President Gustavo Petro, Foreign Minister Rosa Yolanda Villavicencio has told RT. In an exclusive interview aired on Sunday, Villavicencio insisted that the decisive factor behind US sanctions on Petro was not his alleged failure to combat drug trafficking but rather his outspoken support for Palestine and repeated accusations that Israel was committing genocide in Gaza. Relations between Bogota and Washington – Colombia’s largest trading partner – steadily deteriorated during Petro’s presidency over US policy in Latin America, particularly toward Venezuela and Cuba, regional anti-drug efforts, and broader geopolitical differences, most notably Petro’s outspoken support for Palestine and criticism of Israel. This culminated in Washington sanctioning Petro last year, accusing him of“allowing drug cartels to flourish”and“refusing to stop”narcotics trafficking. US President Donald Trump called Petro an“illegal drug leader,”and openly backed right-wing presidential candidate Abelardo de la Espriella, who campaigned on restoring closer ties with Washington, over Petro ally and left-wing Senator Ivan Cepeda in the election earlier this year. Villavicencio rejected Washington’s justification for sanctioning Petro, arguing that his administration had delivered record results in combating drug trafficking. “We are talking about record-breaking seizures ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:32:20 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643770-colombia-trump-palestine-israel/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:25
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US and Israel staged Spain migration invasion – Iran,US and Israel staged Spain migration invasion – Iran,"US and Israel staged Spain migration invasion – Iran <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6f4942203027726045c406.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Iran has accused the US and Israel of engineering Spain’s deadly migrant crisis in Ceuta to punish Madrid over Gaza and Iran war stance <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643773-us-israel-staged-spain-migrant-crisis/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US and Israel orchestrated the mass migrant crossing from Morocco into Spain’s North African enclave of Ceuta to punish Madrid for its refusal to bow to pressure on the Middle East conflicts, Iran’s embassy in Kenya has suggested. Spain has been at odds with Washington and West Jerusalem over the Gaza war and strikes on Iran. Over the past several days, roughly 50,000 to 60,000 migrants crossed from Morocco into Ceuta by land and sea in numbers equivalent to some 70% of the enclave’s regular population. The local authorities admitted they had been“completely overwhelmed”by the sudden surge. The crisis, the largest human traffic invasion in the EU’s history, claimed the lives of at least 86 people, a toll expected to rise further. Many of the victims drowned in the sea or were crushed in the stampede at border checkpoints. On Friday, the Iranian Embassy in Nairobi described the migrant surge as“an operation organized by Washington and Tel Aviv – coordinated with certain neighboring authorities – to destabilize Spain.” It also branded the crisis“a gift to Europe’s far right”and“punishment for the country that dared to challenge the American Empire and its Israeli henchmen,”warning that“the empire never tolerates defiance.” Neither the US nor Israel commented on the accusation. However, Israeli Ambassador to the UN Danny Danon slammed Spain’s handling of the crisis.“Spain, which never misses an opportunity to lecture Israel, has declared a state of emergency in Ceuta f","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:10:37 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643773-us-israel-staged-spain-migrant-crisis/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:26
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,ASEAN: The last place where serious diplomacy still happens,ASEAN: The last place where serious diplomacy still happens,"ASEAN: The last place where serious diplomacy still happens <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6b667c20302762cc5441d5.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> With conflict spreading and old forums faltering, Manila became one of the rare places where powers still chose dialogue <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643671-asean-diplomacy-still-happens/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByLadislav Zemánek, non-resident research fellow at China-CEE Institute and expert of the Valdai Discussion Club ByLadislav Zemánek, non-resident research fellow at China-CEE Institute and expert of the Valdai Discussion Club In late July, the Philippines did something that has become increasingly rare. It made great powers sit down. Under the chairmanship of the Philippines, the 59th ASEAN Foreign Ministers’ Meeting in Manila and its dense constellation of related gatherings turned the capital into one of the few reliable stages where rivals still appear in the same rooms, exchange views, and keep channels open. From July 20 to 24, foreign ministers from Southeast Asia, the United States, China, Russia, Japan, India, Europe, and beyond convened against a distinctly unsettled backdrop of escalating hostilities between the US and Iran and rising tensions between Beijing and the Philippines after incidents in the South China Sea. Yet ASEAN did what it has long done best – it refused to let the friction dictate the terms. The organization offered something that is in very short supply in the modern world of competing geopolitical blocs: a neutral platform where conversation remains possible and practical cooperation continues. The timing was anything but comfortable. The Middle East conflict has already begun to squeeze energy prices, shipping insurance, and supply-chain calculations across Asia. For a region whose growth remains tightly linked to imported fuel, the risks are ve","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 11:47:38 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643671-asean-diplomacy-still-happens/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:27
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump cancels planned attack on Iran,Trump cancels planned attack on Iran,"Trump cancels planned attack on Iran <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6ecd8a85f54057a766c94c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump has canceled a planned attack on Iran after saying the outlines of a deal had been agreed to reopen the Strait of Hormuz <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643765-trump-cancels-planned-attack-iran/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has canceled a planned attack on Iran after saying the outlines of an agreement had been reached that could reopen the Strait of Hormuz and address what he described as Tehran’s“nuclear threat.” CBS News reported that the US and Israel had been preparing a major bombing campaign against the Islamic Republic’s energy infrastructure that could begin as early as the weekend. The network said the proposed operation, which it described as potentially one of the harshest campaigns against Iran to date, was expected to target power plants and oil refineries, while military officials also reportedly discussed cutting electricity across Tehran. In a post on Truth Social on Saturday, Trump wrote that despite the US being“locked and loaded”to strike Iran at“levels of Military Terror, Strength, and Power not seen since World War II,”he had agreed to requests from Tehran and Middle Eastern nations to hold off on the attack because the“parameters”of a deal had been agreed upon. Trump said the proposed agreement would include“the Immediate, Complete, and Total OPENING OF THE HORMUZ STRAIT, and an end to Iran’s nuclear threat.” “Based on this request, I have agreed, for the future benefit of the WORLD and, likewise, the survival of a successful and prosperous Iran, to cancel the attack, subject to being able to rapidly make a DEAL,”Trump wrote, adding that Israel had joined Washington in the commitment. Iranian officials, however, disputed Trump’s account. A source ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 10:37:03 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643765-trump-cancels-planned-attack-iran/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:28
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,WATCH devastating wildfires tear through Washington state,WATCH devastating wildfires tear through Washington state,"WATCH devastating wildfires tear through Washington state <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6ef5312030276e9d72ad78.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Thousands of families have been ordered to evacuate as fast-moving wildfires sweep through Spokane County in Washington state <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643767-wildfires-spokane-washington-us/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Wildfires burning across more than 100,000 hectares in Washington state, US, have triggered widespread evacuations and power outages around the city of Spokane, state officials said on Saturday. Large parts of Spokane County were placed under the highest Level 3 evacuation order as strong winds drove flames into residential areas. Officials urged residents to leave immediately“due to the life-threatening conditions,”while an evacuation shelter was opened at a local community college. The largest blaze, the Old Trails Fire, ignited around noon and had burned more than 1,000 hectares by late afternoon, according to the Washington State Department of Natural Resources (DNR). The fire spread rapidly through brush and grass into residential neighborhoods. Videos circulating on social media showed burning homes, towering plumes of smoke, and orange skies as long lines of vehicles fled the area. Volleyball friends on the way out of the evacuation zone in Spokane on W Strong, after evacuating from Spike and Dig but then being trapped at the Indian Trail Safeway#OldTrailsFire#WAWildfirepic.twitter.com/fBGmRbktYD Washington State Forester George Geissler said the blaze threatened about 4,000 structures. Man this is not good. A community off of Tiffany Ave. in Spokane, with homes on fire, and not a single fire engine in sight. After watching the devastation unfold in Altadena and the Palisades in 2025, seeing neighborhoods once again surrounded by flames is gut-wrenching.🎥KHQ…pic.twitte","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:44:29 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643767-wildfires-spokane-washington-us/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:29
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US politicians are swearing more than ever – study,US politicians are swearing more than ever – study,"US politicians are swearing more than ever – study <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6eea6185f540562067dcf3.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump and Biden accounted for 78% of all swear words publicly used by US presidents since 1919, a Cardiff University study has found <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643766-us-politicians-public-profanity/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US politicians are using profanity in public far more frequently than in the past, according to research published by Cardiff University politics lecturer Dr Joseph Phillips. Some 87% of the 692 documented instances of presidents, vice presidents, and presidential candidates using profanity in public have occurred in just the last decade, Phillips wrote. The overwhelming majority of those cases – 78% – came from President Donald Trump and his predecessor Joe Biden, according to the study published this week. On Wednesday, Trump was heard using another expletive following an Iranian attack on US forces in Jordan. According to Fox News’ chief foreign affairs correspondent, Trey Yingst, the president said:“We’re going to beat the f**king s**t out of them.”Biden previously made headlines while serving as vice president, when he was caught on a hot mic telling then-President Barack Obama that signing the 2010 Affordable Care Act was a“big f**king deal.” For US presidents to use profanity publicly was once exceptionally rare, Phillips noted. According to the study, President Woodrow Wilson became the first to publicly use a naughty word, when he said he’d made a“conspicuous *ss of himself”in 1919. However, Trump has introduced a broader range of profanities into presidential rhetoric, using words such as“bullsh*t,”“ba***rd,”“b***ch,”and“f**k”in speeches, interviews, and social media posts, according to Phillips. The researcher argued that the trend reflects broader changes in polit","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 07:09:26 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643766-us-politicians-public-profanity/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:31
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Killers of Russian siblings confess to more murders in Thailand (PHOTOS, VIDEOS)","Killers of Russian siblings confess to more murders in Thailand (PHOTOS, VIDEOS)","Killers of Russian siblings confess to more murders in Thailand (PHOTOS, VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e9aa785f54046c0131f15.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Four suspects have been arrested in Thailand in connection with the high-profile murders of two Russian nationals and a local family <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643761-russians-killed-thailand-kidnapping/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Thai police have arrested four suspects in a high-profile case involving the kidnapping and murder of two Russian nationals and a local family of three. Diana Nazimova, 22, and her brother Roman, 17, disappeared near the resort city of Pattaya earlier this week. The siblings moved to Thailand with their mother several years ago and lived in the Huai Yai area southeast of Pattaya. According to police, they left their home on a rented Honda ADV 150 motorcycle before dawn on July 26. Shortly afterwards, Diana sent her mother a message saying that someone appeared to be following them, before contact with the two was lost. CCTV footage showed them speaking with another motorcyclist not far from their home before their disappearance, according to local media. The incident prompted a search operation, and their vehicle was discovered three days later, dismantled and buried in a wooded area near an abandoned cemetery. Police identified two men – Thana ‘Pong’Koedthong, 43, and Thongchai ‘Thong’Srinil, 39 – as the principal suspects in the case. The two were detained near Thailand’s border with Cambodia on July 31 following a five-day manhunt. BREAKING: Two Russian siblings missing in#Thailandhave been killed over a motorcycle.17-year-old Roman was shot dead.His 22-year-old sister Diana was beaten to death.Thai police arrested two suspects near the#Cambodian🇰🇭 border. The men confessed to murdering the pair…pic.twitter.com/hFMz769EFh During questioning, th","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 04:07:58 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643761-russians-killed-thailand-kidnapping/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:32
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Chaotic shootout outside US burger joint kills three (VIDEOS),Chaotic shootout outside US burger joint kills three (VIDEOS),"Chaotic shootout outside US burger joint kills three (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6eabd985f54061244ce8bd.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Three people were killed and two others injured in a shooting at an Idaho In-N-Out, where witnesses say an armed bystander returned fire. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643762-idaho-restaurant-shootout-killed/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Three people were killed and at least two others injured when a gunman opened fire at a crowded In-N-Out restaurant in Idaho, triggering an apparent exchange of gunfire with an armed bystander. The attack unfolded at around 2:30pm on Saturday in Twin Falls, approximately 130 miles (210km) southeast of Boise. The restaurant had opened only about a week earlier and was packed with customers in one of the city’s busiest commercial districts. The shooting apparently began inside the restaurant before spilling into the surrounding area, according to footage showing terrified customers and employees fleeing into the parking lot and onto the road as shots rang out. Video circulating online shows a man armed with an AR-style rifle and dressed in a black shirt and jeans walking out of the venue as the crowd flees. He then approaches a white car, opens its trunk and reaches inside. BREAKING: Active shooter reported near the In-N-Out Burger at Canyon Rim in Twin Falls, Idaho; according to police.pic.twitter.com/RbWtWahDq8 In another clip, the suspect is seen walking through a parking lot near a Tesla charging station and firing several shots. WATCH: Active shooter roaming around Twin Falls Visitor Center in Idaho, seen firing at a Tesla vehicle.pic.twitter.com/QGOViBoLMR Separate footage appears to show another man firing a pistol at the rifleman. Eyewitness Lane Koehn, 34, also told the Associated Press that he saw a man with a handgun open fire after the suspected attacker","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 02:34:29 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643762-idaho-restaurant-shootout-killed/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:33
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"No spontaneous combustion? Regarding the causes of the Ceuta migrant surge, look who’s gloating","No spontaneous combustion? Regarding the causes of the Ceuta migrant surge, look who’s gloating","No spontaneous combustion? Regarding the causes of the Ceuta migrant surge, look who’s gloating <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e60ee20302733fe3a9e43.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The Ceuta migrant surge was sold as a border panic. The harder question is who benefited from lighting the fuse. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643757-no-spontaneous-combustion-regarding-causes/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory The recent burst of illegal migration into Spain’s Moroccan exclave of Ceuta was, above all, a sensational media event produced for political effect. It will have lasting consequences, but not in terms of who ended up where: Of the about 50,000 migrants who suddenly, as if on command, stormed Ceuta by land and sea,almost all quickly went back to Morocco. According to the EU’s home affairs commissioner,not a singleCeuta-crasher made it to the European mainland. In that sense, the whole thing might as well not have happened. Apocalyptic fantasies of Ceuta turning into a wide open gate to the rest of fortress Europe were always, at best, silly: no, you can’t just travel on into Spain from there or to British Gibraltar, for that matter. Worse, there have been many deliberate attempts at political profiteering by spreading panic. All through the West, figures from across the political spectrum did not miss a beat trying to exploit the Ceuta emergency: In America, PresidentDonald Trump– under pressure from his self-imposed fiasco in Iran – spoke of a“catast","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 21:17:44 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643757-no-spontaneous-combustion-regarding-causes/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:35
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Why Western Europe needs a Russian threat,Why Western Europe needs a Russian threat,"Why Western Europe needs a Russian threat <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6e105220302739ea08d354.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> As the US steps back from Europe, the Russian threat offers Brussels a unifying cause – and Ukraine the army needed to sustain confrontation <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643747-western-europe-needs-russian-threat/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByFyodor Lukyanov, the editor-in-chief of Russia in Global Affairs, chairman of the Presidium of the Council on Foreign and Defense Policy, and research director of the Valdai International Discussion Club. ByFyodor Lukyanov, the editor-in-chief of Russia in Global Affairs, chairman of the Presidium of the Council on Foreign and Defense Policy, and research director of the Valdai International Discussion Club. The term 'collective West', widely used in Russia, is rarely employed in the West itself, except perhaps when discussing Russian political thinking. What’s commonly heard, however, is the long-running debate over what the West actually is and that discussion has continued in philosophy and politics since at least the 18th century. The concept has never had a fixed definition, even among those who are supposedly part of it so instead, the West has usually been defined in opposition to something else. At different times, that “other” has been Byzantium and Eastern Orthodoxy, the Ottoman Empire and the Islamic world, or even Germany, which was once regarded by some as alien to the European spirit. Russia has frequently occupied the same role, albeit there have been periods when Russia was considered part of the Western community, but this generally happened when Western Europe’s great powers needed the support of a major ally against one of their own rivals, and once that purpose had been served, Russia was once again treated as an outsider. There was also a longstanding d","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 20:15:13 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643747-western-europe-needs-russian-threat/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:36
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Germany has reached a new low in election rigging,Germany has reached a new low in election rigging,"Germany has reached a new low in election rigging <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6b56b885f5402e8747fc49.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Local officials in Lower Saxony are blocking AfD candidates from running, using intelligence reports instead of courts or due process. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643665-germany-afd-voter-suppression/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory ByTarik Cyril Amar, a historian from Germany working at Koç University, Istanbul, on Russia, Ukraine, and Eastern Europe, the history of World War II, the cultural Cold War, and the politics of memory Today’s Germany is a grim, unhappy place. Thirty-six years after West Germany’s take-over of the former East Germany (polite term: re-unification), which was supposed to herald a golden age of national fulfilment, citizens are in a very foul mood. According to Ipsos, one of Germany’s go-to pollsters, their morale is at a“historic nadir,”and they are“losing confidence about the country’s future.”As of last month, fear of poverty and inequality was“clearly increasing,”with 37 percent of all respondents picking it as their number-one angst, followed by“migration”(31 percent),“inflation”(30 percent), worries over the healthcare system (26 percent) and“criminality and violence”(25 percent). Note that all top five anxieties focus on what is going wrong at home. That doesn’t mean, though, that Germans are optimistic about the world or Germany’s place in it: 24 percent of the Ipsos poll respondents fear“military conflicts between states.” If the mood is sour, it’s very good reasons: Germany’s abysmally,unprecedentedly unpopularandembattledchancellor, Friedrich Merz, is desperately trying t","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 15:00:02 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643665-germany-afd-voter-suppression/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:37
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US to step back from NATO Ukraine aid group leadership – Politico,US to step back from NATO Ukraine aid group leadership – Politico,"US to step back from NATO Ukraine aid group leadership – Politico <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6df83f85f54057a766c8ec.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The Pentagon will reportedly hand command of Ukraine aid mission to another bloc member as the US scales back its military role in Europe <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643743-us-drop-nato-ukraine-assistance/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The Pentagon is planning to transfer leadership of the Germany-based NATO command coordinating military aid to Ukraine to another member of the military bloc as Washington continues to scale back its military presence in Europe, Politico reported on Friday, citing an unnamed NATO official. Ukraine has been heavily dependent on weapons supplies from its Western backers throughout the conflict, which is now in its fifth year. Moscow has condemned the weapons shipments to Ukraine, arguing that they only prolong the conflict without changing the outcome, and warning that the military assistance shows that NATO is a direct party to the conflict, thereby risking a direct confrontation between Russia and the bloc. The reported plan follows a broader shift in US defense policy under President Donald Trump, whose administration plans to reduce troops and critical weapons systems in Europe and redirect some resources to Asia and other regions. The White House has also pushed NATO members in Europe to take greater responsibility for regional security to significantly raise defense spending. The Security Assistance Group-Ukraine (SAG-U), based in the German city of Wiesbaden, coordinates weapons deliveries, training and logistical support for Ukraine. The NATO official told Politico that the transition is expected to take up to a year, while a US deputy will remain involved through the alliance’s military command structure. SAG-U was always intended to be a temporary organ","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 14:16:45 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643743-us-drop-nato-ukraine-assistance/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:38
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Strongest quake in 40 years rocks Italy’s volcanic region, injures dozens (VIDEOS)","Strongest quake in 40 years rocks Italy’s volcanic region, injures dozens (VIDEOS)","Strongest quake in 40 years rocks Italy’s volcanic region, injures dozens (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6df1e9203027325534bc62.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> At least 26 people have been injured after the strongest earthquake in four decades struck Italy’s Campi Flegrei volcanic area near Naples <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643745-quake-italy-volcanic-region/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A magnitude 4.7 earthquake struck the Campi Flegrei volcanic region near Naples in southern Italy on Friday evening, injuring at least 26 people, two of them critically, and damaging dozens of buildings. The earthquake hit at 7:46pm local time at a shallow depth of about 3km, according to Italy’s National Institute of Geophysics and Volcanology (INGV). Its epicenter was between the towns of Pozzuoli and Quarto. Civil protection officials said that it was the strongest quake recorded in the area since continuous instrumental monitoring began, surpassing two magnitude 4.6 tremors registered in 2025. The quake was felt across Naples, Ischia, Procida, and much of the Gulf of Naples. Seismographs have since recorded more than 60 aftershocks, the strongest measuring magnitude 3.8 late on Friday and another of 3.1 early on Saturday. Civil Protection Minister Nello Musumeci warned that the seismic swarm is continuing and that further earthquakes above magnitude 3 remain possible. The worst damage was reported in Pozzuoli, where falling masonry, collapsing facades, and landslides damaged homes, businesses, and parked vehicles, according to multiple videos posted online. Grietas en casas, derrumbes, coches dañados y diez personas levemente heridas. Este es el primer reportaje del fuerte terremoto de magnitud 4.7 que sacudió la zona de Campi Flegrei esta tarde, con el epicentro en la zona de Solfatara de Pozzuoli. En las comunas de Flegrei, los…pic.twitter.c","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 14:09:23 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643745-quake-italy-volcanic-region/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:39
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,OpenAI uncovers more AI breakout incidents – Reuters,OpenAI uncovers more AI breakout incidents – Reuters,"OpenAI uncovers more AI breakout incidents – Reuters <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6ddccd85f54048606bedb2.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> OpenAI has found more AI containment breaches while investigating last month’s Hugging Face hack, Reuters reports citing sources <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643742-openai-ai-breakouts-probe/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> OpenAI has uncovered additional cases in which its autonomous AI models breached containment and acted without human instruction, Reuters has reported, citing sources. The findings come as the company expands its investigation into a hacking incident last month in which an AI bot went rogue while attempting to cheat in an internal cybersecurity test. During tests of GPT-5.6 Sol and another unreleased model, both stripped of their safety guardrails, the systems were assigned ExploitGym – a benchmark designed to measure AI models’ ability to identify and exploit known software vulnerabilities. Instead of completing the tasks, one model escaped its supposedly isolated testing environment, gained internet access and hacked into Hugging Face – an online repository for AI models and datasets – in search of ready-made answers. OpenAI initially said the intrusion was limited to Hugging Face. However, in a statement on Wednesday, it acknowledged the hacking spree had also compromised four accounts across four separate services. On Friday, Reuters reported that additional containment breaches had since been uncovered, although it remains unclear how many incidents occurred, when they happened or what systems they targeted. One source told the news agency the breaches were limited in scope and that none of the AI bots are believed to have left OpenAI’s internal network. Reuters said OpenAI and outside experts are also reviewing logs from earlier this year to determine whether other simi","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 13:51:24 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643742-openai-ai-breakouts-probe/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:41
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump warns US faces Spain-style migrant invasion,Trump warns US faces Spain-style migrant invasion,"Trump warns US faces Spain-style migrant invasion <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6dbf3085f54045b852962a.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US President Donald Trump used Spain’s migration crisis to claim the US was overrun by illegal newcomers under his predecessor <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643740-trump-us-faces-spain-migrants/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The surge of migrants across the border from Morocco into Spain is an example of what could happen to the US if Republicans aren’t elected, US President Donald Trump has claimed. Trump has repeatedly attacked his political opponents over immigration, blaming his predecessor Joe Biden for illegal border crossings. An estimated 50,000 migrants, mostly young men, swam from Morocco and crossed into the Spanish exclave of Ceuta earlier this week in an unprecedented influx that triggered a humanitarian crisis in the city. The Spanish Interior Ministry has reported that around 48,000 had voluntarily returned by Friday evening. “What’s happening with Spain, with tens of thousands of Illegal Immigrants invading it, happened in the United States during the Sleepy Joe Biden Administration, and it will happen again, only worse, if the Dumocrats ever again gain power,”Trump said late on Friday in a brief post on Truth Social, urging Americans to vote Republican in the midterm elections. The remarks come ahead of US midterm elections scheduled for November as Trump faces slipping approval ratings. A recent poll found that most US adults believe he has not focused enough on the everyday concerns of ordinary Americans, that his economic policies have worsened conditions, and that his military decisions in Iran have harmed the US. White House principal deputy press secretary Anna Kelly said on Friday that Trump“has long warned Europe what would happen if they continue to implement far-left, g","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 09:45:43 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643740-trump-us-faces-spain-migrants/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:42
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US can take ‘whatever we want’ from Ukraine – Trump,US can take ‘whatever we want’ from Ukraine – Trump,"US can take ‘whatever we want’ from Ukraine – Trump <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.08/thumbnail/6a6da57185f54067fb780f69.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US can take “whatever we want” from Ukraine’s rare earth deposits under a 2025 pact, Donald Trump has claimed <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643741-us-take-whatever-we-want-ukraine-trump/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US can take“pretty much whatever we want”from Ukraine’s rare earth deposits under a minerals agreement signed last year, President Donald Trump has said, adding that profits from the agreement could ultimately exceed total American aid to Kiev since 2022. Trump made the remarks in an interview with Real America’s Voice aired on Friday as he chastised his predecessor Joe Biden for“giving away”a purported $300 billion in military support to Ukraine without securing repayment. “He could have Europe… paid for it. All you had to do is ask,”Trump said, adding that under his administration European nations now cover more of the costs. Trump said Ukraine has“very rich, very fertile soil in terms of rare earth.”“We have a contract signed [with Ukraine] having to do with rare earth. We can go in there at any time we want and take pretty much whatever we want. That was a pretty good deal,”he said. The US president was referring to a rare earth deal signed in Washington in April 2025, which established the US-Ukraine Reconstruction Investment Fund. The deal grants Washington preferential access to new Ukrainian mineral, oil, and gas projects, with emphasis on elements such as lithium, titanium, graphite, and uranium. Ukraine retains formal ownership of its resources and receives 50% of profits from new extraction projects. Trump has portrayed the deal as a way to pay for US military aid to Kiev. While he has claimed it amounted to more than $300 billion, the figure is widely disputed","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 07:52:11 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643741-us-take-whatever-we-want-ukraine-trump/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:43
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,New abuse probe raises Epstein behavior at elite US arts school,New abuse probe raises Epstein behavior at elite US arts school,"New abuse probe raises Epstein behavior at elite US arts school <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6cb867203027597b652985.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A Michigan arts school probe found 70 abuse accounts spanning decades, including allegations against the late pedophile Jeffrey Epstein <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643723-abuse-probe-epstein-art-school/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> An investigation into a prestigious arts school in the US state of Michigan has uncovered decades of alleged sexual misconduct by dozens of faculty and staff members, while also revealing new allegations involving the late pedophile Jeffrey Epstein. The 97-pagereport, released by Sanghavi Law Office earlier this week, was commissioned by the Interlochen Center for the Arts in 2024, to investigate allegations of abuse against several faculty members. The inquiry was later broadened and ultimately included allegations involving Epstein, a donor to the school. Investigators collected 70 accounts from former students alleging physical conduct of a sexual nature involving 47 faculty and staff members between the 1950s and the 2010s, with most of the reported incidents occurring before 2000. The report describes a pattern of misconduct ranging from grooming, flirting, and inappropriate touching to sexual contact. Epstein, who attended Interlochen’s summer camp in 1967 and donated more than $400,000 to the institution between 1990 and 2003, according to media reports, is also the subject of allegations in the report. Two former students accused the disgraced financier of sexual misconduct. One woman told investigators Epstein repeatedly touched her inappropriately under the guise of accidental contact while she was staying in a camp building that then bore his name. She said he later paid for trips to New York, where the unwanted touching continued. Another former student ","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 03:02:11 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643723-abuse-probe-epstein-art-school/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:44
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Anthropic says Claude AI models launched three unintended cyberattacks,Anthropic says Claude AI models launched three unintended cyberattacks,"Anthropic says Claude AI models launched three unintended cyberattacks <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6c952e203027266a7af00c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Anthropic has reported three cases in which its Claude AI models unintentionally targeted real companies during cybersecurity evaluations. <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643717-anthropic-accidental-hacking-review/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> AI developer Anthropic has disclosed three incidents in which its Claude AI models unintentionally targeted real-world organizations during cybersecurity evaluations that were supposed to take place in an isolated environment. The cases were identified retrospectively during a review prompted by a similar incident involving OpenAI and Hugging Face, an online repository for AI models and datasets, which was reported this month. Anthropic said that it had found three incidents dating back to April. In each case, a misconfigured test environment retained access to the internet, enabling Claude to interact with real companies and public services. The company attributed the problem to a“misunderstanding”with its evaluation partner, Irregular. The tests involved“capture the flag”exercises requiring Claude to obtain restricted information from simulated targets. However, the model was incorrectly told that the network had no connection to the outside world, pushing it toward treating any systems it encountered as part of the exercise. In one case, the fictional company that Claude had been instructed to infiltrate shared its name with a real internet domain. The model accessed the genuine site during four separate test runs and extracted information that reportedly included application and infrastructure credentials. During another evaluation, Claude encountered fictional instructions directing a software engineer to install Python code. It then uploaded a m","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:52:40 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643717-anthropic-accidental-hacking-review/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:45
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Kiev’s dirty war goes global,Kiev’s dirty war goes global,"Kiev’s dirty war goes global <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6b4cc8203027435c32f401.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> From Africa to the Caspian Sea, each strike is an attempt to market Ukraine as a useful Western asset that still deserves cash and weapons <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643658-kiev-drone-war-global/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByMurad Sadygzade, President of the Middle East Studies Center, Visiting Lecturer, HSE University (Moscow). ByMurad Sadygzade, President of the Middle East Studies Center, Visiting Lecturer, HSE University (Moscow). On the morning of July 25, Ukrainian drones attacked an Iranian merchant vessel in the Caspian Sea. An explosion occurred on board, killing one sailor and injuring another. Tehran described the incident as an act of aggression, summoned Ukraine’s chargé d’affaires and warned that retaliatory measures could follow. Vladimir Zelensky did not deny that the operation had taken place, claiming that the targets were vessels allegedly involved in transporting military cargo linked to Iran. Yet within days, Ukrainian diplomacy abruptly changed its tone. Foreign Minister Andrey Sibiga told his Iranian counterpart that the merchant vessel had been struck unintentionally, after which discussions over compensation began. So long as the operation could be presented to Western audiences as another demonstration of the long-range capabilities of the Ukrainian security services, Kiev was eager to speak of success. Once it became clear that Tehran intended to demand accountability, the initial bravado gave way to attempts to portray the incident as an accident. In other words, the Ukrainian leadership sought to reap the publicity benefits of the strike without showing any willingness to accept responsibility for its consequences. At almost the same time, reports emerged from Iraq ","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:28:53 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643658-kiev-drone-war-global/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:46
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US and Israel preparing to bomb Iranian energy infrastructure – media,US and Israel preparing to bomb Iranian energy infrastructure – media,"US and Israel preparing to bomb Iranian energy infrastructure – media <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6d4a7985f54045b852961d.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US and Israel are reportedly preparing a major bombing campaign against Iranian energy sites that could begin as early as this weekend <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643737-us-israel-strikes-iran/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US and Israel are preparing a major bombing campaign against Iranian energy infrastructure that could begin as early as this weekend, according to multiple media reports. The proposed operation would target power plants, oil refineries, and other energy-related facilities in what CBS News described as potentially one of the harshest bombing campaigns against Iran to date. American and Israeli forces are reportedly coordinating their preparations, although the precise scope and duration of the operation have not been finalized. CBS and Axios reported that US President Donald Trump is seriously considering the strikes but has not yet issued final authorization. The Wall Street Journal, citing separate US officials, subsequently claimed that Trump has already ordered a new attack that could begin over the weekend and last several days. US officials have reportedly discussed completing the strikes before financial markets open on Monday because of concerns that attacks on Iranian energy facilities could disrupt oil prices and damage the US and global economies. The strike plan was reportedly discussed during Trump’s cabinet meeting at Camp David on Friday. Some White House aides focused on domestic politics strongly opposed the escalation, CBS reported, although the president publicly indicated that heavier attacks are approaching. “We’ll be hitting them very hard,”Trump told reporters.“At some point, they’re going to say, ‘We just can’t take it anymore.’” Military","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 22:34:51 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643737-us-israel-strikes-iran/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:47
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US loses F-35B stealth jet in unexplained ‘mishap’ (VIDEOS),US loses F-35B stealth jet in unexplained ‘mishap’ (VIDEOS),"US loses F-35B stealth jet in unexplained ‘mishap’ (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6d1a9785f5404fd6471e19.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A US Marine Corps F-35B stealth fighter crashed and caught fire at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar in San Diego, California, on Friday <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643736-f35-jet-crash-california/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A US Marine Corps F-35B stealth fighter crashed and caught fire at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar in San Diego, California, on Friday, apparently resulting in the total loss of the $109 million aircraft, according to footage from the scene. Emergency crews responded at around 10 AM local time to what the military described as a“Class A mishap,”its category for the most serious accidents. The aircraft was assigned to Marine Aircraft Group 11 of the 3rd Marine Aircraft Wing. “The pilot ejected, was transported to a local medical facility in stable condition for evaluation and treatment of non-life-threatening injuries,”the Marine Corps said in a follow-up statement, adding that the crash occurred on the base’s flightline. JUST IN: An F-35 caught fire after a mishap at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar in San Diego on Friday morning. Emergency crews responded to heavy smoke around 10 a.m. Cause under investigation.- FOX 5pic.twitter.com/oDthXqbQRf Footage from the scene showed a thick column of black smoke rising above the base. Aerial video showed the burned-out jet lying in a scorched dirt field near the runway as military personnel and firefighters surrounded the wreckage. Exclusive video sent by our follower.Initial reports indicate that a U.S. Marine Corps F-35B Lightning II has crashed at Marine Corps Air Station Miramar, home of the 3rd Marine Aircraft Wing, in San Diego, California.pic.twitter.com/qze3GLm8Og The crash also sparked a vegetation fire, prompting a response","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:59:25 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643736-f35-jet-crash-california/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:48
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,German officials trade blame after deadly Berlin attack,German officials trade blame after deadly Berlin attack,"German officials trade blame after deadly Berlin attack <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6d139f2030274e07634ae5.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> German officials are struggling to explain how a known Islamist radical was allowed to launch a car ramming attack on a gay pride parade <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643734-german-trade-blame-berlin-attack/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> German officials are trading blame after it emerged that the suspect behind last weekend’s deadly Berlin attack had been released from prison on probation just months before the attack despite reportedly being considered a“high-risk individual.” A van plowed into a crowd during the festivities known as Christopher Street Day, the German capital’s annual pride event, last Saturday. A Polish woman was killed in the attack and 31 people were injured, according to the authorities. The suspect, identified as 21-year-old Abdul Ballout, a German national of Lebanese descent, was fatally shot by police during an attempted arrest on Sunday following a large-scale manhunt. Law enforcement officials later revealed that Ballout was a known Islamist who had previously tried to join Islamic State (IS, formerly ISIS) and had pledged allegiance to the terrorist group in a video allegedly recorded on the day of the attack. Ballout was arrested at Berlin Airport in November 2025 upon his return from Lebanon, where he had spent three months behind bars over“inciting a religious conflict.”According to German officials, he had traveled to Lebanon earlier that year in a bid to join IS jihadists in neighboring Syria. In Germany, he was charged with“preparing a serious act of violence endangering the state”in connection with his attempt to join IS. He was tried by a juvenile court in May 2026, which sentenced him to a year and ten months behind bars. The court immediately suspended the sentence","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:36:49 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643734-german-trade-blame-berlin-attack/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:49
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Hybrid war hypocrisy: How the migrant attack on Spain shattered the ‘EU solidarity’ delusion,Hybrid war hypocrisy: How the migrant attack on Spain shattered the ‘EU solidarity’ delusion,"Hybrid war hypocrisy: How the migrant attack on Spain shattered the ‘EU solidarity’ delusion <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6ceced2030276684770059.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The EU has descended into infighting over the migrant invasion of Spain’s Ceuta, and Brussels is taking a hands-off approach <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643733-eu-ceuta-migrants-response/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The EU has responded to the migrant invasion of Ceuta with watery statements on solidarity, and a stone-faced refusal to blame Morocco for opening its borders. But when Brussels could blame Russia, it sang a different tune. As nearly 60,000 north African migrants poured into the Spanish exclave of Ceuta from Morocco on Thursday and Friday, right-wing and center-right European leaders immediately blamed Spain, where Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez had only three months earlier granted legal status to 500,000 illegal immigrants. Sanchez refused calls from local authorities in Ceuta to declare a national emergency, but deployed a token force of 60 troops to the exclave – a gesture perceived by the European right as inadequate. Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni was first to respond, calling for Spain’s exclusion from the EU’s border-free Schengen Area. Spanish Foreign Minister Jose Manuel Albares replied angrily, demanding“European solidarity, not partisan demagoguery”from Italy. Nevertheless, Italy suspended visa-free entry from Spain on Friday evening. There was little sympathy for Spain on the European right, with the following leaders and officials joining Meloni in blaming the migrant surge on Sanchez’ policies: Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk – demanded Spain secure its borders“if Schengen is to survive” Austrian Chancellor Christian Stocker – threatened to close Austria’s borders, accused Sanchez of creating“additional incentive for illegal migra","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 19:13:21 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643733-eu-ceuta-migrants-response/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:50
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Israel strikes Gaza hours after Trump announces Hamas disarmament plan,Israel strikes Gaza hours after Trump announces Hamas disarmament plan,"Israel strikes Gaza hours after Trump announces Hamas disarmament plan <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6ce06a85f5404fd6471df0.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israel has continued to strike Gaza after US President Donald Trump announced a Board of Peace roadmap for Hamas’ disarmament <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643725-israel-strikes-gaza-trump/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Israeli strikes have continued across Gaza hours after US President Donald Trump announced a“historic agreement”under which Hamas would be disarmed and the IDF would completely withdraw from the enclave. At least one Palestinian was killed and several others were wounded in the attacks on Friday, according to Palestinian health officials cited by media reports. The agreement was reached late on Thursday following talks mediated by Egypt, Qatar, Türkiye and the US under the Washington-led Board of Peace. Trump hailed it as a“monumental step toward lasting peace and security”and a major milestone in his 20-point plan for the enclave. However, both Hamas and Israeli officials have since questioned key provisions of the deal. Israeli National Security Minister Itamar Ben Gvir described the draft agreement as“unacceptable to Israel.”Writing on Telegram, he said that the“targeted killings”of“Hamas terrorists”in Gaza must continue, along with the“encouragement”of Palestinian“emigration”from the enclave. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has maintained that Israeli forces will“remain in the security zones as long as necessary.” Hamas has insisted that no disarmament will take place while Israeli forces remain in Gaza. In a statement, the group said any discussion of the handover of heavy weapons was conditional on a complete end to hostilities, a full Israeli withdrawal, reconstruction, international guarantees and progress toward Palestinian statehood. According to AFP, Hamas sour","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:20:22 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643725-israel-strikes-gaza-trump/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:51
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Why did nearly 60,000 migrants suddenly storm the border into Spain?","Why did nearly 60,000 migrants suddenly storm the border into Spain?","Why did nearly 60,000 migrants suddenly storm the border into Spain? <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6cb8ea85f54046f16daf7a.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Nearly 60,000 migrants have entered Spain’s Ceuta enclave in a day, raising questions over Morocco’s role and the timing of the surge <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643727-spain-ceuta-crisis-explainer/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Up to 60,000 migrants crossed from Morocco into Spain’s North African enclave of Ceuta in roughly 24 hours, overwhelming border forces and increasing the territory’s population by as much as 70%. The unprecedented influx has triggered a political crisis, raised questions over the true nature of the incident, and exposed deep divisions in the West. Tens of thousands of migrants stormed a weak point in the town of Ceuta, on the Spanish border with Morocco on Thursday. Ceuta’s regional president, Juan Jesus Vivas, said on Friday that around 60,000 people had entered the city since the border crisis erupted the previous day. The magnitude is such that it represents the single greatest human traffic invasion in the EU’s history. Even more conservative estimates from Spanish media and security sources ranging from 30,000 to 49,000 would still mean that Ceuta’s regular population of some 84,000 had increased overnight by some 50%. At least 41 migrants reportedly died. Many drowned while attempting to swim around the border barriers, while others were allegedly killed in a stampede near the Tarajal breakwater. Widely circulated footage showed predominantly young adult men swimming around the breakwater, climbing border structures, and pouring through crossing points as Spanish officers struggled to contain them. Some later marched through Ceuta chanting:“Bye bye Morocco, hello Spain.” Local police said they had been“completely overwhelmed”by the influx, while the regional ","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:53:40 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643727-spain-ceuta-crisis-explainer/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:52
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Zionists celebrate Spanish migrant invasion,Zionists celebrate Spanish migrant invasion,"Zionists celebrate Spanish migrant invasion <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6cb6892030274e5543c021.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Right-wing Israeli politicians and Zionist influencers see the migrant invasion of Ceuta as punishment for Spain’s pro-Palestine government <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643726-israel-zionists-celebrate-migrants-ceuta/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> As nearly 50,000 North African migrants surged into the Spanish exclave of Ceuta overnight, one group responded with mockery and glee: Israeli politicians and their Zionist supporters, who celebrated the slap in Spanish President Pedro Sanchez’ face. An estimated 49,000 migrants, predominantly young Moroccan men, stormed across Morocco’s border with the Spanish exclave of Ceuta between Thursday and Friday, after guards on the Moroccan side seemingly decided to open the barbed wire gates built to prevent such a surge. As videos of the migrants marauding through Ceuta spread on social media, local authorities in the city begged for military intervention from Madrid. Spanish Prime Minister Sanchez refused to declare a national emergency, but sent a token force of 60 troops to the exclave. Right-wing politicians across Europe condemned Sanchez’ half-hearted response, with Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni, Finnish Interior Minister Mari Rantanen, and Austrian Chancellor Christian Stocker all calling for Spain’s exclusion from the EU’s Schengen borderless travel zone. In certain Israeli circles, however, the reaction was one of jubilation. Although Israeli politicians and influencers have spent decades lamenting the supposed“Islamization”of Europe, they celebrated on Friday as tens of thousands of Muslims poured into EU territory. After Sanchez labeled Israel’s war on Gaza a“genocide,”banned the transit of military goods to Israeli via its territory, and denied the US use ","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:02:25 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643726-israel-zionists-celebrate-migrants-ceuta/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:53
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Heatwave burning Europe triggers nuclear powerdown,Heatwave burning Europe triggers nuclear powerdown,"Heatwave burning Europe triggers nuclear powerdown <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6ca53820302750df46e225.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A severe heatwave in Europe has driven Rhine and Danube to record lows, cutting power output and disrupting key supply routes <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643719-heatwave-europe-nuclear-powerdown/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The disastrous heatwave and drought across Europe have pushed the Rhine and Danube rivers to historic water lows, forcing two EU countries into atomic energy power-downs while disrupting industrial output and major trade routes. The Rhine and Danube serve as vital commercial corridors, historic borders and a continuous navigable link between the North Sea and the Black Sea. Many European power plants rely on the rivers for cooling water, and that is why record-low levels have sharply reduced electricity output. Hungary faces ‘unprecedented’ energy crunch The Danube, which flows through or borders ten countries from southwestern Germany to the Black Sea, has reached historically low levels this July. In Budapest, the river fell to a record-low of 23 cm on Thursday, 10 cm below the previous record set in 2018, according to Hungary’s official water-monitoring service. Hungary’s Paks nuclear plant, the country’s largest source of domestic power, generating nearly half of its electricity, was forced to cut output at three of its four reactors, reducing production to about 60% of capacity. On Thursday, Hungarian Prime Minister Peter Magyarwarnedthe plant could be shut down altogether within 24 to 72 hours“for the first time in 44 years,”because its cooling-water intake nozzles can no longer reach the receding Danube. “An energy crisis situation may arise from Monday,”Magyar warned, urging the public to reduce electricity use. He stressed the national energy supply remains secure fo","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:40:04 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643719-heatwave-europe-nuclear-powerdown/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:54
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Germany bets on AI to tackle migration,Germany bets on AI to tackle migration,"Germany bets on AI to tackle migration <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6c7e1e2030271a845bdc85.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Berlin backed using AI to help in processing asylum, visa and residence permit applications as Germany grapples with migration pressures <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643698-germany-ai-asylum-migration-crisis/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The German government has approved a bill to deploy artificial intelligence in processing asylum, visa and residence permit applications. The initiative aims to accelerate procedures and reduce pressure on immigration authorities. It was endorsed by the cabinet on Wednesday but still requires backing from the federal parliament and Federal Council. The EU’s economic powerhouse, Germany has long been the bloc’s leading destination for asylum seekers. In 2025, the country received more than 163,000 applications, accounting for about one in five claims lodged across the bloc’s 27 member states, according to the EU Agency for Asylum. The country also hosts the EU’s largest migrant population in absolute terms, with nearly 17 million foreign-born residents accounting for about 20% of Germany’s population. Over the past year, the federal government has tightened Germany’s migration policy by expanding border checks, increasing the number of migrants turned back at the border, and accelerating asylum procedures and deportations. The measures marked a sharp break with the open-border policy adopted by Chancellor Angela Merkel in 2015. Under the proposed AI Migration Administration Act, based on legislation adopted in November 2025, the authorities would be allowed to use personal data from asylum and immigration proceedings to develop AI systems and other automated software. The government says the tools would help analyze administrative workflows, process applications more quickly a","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:15:22 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643698-germany-ai-asylum-migration-crisis/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:55
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Why Western Europe needs the Ukraine conflict to continue,Why Western Europe needs the Ukraine conflict to continue,"Why Western Europe needs the Ukraine conflict to continue <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6c7cfb2030271def6a0249.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Drone warfare has altered the balance in Ukraine, weakened the spirit of Anchorage, and given Europe a new political case for the conflict <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643691-why-western-europe-needs-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByFyodor Lukyanov, the editor-in-chief of Russia in Global Affairs, chairman of the Presidium of the Council on Foreign and Defense Policy, and research director of the Valdai International Discussion Club. ByFyodor Lukyanov, the editor-in-chief of Russia in Global Affairs, chairman of the Presidium of the Council on Foreign and Defense Policy, and research director of the Valdai International Discussion Club. The military-technical balance of power is a key element of every political system and changes in that balance, including those brought about by the emergence of new forms of warfare, shape political intentions and determine what is possible in international affairs. The rapid transformation of warfare, driven by the drone revolution and demonstrated over the past year in both Ukraine and the conflict around Iran, offers an opportunity to reassess familiar concepts and how they are evolving. The spirit has changed, but let us leave the military aspects of drone warfare to the specialists and focus instead on the political consequences. August 2025 can be seen as the turning point, when Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin held their much-discussed meeting in Alaska. Whether any concrete agreements were reached remains disputed, but what’s clear is the essence of what became known as the ‘spirit of Anchorage’. Trump believed that although Ukraine was resisting stubbornly, its defeat was ultimately inevitable and the sooner Kiev accepted concessions, the less severe t","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:50:12 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643691-why-western-europe-needs-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:56
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Netanyahu accuses NYC Mayor Mamdani of backing Iran, Hamas, and Hezbollah","Netanyahu accuses NYC Mayor Mamdani of backing Iran, Hamas, and Hezbollah","Netanyahu accuses NYC Mayor Mamdani of backing Iran, Hamas, and Hezbollah <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6c66bc2030271ba2083342.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has accused New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani of supporting Iran, Hamas, and Hezbollah <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643700-netanyahu-mamdani-public-feud/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has renewed his criticism of New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani, who has said the Israeli leader could be arrested on war-crimes charges if he visits the city. The International Criminal Court (ICC) issued an arrest warrant for Netanyahu in 2024 over Israel’s military campaign in Gaza. Mamdani has said his administration would seek toenforcethe warrant if presented with an opportunity to do so. Speaking to Fox News host Sean Hannity this week, Netanyahu accused the mayor of siding with Iran, which he described as a mortal enemy of both Israel and the United States. “The army of Israel, the young men and women of Israel, the public in Israel… stand up and say, ‘Yes, we’re willing to stand up at this moment and stand in the breach with the United States.’ This is the ally that Mamdani and his ilk are vilifying,”Netanyahu said. Netanyahu claims NYC mayor Zohran Mamdani ""supports Iran, Hamas and Hezbollah.""Source: Hang Out with Sean Hannitypic.twitter.com/3Lahrohbcc “And what is he supporting? Iran. Who is he supporting? Hamas. Who is he supporting? Hezbollah,”he added, accusing Mamdani and other critics of Israel of“moral cynicism”and“absurdity.” Iran, Hamas, and the Lebanon-based Hezbollah movement are part of what Tehran calls the regional“axis of resistance,”an alliance opposed to Israel and its influence in the Middle East. Public opinion in the US has shifted against Israel in recent years as Netanyahu’s government expanded milit","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:27:22 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643700-netanyahu-mamdani-public-feud/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:57
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Merz readies secret plan to move German troops to Russian border – media,Merz readies secret plan to move German troops to Russian border – media,"Merz readies secret plan to move German troops to Russian border – media <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6c223f85f54046f16daf11.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Berlin is reportedly developing a way to bypass regional governments that could oppose turning Germany into a NATO hub in a war with Russia <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643694-berlin-nato-troops-loophole-russia/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The German government is developing a“secret plan”to prevent regional authorities from potentially obstructing the deployment of NATO troops to the Russian border, according to a joint investigation by The Telegraph and Die Welt. The“contingency”measures are reportedly driven by fears that the Alternative for Germany (AfD) party could secure enough support in upcoming regional elections in two eastern states to form local governments. Known for criticizing Berlin’s anti-Russia policies as harmful to Germany’s national interests, the right-wing party has grown to become the country’s most popular political force after once again being excluded from last year’s federal coalition talks. In the state of Saxony-Anhalt, the AfD currently enjoys the support of 41% of voters, a recent survey suggested, compared with only 24% for Chancellor Friedrich Merz’s Christian Democratic Union (CDU). In the northeastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, the AfD is polling at 36%, seven points ahead of its closest competitors, the Social Democratic Party. Berlin has long accused the AfD of extremism, while Defense Minister Boris Pistorius has claimed that the party has“undeniable”ties to Russia and must be deprived of access to classified information if it comes to power. The federal government is now seeking a way to rein in what The Telegraph bluntlydescribedas“pro-Kremlin traitor states”in the event that NATO decides it is time to go to war with Moscow. The sc","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 04:22:35 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643694-berlin-nato-troops-loophole-russia/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:58
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Merz is chancellor of Ukraine, not Germany – senior opposition MP (VIDEO)","Merz is chancellor of Ukraine, not Germany – senior opposition MP (VIDEO)","Merz is chancellor of Ukraine, not Germany – senior opposition MP (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6bcf7620302762cc5441f4.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Chancellor Friedrich Merz’s government is spending billions of euros on Ukraine while doing “almost nothing” for Germans, according to an MP <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643689-merz-chancellor-ukraine-germany-mp/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> German Chancellor Friedrich Merz is caring more for Ukraine than his own nation, an opposition MP, Marcus Frohnmaier, told Rick Sanchez on the latest episode of Sanchez Effect aired on Wednesday. The government has neglected the ongoing competitiveness and energy crisis in Germany while directing billions of euros in aid to Kiev, according to the lawmaker from the right-wing Alternative for Germany (AfD) party. Merz“is the chancellor of Ukraine and not the chancellor of Germany,”Frohnmaier stated. Merz, who came to power in 2025 following a snap election, has become the least popular German chancellor in decades in less than two years since taking office. A total of 84% of Germans were dissatisfied with his performance, including more than half of his own Christian Democratic Union (CDU) party supporters, according to an ARD-DeutschlandTrend poll published earlier this month. According to Frohnmaier, Merz either reneged upon or failed to deliver on almost all his campaign promises. The chancellor“promised people to [build] a strong economy, to make Germany safe again, and so on, and he failed,”said the MP, who represents the nation’s most popular party, according to the polls. The lawmaker also argued that the Merz government outright ignored the most pressing issues faced by the nation.“German companies [are] leaving the country, they’re going to Poland, they’re going to the US,”he said, adding that those that are“not big enough”just go“bankrupt.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 03:13:37 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643689-merz-chancellor-ukraine-germany-mp/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:29:59
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump pours cold water on Kiev’s Patriot dream,Trump pours cold water on Kiev’s Patriot dream,"Trump pours cold water on Kiev’s Patriot dream <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6bfae32030276b26646ebd.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US must be careful about sharing Patriots with Ukraine, President Trump has said, despite previously promising to grant Kiev a license <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643693-trump-ukraine-patriot-missiles/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has cast doubt on whether Washington will allow Ukraine to manufacture Patriot interceptor missiles, despite previously promising to grant Kiev a production license. Trump told the Financial Times in a telephone interview on Thursday that he was“not sure”whether Ukraine would receive permission to produce the missiles, adding that Washington was still considering the request. Describing the Patriot as a“very extraordinary weapon,”Trump said the US had to be“a little bit careful”about granting other countries access to its advanced military technology. The remarks appear to contradict Trump’spublic pledgeat the NATO summit in Türkiye earlier this month, when he told Ukrainian leader Vladimir Zelensky that Washington would provide Kiev with a license to manufacture Patriot interceptors. “We’ll give them the right to make Patriots. We’ll show them how to do it,”Trump said at the time, suggesting that Ukraine could produce the missiles rather than complain that the US was not supplying enough of them. Zelensky emerged from closed-door talks with Trump at the White House on Tuesday, claiming that they had discussed licenses for interceptor production. Trump, however, offeredno indicationthat any agreement had been reached, saying only that“many things were discussed”and that the meeting went“very well.” The initiative is also facing resistance from US manufacturers, with Boeing reportedly reluctant to transfer sensitive technology used in the seeker warhe","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 01:35:45 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643693-trump-ukraine-patriot-missiles/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:30:00
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Hamas accepts Trump’s Gaza disarmament plan in principle – official (VIDEOS),Hamas accepts Trump’s Gaza disarmament plan in principle – official (VIDEOS),"Hamas accepts Trump’s Gaza disarmament plan in principle – official (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.07/thumbnail/6a6bdf7b203027688c7907df.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Hamas has agreed to Donald Trump’s Board of Peace plan to completely disarm in Gaza, a senior official has said <br /><a href=""https://www.rt.com/news/643692-trump-gaza-peace-board-hamas/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Palestinian militant group Hamas has agreed to completely disarm in Gaza under US President Donald Trump’s Board of Peace plan, although Israel must also meet a series of conditions as part of the agreement, according to a senior official. Ghazi Hamad, a member of the Hamas negotiating delegation, confirmed to Al Jazeera on Friday that an agreement has been reached, adding that an official statement will be released soon. “These negotiations were difficult and hard, and we tried to reach the best possible formula that was achievable,”Hamad, whose remarks were also carried by Reuters and the BBC, was cited as saying. He stressed, however, that Israel must approve the phased disarmament, adding that Hamas will not implement any part of the agreement unless Israeli forces fulfilled their obligations, particularly withdrawing from Gaza and advancing reconstruction in the Palestinian territory. “We will not take any action regarding disarmament prior to Israel’s withdrawal from the [Gaza] Strip,”he stated. Hamad also told the BBC that the group insists on the wording“inventorying and storing weapons”under Palestinian oversight rather than handing them over to Israel. Trump breaks the news The news first emerged when Trumpannouncedon Truth Social on Thursday that his Board of Peace has reached a“historic agreement”on the complete disarmament of Hamas and every other armed group in Gaza, calling it a“monumental step toward lasting peace and security”and a major milestone in his 20-p","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 23:34:49 +0000",https://www.rt.com/news/643692-trump-gaza-peace-board-hamas/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-08-03 01:30:01
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"US, Iran to begin negotiations on August 3 — President Trump","US, Iran to begin negotiations on August 3 — President Trump","US, Iran to begin negotiations on August 3 — President Trump The US leader added that the allies ""think there’s a deal"" WASHINGTON, August 3. /TASS/. The United States and Iran are set to resume negotiations on August 3, US President Donald Trump said. Speaking to the press aboard Air Force One on Sunday, August 2, Trump said that the United States had decided against delivering ""a massive attack"" on Iran at the request of Saudi Arabia, Qatar, the United Arab Emirates (UAE), and Iran. ""They knew the extent of the attack because they saw it forming. Now what we’re doing is we’re talking to them in the form of a negotiation. It begins tomorrow afternoon, and we’ll see,"" Trump stated. ""We’re all set to go, but when the allies asked to call it off, they got us sort of saying, ‘Well, let’s see.’ And the reason they ask is they think there’s a deal,"" the US president noted. Trump also said that a deal has been finalized regarding the Strait of Hormuz, and Iran’s nuclear issue was the next to be settled. ""There’s a deal on Hormuz, and then there will be a deal on the nuclear, or you might call it the denuclearization of Iran. I call it the denuclearization of Iran,"" he added. TheFarsnews agency reported earlier, citing a source in the Iranian negotiating team, that there was no agreement on resuming shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, and the previous reports spread on this deal were false. The Israeli TV Channel 12 reported earlier on August 2 that Trump agreed to cancel the planned powerful strike on Iran after Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi accepted a compromise proposal by Qatari medi","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:10:45 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168221,2026-08-03 01:30:03
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Brent falls below $82 per barrel, first time since July 13","Brent falls below $82 per barrel, first time since July 13","Brent falls below $82 per barrel, first time since July 13 By 10:10 p.m. GMT, August 2, Brent had pared losses to trade at $82.89 a barrel MOSCOW, August 3. /TASS/. The price of Brent crude futures contract with September delivery on the ICE exchange in London fell below $82 a barrel for the first time since July 13, according to trading data. As of 1:00 Moscow time (10:00 p.m. GMT, August 2), Brent was down 6.74% at $82 a barrel. By 1:10 Moscow time (10:10 p.m. GMT, August 2), Brent had pared losses to trade at $82.89 a barrel, down 5.73%.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 01:50:01 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2168219,2026-08-03 01:30:04
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Kiev troops bombard Donetsk People’s Republic 14 times over past day,Kiev troops bombard Donetsk People’s Republic 14 times over past day,"Kiev troops bombard Donetsk People’s Republic 14 times over past day Two civilians were reported to sustain wounds DONETSK, August 3. /TASS/. The Ukrainian military shelled residential areas in the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) 14 times over the past 24 hours, two civilians were wounded, the department for documenting Ukraine’s war crimes at the DPR head’s office and government said in a statement on Monday. ""Over the past 24-hour period, 14 shelling attacks by Ukraine’s armed formations were registered. Two civilians were reported to sustain wounds,"" the statement said. According to the statement, 24 munitions of various types were fired from Ukraine. A truck and a car, a residential house, and four civilian infrastructure facilities were damaged.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:58:06 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168209,2026-08-03 01:30:05
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,At least 19 Palestinians killed in Gaza during day as result of Israel’s operations,At least 19 Palestinians killed in Gaza during day as result of Israel’s operations,"At least 19 Palestinians killed in Gaza during day as result of Israel’s operations Sources in Gaza hospitals told Al Jazeera that 12 people were killed in the city of Gaza in the north of the enclave TUNIS, August 2. /TASS/. At least 19 Palestinians have died during the day as result of Israeli operations in the Gaza Strip, theAl Jazeeratelevision channel said, citing sources in Gaza hospitals. According to the sources, 12 people were killed in the city of Gaza in the north of the enclave. Two people died and several others were wounded after a strike on a car in the city of Deir al-Balah in the central Gaza Strip. Three people were wounded in a drone attack near the al-Mawasi humanitarian zone west of Khan Yunis in the south of the enclave, the ambulance and emergency response service said. According to the Nasser medical compound, one person received a gunshot wound as a result of the Israeli military’s actions south of Khan Yunis, outside the areas under their control. The Palestinian Red Crescent Society reported that a girl was wounded after Israel’s shelling attack in Jabalya in the northern Gaza Strip.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:02:24 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168207,2026-08-03 01:30:06
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Top Saudi, Iranian diplomats discuss de-escalation efforts in region","Top Saudi, Iranian diplomats discuss de-escalation efforts in region","Top Saudi, Iranian diplomats discuss de-escalation efforts in region Prince Faisal bin Farhan Al-Saud stressed that Riyadh is committed to continuing to play its regional role in ensuring security and stability DOHA, August 2. /TASS/. Diplomatic efforts toward easing tensions in the Gulf were the focus of a phone call between Foreign Ministers Prince Faisal bin Farhan Al-Saud of Saudi Arabia and Abbas Araghchi of Iran, the Saudi Foreign Ministry said. ""The sides discussed recent developments amid the current situation and diplomatic efforts geared toward de-escalation,"" it said. The top Saudi diplomat stressed that Riyadh is committed to continuing to play its regional role in ensuring security and stability. Earlier, Saudi Crown Prince and Prime Minister Mohammed bin Salman Al-Saud held a phone call with US President Donald Trump to discuss ways of easing tension in the Middle East. According to theAxiosportal, the Saudi Crown Prince expressed concern over Washington’s plans and warned the US leader against delivering massive strikes against Iran. According to the US media, Saudi Arabia and other Gulf countries were afraid that an American attack would entail Iran’s strikes on their oil infrastructure. Meanwhile, Trump agreed to cancel a planned powerful strike on Iran for the sake of reaching a deal with Tehran. According to the US leader, the sides agreed on an outline of a future agreement that will envisage an immediate opening of the Strait of Hormuz and removing Iran’s nuclear threat.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:41:03 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168205,2026-08-03 01:30:07
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian Maritime Board chief holds talks on maritime logistics cooperation in Algeria,Russian Maritime Board chief holds talks on maritime logistics cooperation in Algeria,"Russian Maritime Board chief holds talks on maritime logistics cooperation in Algeria The sides also discussed ensuring security of navigation in the Mediterranean ALGIERS, August 2. /TASS/. Russian Presidential Aide and head of the Maritime Board Nikolay Patrushev held talks with Secretary General of Algeria's Ministry of Interior, Local Authorities and Transport is Djamel Eddine Abdelghani Dridi, a TASS correspondent reported. The sides discussed promising cooperation projects in the area of maritime logistics, as well as issues of ensuring security of navigation in the Mediterranean. Patrushev and Dridi also discussed plans for future contacts between various ministries, agencies, and companies regarding maritime activities.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:26:05 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168203,2026-08-03 01:30:09
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Israeli court bans use of crocodiles to secure prisons with terrorists,Israeli court bans use of crocodiles to secure prisons with terrorists,"Israeli court bans use of crocodiles to secure prisons with terrorists According to a report by The Jerusalem Post, the court issued this ruling based on a motion from the animal rights organization Let the Animals Live TEL AVIV, August 2. /TASS/. A court in Israel has prohibited National Security Minister Itamar Ben-Gvir to use crocodiles to secure terrorists in prisons,The Jerusalem Postreported. According to the newspaper, the Jerusalem District Court issued this ruling based on a motion from the animal rights organization Let the Animals Live. Meanwhile, Ben-Gvir accused the court of siding with terrorists. ""Once again, in a time of war, the legal system sides with the terrorists, thwarting important steps for Israeli deterrence,"" he was quoted as saying. ""We know that the terrorists are worried about the arrival of the crocodiles, but today the court came to their aid."" The newspaper noted that pressure has been exerted on the Israel Nature and Parks Authority for several months ago to allow the National Security Ministry to place crocodiles in moats around prisons holding inmates convicted for security-related crimes. The pilot project was expected to kick off at Ketziot Prison in the Negev desert in southern Israel.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:13:21 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168201,2026-08-03 01:30:10
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Teenage girl dies, two more children wounded after Ukraine drone attack in Belgorod Region","Teenage girl dies, two more children wounded after Ukraine drone attack in Belgorod Region","Teenage girl dies, two more children wounded after Ukraine drone attack in Belgorod Region Two more girls, of seven and nine years of age, received shrapnel wounds and were taken to a hospital, the region’s acting governor, Alexander Shuvayev said BELGOROD, August 2. /TASS/. A teenage girl died and two more children were wounded after Ukraine’s drone attack on a playground in Russia’s borderline Belgorod Region, the region’s acting governor, Alexander Shuvayev said. ""I am grieved to say that a child died and two others received wounds after a terror attack by Kiev’s neo-Nazis in the Valuisky district. A Ukrainian drone struck near a playground in the village of Printsevka,"" he wrote on messaging app Max. AS a result of the strike, a 13-year-old girl received grave wounds and medics failed to save her. ""I share the grief of this loss with the family. Of course, no words can express the pain of losing a child. This is a great tragedy not only for the family, but for all of us. My sincere condolences to the girl’s parents,"" he wrote. Two more girls, of seven and nine years of age, received shrapnel wounds and were taken to a hospital.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:46:08 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168199,2026-08-03 01:30:11
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Another batch of Russian humanitarian aid arrives in Iran,Another batch of Russian humanitarian aid arrives in Iran,"Another batch of Russian humanitarian aid arrives in Iran Тhe cargoes have been handed over to the Iranian Red Crescent Society, a Dagestan government representative to the Russian trade mission in Iran Andrey Tanayev said TEHRAN, August 2. /TASS/. Another batch of humanitarian aid from Russia has arrived in Iran amid the current spiral of escalation between Tehran and Washington, a Dagestan government representative to the Russian trade mission in Iran Andrey Tanayev said. ""Today, a batch of humanitarian aid arrived from Moscow. It was sent by the Medargo company with the support from the Great Fatherland charity foundation. The aid includes basically medical equipment and medicine, some 11 tons in all,"" he told TASS. According to Tanayev, the cargoes have been handed over to the Iranian Red Crescent Society. ""Deliveries [of humanitarian aid] will continue in the future,"" he pledged. The United States and Israel launched a war against Iran on February 28. In June, Washington and Tehran signed a memorandum of understanding envisaging an immediate ceasefire on all fronts, including in Lebanon. However, the United States resumed large-scale attacks on Iran overnight to July 8, having accused it of breaching the existing agreements in what concerned the Strait of Hormuz. According to the Iranian health ministry, 59 people have died and at least 666 have been injured since June 27.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:18:25 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168197,2026-08-03 01:30:11
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Iran-Oman talks on Strait of Hormuz nearing completion — top Iranian diplomat,Iran-Oman talks on Strait of Hormuz nearing completion — top Iranian diplomat,"Iran-Oman talks on Strait of Hormuz nearing completion — top Iranian diplomat Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi noted progress in the negotiations TEHRAN, August 2. /TASS/. Negotiations between Iran and Oman on issues of the navigation in the Strait of Hormuz are nearing completion, Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said. ""At the beginning of today’s government meeting, Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi presented a report on the current state of the talks between Iran and Oman. He noted progress in the negotiations and stated that the talks are at the final stage and nearing completion,"" according to a post on Araghchi’s Telegram channel. The Fars agency reported earlier that Iran had not given its permission to opening the Strait of Hormuz while reports by the Israeli N12 television channel claiming that Tehran has accepted a proposal by Qatari mediators to resume the waterway’s operation have nothing to do with reality.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:56:37 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168179,2026-08-03 01:30:12
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian drone operators hit gas station used by Ukrainian army in Kramatorsk,Russian drone operators hit gas station used by Ukrainian army in Kramatorsk,"Russian drone operators hit gas station used by Ukrainian army in Kramatorsk The station was used in the interests of the Ukrainian army, the Russian defense ministry said MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. Russian Battlegroup Center’s FPV drone operators have wiped out a gas station in Kramatorsk that was used in the interests of the Ukrainian army, the Russian defense ministry said. ""FPV drone operators of the 51st army of the Battlegroup Center continue delivering pin-point trikes on the Ukrainian army’s military infrastructure facilities. In Kramatorks, kamikaze drones wipe out a gas station used in the interests of Ukrainian troops,"" it said.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:55:06 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168171,2026-08-03 01:30:13
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian forces jit Ukraine’s Pelican radar system in Dnepropetrovsk Region,Russian forces jit Ukraine’s Pelican radar system in Dnepropetrovsk Region,"Russian forces jit Ukraine’s Pelican radar system in Dnepropetrovsk Region Pelican radar system was hit with the use of a Geran drone, the Russian defense ministry said MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. Russian forces hit Ukraine’s Pelican radar system near Kalinovka in he Dnepropetrovsk Region with the use of a Geran drone, the Russian defense ministry said. ""The footage of radar control of the Geran-4 Seeker unmanned aerial vehicle’s strike against a Pelican radar system of the Ukrainian army near the settlement of Kalinovka in the Dnepropetrovsk Region. The target was hit,"" it said.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:54:11 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168169,2026-08-03 01:30:14
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Russian forces continue striking port infrastructure, ships used to supply Ukrainian army","Russian forces continue striking port infrastructure, ships used to supply Ukrainian army","Russian forces continue striking port infrastructure, ships used to supply Ukrainian army Russian forces continued striking Ukrainian transport infrastructure, the Russian defense ministry said MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. Throughout the day, Russian forces continued striking Ukrainian transport infrastructure used in the interests of the Ukrainian army at the port of Nikolayev and in the Black Sea, the Russian defense ministry said. ""During the day, the Russian armed forces continue delivering strikes on Ukrainian transport infrastructure used in the interests of the Ukrainian army. Russian unmanned aerial vehicles hit: a dry cargo vessel carrying military cargoes in the Black Sea, port infrastructure, two dry cargo vessels delivering cargoes for the Ukrainian army and a tugboat reequipped for using uncrewed boats at the port of Nikolayev,"" it said.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:52:48 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168163,2026-08-03 01:30:15
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Over 35 minors killed, some 300 wounded in Ukraine’s attacks in 2026 — diplomat","Over 35 minors killed, some 300 wounded in Ukraine’s attacks in 2026 — diplomat","Over 35 minors killed, some 300 wounded in Ukraine’s attacks in 2026 — diplomat ""Deliberate strikes against children, their murder, and the wounding of children constitute an appalling war crime committed by Ukrainian monsters,"" Russian Foreign Ministry’s Ambassador at Large Rodion Miroshnik said MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. More than 35 minors have died and around 300 more have been injured in Ukraine’s attacks since the beginning of this year, Russian Foreign Ministry’s Ambassador at Large Rodion Miroshnik said. ""Deliberate strikes against children, their murder, and the wounding of children constitute an appalling war crime committed by Ukrainian monsters,"" the diplomat stated on his Telegram channel. ""Since the beginning of the year, more than 35 minors have been killed and about 300 wounded"" by the Kiev regime. Earlier on Sunday, a 13-year-oil girl died and two more children were badly wounded after Ukraine’s targeted strike on a playground in the village of Printsevka in Russia’s borderline Belgorod Region.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:49:43 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168193,2026-08-03 01:30:16
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,245 Ukrainian drones taken down over Russian regions during day,245 Ukrainian drones taken down over Russian regions during day,"245 Ukrainian drones taken down over Russian regions during day From 8:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. Moscow time Russian air defense systems intercepted and destroyed 245 Ukrainian fixed-wing unmanned, the Russian defense ministry said MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. More than 240 Ukrainian drones were shot down over Russian regions and the Black Sea during the day, the Russian defense ministry said. ""From 8:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. Moscow time (5:00 a.m. to 5:00 a.m. GMT), Russian air defense systems intercepted and destroyed 245 Ukrainian fixed-wing unmanned aerial vehicles over Crimea, the Belgorod, Bryansk, Kaluga, Kursk, Kirov, Lipetsk, Oryol, Omsk, Ryazan, Samara, Tula, Moscow, Krasnodar, and Perm Regions, the Republic of Bashkortostan, the Khanty-Mansi autonomous area, and the Black Sea,"" it said.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:19:21 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168187,2026-08-03 01:30:17
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Implementation of agreement with Lebanon to depend on Hezbollah’s disarmament,Implementation of agreement with Lebanon to depend on Hezbollah’s disarmament,"Implementation of agreement with Lebanon to depend on Hezbollah’s disarmament ""Israel’s security is not a bargaining chip,"" adviser in the Israeli prime minister’s office Dmitri Gendelman said. TEL AVIV, August 2. /TASS/. The implementation of the framework agreement with Lebanon, including the withdrawal of Israeli troops, will depend on Hezbollah’s disarmament, adviser in the Israeli prime minister’s office Dmitri Gendelman said. ""Any progress under the framework agreement can be possible only if the Lebanese side takes concrete and verifiable steps to disarm Hezbollah. As long as the threat persists, the IDF (Israel Defense Forces - TASS) will continue to carry out its missions near our (Israel’s - TASS) northern borders,"" he told TASS. ""Israel’s security is not a bargaining chip,"" he stressed. Following five round of US-brokered consultation in Washington, Lebanon and Israel signed, on June 26, a framework agreement, under which the Lebanese military is to gradually restore effective sovereign control over the entire Lebanese territory while Israel is to withdraw its troops of the occupied areas. Axios and Israel’s Channel 12 correspondent Barak Ravid wrote on his X page on July 28, citing a US Department of State official that Israel and Lebanon would hold another round on talks in Rome on August 4 through 6. According to Ravid, representatives of the two countries, as well as of the United States will hold talks ""on potentially expanding the process of Israeli military redeployment in Southern Lebanon and discuss the land border disputes between the countries."" ""In Rome, technical groups will focus on advancing the full implementation of the framework agreemen","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 21:18:14 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168183,2026-08-03 01:30:17
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"At least 14 die, 20 wounded in terror attack in northwestern Pakistan","At least 14 die, 20 wounded in terror attack in northwestern Pakistan","At least 14 die, 20 wounded in terror attack in northwestern Pakistan According to the local police chief, a suicide bomber activated an explosive device after police officers tried to search him at the entrance to the police station near ISLAMABAD, August 2. /TASS/. At least 14 people died and 20 others were injured after a terror attack near a police station in the Pakistani northwestern Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province, the Dawn newspaper reported, citing the police. According to the local police chief, a suicide bomber activated an explosive device after police officers tried to search him at the entrance to the police station near. The incident occurred near the Kabal Chowk square in the town of Kabal when it was crowded by people protesting against growing terrorist activities in the Swat Valley.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:26:15 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168181,2026-08-03 01:30:18
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Over 1,000 migrants remaining near center for migrants in Ceuta — agency","Over 1,000 migrants remaining near center for migrants in Ceuta — agency","Over 1,000 migrants remaining near center for migrants in Ceuta — agency According to the EFE agency, the center is overcrowded MADRID, August 2. /TASS/. More than 1,000 migrants are remaining near the center for their temporary allocation in the Spanish autonomous city of Ceuta, located on the northern coast of Africa, hoping to be admitted there, the EFE agency reported. According to the agency, the center is overcrowded. Hundreds of migrants have set up a camp in the mountainous area near the center, waiting for vacant places. Most of the migrants are from African countries south of the Sahara. A nearby beach is occupied by migrants. According to earlier reports, several dozen migrants attempted to break into the center’s territory by force but failed. Tens of thousands of migrants managed to reach Ceuta by swimming or walking around the breakwater separating the city from Morocco in late July. Amid the migration crisis, the Spanish authorities have deployed troops to help ensure security in the city. At least 72 people have reportedly died while trying to reach Ceuta. Meanwhile, according to latest reports, most of the migrants have returned to Morocco.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:59:22 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168177,2026-08-03 01:30:19
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,US discussing with Ukraine potential transfer of Patriot production technologies — MP,US discussing with Ukraine potential transfer of Patriot production technologies — MP,"US discussing with Ukraine potential transfer of Patriot production technologies — MP US President Donald Trump said on July 31 that the United States should be very careful with granting licenses to other countries to manufacture its weapons WASHIGTON, August 2. /TASS/. The United States and Ukraine are in consultations on issues related to the possible transfer of technology for the production of Patriot air defense systems to Kiev, US Congressman Mike Turner (Republican from Ohio) said. ""I do think that there are ongoing negotiations concerning providing a broader opportunity for Ukraine to have access to Patriot technology to be able to have production and defensive technology,"" he told CBS. ""I think it's still in process,"" he said, adding that it will be ""very, very difficult"" to settle these matters. US President Donald Trump said on July 31 that the United States should be very careful with granting licenses to other countries to manufacture its weapons. He said that Washington had not agreed to supply Kiev with either Patriot system technology or Tomahawk cruise missiles, and questioned this possibility.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:58:42 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168175,2026-08-03 01:30:20
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,35 vessels redirected by US military since resumption of blockade of Iran — CENTCOM,35 vessels redirected by US military since resumption of blockade of Iran — CENTCOM,"35 vessels redirected by US military since resumption of blockade of Iran — CENTCOM Disabled 2, and boarded 2, it wrote on X NEW YORK, August 2. /TASS/. The US military has redirected 35 commercial vessels since July 14 when the United States resumed its naval blockade against Iran, the US Central Command (CENTCOM) said. ""As of Aug. 2, CENTCOM has redirected 35 commercial vessels, disabled 2, and boarded 2,"" it wrote on X. CENTCOM said earlier that more than 20 US ships were operating in the Middle East to enforce the blockade against Iran.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:12:07 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168167,2026-08-03 01:30:21
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Georgia optimistic about restoring strategic partnership with US — PM,Georgia optimistic about restoring strategic partnership with US — PM,"Georgia optimistic about restoring strategic partnership with US — PM Relations between Tbilisi and Washington became strained in 2024 after Georgia passed a law on foreign agents TBILISI, August 2. /TASS/. Georgia’s authorities maintain contacts with the American side and are optimistic about the restoration of strategic partnership with the United States, Georgian Prime Minister Irakli Kobakhidze said. ""We remain optimistic that the strategic partnership between Georgia and the United States will be restored. We are maintaining communication with our American partners. We hope to see reciprocal steps that will ultimately lead to the restoration of the strategic partnership. This is our goal, and we are patiently awaiting reciprocal steps from the American side,"" he told reporters. Relations between Tbilisi and Washington became strained in 2024 after Georgia passed a law on foreign agents. Following the Georgian prime minister’s November 28, 2024 statement on freezing the process of launching accession talks with the European Union, the US Department of State suspended strategic partnership with the country. Before Donald Trump took office as president of the United States, Georgia’s authorities had been saying that they were hoping for a change of power in the United States and a reset in relations with Washington. The Georgian leadership has also been saying that it is awaiting reciprocal steps from the United States. Contacts between the Georgian and US leadership have intensified in recent time.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:10:00 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168165,2026-08-03 01:30:22
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Two firefighting helicopters collide west of Athens, two die — TV","Two firefighting helicopters collide west of Athens, two die — TV","Two firefighting helicopters collide west of Athens, two die — TV According to the television channel, one of the helicopters caught fire and crashed, while the other one made an emergency landing ATHENS, August 2. /TASS/. Two helicopters collided in Greece while fighting wildfires west of Athens, leaving two people dead, the Greek Skai television channel reported. According to the television channel, one of the helicopters caught fire and crashed, while the other one made an emergency landing. The crew of the first helicopter contacted the operations center. Medics are rushing to the scene to evacuate the pilot and his assistant who received minor injuries. Rescuers have reached the second helicopter as well. According to the documentonews.gr news portal, the second helicopter’s crew have died. According to the Proto Thema newspaper, the helicopters were leased from Romani’s fire service. Both pilots are Romanian nationals while their assistants are Gtreeks.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 18:09:20 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168155,2026-08-03 01:30:23
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Israel eliminates three radicals in Gaza Strip — IDF,Israel eliminates three radicals in Gaza Strip — IDF,"Israel eliminates three radicals in Gaza Strip — IDF The three terrorists attempted to advance terror attacks against Israeli civilians and IDF troops, the Israel Defense Forces said TEL AVIV, August 2. /TASS/. The Israeli military has eliminated three armed radicals, including a Hamas battalion commander, in the Gaza Strip, the Israel Defense Forces (IDF) said. ""Yesterday (Saturday), the IDF struck in the area of Gaza City and eliminated Alaa Imad Khamis Tarams, a terrorist from the ‘Army of Islam’ terrorist organization, and Hassan Ibrahim Shehadeh Qahman, a terrorist from the Islamic Jihad terrorist organization,"" the IDF said. ""In an additional strike in the northern Gaza Strip last week, the IDF eliminated Ahmad Khudar, a commander in the Jabalya battalion of the Hamas terrorist organization."" ""The three terrorists attempted to advance terror attacks against Israeli civilians and IDF troops, and were eliminated in order to remove the threat,"" it added.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 17:50:02 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168151,2026-08-03 01:30:24
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Workers’ Party nominates Lula da Silva candidate for Brazilian president,Workers’ Party nominates Lula da Silva candidate for Brazilian president,"Workers’ Party nominates Lula da Silva candidate for Brazilian president Incumbent Vice President Geraldo Alckmin will run alongside the Brazilian leader for the vice presidency, the party’s convention decided RIO DE JANEIRO, August 2. /TASS/. The Brazilian Workers’ Party has nominated incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva as candidate for president. Incumbent Vice President Geraldo Alckmin will run alongside the Brazilian leader for the vice presidency, the party’s convention decided. Along with the Workers’ Party, the election coalition includes the Communist Party of Brazil, the Green Party, the Socialism and Liberty Party, the Sustainable Development Solutions Network, the Brazilian Socialist Party, and the Democratic Labor Party. The presidential election will be held in Brazil in October. This will be fourth presidential campaign for Lula da Silva. His key rival will be Flavio Bolsonaro, a rightist opposition candidate.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 17:40:16 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168149,2026-08-03 01:30:25
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Donbass Dome system thwarts nearly 140 Ukrainian drone attacks in past week,Donbass Dome system thwarts nearly 140 Ukrainian drone attacks in past week,"Donbass Dome system thwarts nearly 140 Ukrainian drone attacks in past week Ukrainian troops tried to attack a power substation in Donetsk with the use of a FP-2 fixed-wing drone equipped, the Federal Security Service’s department for the Donetsk People’s Republic said DONETSK, August 2. /TASS/. The Donbass Dome air defense system and mobile fire teams have intercepted and neutralized nearly 140 Ukrainian drones over the past week, the Federal Security Service’s (FSB) department for the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) said. ""During the past week, the Donbass Dome system and mobile fire teams prevented 138 enemy terror attacks. Ukrainian militants continue using the tactic of combined attacks on civilians and the republic’s infrastructure,"" it said. Thus, according to it, Ukrainian troops tried to attack a power substation in Donetsk with the use of a FP-2 fixed-wing drone equipped with a FP-105 100 kg shrapnel-stuffed warhead. A Ukrainian Blyskavka drone with a shrapnel-stuffed warhead was intercepted in Makeyevka. Hornet, Darts, and Baton drones, also stuffed with shrapnel, were shot down near a railway hub near Shakhterskoye. In Gorlovka, Ukrainian terrorists tried to strike civilians at a market, near a boiler house, and residential quarters. ""Specialists intercepted the enemy drones, which were later rendered harmless by comb specialists. No damage was done to civilians and civilian infrastructure,"" it added.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 17:18:12 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168147,2026-08-03 01:30:26
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"15 civilians killed, 51 injured in Ukraine’s attacks on Energodar since late April","15 civilians killed, 51 injured in Ukraine’s attacks on Energodar since late April","15 civilians killed, 51 injured in Ukraine’s attacks on Energodar since late April Five apartments were destroyed by fire, CEO of Russia’s state nuclear corporation Rosatom Alexey Likhachev said MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. Fifteen people have died and 51 more have been injured in Ukraine’s attacks since the outbreak of the current escalation around Energodar, the satellite city of the Zaporozhye Nuclear Power Plant, CEO of Russia’s state nuclear corporation Rosatom Alexey Likhachev said. ""On Friday evening, a drone hit a five-storey residential house. As a result, five apartments were destroyed by fire. Regrettably, a woman bornin in 1952 died. In all, since the outbreak of the current escalation around Energodar on April 27, as many as 15 city residents have died and 51 have been injured,"" he said. According to Likhachev, Ukraine’s attacks targeted a fire station, passenger transport, and residential quarters.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:51:37 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168145,2026-08-03 01:30:27
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,OPEC+ Monitoring Committee concerned over attacks on global energy infrastructure,OPEC+ Monitoring Committee concerned over attacks on global energy infrastructure,"OPEC+ Monitoring Committee concerned over attacks on global energy infrastructure The Committee also analyzed the current market situation and ""emphasized the essential role of the Declaration of Cooperation in supporting the stability of global energy markets MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. The OPEC+ Joint Ministerial Monitoring Committee (JMMC) has expressed concern over continuing attacks on glocal energy infrastructure facilities affecting overall supply ability, according to a statement posted on the OPEC website. The JMMC ""also expressed concern regarding attacks on energy infrastructure, noting that restoring damaged energy assets to full capacity is both costly and takes a long time, thereby affecting overall supply availability,"" the JMMC. ""Accordingly, the Committee stressed that any actions undermining energy supply security, whether through attacks on infrastructure or disruption of international maritime routes, increase market volatility and weaken the collective efforts under the DoC to support market stability for the benefit of producers, consumers, and the global economy."" The Committee also analyzed the current market situation and ""emphasized the essential role of the Declaration of Cooperation (DoC) in supporting the stability of global energy markets. ""In this context, the Committee highlighted the critical importance of safeguarding international maritime routes to ensure the uninterrupted flow of energy,"" it stressed.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:44:59 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2168143,2026-08-03 01:30:28
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukraine’s attacks on Zaporozhye NPP’s critical facilities create risks to nuclear safety,Ukraine’s attacks on Zaporozhye NPP’s critical facilities create risks to nuclear safety,"Ukraine’s attacks on Zaporozhye NPP’s critical facilities create risks to nuclear safety CEO of Russia’s Rosatom civil nuclear power corporation Alexey Likhachev said earlier that overnight a Ukrainian combat drone hit the gallery connecting all the six power units MELITOPOL, August 2. /TASS/. Ukraine’s attacks in the vicinity of the critical facilities of the Zaporozhy Nuclear Power Plant (ZNPP) create additional risks to nuclear safety, the ZNPP said. CEO of Russia’s Rosatom civil nuclear power corporation Alexey Likhachev said earlier that overnight a Ukrainian combat drone hit the gallery connecting all the six power units, which is intended for personnel movement. The strike was several meters away from the reactor building of power unit No. 3 ""Such actions create additional risks to nuclear safety and demonstrate that attacks target inside the facility’s perimeter, i.e. areas in the exact vicinity of facilities that are critical for its safe operation,"" according to a post on the ZNPP’s Telegram channel. Despite Kiev’s provocations, the facility’s personnel continue to ""control all safety parameters,"" it noted. ""The facility is in a safe state, with the radiation background remaining within natural limits."".","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:42:37 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168141,2026-08-03 01:30:29
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia’s Mariia Zhovner wins gold at European Rowing Championships,Russia’s Mariia Zhovner wins gold at European Rowing Championships,"Russia’s Mariia Zhovner wins gold at European Rowing Championships The Russian female athlete competing under a neutral status in the lightweight women’s single sculls cleared the distance in 7 minutes and 30.47 seconds ROME, August 2. /TASS/. Russia’s Mariia Zhovner has won a gold medal at the 2026 European Rowing Championships in the city of Varese in Italy. The Russian female athlete competing under a neutral status in the lightweight women’s single sculls cleared the distance in 7 minutes and 30.47 seconds, followed by Tosca Kettler from the Netherlands (7 minutes and 36.58 seconds) and Greece’s Gavriela Lioliou (7 minutes and 39.14 seconds). The 2026 European Rowing Championships will conclude on August 2. Russian athletes are competing in the tournament under a neutral status.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:16:38 +0300",https://tass.com/sports/2168139,2026-08-03 01:30:30
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Seven OPEC+ nations to increase daily oil production in September by 188,000 barrels","Seven OPEC+ nations to increase daily oil production in September by 188,000 barrels","Seven OPEC+ nations to increase daily oil production in September by 188,000 barrels As follows from the OPEC table, Russia’s quota will be increased by 62,000 barrels a day MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. The seven OPEC+ nations, namely Saudi Arabia, Russia, Iraq, Kuwait, Kazakhstan, Algeria, and Oman, have agreed to increase daily oil production in September by 188,000 (on August), OPEC said after their meeting. ""In their collective commitment to support oil market stability, the seven participating countries decided to implement a production adjustment of 188 thousand barrels per day from the additional voluntary adjustments announced in April 2023. This adjustment will be implemented in September 2026,"" it said. ""The seven OPEC+ countries also noted that this measure will provide an opportunity for the participating countries to accelerate their compensation."" Apart from that, they agreed to compensate for the overproduced volume until the end of 2026. ""They also confirmed their intention to fully compensate for any overproduced volume since January 2024,"" OPEC said. As follows from the OPEC table, Russia’s quota in September 2026 will be increased by 62,000 barrels a day to 9.949 mln barrels a day, Saudi Arabia’s - by 62,000 barrels a day to 10.478 mln barrels a day, Iraq’s - by 26,000 barrels a day to 4.431 mln barrels a day, Kuwait’s - by 16,000 barrels a day to 2.676 mln barrels a day, Kazakhstan’s - by 10,000 barrels a day to 1.628 mln barrels a day, Algeria’s - by 6,000 barrels a day to 1.007 mln barrels a day, and Oman’s - by 5,000 barrels a day to 841,000 barrels a day. The next OPEC+ meeting will be held on September 6.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:15:31 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168137,2026-08-03 01:30:31
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukrainian drone hits site several meters away from reactor unit at Zaporozhye nuke plant,Ukrainian drone hits site several meters away from reactor unit at Zaporozhye nuke plant,"Ukrainian drone hits site several meters away from reactor unit at Zaporozhye nuke plant Such actions by the Ukrainian side create direct risks for the nuclear facility, Head of Russia’s Rosatom civil nuclear power corporation Alexey Likhachev said MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. A Ukrainian combat drone hit a site several meters away from the reactor building of power unit No. 3 at the Zaporozhye Nuclear Power Plant, Head of Russia’s Rosatom civil nuclear power corporation Alexey Likhachev said. ""Last night, a combat drone hit the gallery connecting all the six power units, which is intended for personnel movement. Fortunately, no explosion followed. The strike was literally several meters away from the reactor building of power unit No. 3,"" the Rosatom press office quoted Likhachev as saying. Such actions by the Ukrainian side create direct risks for the nuclear facility and are yet another piece of evidence of Kiev’s purposeful attacks on nuclear infrastructure, he said. The Ukrainian military also attempted to attack a dry spent nuclear fuel storage facility at the Zaporozhye nuke plant, Likhachev said. ""On July 30, an attempt was made to attack the dry spent nuclear fuel storage site. The drone that did not explode was found in close proximity to the storage building for the transporter - a unique vehicle designed to move containers with spent fuel,"" the Rosatom head said.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:14:22 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168135,2026-08-03 01:30:31
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Moscow mayor conveys condolences to families of persons killed in restaurant blast,Moscow mayor conveys condolences to families of persons killed in restaurant blast,"Moscow mayor conveys condolences to families of persons killed in restaurant blast The perpetrators of this crime will necessarily be found and will face punishment they deserve, Sergey Sobyanin stressed MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. Moscow Mayor Sergey Sobyanin has expressed his condolences to the families of persons killed in a blast in a restaurant in the center of the Russian capital, saying that all those injured were receiving necessary medical assistance. ""Yesterday, a cruel terrorist act that claimed human lives was committed in Moscow. I express the deepest condolences to the families of those killed. I wish the quickest recovery to those injured,"" the Moscow mayor said on his Max social media platform. The persons injured in the blast are receiving all the necessary medical assistance at Moscow hospitals. Law-enforcement agencies are establishing the circumstances of the bomb attack, he said. ""The perpetrators of this crime will necessarily be found and will face punishment they deserve,"" the Moscow mayor stressed. On the evening of August 1, an improvised explosive device went off near a restaurant in Kudrinskaya Square in downtown Moscow. A woman tried to bring the bomb into the restaurant and was stopped by a security guard. Both of them and a restaurant visitor were killed in the blast while 21 others were injured.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:50:00 +0300",https://tass.com/society/2168127,2026-08-03 01:30:33
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Armenian president signs decree on appointing Pashinyan as republic’s PM,Armenian president signs decree on appointing Pashinyan as republic’s PM,"Armenian president signs decree on appointing Pashinyan as republic’s PM At the parliamentary elections held in Armenia on June 7, the ruling Civil Contract party led by Nikol Pashinyan gained 49.75% of the electors’ votes YEREVAN, August 2. /TASS/. Armenian President Vahagn Khachaturyan has appointed leader of the Civil Contract party Nikol Pashinyan as the country’s prime minister, following the results of the parliamentary elections in the South Caucasus republic. ""To appoint Nikol Pashinyan as the prime minister pursuant to Part 1, Article 149 of the Constitution,"" says the decree posted on the website of the republic’s head. At the parliamentary elections held in Armenia on June 7, the ruling Civil Contract party led by Pashinyan gained 49.75% of the electors’ votes, the ""Strong Armenia"" bloc led by businessman Samvel Karapetyan secured 23.27%, followed by former President Robert Kocharyan's ""Armenia"" bloc with 9.92%.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:24:36 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168125,2026-08-03 01:30:33
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Russian troops strike Ukrainian army’s transport, energy sites over past day — top brass","Russian troops strike Ukrainian army’s transport, energy sites over past day — top brass","Russian troops strike Ukrainian army’s transport, energy sites over past day — top brass The Ukrainian army lost roughly 1,415 troops in battles with Russian forces in all the frontline areas over the past 24 hours MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. Russian troops struck transport and energy infrastructure and logistics centers used by the Ukrainian army over the past 24 hours, Russia’s Defense Ministry reported. ""Operational/tactical aircraft, attack unmanned aerial vehicles, missile troops and artillery of the Russian groups of forces struck transport and energy infrastructure and logistics centers used by the Ukrainian army and temporary deployment areas of Ukrainian armed formations and foreign mercenaries in 156 locations,"" the ministry said in a statement. The Ukrainian army lost roughly 1,415 troops in battles with Russian forces in all the frontline areas over the past 24 hours, according to the latest data on the special military operation in Ukraine released by Russia’s Defense Ministry. The latest figures show that the Ukrainian army lost over 240 troops and an armored combat vehicle in the responsibility area of Russia’s Battlegroup North, more than 220 troops and an armored combat vehicle in the responsibility area of the Battlegroup West and roughly 210 troops and four armored combat vehicles in the responsibility area of the Battlegroup South. During the last 24-hour period, the Ukrainian army also lost roughly 360 troops and an armored combat vehicle in the responsibility area of Russia’s Battlegroup Center, over 355 troops and four armored combat vehicles in the responsibility area of the Battlegroup East and around 30 troops and 17 motor vehicles in the responsibility area of t","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:09:11 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168123,2026-08-03 01:30:34
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Iran denies reaching compromise deal with US on opening Strait of Hormuz,Iran denies reaching compromise deal with US on opening Strait of Hormuz,"Iran denies reaching compromise deal with US on opening Strait of Hormuz There is no agreement on resuming shipping through the Strait of Hormuz and the reports spread on this score are false, the news agency Fars said TEHRAN, August 2. /TASS/. Iran will not give its permission to opening the Strait of Hormuz while the reports claiming that Tehran has accepted a proposal by Qatari mediators to resume the waterway’s operation have nothing to do with reality, the news agencyFarsreported, citing a source in the Iranian negotiating team. There is no agreement on resuming shipping through the Strait of Hormuz and the reports spread on this score are false, the news agency said. The waterway will remain closed as long as ""the United States continues its hostile actions,"" the source stressed. The Israeli TV Channel 12 reported earlier on August 2 that US President Donald Trump agreed to cancel the planned powerful strike on Iran after Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi accepted a compromise proposal by Qatari mediators on resuming the operation of the Strait of Hormuz. Trump said on his Truth Social media platform on August 1 that he had agreed to cancel the planned strike on Iran for the sake of reaching a deal with Iran. The American leader said that Iran and other Mideast states had requested Washington to refrain from the attack as the parties involved were agreeing on the outlines of a future deal. He further said that the deal should include the provisions to immediately open the Strait of Hormuz and eliminate the Iran nuclear threat.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 13:34:58 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168119,2026-08-03 01:30:35
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Trump cancels strike on Iran after compromise proposal on Hormuz Strait operation — TV,Trump cancels strike on Iran after compromise proposal on Hormuz Strait operation — TV,"Trump cancels strike on Iran after compromise proposal on Hormuz Strait operation — TV According to TV Channel 12, the compromise proposal implies that vessels entering the Persian Gulf through the Strait of Hormuz will stay in Iran’s territorial waters while vessels exiting the waterway will pass through Oman’s territorial waters TEL AVIV, August 2. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump agreed to cancel a planned powerful strike on Iran after Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi accepted a compromise proposal by Qatari mediators on resuming the operation of the Hormuz Strait, the Israeli TV Channel 12 reported, citing two diplomats familiar with the talks. ""Araghchi’s positive response was one of the reasons why Trump agreed to cancel the attack on Iran,"" the TV channel reported, citing the diplomats. According to TV Channel 12, the compromise proposal implies that vessels entering the Persian Gulf through the Strait of Hormuz will stay in Iran’s territorial waters while vessels exiting the waterway will pass through Oman’s territorial waters. The Qatari mediators continue the talks with Iran to secure support for the agreement by the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (the elite military force of the Iranian army), the TV channel said. Trump said on his Truth Social media platform on August 1 that he had agreed to cancel the planned strike on Iran for the sake of reaching a deal with Iran. The American leader said that Iran and other Mideast states had requested Washington to refrain from the attack as the parties involved were agreeing on the outlines of a future deal. He further said that the deal should include the provisions to immediately open the Strait of Hormuz and eliminate the Iran nuclear threat.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 13:12:50 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2168115,2026-08-03 01:30:36
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Woman who brought explosive to Moscow eatery could have been unaware of parcel’s contents,Woman who brought explosive to Moscow eatery could have been unaware of parcel’s contents,"Woman who brought explosive to Moscow eatery could have been unaware of parcel’s contents All the threats cannot be neutralized, Alpha counter-terror group veteran Sergey Goncharov told MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. The woman who tried to bring an explosive to a restaurant in the center of Moscow could have been unaware of the parcel’s contents, Alpha counter-terror group veteran Sergey Goncharov told TASS. ""Each day, [Ukrainian intelligence] agents are arrested. Naturally, all the threats cannot be neutralized. And so, we have this tragedy. <…> The woman was a courier. She was promised good money. They told her, for example: ‘A friend of ours is celebrating a jubilee and your job is just to bring this parcel to the party and hand it over to the person celebrating his jubilee. This was her sole task. <…> We have had such instances,"" he said. On the evening of August 1, an improvised explosive device exploded near a restaurant in Kudrinskaya Square in downtown Moscow. A woman tried to bring the bomb into the restaurant and was stopped by a security guard. Both of them and a restaurant visitor were killed in the blast while 21 others were injured.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 11:44:08 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2168101,2026-08-03 01:30:37
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Putin congratulates Russian paratroopers on Airborne Force Day,Putin congratulates Russian paratroopers on Airborne Force Day,"Putin congratulates Russian paratroopers on Airborne Force Day Russian President said he was confident that the Airborne Force personnel would accomplish the assigned objectives with honor and make considerable contribution to ensuring Russia’s defense capability MOSCOW, August 2. /TASS/. Russian President Vladimir Putin congratulated paratroopers on Airborne Force Day, highlighting their heroism and courage in the most responsible areas of the special military operation. ""You are rightly proud of the names of the Airborne Force founders, immortal feats and outstanding achievements of your predecessors and you look at veterans as role models. Let me specially note skillful and decisive operations by the paratroopers who are today defending Russia shoulder to shoulder with their comrades-in-arms in the special military operation, displaying heroism and courage in the most responsible frontline areas,"" the head of state said in a congratulatory message posted on the Kremlin’s website. As the head of state pointed out, ""people of a hardy mold and a strong spirit with unyielding character, bound by fraternal solidarity and mutual support"" have always served in the Airborne Force ranks. The Russian leader said he was confident that the Airborne Force personnel would accomplish the assigned objectives with honor and make considerable contribution to ensuring Russia’s defense capability, sovereignty and security. ""I wish you and your nears and dears success and all the best,"" Putin said.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 10:54:50 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2168099,2026-08-03 01:30:38
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia’s Battlegroup North downs over 120 Ukrainian UAVs heading to border areas at night,Russia’s Battlegroup North downs over 120 Ukrainian UAVs heading to border areas at night,"Russia’s Battlegroup North downs over 120 Ukrainian UAVs heading to border areas at night Air defense crews of the Battlegroup North destroyed all the detected UAVs of the Ukrainian army KURSK, August 2. /TASS/. Air defense teams of Russia’s Battlegroup North destroyed over 120 Ukrainian unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) in the Kharkov and Sumy Regions heading to Russian border areas overnight, a spokesman for the Battlegroup North told TASS. ""While on combat alert, radar teams of the Battlegroup North detected the flight of over 120 UAVs of the Ukrainian army in the Kharkov and Sumy Regions heading to Russian border areas during the past night. The target coordinates were immediately transmitted to air defense crews deployed in the areas of UAV flights,"" he said. Air defense crews of the Battlegroup North destroyed all the detected UAVs of the Ukrainian army, the spokesman said.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 07:30:00 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168077,2026-08-03 01:30:39
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Air defense forces repelled nearly 150 UAVs in Rostov region,Air defense forces repelled nearly 150 UAVs in Rostov region,"Air defense forces repelled nearly 150 UAVs in Rostov region In the Millerovsky District, falling UAV debris caused a cable fire on the roof of a grain elevator ROSTOV-ON-DON, August 2. /TASS/. Overnight, Russia’s air defense forces repelled nearly 150 UAVs in the city of Kamensk-Shakhtinsky and seven districts of the Rostov region, Governor Yury Slyusar reported on the Max channel. ""Last night, air defense forces repelled a massive attack on the Rostov Region. Nearly 150 UAVs were destroyed in the city of Kamensk-Shakhtinsky and seven other districts of the region: Chertkovsky, Tarasovsky, Millerovsky, Morozovsky, Kamensky, Sholokhovsky, and Azovsky,"" he wrote. In the Millerovsky District, falling UAV debris caused a cable fire on the roof of a grain elevator. There were no injuries, and the fire has been extinguished. The governor reported that the drone threat remains in the region.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 07:25:01 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2168075,2026-08-03 01:30:39
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Poll on China's summer economy,Poll on China's summer economy,"Poll on China's summer economy Poll on China's summer economy Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Foreign tourists in Beijing, July 30, 2026. /VCG As heat waves sweep across the Northern Hemisphere, China's summer economy is demonstrating remarkable vitality and injecting strong momentum into global growth. Please take thesurveyand share your views.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 05:07:18 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Poll-on-China-s-summer-economy-1PfsHe3VZIY/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:40
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Innovation seen as key growth engine in first half of 2026,Innovation seen as key growth engine in first half of 2026,"Innovation seen as key growth engine in first half of 2026 Innovation seen as key growth engine in first half of 2026 Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied At a meeting on Thursday, the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee reviewed the country's economic performance during the first half of 2026 and outlined key priorities for the months ahead. CGTN reporter Dai Kaiyi speaks with Tian Xuan, Dean of the Guanghua School of Management at Peking University, to examine the meeting's major policy signals and what they could mean for the trajectory of China's economy in the second half of the year.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 10:55:45 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Innovation-seen-as-key-growth-engine-in-first-half-of-2026-1PfMsUbNkjK/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:41
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Brazil accuses US of extending trade powers on 'baseless' claims,Brazil accuses US of extending trade powers on 'baseless' claims,"Brazil accuses US of extending trade powers on 'baseless' claims Brazil on Wednesday denounced the United States for using ""baseless and false"" claims to extend its emergency trade powers against the South American country for another year, a move that justifies the continued imposition of punitive tariffs on Brazilian exports. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Cargo vessels are seen near port facilities in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, July 16, 2026. /VCG Brazil on Wednesday denounced the United States for using what it called ""baseless and false"" claims to extend its emergency trade powers against the South American country for another year, a move aimed at justifying the continued imposition of punitive tariffs on Brazilian exports. In a statement, the Brazilian government condemned the US decision, criticizing the repeated use of ""baseless and false arguments"" alleging that Brazil poses an ""unusual and extraordinary threat to US national security, foreign policy and the economy."" Designating Brazil as a threat requiring emergency economic measures has allowed Washington to impose tariffs of up to 35% on a range of Brazilian industrial goods as part of the tariff policy launched by US President Donald Trump in 2025. According to Washington, the emergency measures are necessary due to alleged human rights violations, the suppression of free speech for US individuals and companies, and the political persecution of former President Jair Bolsonaro. Bolsonaro was recently found guilty of attempting a coup after losing his reelection bid. Categorically rejecting these accusations, Brazil said the allegations had already been thoro","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 06:16:06 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/Brazil-accuses-US-of-extending-trade-powers-on-baseless-claims-1PccVH60vmM/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:41
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China takes women's team sabre silver at Fencing World Championships,China takes women's team sabre silver at Fencing World Championships,"China takes women's team sabre silver at Fencing World Championships China takes women's team sabre silver at Fencing World Championships Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Sports Scene Copied L-R: China's Zhang Xinyi, Wei Jiayi, Rao Xueyi and Pan Qimiao display their silver medals after finishing the women's team sabre final against Hungary at the Fencing World Championships in China's Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, July 29, 2026. /Xinhua China earned the silver medal in the women's team sabre event at the FIE Fencing World Championships after a narrow 45-41 defeat to Hungary in the final in China's Hong Kong Special Administrative Region on Wednesday. The result matched China's best-ever finish in the event at the world championships, equaling the silver medal won in 2003. China fielded a young lineup of Pan Qimiao, Rao Xueyi, Zhang Xinyi and Wei Jiayi. The team made a fast start in the final, with 17-year-old Pan giving China an early 5-2 advantage before Rao extended the lead to 10-3. Hungary responded strongly in the third bout and overturned the deficit, leaving China chasing for the remainder of the match. Rao led a late fightback in the ninth and final bout, cutting Hungary's lead to 44-41, but the European side remained focused to seal the title. Pan said China had produced a strong display but still needed to improve its execution in attacking exchanges. Rao also pointed to missed opportunities, saying several unsuccessful att","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 05:09:06 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/China-takes-women-s-team-sabre-silver-at-Fencing-World-Championships-1Pc5MAcG3rW/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:41
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,The other final whistle: World Cup and global health's unfinished game,The other final whistle: World Cup and global health's unfinished game,"The other final whistle: World Cup and global health's unfinished game Drawing on the stark contrast between the conclusion of the 2026 FIFA World Cup and the accelerating Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, this article analyzes the structural limits of leveraging mega-sporting events for global health governance. It shows that while partnerships like the FIFA-WHO alliance advance health advocacy, their impact remains constrained by non-binding terms and event-bound scopes, calling for stronger multilateral mechanisms. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Wu Yanni, Zhou Qing'an Copied Editor's Note:In this article, Wu Yanni and Zhou Qing'an, researchers from the Global Development and Health Communication Center at China's Tsinghua University, examine the structural divide between global sports spectacles and acute public health crises. Drawing on the stark contrast between the conclusion of the 2026 FIFA World Cup and the accelerating Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, they argue that while institutional partnerships like the FIFA-WHO alliance have made meaningful strides in health advocacy and host-nation protocols, they remain inherently limited by non-binding commitments, host-government resource dependencies, and an inward-facing scope. They call for a more serious examination and evolution of international governance frameworks to credibly turn mass media platforms into sustainable mechanisms for addressing broader, global-scale health emergencies. When Spain claimed their second World Cup title at MetLife Stadium in New Jersey on July 19, over 80,000 fans in the stadium and billions worldwide captured the moment. Across 39 days, 48 teams, and 104 matches spread across the United States, Canada, and Mexico, the 2026 FIFA World Cup drew what is likely the l","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:10:08 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/The-other-final-whistle-World-Cup-and-global-health-s-unfinished-game-1PcPCLticTu/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Death toll from Japan's Kumamoto Earthquake rises to 35,Death toll from Japan's Kumamoto Earthquake rises to 35,"Death toll from Japan's Kumamoto Earthquake rises to 35 Death toll from Japan's Kumamoto Earthquake rises to 35 Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A collapsed house in the city of Kumamoto, Japan, July 29, 2026. /VCG The death toll from a powerful earthquake that struck Japan's Kumamoto Prefecture has risen to 35, the prefectural government said Friday. At a disaster response headquarters meeting held Friday morning, Kumamoto Prefecture Government officials announced that 35 people had died, including those whose deaths are still being investigated to determine whether they were caused by the quake.","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:37:29 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/news-1PdDyzS7FDy/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"August inferno warning as Western Europe heats up faster, expert says","August inferno warning as Western Europe heats up faster, expert says","August inferno warning as Western Europe heats up faster, expert says August inferno warning as Western Europe heats up faster, expert says Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Spanish climate expert Ruben del Campo warned on Friday that the wildfire threat is likely to persist throughout August, with temperatures expected to remain high and weather conditions continuing to favor large fires. ""Some studies show that Western Europe – including the United Kingdom, France, Italy, Spain and Portugal – is warming faster than many other parts of the world, and that we are also more prone to heatwaves,"" del Campo, a spokesperson for Spain's State Meteorological Agency (AEMET), said. A firefighting helicopter flies over a wildfire in the Iruelas Valley Nature Reserve in the Avila region, Spain, July 30, 2026. /VCG ""There is a clear link with climate change. A rise in average temperature always leads to an increase in episodes of extreme heat, and this is exactly what we are seeing,"" he said. Countries around the Mediterranean ""are among the most vulnerable to heatwaves under the new climatic conditions,"" he added. Temperatures in parts of Spain had already reached 35 degrees Celsius by the end of May. The heat has fueled wildfires that have incinerated almost 180,000 hectares in Spain, about six times the 29,817 recorded over the same period in 2025, and around 200,000 people have been forced to flee their homes amid the inferno in Spain and sout","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 11:07:45 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/August-inferno-warning-as-Western-Europe-heats-up-faster-expert-says-1PfSbnlXfzO/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,DR Congo says Rwanda-linked armed group agrees to disarm,DR Congo says Rwanda-linked armed group agrees to disarm,"DR Congo says Rwanda-linked armed group agrees to disarm Kinshasa described the development as a significant step toward restoring peace in the conflict‑hit east and implementing the US‑brokered Washington peace agreement signed by the DRC and Rwanda in June 2025. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied An M23 officer inspects a convoy of soldiers repatriated from the Democratic Forces for the Liberation of Rwanda (FDLR) at a major border crossing between the Democratic Republic of the Congo and Rwanda, in Goma, the Democratic Republic of the Congo on March 1, 2025. /CFP The Democratic Republic of the Congo says the Democratic Forces for the Liberation of Rwanda (FDLR), an armed group operating in eastern Congo, has signed a protocol committing to disarmament and the unconditional repatriation of its fighters to Rwanda. The protocol, signed following talks facilitated by Qatar, commits the FDLR to voluntarily lay down its arms, cease hostilities and return to Rwanda. Kinshasa described the development as a significant step toward restoring peace in the conflict‑hit east and implementing the US‑brokered Washington peace agreement signed by the DRC and Rwanda in June 2025, which aimed at easing cross‑border tensions and improving security in the Great Lakes region. Rwanda, however, rejected the announcement, saying the protocol falls outside the framework of the Washington accord, which established a jointly supervised mechanism for the neutralisation of the FDLR. (With input from the Wires)","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:37:56 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/DR-Congo-says-Rwanda-linked-armed-group-agrees-to-disarm-1PcWumDMVqw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:42
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Israeli strikes kill four in Gaza as new ceasefire push sees progress,Israeli strikes kill four in Gaza as new ceasefire push sees progress,"Israeli strikes kill four in Gaza as new ceasefire push sees progress Israeli strikes kill four in Gaza as new ceasefire push sees progress Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Palestinians inspect the rubble of a building and tents destroyed in an Israeli airstrike in Gaza City, July 30, 2026. /VCG Israeli strikes killed at least four people, including two children, in the Gaza Strip on Thursday, health officials said, as mediators held new talks with ​Hamas leaders in Cairo to work towards full implementation of a US-brokered Gaza peace plan. A Hamas official and a diplomat close to the Cairo talks with mediators said discussions were ""positive"" and ""making ‌progress."" The official added that the progress made would be tested by whether Israel would accept it to allow a broad agreement to be reached. The diplomat said the negotiations were ongoing and making progress toward a roadmap that would see all heavy and light weapons in Gaza decommissioned. Meanwhile, medics said an Israeli airstrike on a tent encampment in Khan Younis, in the south of the enclave, killed a man and an eight-year-old girl. In the Bureij refugee camp in the central Gaza ​Strip, an Israeli airstrike hit a house, killing an 18-month-old child and wounding at least eight people, medics said. Another Israeli strike targeted a Palestinian man on a bike near a ​tent encampment housing displaced families in Gaza City, killing one person and wounding 10 others. The Israe","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:38:01 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/Israeli-strikes-kill-four-in-Gaza-as-new-ceasefire-push-sees-progress-1PcNYlrLkU8/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:43
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China slams US move to add Chinese firms to 'forced labor' entity list,China slams US move to add Chinese firms to 'forced labor' entity list,"China slams US move to add Chinese firms to 'forced labor' entity list China slams US move to add Chinese firms to 'forced labor' entity list Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China on Saturday slammed the United States' decision to add more than 40 Chinese entities to a list under the ""Uyghur Forced Labor Prevention Act,"" calling the move an act of economic coercion and urging Washington to stop unwarranted suppression of Chinese companies. The US move, announced by the Department of Homeland Security on Friday, lacked a factual basis and abused domestic laws to impose unilateral sanctions on Chinese firms under the pretext of ""human rights"" and ""forced labor,"" a Chinese Commerce Ministry spokesperson told reporters. It was a typical act of economic coercion, undermining the legitimate rights and interests of Chinese companies and disrupting the stability of global industrial and supply chains, the spokesperson said. Noting that trade officials from China and the US held a video call on Thursday and had a candid, in-depth and constructive exchange on maintaining stable economic and trade ties, the spokesperson said Washington's action one day later seriously ran counter to the consensus reached by the two countries' leaders. China strongly condemns and firmly opposes the US move. China has consistently opposed forced labor, the spokesperson said, adding that there is no so-called ""forced labor"" in the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region. A","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 08:30:45 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/China-slams-US-move-to-add-Chinese-firms-to-forced-labor-entity-list-1PfrlfZQvE4/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:43
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Escalating conflict in the Middle East,Escalating conflict in the Middle East,"Escalating conflict in the Middle East Escalating conflict in the Middle East Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Wang Jin Copied A general view of scorched vehicles at the site of a strike in Bartalla after US-Saudi strikes on Iraq, in Nineveh Province, Iraq, July 29, 2026. /VCG Editor's note: Wang Jin is a Middle East expert from China's Northwest University. The article reflects the author's opinion and not necessarily the views of CGTN. The conflict between the United States and Iran remains ongoing, while countries such as Yemen and Iraq have become increasingly drawn into the hostilities. As a result, the security situation across the Middle East continues to deteriorate. Over the past two weeks, the geographical scope of the conflict has expanded significantly. Since the renewed outbreak of hostilities between the United States and Iran in July, tensions have escalated rapidly, with fighting resuming in Yemen and Iraqi Shiite militia groups becoming increasingly involved. The United States and Saudi Arabia have subsequently carried out strikes against militia targets inside Iraq. Coupled with the recent drone attack on Egypt, these developments suggest that the conflict is spreading across the region, with regional actors increasingly realigning their strategic positions. A person watches Houthi military spokesperson Yahya Sarea delivering a televised statement in Sana'a, Yemen, Ju","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 13:10:05 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Escalating-conflict-in-the-Middle-East-1PfVEkKe2Y0/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:43
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,CGTN poll: 93% expect more innovation from Chinese manufacturing,CGTN poll: 93% expect more innovation from Chinese manufacturing,"CGTN poll: 93% expect more innovation from Chinese manufacturing CGTN poll: 93% expect more innovation from Chinese manufacturing Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China's new ""new three"" industries: artificial intelligence, humanoid robots and biopharmaceuticals. /VCG Chinese manufacturing has earned a new label on the global stage: China's new ""new three."" Having evolved from contract manufacturing of clothing, furniture and home appliances to leading the green energy revolution with new energy vehicles, lithium batteries and solar products, China is now making fresh strides in artificial intelligence, robotics and innovative pharmaceuticals, showcasing the remarkable momentum of its high-quality manufacturing transformation. A global online survey conducted by CGTN shows that 93.1% of respondents believe the rise of the new ""new three"" demonstrates that Chinese manufacturing is offering original technologies, intelligent systems and solutions to the international market. They expect more innovation-driven benefits to be unlocked in the future. According to data from the General Administration of Customs of China, China's exports of industrial robots rose 18.6% year on year in the first half of 2026. More than 10,000 intelligent bionic robots were exported to over 90 countries and regions worldwide. In addition, statistics from the National Medical Products Administration (NMPA) show that the total value of out-licensing de","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 06:51:14 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/CGTN-poll-93-expect-more-innovation-from-Chinese-manufacturing-1PfHaYlvG7e/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,How the UN chooses its next Secretary-General,How the UN chooses its next Secretary-General,"How the UN chooses its next Secretary-General How the UN chooses its next Secretary-General Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Elaine Reyes Copied How does the 15-member United Nations Security Council decide who will be recommended for the UN's top job? The selection process begins with a series of secret ""straw poll"" votes, starting on July 24. CGTN's Elaine Reyes explains how the process works. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:44:21 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/How-the-UN-chooses-its-next-Secretary-General-1PdmGMviR6o/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Jordan's army says it shot down 5 Iranian missiles,Jordan's army says it shot down 5 Iranian missiles,"Jordan's army says it shot down 5 Iranian missiles Jordan's army says it shot down 5 Iranian missiles Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Jordan's military in a statement on Thursday said its air defenses shot down five missiles coming from Iran that targeted the kingdom's territory, adding that the attack caused no casualties. The military's official spokesperson said ""air defenses engaged five missiles launched from Iran targeting the Kingdom's territory early this morning, Thursday. The missiles were detected, intercepted and shot down according to established defense plans,"" the statement said.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 04:41:18 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/news-1Pcg4LnEG4g/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Japan starts 22nd round of nuclear-contaminated water discharge,Japan starts 22nd round of nuclear-contaminated water discharge,"Japan starts 22nd round of nuclear-contaminated water discharge Tokyo Electric Power Company (TEPCO) on Thursday began the 22nd round discharge of nuclear-contaminated water of the Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant into the sea. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied An aerial photo shows Tokyo Electric Power Company's Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant in Fukushima Prefecture on May 2, 2026. /VCG Tokyo Electric Power Company (TEPCO) on Thursday began the 22nd round of discharging of nuclear-contaminated water from the Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant into the sea. According to TEPCO's plan, the latest discharge will continue through August 17. About 7,800 tonnes of nuclear-contaminated water are expected to be released, containing a total of about 1.3 trillion becquerels of tritium. Japan began discharging nuclear-contaminated water from the Fukushima plant into the ocean in August 2023 despite strong concerns and opposition from the international community. To date, TEPCO has completed 21 rounds of discharge, releasing a total of about 165,000 tonnes of nuclear-contaminated water.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 08:47:07 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/Japan-starts-22nd-round-of-nuclear-contaminated-water-discharge-1PcpxDuC9Gw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:44
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Fast-moving wildfire in Washington triggers highest evacuation order,Fast-moving wildfire in Washington triggers highest evacuation order,"Fast-moving wildfire in Washington triggers highest evacuation order A swiftly moving wildfire broke out in Spokane County, in the US state of Washington, on Saturday, forcing residents to leave their homes and evacuate to safety as crews hurried to contain the fire, according to CNN reports. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Flames and smoke rise from the Old Trails Fire in Spokane County, Washington, US, August 1, 2026. /VCG A swiftly moving wildfire broke out in Spokane County, in the US state of Washington, on Saturday, forcing residents to leave their homes and evacuate to safety as crews hurried to contain the fire, according to CNN reports. The Old Trails Fire in Spokane County, worsened by extreme fire weather conditions, has triggered a Level 3 evacuation order, the highest level for such situations, asking residents to leave immediately due to the current, life-threatening, and severe danger. Bob Ferguson, the governor of Washington, declared a statewide burn ban due to the critical situation. ""Our record-setting drought and high winds are creating dangerous conditions across the state,"" Ferguson said. ""I am declaring an emergency to help prevent loss of life and property damage. I encourage all Washingtonians to do their part to protect our state during these extreme conditions."" The US National Weather Service issued a Red Flag Warning for Saturday afternoon and evening, alerting residents to ""extreme fire conditions across portions of central and eastern Washington"" and ""very rapid fire growth potential."" No injuries caused by the fire have been reported to date.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 02:02:01 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/Fast-moving-wildfire-in-Washington-triggers-highest-evacuation-order-1Ph0LZkgyEE/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Uncertainty as Temporary Protected Status for Haitians in the US ends,Uncertainty as Temporary Protected Status for Haitians in the US ends,"Uncertainty as Temporary Protected Status for Haitians in the US ends Temporary Protected Status for Haitians in the United States ended this past Monday, July 27th, after the Supreme Court cleared the way for the Trump administration to terminate the program. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Nitza Soledad Perez Copied Temporary Protected Status for Haitians in the United States ended this past Monday, July 27th, after the Supreme Court cleared the way for the Trump administration to terminate the program. Nitza Soledad Perez sat down with a Haitian woman in South Florida who lost her protected status and says she will fight to stay in the U.S., no matter the consequences. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 20:45:31 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/Uncertainty-as-Temporary-Protected-Status-for-Haitians-in-the-US-ends-1PgFHYJaao8/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"At least 9 killed in Russian strike on Kyiv, officials say","At least 9 killed in Russian strike on Kyiv, officials say","At least 9 killed in Russian strike on Kyiv, officials say At least 9 killed in Russian strike on Kyiv, officials say Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A burned-out car stands at the site of a Russian missile attack in Kyiv, Ukraine, August 1, 2026. /VCG Russian strikes on Ukraine's capital killed at least nine people and wounded 28 others, including four children, local authorities said on Saturday after Kyiv's mayor warned of a ballistic missile attack. Kyiv Mayor Vitali Klitschko said nine people were killed in the attack and 28 others were injured, including four children. Russia's Defense Ministry said in a statement that its forces had carried out a ""massive strike"" on military-industrial facilities and logistics centers in Kyiv and the surrounding Kyiv region.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 03:18:04 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/news-1PftW40DZQI/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:45
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Trump says US, Israel agree to hold off Iran strikes if deal reached","Trump says US, Israel agree to hold off Iran strikes if deal reached","Trump says US, Israel agree to hold off Iran strikes if deal reached Trump says US, Israel agree to hold off Iran strikes if deal reached Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied US President Donald Trump said on Saturday that the United States and Israel had agreed to hold off on planned strikes on Iran at the request of Tehran and other countries in the region, provided a deal is quickly reached. ""The USA is locked and loaded and ready to go against the Islamic Republic of Iran, at levels of Military Terror, Strength, and Power not seen since World War II,"" Trump said in a post on his Truth Social platform. ""Despite this, we have just been asked by Iran, and other Middle Eastern Countries, to hold off any attack,"" he said. ""Based on this request, I have agreed... to cancel the attack, subject to being able to rapidly make a DEAL. The Country of Israel joins me in this commitment.""","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 02:06:49 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/news-1Ph3Ktn1AYw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Gaza deal reached over Hamas disarmament, Israel withdrawal","Gaza deal reached over Hamas disarmament, Israel withdrawal","Gaza deal reached over Hamas disarmament, Israel withdrawal Hamas has reached an agreement with Israel over the group's disarmament and gradual withdrawal of Israeli military from the Gaza region, according to Hamas officials on Wednesday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Palestinians inspect the debris following an Israeli air strike the day before in Gaza City, Gaza, July 30, 2026. /VCG Hamas has reached an agreement with Israel over the group's disarmament and gradual withdrawal of Israeli military from the Gaza region, according to Hamas officials on Wednesday. They also said that Palestinian technocratic committee will supervise the storing of group's arms and will soon issue a formal statement about the agreement. Before the announcement by Hamas, US President Donald Trump also claimed on his social media account that an agreement was reached on complete disarmament of Hamas and other armed groups in Gaza. ""This agreement is a critical step towards Gaza finally being governed by a new Palestinian government that will work closely with the Board of Peace to help the Palestinian people,"" Trump wrote on Truth Social. ""At the same time, Israel will have the security it deserves, with Gaza no longer used as a base for terror attacks,"" he added. The agreement will be carried out in structured phases, according to Trump, who noted that as disarmament is completed, Israeli forces will withdraw, and the International Stabilization Force will work with a new Palestinian police force to take responsibility for Gaza's security. He said Eg","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 23:50:16 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/news-1PdAbjW8Bgc/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Measles resurgence raising alarm internationally,Measles resurgence raising alarm internationally,"Measles resurgence raising alarm internationally The United States has just recorded its worst measles outbreak in more than three decades, and it’s part of a resurgence playing out on multiple continents. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Nitza Soledad Perez Copied The United States has just recorded its worst measles outbreak in more than three decades, and it’s part of a resurgence playing out on multiple continents. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 19:22:07 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/Measles-resurgence-raising-alarm-internationally-1PgAzc8NYsg/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,African Union condemns drone strike on Egypt's Damietta Port,African Union condemns drone strike on Egypt's Damietta Port,"African Union condemns drone strike on Egypt's Damietta Port In a statement, African Union Commission Chairperson Mahmoud Ali Youssouf expressed solidarity with Egypt and reaffirmed the bloc's support for efforts to safeguard the country's sovereignty and critical infrastructure. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Ships docked on the wharf of the Mediterranean seaport of Damietta in Damietta, Egypt, on July 30, 2026. /CFP The African Union on Friday condemned a drone attack on vessels at Egypt's Port of Damietta, calling it a violation of the sovereignty and territorial integrity of one of its member states and urging restraint to prevent further escalation. In a statement, African Union Commission Chairperson Mahmoud Ali Youssouf expressed solidarity with Egypt and praised authorities for their response, saying it had prevented any loss of life. ""Africa must not become a theatre for the spillover of conflicts originating beyond the continent, nor should its critical civilian infrastructure be exposed to such threats,"" the statement said. The statement came days after Egypt confirmed that a drone caused a fire aboard two gas vessels at Damietta port earlier this week. The blaze, which damaged the US-owned floating storage and regasification unit Energos Winter before spreading to another vessel, was extinguished without any reported injuries or fatalities. No group has claimed responsibility for the attack, and Egyptian authorities are continuing their investigation. Damietta is one of Egypt's most important Mediterranean ports and a key hub for liquefied natural gas exports","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 13:15:26 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/African-Union-condemns-drone-strike-on-Egypt-s-Damietta-Port-1Pg4BQdAbCM/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Kuwait: Iranian attack hits Chinese firm, killing a Nepalese driver","Kuwait: Iranian attack hits Chinese firm, killing a Nepalese driver","Kuwait: Iranian attack hits Chinese firm, killing a Nepalese driver Kuwait: Iranian attack hits Chinese firm, killing a Nepalese driver Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied An attack that Kuwait said was launched by Iran on Thursday killed a Nepalese driver working for a Chinese company in northern Kuwait and damaged the company's property, according to Kuwait's Ministry of Defense. The Chinese Embassy in Kuwait confirmed that no Chinese nationals were killed or injured in the incident.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 11:15:09 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/Kuwait-Iranian-attack-hits-Chinese-firm-killing-a-Nepalese-driver-1PcEsTCSNMc/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:46
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"China, EU to hold 2nd trade consultation mechanism meeting this autumn","China, EU to hold 2nd trade consultation mechanism meeting this autumn","China, EU to hold 2nd trade consultation mechanism meeting this autumn China and the European Union (EU) have agreed to hold the second meeting of the China-EU trade and investment consultation mechanism this autumn, a commerce official said on Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China and the European Union (EU) have agreed to hold the second meeting of the China-EU trade and investment consultation mechanism this autumn, a commerce official said on Thursday. Over the past month, both sides have been actively implementing the outcomes of the first meeting and making full preparations for the second, He Yadong, spokesperson for China's Ministry of Commerce, said at a regular press briefing in response to intensive consultations between the two sides recently. The working teams from both sides have held more than 20 consultations, while the four workstreams under the China-EU Trade and Investment Consultation Mechanism have conducted in-depth, professional exchanges on each other's economic and trade concerns, He said. China is willing to continue maintaining high-frequency communication with the EU, respect each other and work in the same direction to explore practical and feasible solutions to trade and economic issues of mutual concern, promote balanced and positive development of bilateral trade, and maintain the stability and balance of the China-EU key trading partnership, He said.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 09:51:21 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/China-EU-to-hold-2nd-trade-consultation-mechanism-meeting-this-autumn-1PczFgQzQyc/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:47
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Drone strike in Egypt's port raises new threat in widening war,Drone strike in Egypt's port raises new threat in widening war,"Drone strike in Egypt's port raises new threat in widening war Drone strike in Egypt's port raises new threat in widening war Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A drone strike on gas vessels in Egypt's Mediterranean port of Damietta signaled a potential new front in the US-Iran war, raising ‌the prospect of threats to navigation through the Suez Canal, a last remaining safe export route for Saudi oil. The Egyptian cabinet said on Thursday that an initial investigation showed that an unidentified drone caused a fire on Wednesday on two vessels at Damietta port, near the Suez Canal, which links the Mediterranean with the Red Sea. No group has claimed responsibility, the cabinet said, adding that authorities were taking measures to protect Egypt's national security. Trading sources familiar with the incident said ​the drone hit US-owned gas storage tanker Energos Winter, causing a fire that spread to another vessel. Overnight, the US military said it struck Iran's Revolutionary Guards' military command centers and ​drone facilities after Tehran fired at US forces in the region. Iranian state media, quoting the Guards, said three civilians were killed and two children wounded ⁠in US strikes on Qeshm Island, while three Guards members were killed in Zanjan province. The governor of Khuzestan province, cited by Iranian state media, said two student dormitory complexes in the southwestern city ​of Ahvaz were damaged in the overni","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:19:41 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/Drone-strike-in-Egypt-s-port-raises-new-threat-in-widening-war--1PcNEoAFeGA/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:47
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Ebola cases top 3,500 in DR Congo","Ebola cases top 3,500 in DR Congo","Ebola cases top 3,500 in DR Congo The number of confirmed Ebola cases in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) has risen to 3,532, with 1,556 confirmed deaths, according to the latest figures released on Friday by the country's public health authorities. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The number of confirmed Ebola cases in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) has risen to 3,532, with 1,556 confirmed deaths, according to the latest figures released on Friday by the country's public health authorities. The outbreak has now spread across five eastern provinces: Ituri, North Kivu, South Kivu, Haut-Uele and Tshopo. Currently, 807 patients remain in isolation or under hospital care, while 626 people have recovered. The Africa Centres for Disease Control and Prevention (Africa CDC) has warned of mounting operational constraints hampering the Ebola response in the DRC while praising Uganda for successfully containing the outbreak. During an online press briefing on Thursday evening, Africa CDC Director-General Jean Kaseya said the continued outbreak ""is the fastest-growing Ebola outbreak ever recorded"" and is now the second-largest by total confirmed cases. A health worker prepares to work at the Evangelical Medical Center in Bunia, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, July 3, 2026. /VCG Kaseya expressed concern over critical constraints hindering response efforts in the DRC, citing limited contact tracing capabilities, rising community cases and deaths, an increasing case fatality rate, and inadequate bed capacity. He also cited persistent fundi","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 06:12:16 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Ebola-cases-top-3-500-in-DR-Congo--1PfBLjmTFgQ/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:47
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,SpaceX Starship floats belly up 6 days after historic soft splashdown,SpaceX Starship floats belly up 6 days after historic soft splashdown,"SpaceX Starship floats belly up 6 days after historic soft splashdown SpaceX Starship floats belly up 6 days after historic soft splashdown Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A side view of the Starship upper stage floating on the water after splashdown, Indian Ocean off Western Australia. /VCG Six days after SpaceX's Starship upper stage made its softest-ever ocean splashdown during Flight 13, the 171-foot (about 52 meters) vehicle is floating belly-up in the Indian Ocean off Western Australia, still transmitting telemetry. ""This is the first time we've put an intact Starship in the water,"" SpaceX's Dan Huot said during the July 24 launch livestream, as drone footage showed the blackened rocket booster bobbing on the waves. On previous flights, the upper stage typically broke apart or exploded on impact. This time, it survived reentry, with cameras capturing stunning views of the vehicle wrapped in superheated plasma as it descended toward the ocean. It executed a controlled engine burn to flip into a vertical position and gently tipped over to rest on the open sea. During the suborbital flight, Starship released 20 Starlink V3 internet satellites in the first-ever deployment from the rocket. SpaceX CEO Elon Musk confirmed the vehicle was ""intact, floating in the ocean and transmitting telemetry."" The Super Heavy booster, however, had a harder landing in the Gulf of Mexico, with only five of its 13 landing engines still lit at splashdo","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:58:03 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/SpaceX-Starship-floats-belly-up-6-days-after-historic-soft-splashdown-1PcLFkRaOZO/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:47
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,USCBC president: US companies recognize China's economic strengths,USCBC president: US companies recognize China's economic strengths,"USCBC president: US companies recognize China's economic strengths US companies recognize the strengths of China's economy and innovation system and are seeking to partner with Chinese companies to boost their competitiveness, Sean Stein, president of the US-China Business Council (USCBC), said on Friday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Sean Stein, president of the US-China Business Council, fifth from left, speaks during a meeting with a delegation of Chinese entrepreneurs in Washington, DC, August 1, 2026. /VCG US companies recognize the strengths of China's economy and innovation system and are seeking to partner with Chinese companies to boost their competitiveness, Sean Stein, president of the US-China Business Council (USCBC), said on Friday. Stein made the remarks ahead of a discussion and exchange event between a delegation of Chinese entrepreneurs led by the China Council for the Promotion of International Trade (CCPIT) and the USCBC and its member companies in Washington, D.C. He said many American companies are eager to engage with Chinese partners through the event and are committed to deepening cooperation with Chinese companies. On potential areas of cooperation, Stein said that beyond frequently mentioned industries such as agriculture and aviation, US businesses are eager to advance partnerships with Chinese companies in fields including financial services, life sciences, research and manufacturing. He said that in recent conversations with American CEOs, ""what they're talking about is they recognize some of the strengths of the Chinese economy and the Chinese innovation system, an","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 01:26:02 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/USCBC-president-US-companies-recognize-China-s-economic-strengths-1PgYg2UPYje/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,22 EU states demand emergency talks over Ceuta migrant surge,22 EU states demand emergency talks over Ceuta migrant surge,"22 EU states demand emergency talks over Ceuta migrant surge 22 EU states demand emergency talks over Ceuta migrant surge Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A majority of EU countries on Saturday called for emergency talks on the sudden influx of tens of thousands of migrants into the Spanish North African enclave of Ceuta. An open letter from the leaders of 22 of the EU's 27 countries demanded the bloc's interior ministers hold a video meeting ""as a matter of urgency"" to agree a speedy coordinated response, and to ""prevent further uncontrolled crossings.""","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 10:11:47 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/news-1PfXv4ULS1y/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China's visa-free policy boosts travel between Canada and China,China's visa-free policy boosts travel between Canada and China,"China's visa-free policy boosts travel between Canada and China China's visa-free policy boosts travel between Canada and China Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Nina Devries Copied Earlier this year, China announced that Canadian passport holders can now visit the country visa-free for up to 30 days, aiming to strengthen cooperation and people-to-people exchanges between the two nations. Early signs suggest the policy is already encouraging more travel. CGTN’s Nina Devries reports from Toronto. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:45:05 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/China-s-visa-free-policy-boosts-travel-between-Canada-and-China-1Pdnrv30uwU/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:48
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Spanish PM urges EU unity over Ceuta migrant crisis,Spanish PM urges EU unity over Ceuta migrant crisis,"Spanish PM urges EU unity over Ceuta migrant crisis Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Saturday called on the European Union to convene an extraordinary meeting of interior ministers to coordinate a common response to the recent migrant crisis in Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta while criticizing what he described as the ""selfish"" attitude of some member states. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A Spanish soldier uses a megaphone to speak to migrants sitting on the pavement prior to escorting them back to Morocco, in Spain's North Africa's Ceuta enclave, August 1, 2026. /VCG Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Saturday called on the European Union to convene an extraordinary meeting of interior ministers to coordinate a common response to the recent migrant crisis in Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta while criticizing what he described as the ""selfish"" attitude of some member states. In a letter addressed to European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen, Sanchez expressed his ""serious concern"" over the reaction of some European governments following the mass irregular crossings into Ceuta. Sanchez said around 50,000 migrants had entered Ceuta irregularly, but that Spain had restored control of the border in less than 48 hours, provided humanitarian assistance, returned virtually all of those who had crossed illegally and prevented any unauthorized onward movement to mainland Europe. He said these efforts were made possible through close cooperation with Moroccan authorities and with the support of other EU member states while highlighting Spain's long-standing migration policy, which he said had made the country one of the EU's most secure ex","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 12:04:54 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Spanish-PM-urges-EU-unity-over-Ceuta-migrant-crisis-1Pg3qmlpJ3a/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Thousands of migrants voluntarily leave after crossing into Ceuta,Thousands of migrants voluntarily leave after crossing into Ceuta,"Thousands of migrants voluntarily leave after crossing into Ceuta Spain's Interior Ministry said around 50,000 people crossed into the enclave from Thursday morning and estimated that 48,300 had returned by 6 p.m. (1600 GMT) on Friday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Migrants wait to board coaches as the Moroccan authorities transfer some back to their hometowns after they left Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta following an attempt to cross at the Morocco-Spain border, at Fnideq in northern Morocco on August 1, 2026. /CFP Spain said on Friday it had brought under control a massive influx of migrants into its North African enclave of Ceuta, with the vast majority of more than 50,000 people who crossed by land and sea already returning voluntarily to Morocco. The Spanish government's representative in Ceuta said 57 bodies had been recovered on the Spanish side of the border, adding that there could be additional casualties on the Moroccan side. Authorities said some migrants drowned, while others were crushed while trying to climb the breakwater supporting the border fence. Spain's Interior Ministry said around 50,000 people crossed into the enclave from Thursday morning and estimated that 48,300 had returned by 6 p.m. (1600 GMT) on Friday. Ceuta's regional leader, Juan Jesús Vivas, said the total number of crossings over the previous two days could have reached 60,000. On the Moroccan side, security forces used batons and tear gas to disperse crowds gathered near the gates to Ceuta, seeking to prevent further crossings. The","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 11:17:03 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Thousands-of-migrants-voluntarily-leave-after-crossing-into-Ceuta-1PfRdOSJibm/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,EU to hold videoconference on Ceuta migrant crisis,EU to hold videoconference on Ceuta migrant crisis,"EU to hold videoconference on Ceuta migrant crisis The European Union (EU) will hold an extraordinary videoconference on Tuesday to discuss the situation in Ceuta, a Spanish enclave in North Africa, according to Italy's ANSA news agency on Saturday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Spanish forces escort migrants to the Ceuta-Morocco border gate in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta in North Africa, August 1, 2026. /VCG The European Union (EU) will hold an extraordinary videoconference on Tuesday to discuss the situation in Ceuta, a Spanish enclave in North Africa, according to Italy's ANSA news agency on Saturday. The announcement was made by Micheal Martin, the Irish prime minister whose country currently holds the rotating presidency of the Council of the European Union, following calls from Spain and a 22-country initiative led by Italy and Denmark for a coordinated European response to the migrant crisis. Italy and Denmark on Saturday spearheaded a joint initiative calling for a coordinated European response to recent developments at the EU's external border in Ceuta, according to a statement released by the Italian government. The letter, signed by the leaders of 22 European countries, was sent to top EU officials. It expressed ""serious concern"" over the situation in Ceuta and stressed the need to prevent uncontrolled irregular crossings, combat migrant trafficking networks, eliminate factors that may incentivize new illegal entries and ensure a unified and effective European response. ""We are determined to prevent smugglers from challenging t","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 01:59:33 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-02/EU-to-hold-videoconference-on-Ceuta-migrant-crisis-1Ph1bLKlZio/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Kuwait says it downed hostile drones, Iran targeted vital facilities","Kuwait says it downed hostile drones, Iran targeted vital facilities","Kuwait says it downed hostile drones, Iran targeted vital facilities Kuwait says it downed hostile drones, Iran targeted vital facilities Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Kuwait's army ​said on Saturday ‌it ⁠had detected and destroyed hostile ‌drones ‌in the country's ‌airspace since dawn ‌and that what it described ⁠as ‌an Iranian attack had targeted several ‌vital facilities. A ​government facility in northern Kuwait and civilian property belonging to ⁠a company ⁠on ⁠Bubiyan Island ​were ​hit, ‌it said, adding that ‌falling shrapnel ⁠caused material damage but no casualties.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 08:01:45 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/news-1PfOcUuwTmM/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:49
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Poland says object entered airspace amid Russian strikes on Ukraine,Poland says object entered airspace amid Russian strikes on Ukraine,"Poland says object entered airspace amid Russian strikes on Ukraine Poland's military said on Thursday that it had scrambled F-16 fighter jets and an airborne early warning aircraft overnight after detecting intense activity by Russian long-range aviation during strikes on Ukraine. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Smoke rises in the sky above Ukraine's western city of Lviv, July 30, 2026. /VCG Poland's military said on Thursday that it had scrambled F-16 fighter jets and an airborne early warning aircraft overnight after detecting intense activity by Russian long-range aviation during strikes on Ukraine. The military said it detected an unidentified object that briefly entered Polish airspace before disappearing from radar. A military helicopter later located the object's suspected crash site near the village of Tarnawa-Kolonia in Poland's eastern Lublin region, the Operational Command of the Polish Armed Forces said on X on Thursday. Russian air strikes killed at least 13 people in Ukraine on Thursday, including one person in Kyiv, with attacks reaching as far west as the city of Lviv, Ukrainian officials said. Russia's defense ​ministry said on Thursday ‌its ⁠forces struck what it ‌described as ‌military facilities across Ukraine, from the capital Kyiv to ⁠Lviv ‌and Dnipropetrovsk, as well as three ‌cargo ships. The ​dry cargo vessels, which the ministry accused of carrying weapons ⁠and military ⁠equipment, ⁠were struck ​near ​the Black ‌Sea city of ‌Odesa, the ministry said.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 05:08:25 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/news-1Pci0UyhaLu/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Africa CDC flags constraints on DRC's Ebola response,Africa CDC flags constraints on DRC's Ebola response,"Africa CDC flags constraints on DRC's Ebola response Africa CDC Director-General Jean Kaseya stressed that the continued outbreak ""is the fastest-growing Ebola outbreak ever recorded"" and is now the second-largest by total confirmed cases. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Laboratory Technologist wearing protective equipment as she prepares to enter the Viral Hemorrhagic Fever Laboratory at Uganda Virus Research Institute on May 26, 2026 in Entebbe, Uganda. /CFP The Africa Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (Africa CDC) has warned of mounting operational constraints hampering Ebola response in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), while praising Uganda for successfully containing the outbreak. During an online press briefing on Thursday evening, Africa CDC Director-General Jean Kaseya stressed that the continued outbreak ""is the fastest-growing Ebola outbreak ever recorded"" and is now the second-largest by total confirmed cases. ""It is a very serious outbreak. We are now fighting because we don't want this outbreak to become the (largest ever) Ebola outbreak,"" he said. According to Kaseya, he will join World Health Organization (WHO) Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus to visit Bunia, the capital of the eastern DRC's Ituri Province and the epicenter of the outbreak, on Aug. 2. They are scheduled to meet with national authorities, frontline health workers, affected communities, and response partners. ""We really need to strengthen our capacity to stop the spread of this outbreak to other new zones. We need to cont","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 11:20:17 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Africa-CDC-flags-constraints-on-DRC-s-Ebola-response-1PfPvni6iL6/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,US forces launch new strikes on Iran as conflict widens,US forces launch new strikes on Iran as conflict widens,"US forces launch new strikes on Iran as conflict widens US forces launch new strikes on Iran as conflict widens Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied US forces on Wednesday night conducted fresh strikes against Iran in retaliation for Tehran's latest attacks as the conflict widened across the region. The US Central Command (CENTCOM) said on social media that its forces completed ""a heavy wave of strikes"" at 10 p.m. Eastern Time on Wednesday (0200 GMT Thursday) in response to Iran's attempted missile attacks a day earlier. According to CENTCOM, US forces struck dozens of targets belonging to Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, including military command centers, missile and drone facilities, coastal surveillance and defense sites, and maritime capabilities. More than 50,000 US service members are currently deployed to the Middle East and remain ""highly vigilant, focused, lethal and ready,"" CENTCOM said. Earlier on Wednesday, US President Donald Trump vowed twice that Washington would retaliate forcefully against Iran. He also said he had been briefed that an American-owned liquefied natural gas carrier at an Egyptian port was set on fire in an apparent drone attack earlier in the day. Iranian media earlier reported explosions in the country's southern regions. Iran's semi-official Tasnim news agency said that Qeshm Island in the Strait of Hormuz and locations in Bushehr province had come under attack. The W","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 07:16:50 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/news-1PcrbSNmt2M/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese vice premier holds video call with US treasury secretary,Chinese vice premier holds video call with US treasury secretary,"Chinese vice premier holds video call with US treasury secretary Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng held a video call on Thursday with US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng, also China's lead person for China-US economic and trade affairs, held a video call on Thursday with US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer. The two sides held candid, in-depth and constructive exchanges on implementing the important consensus reached between the two heads of state at their meeting in Beijing, and on maintaining stable economic and trade relations, expanding practical cooperation, and properly addressing each other's concerns in the next stage. The Chinese side expressed serious concern over the recent economic and trade restrictions imposed by the United States on China. Both sides agreed that under the strategic guidance of the two heads of state, they would further leverage the role of the China-US economic and trade consultation mechanism to enhance communication, build mutual trust and dispel doubts, expand cooperation, promote the stable and positive development of China-US economic and trade relations, and contribute to building a constructive China-US relationship of strategic stability.","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:21:48 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-31/Chinese-vice-premier-holds-video-call-with-US-treasury-secretary-1Pd2OqqkiJi/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,OpenAI says rogue AI agent attack hit other companies,OpenAI says rogue AI agent attack hit other companies,"OpenAI says rogue AI agent attack hit other companies ChatGPT maker OpenAI has revealed that an autonomous artificial intelligence (AI) agent which hacked a popular platform for computer programmers also attempted to breach four other companies during the incident. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Logos of OpenAI and Hugging Face. /VCG ChatGPT maker OpenAI has revealed that an autonomous AI agent which hacked a popular platform for computer programmers also attempted to breach four other companies during the incident. In an update Tuesday to its investigation blog post, OpenAI said its AI agent accessed four ""publicly available services,"" but did not identify the companies. The disclosure expands a cyber incident OpenAI described as unprecedented, which began when two of its modelshacked Hugging Face, a site where developers store and share AI models and code. OpenAI admitted last week that during testing, the models powering the agent broke out of their confined environment and connected to the internet to find ways to infiltrate Hugging Face. AI agents, systems that can independently complete tasks rather than just respond to chatbot prompts, are widely viewed as the next major phase of AI development. But their ability to act autonomously has also fueled concerns about uncontrolled systems. OpenAI said it found a handful of instances where the AI models came across login details that other companies had left exposed online, and used them to get into accounts on outside services. During the Hugging Face incident, the models gained access to four accounts a","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 04:55:33 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-07-30/OpenAI-says-rogue-AI-agent-attack-hit-other-companies-1Pc8BnszuMw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:50
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Spain says Ceuta migrant crisis under control as over 48,000 return","Spain says Ceuta migrant crisis under control as over 48,000 return","Spain says Ceuta migrant crisis under control as over 48,000 return Spain said Friday that it had brought a massive influx of migrants into the Spanish enclave of Ceuta under control, with the vast majority of those who crossed the border in recent days voluntarily returning to Morocco. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Undocumented migrants who entered Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta illegally, begin returning to Morocco after realizing their chances of obtaining legal status in Spain are unlikely, July 31, 2026. /VCG Spain said Friday that it had brought a massive influx of migrants into the Spanish enclave of Ceuta under control, with the vast majority of those who crossed the border in recent days voluntarily returning to Morocco. Spain's Interior Ministry said around 50,000 people had crossed into Ceuta by land and sea since Thursday morning, estimating that 48,300 had returned by 6 p.m. local time on Friday. Juan Jesús Vivas, president of Ceuta's regional government, said the number of people involved could have reached 60,000 over the past two days. The Spanish government's representative in Ceuta said 57 bodies had been recovered on the Spanish side of the border, while additional casualties could be found on the Moroccan side. Some migrants drowned, while others were crushed during attempts to climb the breakwater surrounding the border fence, officials said. Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez traveled to Ceuta on Friday, describing the mass crossing as a ""violation of Spain's territorial sovereignty."" He said authorities were accelerating the return of people wh","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 04:22:08 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-08-01/Spain-says-Ceuta-migrant-crisis-under-control-as-over-48-000-return-1PfqdlduMEg/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-08-03 01:30:51
