Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Ukraine seeks more US Patriot interceptors as bomb shelter probe deepens,Ukraine seeks more US Patriot interceptors as bomb shelter probe deepens,"Ukraine seeks more US Patriot interceptors as bomb shelter probe deepens A former Ukrainian official describes &quot;scandalous situations&quot; in bomb shelters as Volodymyr Zelenskyy pushes partners for 300 Patriot interceptors. Fox News correspondent Alex Hogan gives details on a Russian attack on Ukraine, a shooting near the White House and the ongoing conflict in Iran. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy renewed his appeal for U.S.-made Patriot missile interceptors after an overnight Russian missile and drone barrage on Kyiv killed at least 10 people and injured dozens more, Ukrainian officials said Aug. 1. ""The world has Patriot missiles. What matters now is for our partners to make the political decision to provide the necessary packages. The United States knows what we need. Europe knows what we need,"" Zelenskyy said in a video messageshared on X. ""Anti-ballistic missiles must protect people – not sit in stockpiles,"" he added. Zelenskyy's appeal came as a former Ukrainian government official told Fox News Digital that Ukraine's civilian protection crisis extends far beyond air defenses, describing ""scandalous situations"" amid a widening bomb shelter probe that has allegedly exposed deficiencies despite billions spent on construction and repairs. RUSSIA LAUNCHES BALLISTIC MISSILE ATTACK ON KYIV HOURS AFTER ZELENSKYY WARNS OF MAJOR STRIKE A Patriot system received by Ukraine is seen on the Day of Ukrainian Air Force on August 4, 2024.(Vitalii Nosach/Global Images Ukraine via Getty Images) Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, is also auditing its shelter spending, according to localreports. ""It's not possible to keep begging for missiles all the time. This is not how one protects the population,"" ex-Ukrai","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:20:55 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/ukraine-seeks-more-us-patriot-interceptors-bomb-shelter-probe-deepens,2026-08-03 01:31:16
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,At least 72 dead amid mass migrant rush to storm Spanish enclave of Ceuta sparking border crisis,At least 72 dead amid mass migrant rush to storm Spanish enclave of Ceuta sparking border crisis,"At least 72 dead amid mass migrant rush to storm Spanish enclave of Ceuta sparking border crisis At least 72 migrants are dead as Spain searches for more victims and a deadly border crossing sparks renewed political tensions across Europe. Fox News correspondent Stephanie Bennett reports on the political repercussions of migrants storming the Spanish enclave of Ceuta on ‘Fox Report.’ At least 72 migrants are dead after a chaotic rush to storm theSpanish enclave of Ceuta, turning one of Europe's latest border crises into a humanitarian disaster that is reigniting debate over immigration across the continent. Spanish authorities continued searching the waters off Ceuta over the weekend for additional victims after an estimated 50,000 to 60,000 migrants — most of them young men — poured into the tiny Spanish territory inNorth Africa. Officials said many of the victims drowned while attempting the crossing, while others were killed in a stampede near a breakwater barrier. The mass crossing unfolded over several days, temporarily increasing Ceuta's population of roughly 84,000 by more than half. By Sunday, many migrants had returned to neighboring Morocco, while others remained in the city or tried to avoid authorities. SPAIN DEPLOYS MILITARY AFTER THOUSANDS OF MIGRANTS OVERWHELM BORDER ENCLAVE, AT LEAST 18 DEAD Migrants who crossed into Spain return to Morocco from the Spanish enclave of Ceuta, Saturday, Aug. 1, 2026.(AP Photo/Bernat Armangue) The deaths have intensified thepolitical fight over immigrationin Spain and across Europe. Far-right leaders called for tighter border security and the removal of migrants who remained in the enclave. Santiago Abascal, leader of Spain's nationalist Vox party,visited Ceutaon S","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 13:01:11 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/least-72-dead-mass-migrant-rush-storm-spanish-enclave-ceuta-sparking-border-crisis,2026-08-03 01:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Mayor calls upscale restaurant bombing a 'brutal terrorist act' after 3 killed, 21 injured","Mayor calls upscale restaurant bombing a 'brutal terrorist act' after 3 killed, 21 injured","Mayor calls upscale restaurant bombing a 'brutal terrorist act' after 3 killed, 21 injured Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin vowed to hunt down those responsible after a body-worn bomb detonated at an upscale restaurant on Saturday killing three. Fox News Flash top headlines are here. Check out what's clicking on FoxNews.com. A bombing at an upscale restaurant inMoscowthat killed three people and wounded at least 21 others on Saturday was a ""brutal terrorist act,"" according to the city’s mayor, who vowed to hunt down those responsible for the attack. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin made the declaration Sunday, a day after the explosion tore through the Balzi Rossi Italian restaurant in the Russian capital. ""Yesterday, abrutal terrorist actwas committed in Moscow that claimed human lives. The victims are currently in the city’s hospitals, where they are receiving all necessary care,"" Sobyanin wrote on social media Sunday. EXPLOSION AT RESTAURANT IN CENTRAL MOSCOW LEAVES THREE DEAD, MORE THAN A DOZEN INJURED Police block an area near a deadly explosion at a restaurant in Moscow, Saturday, Aug. 1, 2026.(Sergei Vedyashkin/Moscow News Agency via AP) He added investigators are working to identify those behind the attack and vowed they ""will certainly be found and will face the punishment they deserve."" Russian authorities have not identified any suspects, and no group had claimed responsibility as of Sunday. Emergency vehicles are parked in an area near a deadly explosion at a restaurant in Moscow, Saturday, Aug. 1, 2026.(Sergei Vedyashkin/Moscow News Agency via AP) Russia's National Anti-Terrorism Committee said the blast was caused by a homemadeexplosive device. Russian state news agency RIA Novosti, citing local officials, ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 11:18:25 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/mayor-calls-upscale-restaurant-bombing-brutal-terrorist-act-3-killed-21-injured,2026-08-03 01:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Satellite images show evidence of oil leak spreading from sanctioned vessel near Oman,Satellite images show evidence of oil leak spreading from sanctioned vessel near Oman,"Satellite images show evidence of oil leak spreading from sanctioned vessel near Oman The Caroline Bezengi, reportedly carrying over 800,000 barrels of Russian crude, is leaking oil into a marine reserve home to endangered wildlife off Oman&apos;s coast. Fox News Flash top headlines are here. Check out what's clicking on FoxNews.com. A sanctioned tanker loaded with crude is leaving agrowing trail of oilin protected waters off the coast of Oman, according to newly reviewed satellite images, as experts warn the stranded vessel could break apart during the region's rough monsoon season. Satellite images reviewed by The Associated Press show an oil sheen covering roughly 20 square kilometers, or about 8 square miles, around Dhofar's Qibliyah Island, part ofOman's protected Hallaniyat Islands. Dark patches of crude have also reached the shoreline. Experts say the leak has worsened in recent days, fueling fears that rough weather could trigger a much larger spill. ""The last few days, the imagery indicates an increase in oil coming out, as the size of the sheen is growing,"" Wim Zwijnenburg, an environmental expert with the Dutch peace organization PAX, told the AP. REPORT WARNS RUSSIA USING SHADOW FLEET TO PROBE NATO DRONE DEFENSES This satellite image from Planet Labs PBC shows crude oil leaking and spreading from the sanctioned Suezmax tanker Caroline Bezengi grounded off the coast of Oman, on Friday, July 31, 2026.(Planet Labs PBC via AP) He said the biggest risk is that the vessel could break apart as strong winds and rough seas during the annualmonsoon seasoncontinue to pound the ship's hull. The 899-foot, Cameroon-flagged Caroline Bezengi has been stranded off Oman's southern coast since June after its crew reported an onboard","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:35:53 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/satellite-images-show-evidence-oil-leak-spreading-sanctioned-vessel-near-oman,2026-08-03 01:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Iran's war on Americans began decades ago. These families still carry the scars,Iran's war on Americans began decades ago. These families still carry the scars,"Iran's war on Americans began decades ago. These families still carry the scars Robert Bartlett says he died three times after an Iranian-supplied EFP tore through his Humvee in Baghdad, launching a decades-long fight for justice. The sister of Maj. Stuart Wolfer and widow of Capt. Shawn English say Iranian-backed attacks in Iraq left wounds that remain raw nearly 20 years later. Nearly two decades before the latest war with Iran, an explosively formed penetrator tore through a U.S. Army vehicle on a Baghdad road, killing Staff Sgt. William Brooks and leaving retired Sgt. Robert Bartlett with injuries so severe that he says he ""died three times."" The weapon was part of a broader Iranian campaign that armed and trained proxy forces to target American troops in Iraq, according to federal court findings. In cases involving hundreds of U.S. victims, judges found that Iran manufactured or supplied the weapons used in the attacks and that the assailants were trained or directed by the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps. ""It cut me in half from my temple down through my jaw, and then took my gunner’s legs off, and then took the top of my truck commander’s head off,"" Bartlett told Fox News Digital. ""I would end up dying three times and spent four years at the old Walter Reed receiving surgeries, reconstruction and rebuilding."" ARMY IDS 2 VICTIMS KILLED IN JORDAN AIR BASE ATTACK; TRUMP: IRAN WILL PAY 'MANY TIMES OVER' The vehicle driven by Sgt. Robert Bartlett after it was struck by an explosive device on Route Pluto in Baghdad on May 3, 2005. Staff Sgt. William Brooks was killed, while Bartlett and two other soldiers were wounded.(Fox News) Bartlett was driving an armored Humvee on Route Pluto in Baghdad, May 3","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:00:13 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/irans-war-americans-began-decades-ago-families-still-carry-scars,2026-08-03 01:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Israeli orphans of fallen heroes find pride, connection on US journey","Israeli orphans of fallen heroes find pride, connection on US journey","Israeli orphans of fallen heroes find pride, connection on US journey A young Oct. 7 hostage survivor shared his story with fellow bereaved children during the IDF Widows &amp; Orphans Organization&apos;s Bar/Bat Mitzvah trip. Aviva and Keith Siegel, freed hostages from Hamas, recount their harrowing experiences in Gaza and thank first lady Melania Trump for her efforts to secure their release. Twenty-eight children from acrossIsraelwho lost a parent killed while serving in the country's security forces participated in a three-week delegation to North America as part of the IDF Widows & Orphans Organization's annual Bar/Bat Mitzvah program. The journey began last month inChicago, where the children spent a weekend with host families before traveling to Camp Chi in Wisconsin for nearly a week of activities with American kids. They then continued to New York City, where they visited Times Square and saw ""The Lion King"" on Broadway, before heading to New Jersey. For many, it was their first visit to the United States. FREED HOSTAGE ROM BRASLAVSKI DETAILS ABUSE, STARVATION DURING 738 DAYS IN GAZA CAPTIVITY The IDF Widows & Orphans Organization's annual Bar/Bat Mitzvah program delegation in NYC at Times Square.(Yiftach Moran) ""Everything is planned very carefully. ‘The Lion King,’ for instance, is more than a Broadway show for them. It’s the story of an orphan who is able to honor his father’s memory and move forward because of the support of his friends. Nothing about this trip is accidental. It is deliberately designed to give them as powerful and meaningful an experience as possible,"" Daniel Elbaum, executive director of the IDF Widows & Orphans USA Organization, told Fox News Digital. With the Unite","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 06:00:41 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/israeli-orphans-fallen-heroes-find-pride-connection-us-journey,2026-08-03 01:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,US companies win billions in African data center deals in direct competition with China,US companies win billions in African data center deals in direct competition with China,"US companies win billions in African data center deals in direct competition with China From Lesotho to Gabon, American firms are winning AI data center and power contracts worth billions as the U.S.-China trade war intensifies in Africa. President Donald Trump inks a deal with Australia on critical minerals. JOHANNESBURG:The U.S. is beating China in a high-tech trade war over data centers in a fierce battle being waged acrossAfrica. Major new deals have been engineered in a public-private partnership between the Trump administration and U.S. companies in Africa, while States across the U.S. clamp down on the centers over their massive reliance on electricity. The administration’s Bureau of African Affairs has reported it has worked on 37 commercial transactions that have closed since the beginning of President Donald Trump’s second term — representing $25.67 billion in total value, with more still being reported. RESOURCE-RICH NATION PRAISES US TIES AMID WASHINGTON-BEIJING CRITICAL MINERALS RACE A rendering of BESS battery storage facilities, to be constructed in Lesotho by U.S. company Convalt Energy, as part of a $6.2 billion deal with the government of Lesotho facilitated with the assistance of the U.S. government.(Convalt Energy) Data centers are at the heart of today's global economy — fueling the massive demand for AI and hosting everything from video streaming to housing cloud networks. In Lesotho, with U.S. help, an American company has won a $6.2 billion deal for a data center and hydropower plant. It is the largest transaction in this Southern African country’s history. In Gabon, the U.S. Embassy helped win $600 million in business for American companies in 2025. And this year, the embassy in this c","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 06:00:03 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/us-companies-win-billions-african-data-center-deals-direct-competition-china,2026-08-03 01:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Famed mountaineer Nirmal Purja, 43, among 10 climbers killed after avalanche in Pakistan","Famed mountaineer Nirmal Purja, 43, among 10 climbers killed after avalanche in Pakistan","Famed mountaineer Nirmal Purja, 43, among 10 climbers killed after avalanche in Pakistan Nirmal Purja was leading climbers up Broad Peak in Pakistan when a deadly avalanche struck the Karakoram expedition, killing all 10 members of the group. Fox News senior correspondent Claudia Cowan reports on the deadly avalanche near Castle Peak, Calif., where eight skiers have been confirmed dead. Mike Tobin warns there is 'not a lot of reason for optimism' in recovery efforts on ‘The Story.’ Famous mountaineer Nirmal Purja, who was the subject of a2021 Netflix documentary, was among 10 climbers confirmed dead on Saturday on the world’s 12th-tallest mountain in Pakistan. The climbers were killed when they were hit by anavalancheon the 26,414-foot-tall Broad Peak Thursday in the Karakoram mountain range. ""The world has lost one of mountaineering's greatest climbers,"" Elite Exped, the company involved in the expedition, said in a statement, adding, ""we mourn not only Nims, but every life lost in this tragedy."" AMERICAN CLIMBER'S REMAINS FOUND AFTER AVALANCHE IN PAKISTAN, OTHER MOUNTAINEERS STILL MISSING Nirmal Purja speaks during a news conference in Kathmandu, Nepal, on May 28, 2019, after climbing six mountains including Mount Everest as part of an attempt to climb fourteen 8,000-meter peaks in seven months.(REUTERS) The company added, ""No words can ease the pain of this unimaginable loss."" Purja had been leading the group up Broad Peak. A Pakistanirescue team recovered three bodies on Friday, including American Sarah Mallory Geis, but had to temporarily halt the operation in the ""remote and difficult"" area due to weather conditions. NOVICE CLIMBER SURVIVES 1,500-FOOT DROP ON CALIFORNIA'S MOUNT SHASTA AFTER HELICOPTER RESCUE","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 21:59:24 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/famed-mountaineer-nirmal-purja-43-among-10-climbers-killed-avalanche-pakistan,2026-08-03 01:31:17
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,State Department raises travel warning for part of Spain as migrant surge sparks military deployment,State Department raises travel warning for part of Spain as migrant surge sparks military deployment,"State Department raises travel warning for part of Spain as migrant surge sparks military deployment Tens of thousands of migrants surged into Spain&apos;s Ceuta from Morocco, prompting a military deployment and a new State Department travel advisory. Fox News correspondent Stephanie Bennett reports on the political repercussions of migrants storming the Spanish enclave of Ceuta on ‘Fox Report.’ TheState Departmenton Saturday raised its Travel Advisory for Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta to Level 3: Reconsider Travel after tens of thousands of migrants surged into the Spanish territory from neighboring Morocco, prompting a major security response. The updated advisory warns that the ""massive and uncontrolled arrival of migrants from Morocco to Ceuta may lead to unpredictable and dangerous security situations."" ""Spain has deployed the Spanish military, Spanish National Police, and Guardia Civil as a result of this serious situation,"" the advisory states. ""Americans should reconsider travel to the area given the risks posed to their safety and security."" SPAIN DEPLOYS MILITARY AFTER THOUSANDS OF MIGRANTS OVERWHELM BORDER ENCLAVE, AT LEAST 18 DEAD The advisory applies only to Ceuta, an autonomous Spanish city on the northern coast of Africa that borders Morocco. The rest of Spain remains under its existing travel advisory level.Assistant Secretary of State Dylan Johnson said the advisory was updated in response to what he described as the ""mass invasion of tens of thousands of illegal migrants."" ""This invasion is the direct result of the Spanish government's refusal to secure its borders and defend its people — and now threatens the security of Europe,"" Johnson said in a statement to Fox News Digital. TRUMP BLASTS SPAI","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 19:16:46 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/state-department-raises-travel-warning-part-spain-migrant-surge-sparks-military-deployment,2026-08-03 01:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Explosion at restaurant in central Moscow leaves three dead, more than a dozen injured","Explosion at restaurant in central Moscow leaves three dead, more than a dozen injured","Explosion at restaurant in central Moscow leaves three dead, more than a dozen injured A homemade explosive device killed three people at a Moscow restaurant, and injured many more on Saturday night, Russian officials said. Resident-shot footage shows blasts striking the Kapotnya refinery and a nearby building during Ukraine’s massive drone attack on Moscow, June 18, 2026. (Credit: East2West News) Three people were killed on Saturday at an upscale Italian restaurant in central Moscow following amassive explosion. The explosion was caused by a homemade explosive device, Russia's National Anti-Terrorism Committee claimed. The dead included a woman who attempted to bring the explosive device into the Balzi Rossi Italian restaurant, a security guard and a patron, Russian state news agency RIA Novosti reported, adding that the security guard wouldn't let her in. NATO MEMBER SCRAMBLES FIGHTER JETS AS RUSSIAN ATTACK ON UKRAINE KILLS 8 Law enforcement officers and emergency services personnel stand near the site of an explosion at a restaurant in central Moscow, Russia, on Aug. 1, 2026.(REUTERS) MOSCOW, TALIBAN FORGE MILITARY ALLIANCE IN POWER GRAB AFTER US AFGHANISTAN EXIT: REPORTS At least 21 more people were injured in the explosion, which happened around 8 p.m. on a ground-floor terrace restaurant​ at Kudrinksaya Square, which includes seven skyscrapers built during the Stalin regime. Balzi Rossi 's website said it was closed Saturday for a private event. Police vehicles are at the site of an explosion at a restaurant in central Moscow, Russia, on Aug. 1, 2026.(REUTERS) Russia's FSB security service said earlier this year that it planned to increase security within the country for high-level officia","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 17:45:42 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/explosion-restaurant-central-moscow-leaves-three-dead-dozen-injured,2026-08-03 01:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Socialist Spanish PM blasts Meloni over restored border controls after Ceuta surge, demands emergency meeting","Socialist Spanish PM blasts Meloni over restored border controls after Ceuta surge, demands emergency meeting","Socialist Spanish PM blasts Meloni over restored border controls after Ceuta surge, demands emergency meeting Pedro Sánchez called Europe&apos;s response &quot;selfish&quot; and &quot;unlawful&quot; after Italy suspended Schengen Area free-travel arrangements with Spain over the crisis. Fox News foreign correspondent Jeff Paul reports from Ceuta, Spain, where Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez has deployed military forces after a massive surge of Moroccan migrants overwhelmed border crossings and strained local resources. SpanishPrime Minister Pedro Sánchez broadly blasted fellow European leaders for their response to the surge of tens of thousands of migrants from Morocco to the Spanish border, seemingly criticizing Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni for deciding to resume European border controls in the wake of the incident. Sánchez appeared to take issue withItaly'sdecision to temporarily suspend Schengen Area free-travel arrangements with Spain. The Schengen Area is an agreement between 29 European countries that abolishes passport controls and allows people to travel across European borders without providing documents. ""In the current international context, the European Union cannot afford this kind of selfish, polarising and unlawful reaction,"" Sánchez said in a letter obtained by the Agence France-Presse (AFP) newswire. Sánchez, who leads the Spanish Socialist Workers' Party, touted his country's quick turnaround in expelling nearly all of the 50,000-60,000 migrants who crossed the border back to Morocco. ""Despite these indisputable facts,"" Sánchez wrote, ""the reaction of European governments over the past few hours has been rather asymmetric. Most have showed us their support and solidarity, and have offered their assistance. Others, however, have chose","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 14:58:25 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/socialist-spanish-pm-blasts-meloni-restored-border-controls-ceuta-surge-demands-emergency-meeting,2026-08-03 01:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Exclusive: Israeli President Herzog blasts Mamdani, praises Trump, sounds alarm on Iran","Exclusive: Israeli President Herzog blasts Mamdani, praises Trump, sounds alarm on Iran","Exclusive: Israeli President Herzog blasts Mamdani, praises Trump, sounds alarm on Iran Israel&apos;s president praised Trump&apos;s deep support for the Jewish state and addressed Gaza and the board of peace, Karim Khan&apos;s ICC dismissal, U.S.-Israel relations and Zohran Mamdani. Just hours before President Trump announced that Hamas had agreed to a roadmap that includes disarmament, Israel's president discussed the U.S.-Israel alliance, Iran, Mamdani and much more. (Video: Yoav Dudkevitch for Fox News Digitial.) JERUSALEM, Israel — New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani is spreading hateful and antisemitic rhetoric and endangering the lives of New Yorkers, Israeli President Isaac Herzog told Fox News Digital in an exclusive interview at his Jerusalem residence. ""Mamdani does not respect my nation's right for self-determination … the Jewish people's inherent right to have a nation of their own. And he's basically spreading blasphemy, hate, antisemitic rhetoric. He should understand that he's risking his own citizens. He’s risking their safety, well-being and life,"" Herzog said. In an incident that drew global attention, Mamdani posted a video on social media July 21 in which he called Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu ""a war criminal"" and ""the architect of a horrific genocide against the Palestinian people."" HUCKABEE WARNS OF 'BIBLICAL IGNORANCE' AS HE DEFENDS CONSERVATIVE SUPPORT FOR ISRAEL President Isaac Herzog of Israel addressed Mayor Mamdani and Israel's relationship with the U.S. in an interview with Fox News Digital in Jerusalem, Israel.(Yoav Dudkevitch/TPS-IL for Fox News Digital) ""This cannot be accepted in New York, which is a city which is dear to our heart, dear to the Israelis and dear to me personally,"" Herzog said. ""I think New Yor","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 10:57:13 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/exclusive-israeli-president-herzog-blasts-mamdani-praises-trump-sounds-alarm-iran,2026-08-03 01:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,What’s old is new again: Trump-style conservative is back as PM of European nation,What’s old is new again: Trump-style conservative is back as PM of European nation,"What’s old is new again: Trump-style conservative is back as PM of European nation Janez Janša formed a coalition government after losing Slovenia&apos;s election, reversing Robert Golob&apos;s policies on Israel, immigration,and business. Janez Janša secures parliamentary backing and begins a new term in office. (Reuters) ŠKOFJA LOKA, Slovenia:The Republic of Slovenia, the central European nation known for being the birthplace of First LadyMelania Trumpand LA Lakers star Luka Dončić, is undergoing a radical shift in politics as the country comes to terms with its new larger-than-life prime minister. Prime Minister Janez Janša recently scraped together a coalition that did away with the country’s leftist leader, Robert Golob. In what is his fourth term, Janša has begun what many see as Trump-like policy corrections. He has reversed Golob’s anti-Israel policies by announcing his intent to move the Slovenian embassy to Jerusalem, freezing Slovenia’s recognition of a Palestinian state and revoking a 2025 ban on military trade with Israel. EUROPE'S 'GREEN IDEOLOGY' CLIMATE AGENDA RISKS CRUSHING ITS INDUSTRY, ENVIRONMENT MINISTER WARNS Right-wing Slovenian Democratic Party (SDS) leader Janez Jansa addresses the media after his investiture vote as Slovenia's Prime Minister at the National Assembly in Ljubljana on May 22, 2026.(Jure Makovec / AFP via Getty Images) Janša also believes in strong U.S. relations. During anAmerica 250event hosted by the U.S. Embassy in Ljubljana, and with the First Lady's father, Viktor Knavs, in attendance, Janša described how America was the beacon for Slovenian independence. ""We imagined America, the United States of America, as the ideal embodiment of that free world... That Slovenia, ","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 06:00:20 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/whats-old-new-again-trump-style-conservative-back-pm-european-nation,2026-08-03 01:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"American climber's remains found after avalanche in Pakistan, other mountaineers still missing","American climber's remains found after avalanche in Pakistan, other mountaineers still missing","American climber's remains found after avalanche in Pakistan, other mountaineers still missing American climber Sarah Mallory Geis was among at least 10 mountaineers caught in a Broad Peak avalanche as rescue teams search for others. A Sherpa guide who vanished on Mount Everest was found alive and crawling toward base camp nearly a week later. The remains of an American mountain climber who got caught in anavalanchein Pakistan were found on Friday, according to Pakistani officials. Sarah Mallory Geis was climbing Broad Peak in Pakistan's Karakoram mountain range with an international group of at least 10 people when theywent missingon Thursday. A rescue team also found the remains of Nadhira Ahmed Abdullah Al Harthy of Oman and Pur Bahadur Gurung of Nepal on Friday. NURSE IMPALED BY POLE DURING HIKE FORCED TO TREK 10 MILES FOR HELP: 'A FREAK THING' Members of a mountaineers rescue team prepare to depart from an airbase on a search operation for climbers missing after an avalanche on Pakistan's Broad Peak in Skardu, Gilgit-Baltistan, in northern Pakistan, on Friday.(Alpine Club of Pakistan via AP) There were signs of several more bodies where the rescue team was searching, drone footage showed, according to local officials. At 26,414 feet, Broad Peak is the twelfth-tallest mountain in the world. MISSING GRAND CANYON HIKER, 83, RESCUED AFTER GETTING SEPARATED FROM COMPANION ""We hope to continue our operations, both aerial search and the ​ ground rescue, till the time we find the survivors or the dead bodies,"" Irfan Arshad, president of the Alpine Club of Pakistan, said Friday. The rescue operation was temporarily halted Friday night due to weather conditions. Renowned mountaineer Nirmal Purja is among the m","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:57:36 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/american-climber-remains-found-avalanche-pakistan-mountaineers-missing,2026-08-03 01:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Migrant crisis pushes Italy to restore border checks with Spain, testing Europe's open-border system","Migrant crisis pushes Italy to restore border checks with Spain, testing Europe's open-border system","Migrant crisis pushes Italy to restore border checks with Spain, testing Europe's open-border system Conservative leaders across Europe react as an estimated 60,000 migrants crossed into Ceuta from Morocco within 24 hours, threatening its open-border policies. Spain deploys military forces to its enclave of Ceuta after a massive surge of over 49,000 migrants overwhelms the border in a single day. Nile Gardiner, former advisor to Margaret Thatcher, joins Brian Kilmeade to warn that the United States faces a similar catastrophic border threat if current migration policies are not urgently reversed. Italytemporarily restored border controls on travelers arriving from Spain Friday as the mass migrant crossing into Ceuta, Spain, escalated from a Spanish emergency into a wider test ofEurope’s passport-free travel system. The move followed the entry of approximately 60,000 migrants from Morocco into Ceuta, Spain — a Spanish autonomous city on the North African coast. Spain’s Interior Ministry said 48,300 people had since voluntarily returned to Morocco, leaving fewer than 2,000 people in the territory, while the reported death toll among migrants attempting to reach the enclave rose to 57 people. The crisis is reverberating far beyond Spain because it challenges one of theEuropean Union’s central promises: that member states can maintain open internal borders while jointly protecting the bloc’s external frontier. Schengen rests on a tradeoff: participating countries remove most controls between one another while jointly securing the zone’s external borders. Italy’s decision to restore checks, alongside calls for tougher restrictions from conservative leaders across Europe, has raised questions about whether migration pressures could lead ","Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:08:18 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/migrant-crisis-pushes-italy-restore-border-checks-spain-testing-europes-open-border-system,2026-08-03 01:31:18
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Spain deploys military after thousands of migrants overwhelm border enclave, at least 18 dead","Spain deploys military after thousands of migrants overwhelm border enclave, at least 18 dead","Spain deploys military after thousands of migrants overwhelm border enclave, at least 18 dead Video shows thousands of migrants overwhelming Ceuta&apos;s Tarajal border as Spain deploys its military and at least 18 people die during crossings. Video shows migrants swimming and arriving by boat in Ceuta as Spain deploys its military following a mass border crossing that left at least 18 people dead. (Credit: Associated Press) Spainis deploying its military to the North African enclave of Ceuta after thousands of migrants overwhelmed the territory's border with Morocco, prompting a major security response as officials confirmed at least 18 people died during the crossings. The Spanish government said thearmed forceswill support the Civil Guard in restoring order after local officials warned the city could no longer handle the influx. Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez and Interior Minister Fernando Grande-Marlaska are expected to visit Ceuta as Madrid scrambles to contain the crisis. The surge marks one of the largest migrant waves to hit Ceuta since 2021, when more than 8,000 people entered the Spanish territory over two days, triggering a diplomatic dispute between Spain and Morocco. ""The situation is absolute chaos,"" Rachid Sbihi, who heads an association representing Spain's Civil Guard officers in Ceuta, told The Associated Press. ""It's not possible to give precise numbers, but there are thousands of migrants crossing."" WHITE HOUSE BLASTS SPANISH GOVERNMENT AS THOUSANDS OF MIGRANTS SURGE FROM MOROCCO, EMERGENCY REQUEST DENIED Migrants celebrate and make their way toward Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta after crossing from Morocco on Thursday.(AP) Spain's government delegation in Ceuta said at least 18 people die","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:35:41 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/spain-deploys-military-after-thousands-migrants-overwhelm-border-enclave-least-9-dead,2026-08-03 01:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"White House blasts Spanish government as thousands of migrants surge from Morocco, emergency request denied","White House blasts Spanish government as thousands of migrants surge from Morocco, emergency request denied","White House blasts Spanish government as thousands of migrants surge from Morocco, emergency request denied Video captured thousands of migrants stampeding through Ceuta as Spain&apos;s government denies the enclave president&apos;s request for a national emergency. Thousands of migrants from Morocco pored over the country's border with Spain and into Spain's African enclave of Ceuta July 30, 2026. (Reuters) The White House bashed Spain's left-wing government after the border between Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta and Morocco collapsed Thursday. ""President Trump has long warned Europe what would happen if they continue to implement far-left, globalist policies, including enabling mass migration,"" White House principal deputy press secretary Anna Kelly told Fox News in a statement. ""Spain and other countries who have adopted this destructive philosophy should immediately reverse course or risk their own demise."" TRUMP CRITICIZES SPAIN AMID IRAN, NATO RIFT AS PM SANCHEZ FACES QUESTIONS OVER POLITICAL MOTIVES Ceuta's president formally requested a national emergency declaration Thursday after more than 2,000 migrants crossed the border from Morocco in the past 10 days. Videos showed chaotic scenes of migrants pouring into theSpanish territory. Video shows hordes of apparently military-aged men smiling and posing for cameras, some carrying swimming flippers, and sprinting through the streets as authorities struggle to corral the unruly masses. Migrants run and cheer as they cross on foot into the North African enclave of Ceuta from Morocco after swimming over from the Moroccan side and overwhelming police at the city's breakwater, according to Spain's Guardia Civil, in Ceuta, Spain, July 30, 2026.(Faro TV via Reuters) Other footage s","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:19:05 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/white-house-blasts-spanish-government-thousands-migrants-surge-from-morocco-emergency-request-denied,2026-08-03 01:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,NATO member scrambles fighter jets as Russian attack on Ukraine kills 8,NATO member scrambles fighter jets as Russian attack on Ukraine kills 8,"NATO member scrambles fighter jets as Russian attack on Ukraine kills 8 Poland scrambled fighter jets after a suspected Russian Kh-101 missile entered its airspace during a massive barrage of over 70 missiles and 280 drones. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy says Ukraine's military has transformed dramatically, now supported by more than 500 defense companies. He says Russia is losing 30,000 troops each month and argues the initiative in the war is no longer in Russian President Vladimir Putin's hands. Poland, the closest NATO member to theUkraine-Russia war, scrambled fighter jets and placed its air defenses on high alert early Thursday as Russia launched more than 70 missiles and roughly 280 drones across Ukraine, killing at least eight and wounding dozens from Kyiv to the western city of Lviv. Ukrainian PresidentVolodymyr Zelenskyy, just returning from this week's U.S. visit with President Donald Trump and the funeral of late Sen. Lindsey Graham, R-S.C., said the barrage exposed a critical shortage of Western-supplied interceptors, particularly against ballistic missiles. ""The protection of people’s lives depends directly on their willingness"" to provide Ukraine with air-defense missiles, Zelenskyy said of Kyiv’s allies. Hours later Thursday morning, the European Union disbursed $4 billion to Ukraine to finance the procurement of more drones, missiles, air defense and fighter jets, according to the European Commission. RUSSIA LAUNCHES BALLISTIC MISSILE ATTACK ON KYIV HOURS AFTER ZELENSKYY WARNS OF MAJOR STRIKE Ukrainian firefighters work to extinguish a fire at a market following a Russian missile strike in Kyiv on overnight into Thursday morning. Russian strikes killed at least eight pe","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 07:41:10 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/nato-member-scrambles-fighter-jets-russian-attack-ukraine-kills-8,2026-08-03 01:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Trump retaliates after Iran attack as expert warns regime is growing more dangerous,Trump retaliates after Iran attack as expert warns regime is growing more dangerous,"Trump retaliates after Iran attack as expert warns regime is growing more dangerous Trump vowed to hit Iran hard after CENTCOM confirmed all ballistic missiles targeting U.S. forces in Jordan were intercepted with no casualties reported. FDD’s Behnam Ben Taleblu says Tehran is becoming more risk-tolerant and warns the U.S. must restore deterrence or face additional missile and drone attacks. The United States resumed airstrikes inside Iran Wednesday night in retaliation for Tehran’s attempted surprise ballistic-missile attack on American forces, as an Iran expert warned that the regime has become increasingly willing to test Washington despite its weakened military capabilities. ""The strikes are a powerful response to yesterday’s attempted Iranian attack on U.S. forces based in the Middle East,"" U.S. Central Command said as the new operation began, according to The Associated Press. The renewed strikes marked the first U.S. attacks inside Iran sincePresident Donald Trump pausedthe bombing campaign Friday after 13 consecutive nights to allow diplomacy another chance. Iran’s missile launch shattered that brief pause and returned the conflict to direct exchanges between Washington and Tehran. Trump had signaled the retaliation earlier Wednesday, saying the United States would hit Iran ""very hard."" ARMY IDS 2 VICTIMS KILLED IN JORDAN AIR BASE ATTACK; TRUMP: IRAN WILL PAY 'MANY TIMES OVER' Map shows U.S. bases and assets in the Mideast.(Fox News) Behnam Ben Taleblu, senior director of the Iran program at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, said the surprise nature of Iran’s attack reflected a significant shift in Tehran’s strategy. ""What makes this attack different is that it’s basically a surprise attack,""","Thu, 30 Jul 2026 06:00:29 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/trump-retaliates-after-iran-attack-expert-warns-regime-growing-more-dangerous,2026-08-03 01:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Russia launches ballistic missile attack on Kyiv hours after Zelenskyy warns of major strike,Russia launches ballistic missile attack on Kyiv hours after Zelenskyy warns of major strike,"Russia launches ballistic missile attack on Kyiv hours after Zelenskyy warns of major strike Multiple explosions rocked Kyiv after Russia launched ballistic missiles, hours after Volodymyr Zelenskyy warned of a massive overnight assault. Paul Gigot discusses Trump's decision to grant Ukraine a license for Patriot missile production. Seth Jones analyzes the move's impact on Ukraine's defense, current battlefield challenges and potential Russian escalation against NATO. Russianair strikes killed at least 13 people across Ukraine early Thursday, including one in Kyiv, as ballistic missiles targeted the capital and multiple explosions rocked the city, according to Ukrainian officials. Ukrainian PresidentVolodymyr Zelenskyysaid Thursday that Russia launched more than 70 missile and over 280 drones at Ukraine overnight, adding that the country's air defenses intercepted a significant number of the incoming missiles. Kyiv Mayor Vitali Klitschko urged residents to seek shelter as blasts rocked the city. Reuters, citing a witness, reported hearing multiple explosions. The Ukrainian Air Force also said Russia was targeting the capital with ballistic missiles. RUSSIA UNLEASHES NEARLY 600 MISSILES AND DRONES ON KYIV IN DEADLIEST STRIKE SINCE MAY An explosion lights up the sky over the city during a Russian missile and drone strike amid Russia's attack on Ukraine, in Kyiv, July 2, 2026.(Gleb Garanich/Reuters) Ukrainian officials said one person was killed and two more injured in Kyiv, with six more, including two children, killed in the regions of Dnipropetrovsk and Poltava. Klitschko later said several non-residential sites caught fire following the strikes and that a missile struck the home of a large family, warning th","Wed, 29 Jul 2026 21:14:18 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-kyiv-hours-after-zelenskyy-warns-major-strike,2026-08-03 01:31:19
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Sudan's forgotten war leaves millions hungry as global attention remains elsewhere,Sudan's forgotten war leaves millions hungry as global attention remains elsewhere,"Sudan's forgotten war leaves millions hungry as global attention remains elsewhere El Fasher and El Obeid remain flashpoints as UN reports detail war crimes, mass rape, and genocide conditions in Sudan&apos;s escalating civil war. New footage shows families lining up for water as UNICEF warns children continue to bear the brunt of the war. (Video: UNICEF via AP.) As multiple international crises grip the world, from Iran to Russia’s war in Ukraine, Sudan quietly remains one of the largest humanitarian anddisplacement disastersin the world. Since the outbreak of hostilities in 2023, over 14 million people have been displaced and nearly 34 million people are in desperate need ofhumanitarian support, accounting for 10% of global needs, according to the International Rescue Committee. ""The war in Sudan has caused the world's largest humanitarian crisis and has escalated into a regional war involving all of its neighbors as well as numerousMiddle Eastern powers,"" Alan Boswell, Project Director for the Horn of Africa at International Crisis Group, told Fox News Digital. ""Despite this, world leaders continue to ignore the conflict, leaving it to subordinates. That approach continues to fail,"" Boswell added. COULD THIS AFRICAN NATION BECOME TRUMP'S NEXT TERROR TARGET AS JIHADISTS CLOSE IN ON POWER? Women and children queue to receive free food being distributed in al-Mohayra camp for displaced people, near the city of El-Obeid in the southern Kordofan region, on June 29, 2026.(AFP via Getty Images) The United Nations says that some 19.5 million people are experiencing acute hunger, and 4.5 million people have fled the country. The U.S. also recently imposed an additional round ofsanctionsagainst the Sudanese A","Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:13:15 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/sudans-forgotten-war-leaves-millions-hungry-global-attention-remains-elsewhere,2026-08-03 01:31:20
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Antisemitic violence reaches deadliest level since 1994, new global report finds","Antisemitic violence reaches deadliest level since 1994, new global report finds","Antisemitic violence reaches deadliest level since 1994, new global report finds The J7 report reveals 20 people were killed in antisemitic attacks in 2025, marking the deadliest year since 1994 with a 97% rise in violence. Cornell Law professor William Jacobson discusses a report finding that rising antisemitism is forcing many Jewish Americans to hide their identity on ‘America Reports.’ A shocking new report says 2025 was the deadliest year forantisemitic attacksworldwide since 1994. The J7 Large Communities’ Task Force Against Antisemitismreleased its second annual report, which tracks antisemitic hatred in the seven countries outside of Israel where over 90% of Jews live. According to the report, 20 people were killed in antisemitic attacks in 2025. All of the deadly attacks took place in J7 countries. The Anti-Defamation League (ADL) is one of two organizations representing the Jewish diaspora in the U.S. in the J7, which includes similar organizations from Australia, Canada, Argentina, the U.S., the U.K.,Germanyand France. CHRISTIAN LEADERS HOLD EMERGENCY SUMMIT IN JERUSALEM TO CONFRONT GLOBAL RISE IN ANTISEMITISM Police cordon off an area at Bondi Beach after a terrorist attack at a Hanukkah celebration in Sydney, Australia, on Dec. 14, 2025.(Mark Baker/AP Photo) ADL Senior Director of Global Research and Diplomatic Affairs Aykan Erdemir told Fox News Digital that the report’s findings show ""there’s no time to waste"" in combating hate. ""This isn't a warning sign anymore, it's already happening,"" Erdemir said. ""If governments let antisemitism take root and perpetrators walk free, the violence won't stop with Jewish communities. History shows Jews are the canary in the coal mine: when hatr","Wed, 29 Jul 2026 06:20:12 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/antisemitic-violence-reaches-deadliest-level-since-1994-new-global-report-finds,2026-08-03 01:31:20
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"China, Russia, Iran and North Korea form 'axis of aggressors' that could overwhelm US, book warns","China, Russia, Iran and North Korea form 'axis of aggressors' that could overwhelm US, book warns","China, Russia, Iran and North Korea form 'axis of aggressors' that could overwhelm US, book warns A new report documents 616 instances of security cooperation among China, Russia, Iran and North Korea, warning of a dangerous simultaneity problem. FDD report warns America’s adversaries are combining military support, sanctioned energy trade and technology transfers to stretch U.S. defenses. China, Russia, Iran andNorth Koreaare acting as a strategically aligned bloc even without a formal mutual-defense treaty, according to a new Foundation for Defense of Democracies book warning that their cooperation could leave the United States confronting multiple crises simultaneously. The book, ""Axis of Aggressors: Countering the Cooperation of China, Russia, Iran and North Korea,"" examines how the four authoritarian governments support one another across military, economic, cyber and technology domains. Its authors acknowledge that the grouping is not a NATO-style alliance. It has no unified command, comprehensive defense commitment or complete trust among its members. But they argue that its practical effects are already visible in active conflicts. TRUMP TO CONFRONT XI AT HIGH-STAKES SUMMIT OVER CHINA BACKING FOR IRAN, RUSSIA In this pool photograph distributed by the Russian state agency Sputnik, Russiain President Vladimir Putin, Chinese President Xi Jinping and North Korean leader Kim Jong Un walk before a military parade marking the 80th anniversary of victory over Japan and the end of World War II in Beijing’s Tiananmen Square on Sept. 3, 2025. Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is seen at left in the background.(Sergey Bobylev / POOL / AFP via Getty Images) ""I just got back from a couple of weeks inUkraine, and when I’m","Wed, 29 Jul 2026 06:00:16 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/china-russia-iran-north-korea-form-axis-aggressors-overwhelm-us-book-warns,2026-08-03 01:31:20
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,French man discovers 5 dead babies hidden in boxes in his home after argument with wife: prosecutors,French man discovers 5 dead babies hidden in boxes in his home after argument with wife: prosecutors,"French man discovers 5 dead babies hidden in boxes in his home after argument with wife: prosecutors A husband in France found five decomposing babies in cardboard boxes after arguing with his wife, who had given birth at home to a baby boy the day before. Rebecca Papin, an American mother, details the terrifying experience of being trapped with her two young children amidst raging wildfires in Southwest France, which have already forced over 220,000 people to evacuate. Papin recounts the fire's sudden onset and her family's struggle for basic resources. Aman in Francediscovered remains believed to belong to five newborns hidden inside cardboard boxes in his home after his partner gave birth at home and was taken to a hospital, according to prosecutors. He became distressed after he found out about her pregnancy at ⁠a very late stage, despite her repeated denials, and began searching their home, prosecutors said. The couple already had two children, ages 8 and 9. The woman, 32, who was not identified, was allegedly arguing with her husband over what was in the boxes at their home in the town of Orange on Monday after she gave birth at home to a baby boy the day before. She started complaining about abdominal pain during the argument on Monday. She was taken to a hospital and her husband stayed behind and discovered the dead babies hidden in the boxes. NEWBORN VANISHED AFTER SECRET BIRTH, PARENTS ALLEGEDLY CLAIMED BABY 'WAS A PRANK': COPS A man in France discovered five deceased babies inside cardboard boxes in his home after he and his wife had a fight.(Thibaud MORITZ / AFP) The man, also 32, then notified authorities through the hospital ​where the woman was being treated for pain. ""The husband stayed behind when she was taken","Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:55:15 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/french-man-discovers-5-dead-babies-hidden-boxes-home-after-argument-wife-prosecutors,2026-08-03 01:31:20
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Iran inmates sew lips shut in mass hunger strike at notorious US-sanctioned jail: report,Iran inmates sew lips shut in mass hunger strike at notorious US-sanctioned jail: report,"Iran inmates sew lips shut in mass hunger strike at notorious US-sanctioned jail: report Over 1,000 inmates at Ghezel Hesar Prison enter a third week of hunger strike against Iran&apos;s executions, with some sewing their lips shut in protest. Fox News correspondent Greg Palkot reports that Iran's repression of its people has worsened, with nearly 50 executions in the past three months and 6,000 arbitrary detentions. Hadi Ghaemi, Director of the Center for Human Rights in Iran, describes the regime's actions as unchecked, making normal life impossible for dissidents. More than 1,000 death-row inmates held in a unit ofIran’sGhezel Hesar Prison have entered a third week of a mass hunger strike to protest regime executions, with some prisoners sewing their lips shut in protest, according to reports. The escalating demonstration at the U.S.-sanctionedGhezel Hesar Prisonin Karaj near Tehran, also highlights growing international concern over the Islamic Republic's reliance on capital punishment, particularly for drug-related offenses. According to theHuman Rights Activists News Agency(HRANA), the hunger strike started on July 13, after six inmates were transferred to solitary confinement ahead of possible executions. Other Iranian human rights groups said the prisoners had been convicted of drug-related offenses. WHO IS AHMAD VAHIDI? IRAN’S NEW IRGC CHIEF TIED TO GLOBAL ATTACKS AND ‘DEATH TO AMERICA’ IDEOLOGY State executions went up under Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian.(Nooses: Photo by Loredana Sangiuliano/SOPA Images/LightRocket via Getty Images, President of Iran: Photo by Iranian Presidency/Anadolu via Getty Images) Reportsalso indicate that the striking prisoners have been chanting ""No to Execution"" and takin","Tue, 28 Jul 2026 22:08:47 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/iran-inmates-sew-lips-shut-mass-hunger-strike-notorious-us-sanctioned-jail-report,2026-08-03 01:31:21
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'We'll See How It Goes': Trump Says US-Iran Talks to Begin On Monday After Shelving Planned Strike,'We'll See How It Goes': Trump Says US-Iran Talks to Begin On Monday After Shelving Planned Strike,"'We'll See How It Goes': Trump Says US-Iran Talks to Begin On Monday After Shelving Planned Strike Trump further indicated that an agreement could be reached regarding the management of the Strait of Hormuz, while asserting that an accord would be established concerning the denuclearisation of Iran. Washington:US President Donald Trump stated that negotiations with Iran, expected to take place through intermediaries, are scheduled to commence on Monday. Speaking to reporters on board Air Force One, Trump confirmed that discussion channels were active. ""We are talking to them [the Iranians] in the form of a negotiation; it begins tomorrow afternoon, and we'll see how it goes. I'd love to do that. It'll save a lot of lives, a lot of unnecessary power, to be honest with you. We are ready to go whenever we want. Would I rather make a deal? I'm not looking to kill people, because a lot of people die; we don't want that. So they asked us, Iran specifically, but the other three, they asked us,"" Trump said. The US President revealed that diplomatic engagements involving Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Qatar and Iran led him to halt what was originally planned as a ""massive attack"" on Friday. Trump further indicated that an agreement could be reached regarding the management of the Strait of Hormuz, while asserting that an accord would be established concerning the denuclearisation of Iran. The sudden turn towards diplomacy comes as mediators race to reactivate a dynamic framework between Washington and Tehran. According to Israeli media reports on Sunday, regional intermediaries are attempting to revive a memorandum of understanding signed last month to ensure the strategic waterway remains open, fee-free, for 60 days. Iranian state media similarly indicated that discuss","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 06:46:53 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/we-ll-see-how-it-goes-trump-says-us-iran-talks-to-begin-monday-after-shelving-planned-strike-2026-08-03-133887,2026-08-03 01:31:21
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Crude Oil Falls Sharply To $80 After Trump Halts New US Strikes On Iran,Crude Oil Falls Sharply To $80 After Trump Halts New US Strikes On Iran,"Crude Oil Falls Sharply To $80 After Trump Halts New US Strikes On Iran Oil prices fell 5% to $80.79 after Trump said that US strikes on Iran would pause and a Middle East deal was near, easing Gulf shipping fears, though crude remains 20% above pre-conflict levels. New York:Oil prices fell sharply Sunday after President Donald Trump said he would order U.S. forces to hold off on new strikes against Iran, claiming that a deal to end the fighting in the Middle East was near. A resolution to the conflict, which has lasted more than five months, could give oil shippers the ability to send vessels out of the Persian Gulf, where tankers of oil and other products have been trapped during the fighting. The price of U.S. crude oil fell 5% to $80.79 per barrel Sunday night. The price of Brent crude, the international standard, fell 5% to $83.87 per barrel. Oil prices have been swinging widely since the U.S. and Israel launched attacks on Iran in late February, pushing past $100 per barrel multiple times during the spring. As the conflict continued, high oil prices seeped into the cost of gasoline, jet fuel and many other products that are delivered using diesel. Motorists have paid more at the pump and customers shelled out more for airfare due to higher jet fuel costs. In some countries, fuel supplies ran low, leading to rationing and sporadic closures of schools and government offices. Meanwhile, oil and gas companies amassed huge profits in the spring due to the high oil, gasoline and diesel prices that resulted when petroleum shippers couldn't get through the critical Strait of Hormuz, a narrow waterway that borders Iran, due to the fighting. Prices for U.S. crude oil on Sunday night remained about 20% higher than before the conflict began.","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 05:10:49 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/crude-oil-falls-sharply-to-80-after-trump-halts-new-us-strikes-on-iran-2026-08-02-133884,2026-08-03 01:31:21
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,At Least 14 Dead as Suicide Bomber Targets Police Gate Near Swat Peace Rally Gathering in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa,At Least 14 Dead as Suicide Bomber Targets Police Gate Near Swat Peace Rally Gathering in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa,"At Least 14 Dead as Suicide Bomber Targets Police Gate Near Swat Peace Rally Gathering in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa At least 14 people were killed and dozens injured in a suicide bombing near a police station during a peace rally in Pakistan's Swat district. At least 14 people, including five police officers and four civilians, were killed on Sunday after a suicide bomber detonated explosives near a police station close to the venue of a peace rally in Pakistan's northwestern Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province. The attack left over two dozen others injured. The explosion occurred in the Swat district as the Swat Peace Rally was concluding near the Kabal Police Station. Demonstrators had gathered in Kabal town to demand peace and denounce local militancy. According to police reports, the suicide bomber attempted to breach the main entrance of the police station but was intercepted by an officer at the gate. The attacker then set off the explosives, killing both nearby civilians who were participating in the rally and police personnel on duty. District Police Officer Muhammad Umar confirmed the incident, while district police chief Omar Khan noted that at least five police officers were among the dead. The attack struck as participants marched near the facility while chanting anti-militant slogans. Videos circulating on social media showed hundreds of people taking part in the rally shortly before the blast. Moments later, footage captured scenes of panic as thick smoke billowed into the air and crowds ran for cover. Subsequent visuals revealed damaged vehicles, debris scattered across the road, and emergency responders evacuating the wounded in ambulances as local bystanders stepped in to help. Rescue teams and security forces quickly ru","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:22:50 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/at-least-14-dead-as-suicide-bomber-targets-police-gate-near-swat-peace-rally-gathering-in-khyber-pakhtunkhwa-2026-08-02-133882,2026-08-03 01:31:21
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"PPP Flags Polling Delays, Code Violations During PoJK Assembly Elections","PPP Flags Polling Delays, Code Violations During PoJK Assembly Elections","PPP Flags Polling Delays, Code Violations During PoJK Assembly Elections The PPP called on the Election Commission to immediately stop the alleged illegal activity, seize the ballot papers in question, remove the government employee from polling agent duties, investigate both allegations and initiate legal proceedings against those found responsible. Muzaffarabad:Pakistan Peoples Party (PPP) Pakistan-occupied Jammu and Kashmir (PoJK) election cell in-charge Sardar Abdul Shakoor alleged delays in polling and reported electoral irregularities across several constituencies during voting for the PoJK Legislative Assembly, while the Election Commission deferred polling in LA-27 Muzaffarabad-I because of heavy rainfall and landslides. According to Shakoor, polling in LA-28 was delayed as polling personnel had not arrived at 71 polling stations by the scheduled opening time. He said a large number of voters were forced to wait, preventing them from exercising their right to vote. He urged the PoJK Election Commission, district administration and other concerned authorities to immediately deploy polling staff so that voting could commence without any further delay, according to The Express Tribune (TET). In LA-29, Shakoor stated that polling personnel had failed to reach the majority of polling stations by the scheduled time, resulting in a delayed start to voting. He said the absence of polling staff was denying voters the opportunity to cast their ballots and could undermine the transparency and timely conduct of the election process. He called on the Election Commission and district authorities to ensure the prompt deployment of the remaining polling staff, TET reported. Separately, the PoJK Election Commission announced that polling in LA-27 Muzaffarabad-I had been postponed after heavy rain and landslides made it impossible ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:04:23 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/ppp-flags-polling-delays-code-violations-during-pojk-assembly-elections-2026-08-02-133872,2026-08-03 01:31:23
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'Don't Think Iran Has Ever Faced President Like Trump': US Secretary of State Marco Rubio,'Don't Think Iran Has Ever Faced President Like Trump': US Secretary of State Marco Rubio,"'Don't Think Iran Has Ever Faced President Like Trump': US Secretary of State Marco Rubio US Secretary of State Marco Rubio praised President Trump's direct strategy towards Iran, noting a significant shift from past approaches that allowed Tehran to evade accountability. Rubio claimed that US military actions have greatly diminished Iran's defensive capabilities, stripping it of its protective &quot;conventional shield.&quot; Washington:US Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Saturday (local time) praised President Donald Trump's decisive strategy against Tehran, stating that the Iranian regime has never encountered an American leader who acts with such directness. Speaking in an interview with Fox News, Rubio reflected on Washington's approach to the Islamic Republic and highlighted a sharp shift from past precedent, asserting that Tehran can no longer rely on usual tactics to evade consequences. ""I don't think the Iranian regime has ever faced a President like Trump, which is somebody that actually takes action,"" Rubio said. ""They got used to, for 20-30 years -- not just the U.S., but the broader world -- allowing them to get away with things like lying, breaking deals."" Detailing the impact of recent military actions, Rubio stated that US strikes have ""severely degraded"" Iran's defensive capabilities, claiming that the regime has lost the conventional shield it once relied on for protection. ""They still have missiles and they still have drones, and they can still do damage,"" Rubio acknowledged. He emphasised, however, that Iran no longer possesses the ""conventional shield that they were going to hide behind."" He asserted this as the reason why Iran now appears eager to negotiate deals regarding denuclearisation and the Strait of Hormuz, emphasising that Washington is dealing from a position of absolute strength. ""And that's changed the whole dynamic. It's the only reason why they are now willing a","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 10:24:08 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/don-t-think-iran-has-ever-faced-president-like-trump-us-secretary-of-state-marco-rubio-2026-08-02-133864,2026-08-03 01:31:23
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'Adventurous': Iran Warns Against Further US Attacks In Talks With Pakistan and Turkey,'Adventurous': Iran Warns Against Further US Attacks In Talks With Pakistan and Turkey,"'Adventurous': Iran Warns Against Further US Attacks In Talks With Pakistan and Turkey During his discussion with the Saudi foreign minister, Araghchi stated that any assault by the US or Israel, or involvement by regional nations in such operations, would meet a &quot;proportionate response&quot; from Tehran. Washington DC:Iran on Saturday cautioned the United States against any ""adventurous action"", declaring that it would respond decisively should American forces launch fresh strikes on Iranian targets, thereby heightening tensions across the Middle East. The warning followed remarks by US President Donald Trump on Friday, in which he said he was losing faith in talks with Tehran and threatened additional attacks, stating the US would be ""hitting them"" if required. Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi delivered the message in separate telephone conversations with Pakistan Army chief Asim Munir, Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan and Saudi Foreign Minister Prince Faisal bin Farhan. According to Araghchi's Telegram account, he informed the Pakistani and Turkish officials that Iran would respond decisively to any ""aggression"" and reviewed the implications of what he termed destabilising moves by the US, along with the rising threat of regional instability. During his discussion with the Saudi foreign minister, Araghchi stated that any assault by the US or Israel, or involvement by regional nations in such operations, would meet a ""proportionate response"" from Tehran. The warnings were issued hours after Kuwait's army reported that it had intercepted and destroyed hostile drones launched by Iran against several critical sites. Falling debris damaged a government building in northern Kuwait and civilian property on Bubiyan Island, though no injuries were reported. Separately, a ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 09:26:26 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/adventurous-iran-warns-against-further-us-attacks-in-talks-with-pakistan-and-turkey-2026-08-02-133861,2026-08-03 01:31:23
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Tourist Plane Crash Over Peru's Nazca Lines, 13 Killed","Tourist Plane Crash Over Peru's Nazca Lines, 13 Killed","Tourist Plane Crash Over Peru's Nazca Lines, 13 Killed A small tourist plane crashed near the Nazca Lines in Peru on Saturday, killing 13 people. The Cessna, operated by Aerodiana, had 11 foreign tourists and two crew members onboard. It reported an emergency and lost contact before crashing and catching fire. Lima:A small tourist plane crashed on Saturday as it flew over ​the Nazca Lines archaeological site in southern Peru, killing 13 people, Peru's government ‌said. Peru's Ministry of Transport and Communications said in a statement that the plane was carrying 11 foreign tourists - German, Italian and Spanish visitors - and two crew members. The Ministry said the plane crashed in the area ​of Socos, approximately 6 km (4 miles) from the city of Nazca and roughly 19 km (12 miles) from ​the Nazca Lines site. The small plane, a Cessna Caravan C-208 aircraft, belonged ⁠to the local Peruvian airline Aerodiana and had taken off from the Pisco Airport at ​roughly 12:10 p.m. local time. At approximately 1:00 p.m. local time the crew reported an emergency situation ​to the control tower at Nazca airport, after which all radio contact was lost, the Ministry of Transport said in a statement. After crashing, the plane caught fire, making any rescue impossible, according to ​Peruvian broadcaster RPP. Firefighters and municipal police officers were dispatched to extinguish the fire ​and carry out initial rescue efforts. Footage shared on social media showed the smoking wreckage of what appeared ‌to ⁠be a small plane on arid plains. Reuters was unable to independently verify the footage.The cause of the crash is unknown and the government said it is investigating the incident. Aerodiana said in a statement that it ""will assess its flight schedule in accordance with the ​directives of the relev","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 07:24:37 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/thirteen-die-in-tourist-plane-crash-over-peru-s-nazca-lines-2026-08-02-133858,2026-08-03 01:31:24
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Trump Says Mideast Allies Have Reached Outlines of Deal to End Iran War, Says US to Stop New Strikes","Trump Says Mideast Allies Have Reached Outlines of Deal to End Iran War, Says US to Stop New Strikes","Trump Says Mideast Allies Have Reached Outlines of Deal to End Iran War, Says US to Stop New Strikes US President Trump announced on social media that Mideast allies have made progress on a deal to end the Iran war and he will pause new military strikes for now. The deal aims to open the Hormuz Strait and eliminate Iran's nuclear threat. Washington:President Donald Trump in a Saturday evening social media post claimed that Mideast allies have reached the parameters of a deal to end the Iran war and said that he would hold off on ordering new strikes in the five-month old conflict for now. Trump added that the emerging deal “would include the Immediate, Complete, and Total OPENING OF THE HORMUZ STRAIT, and an end to Iran’s nuclear threat.” “Based on this request, I have agreed, for the future benefit of the WORLD and, likewise, the survival of a successful and prosperous Iran, to cancel the attack, subject to being able to rapidly make a DEAL,” Trump said. He added that Israel has agreed to join the U.S. in the commitment to try to complete the agreement with Iran that would bring about an end to the war. Earlier Saturday, Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, the kingdom’s de facto leader, in a phone call with Trump raised concerns about the U.S. potentially escalating the conflict with Iran, according to a person familiar with the leaders’ discussion. The discussion, which was first reported on by the news outlet Axios, came as Trump weighed whether to carry out new strikes on Iran. The Saudis, according to the person briefed on the substance of the call but not authorized to comment publicly, are concerned that if the U.S. targets Iran’s energy infrastructure or carries out massive strikes on other key infrastructure that Tehran could respond by carrying out attacks on the kingdom’s and other Gulf countri","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 08:22:17 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-says-mideast-allies-have-reached-outlines-of-deal-to-end-iran-war-says-us-to-stop-new-strikes-2026-08-02-133859,2026-08-03 01:31:25
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Three Dead After Shooting at Fast Food Restaurant in Southern Idaho,Three Dead After Shooting at Fast Food Restaurant in Southern Idaho,"Three Dead After Shooting at Fast Food Restaurant in Southern Idaho A shooting at an In-N-Out Burger in southern Idaho resulted in multiple deaths and injuries. The shooter is also deceased, but their identity and motive are still unknown. Eyewitnesses reported chaotic scenes with gunfire and people fleeing for safety. Boise:A shooting at an In-N-Out Burger restaurant in southern Idaho on Saturday afternoon left multiple people dead and others injured, police said. The shooter was among the dead, Twin Falls Police Chief Matthew Hicks said in a news conference. Police were still trying to determine the shooter’s identity and motive. “We believe the threat to the community is over,” Hicks said. He added that he did not yet know exactly how many were killed or wounded, and officials were still in the process of notifying next of kin. “It was a very chaotic scene.” Before the news conference, Twin Falls County Commissioner Brent Reinke said Sheriff Jack Johnson had told him five people were hurt. Lane Koehn, 34, said he was at a stoplight near the In-N-Out when he saw a person with an AR-style rifle emerge from the drive-thru. A man with a pistol started firing at the shooter. He then saw someone in an In-N-Out uniform drag a person, also uniformed, bleeding from a gunshot wound in her chest across the parking lot. The employee, Koehn and the man with the pistol stayed until paramedics arrived for her. “She was pretty bad off, but I don’t know. I hope she made it,” Koehn said. Koehn said he was told by police to evacuate because the shooting was still active. He also said the shooter fired at least three or four rounds and it was not clear whether or not anyone in particular was targeted. Video taken by a driver from across the street captured a shooter, who appeared to be dressed in black, wal","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 07:06:23 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/three-dead-after-shooting-at-fast-food-restaurant-in-southern-idaho-2026-08-02-133857,2026-08-03 01:31:26
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Iran Warns Of Retaliation: Plan To Target Saudi, UAE, Qatar Oil And Gas Facilities If US Strikes","Iran Warns Of Retaliation: Plan To Target Saudi, UAE, Qatar Oil And Gas Facilities If US Strikes","Iran Warns Of Retaliation: Plan To Target Saudi, UAE, Qatar Oil And Gas Facilities If US Strikes Iran threatened to target key Middle East energy sites including Saudi Arabia's Ghawar and Qatar's Ras Laffan, if the US or Israel strikes, as Trump weighs attacks on Iranian infrastructure. Tehran:Iran has issued a threat of retaliation following reports indicating that US President Donald Trump is considering launching attacks against Iranian energy infrastructure, according to Iran's state-affiliated Tasnim News Agency. The news agency reported that Tehran has devised a comprehensive blueprint to target crucial energy facilities across the Middle East should the United States or Israel carry out fresh strikes. The warning comes as a US official told Axios that Trump is seriously contemplating strikes on Iranian energy targets, though no final decision has been taken. As per Tasnim News, the Iranian plan is designed to disrupt the oil and gas infrastructure of the Middle East if new attacks are carried out by the US or Israel. The reported target list features Saudi Arabia's Ghawar oil field, which accounts for over 5 per cent of global oil supply, alongside the Abqaiq and Khurais facilities, which produce more than 7 million barrels of oil per day. In the United Arab Emirates, the facilities named in the report include the Zakum oil field and the Ruways refinery, which has a processing capacity of over one million barrels per day. Iran's reported list also encompasses Qatar's North Field and Ras Laffan, which together account for approximately 20 per cent of global liquefied natural gas (LNG) trade. Other sites cited in the report include Kuwait's Burgan oil field, which produces roughly two million barrels per day, Bahrain's Sitrah refinery and Al-Mihaj, as w","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 03:58:36 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/iran-warns-of-retaliation-plan-to-target-saudi-uae-qatar-oil-and-gas-facilities-if-us-strikes-2026-08-01-133856,2026-08-03 01:31:26
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Moscow Explosion: 3 Killed, 21 Injured Near Stalin Skyscraper Restaurant Terrace","Moscow Explosion: 3 Killed, 21 Injured Near Stalin Skyscraper Restaurant Terrace","Moscow Explosion: 3 Killed, 21 Injured Near Stalin Skyscraper Restaurant Terrace At least 3 people were killed and 21 injured in an explosion near a Moscow restaurant terrace at Kudrinskaya Square on Saturday evening, with the security forces taking over the investigation to ascertain the cause. Moscow:A homemade bomb detonated during a private function at an upscale dining venue in central Moscow on Saturday, resulting in three fatalities, including the female suspect carrying the explosive, and leaving 21 others wounded, CNN reported, citing statements from Russia's National Anti-Terrorism Committee provided to state news agency RIA Novosti. According to the committee, an unidentified woman tried to gain access to Balzi Rossi restaurant on Kudrinskaya Square while in possession of what security officials assessed was an improvised explosive device. The device detonated prematurely outside the premises, killing both the security guard who intercepted her and a restaurant patron. Law enforcement agencies have not yet established the identity of the woman or determined the motive behind the attack. It remains unconfirmed whether the suspect intentionally triggered the detonation. The blast occurred at approximately 8:10 p.m. local time (1:10 p.m. ET) adjacent to an outdoor terrace at Building 1 on Kudrinskaya Square, situated just outside the entrance to Balzi Rossi, as reported by Russian state news agency TASS, citing the Main Directorate of the Ministry of Internal Affairs. The establishment was closed to the general public at the time of the explosion to accommodate a private banquet, according to details posted on its official website. In the aftermath of the explosion, an investigative task force, alongside emergency response personnel, immediately secured the a","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 02:49:13 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/moscow-explosion-3-killed-15-injured-near-stalin-skyscraper-restaurant-terrace-2026-08-01-133854,2026-08-03 01:31:26
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,US Urges Citizens To Leave Middle East As Trump Vows To Hit Iran 'Very Hard',US Urges Citizens To Leave Middle East As Trump Vows To Hit Iran 'Very Hard',"US Urges Citizens To Leave Middle East As Trump Vows To Hit Iran 'Very Hard' The US urged Americans to leave the Middle East as Trump vowed to hit Iran &quot;very hard&quot; amid drone strikes in Kuwait, tanker attacks near Hormuz, and escalating Israel-Gaza-Lebanon fighting. Washington:The US Department of State has advised American citizens to consider departing the Middle East or prepare to leave if the security situation deteriorates, following US President Donald Trump's vow to hit Iran ""very hard"" amid escalating regional hostilities involving drone strikes in Kuwait and fresh shipping incidents near the Strait of Hormuz. The expanding conflict also reached Gaza and Lebanon, where Israeli forces carried out new strikes despite Hamas declaring its readiness to disarm under a US-backed ceasefire framework. Addressing reporters during a Cabinet meeting at the Camp David presidential retreat, Trump indicated that Washington was prepared for an extended military campaign against Iran. ""We just want to win,"" Trump said, adding that the US would hit Iran ""very hard"" until ""they can't take it anymore."" Hours later, White House Press Secretary Karoline Leavitt accused Tehran of breaching last month's memorandum of understanding that had temporarily halted hostilities. ""Iran signed a memorandum of understanding with the United States and then broke it, fired at commercial ships and killed American soldiers,"" Leavitt said. ""President Trump is not going to stand by and allow this terrorist behaviour to occur."" She stated that Iran would continue to ""pay"" until it returned to negotiations ""in what President Trump deems a meaningful way."" Kuwait's armed forces stated they intercepted and destroyed hostile drones entering the nation's airspace from dawn, c","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 03:10:02 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/us-urges-citizens-to-leave-middle-east-as-trump-vows-to-hit-iran-very-hard-2026-08-01-133855,2026-08-03 01:31:27
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Famed Climber Nirmal Purja, Nine Others, Die in Avalanche in Pakistan, Hiking Company Says","Famed Climber Nirmal Purja, Nine Others, Die in Avalanche in Pakistan, Hiking Company Says","Famed Climber Nirmal Purja, Nine Others, Die in Avalanche in Pakistan, Hiking Company Says Purja set a record for the ‌fastest ascent of the world's 14 highest mountains and became widely known internationally ​after the Netflix documentary chronicling his journey &quot;14 ​Peaks: ⁠Nothing Is Impossible&quot; was released two years later. Kathmandu:Celebrated Nepali climber ​Nirmal Purja, who set a record for the ‌fastest ascent of the world's 14 highest mountains, died in an avalanche during an expedition in Pakistan, his company ​said on Saturday. “Today it is with profound ​sadness and immense heartbreak that we confirm that ⁠Nirmal 'Nimsdai' Purja tragically lost his life following the ​avalanche on Broad Peak,” his expedition organising company ​Elite Exped said in an Instagram post. “We have also received confirmation that other members of the expedition sadly did not ​survive,” it added, without giving details. Purja, 43, and ​nine others had been missing since Thursday after being struck by ‌an ⁠avalanche on the 8,051-metre (26,414-foot) Broad Peak, the world's 12th highest mountain, a technically difficult climb in Pakistan's Gilgit-Baltistan region. Purja, who served with British special forces ​as a ​Gurkha, completed the ⁠record-breaking feat in six months in 2019. He became widely known internationally ​after the Netflix documentary chronicling his journey ""14 ​Peaks: ⁠Nothing Is Impossible"" was released two years later. The 10 mountaineers were caught in an avalanche around midday on ⁠Thursday. ​Six of the 10 climbers ​were Nepalis and the others were from Pakistan, Oman, the U.S. ​and China.","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 18:58:59 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/famed-climber-nirmal-purja-nine-others-die-in-avalanche-in-pakistan-hiking-company-says-2026-08-01-133847,2026-08-03 01:31:28
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"'Kind of Madness': Iran Vows to Target US, Israeli Energy Assets if Attacked as Trump Weighs Fresh Strikes","'Kind of Madness': Iran Vows to Target US, Israeli Energy Assets if Attacked as Trump Weighs Fresh Strikes","'Kind of Madness': Iran Vows to Target US, Israeli Energy Assets if Attacked as Trump Weighs Fresh Strikes The Iranian official added that the nation's armed forces had evidenced their capability and resolve to carry out such operations during the 40-day war and subsequent engagements. Tehran:Iran has warned that it stands fully prepared to target key Israeli infrastructure and American energy installations throughout the region should it come under attack, following reports that Washington and Tel Aviv may be coordinating new military operations against the Islamic Republic. A senior Iranian security official told Tasnim News Agency on Friday that Western media reports regarding prospective strikes on Iranian infrastructure represented ""a kind of madness"". According to Tasnim, the official stated that Tehran has formulated comprehensive retaliatory strategies encompassing strikes on critical installations in Israel and US energy assets across the Middle East, asserting that Iran maintains complete readiness to execute these measures if provoked. The Iranian official added that the nation's armed forces had evidenced their capability and resolve to carry out such operations during the 40-day war and subsequent engagements. The warning follows heightened speculation surrounding potential military escalation after reports indicated that US President Donald Trump had ordered preparations for renewed strikes on Iranian targets. The Wall Street Journal reported on Friday, citing US officials, that President Trump had directed fresh strikes that could commence as early as this weekend, while issuing a warning to Tehran that it would face substantial military measures unless it re-entered negotiations. Addressing a Cabinet meeting at Camp David on Friday, Presiden","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 10:03:08 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/kind-of-madness-iran-vows-to-target-us-israeli-energy-assets-if-attacked-as-trump-weighs-fresh-strikes-2026-08-01-133820,2026-08-03 01:31:28
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Spain Says Migrants Are Returning from Ceuta After 57 Die in Border Rush,Spain Says Migrants Are Returning from Ceuta After 57 Die in Border Rush,"Spain Says Migrants Are Returning from Ceuta After 57 Die in Border Rush Reuters at the enclave's border saw Moroccan police in riot gear using tear gas to disperse some of the people amassed near the fences. Water cannon trucks were deployed, and the charred remains of a bus and ​seven cars could be seen from clashes with the crowds. Ceuta:Spain said on Friday it had reversed a huge rush of migrants into a Spanish enclave in North Africa, with most of the more than 50,000 people who had crossed the border by land and sea ​already heading back voluntarily. The Spanish government's representative in Ceuta said 57 bodies had been recovered on the Spanish side of the border and that there could be additional casualties on the Moroccan side. ‌It said some drowned and some were crushed while trying to climb the breakwater that holds the border fence. Spain's Interior Ministry said around 50,000 people had crossed the border since Thursday morning, and estimated that 48,300 had returned by 6 p.m. (1600 GMT) on Friday. Juan Jesus Vivas, head of Ceuta's local government, said as many as 60,000 people had pushed across over the past couple of days. Moroccan forces beat back crowds with batons and tear gas at the gates to Ceuta, trying to prevent more from entering the tiny Spanish territory that juts on ​a spit of sandy land into the Mediterranean from Morocco. The rush at the border caused division in Europe, where leaders of other EU states called on Spain to ensure the incident was contained. Italy said it ​was suspending the European Union's border-free Schengen arrangements with Spain, a measure set to affect people travelling by plane or boat between the two countries. Madrid said the move violated ⁠EU treaties. Reuters at the enclave's border saw Moroccan police in riot gear using tear gas to disperse some o","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 13:39:14 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/spain-says-migrants-are-returning-from-ceuta-after-57-die-in-border-rush-2026-08-01-133834,2026-08-03 01:31:28
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'Closely Monitoring': India on US Bill Seeking Upto 100% Tariffs On Russian Oil Buyers,'Closely Monitoring': India on US Bill Seeking Upto 100% Tariffs On Russian Oil Buyers,"'Closely Monitoring': India on US Bill Seeking Upto 100% Tariffs On Russian Oil Buyers Reaffirming India's strategic approach towards fulfilling its domestic power and fuel requirements, the spokesperson emphasised that national interest remains the core pillar of the country's energy policy. New Delhi:India is keeping a close watch on a US bill that empowers Washington to impose tariffs of up to 100 per cent on nations purchasing Russian oil and gas, the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) said on Friday, days after the proposed legislation cleared the US Senate. Addressing the weekly media briefing in the national capital, MEA spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal stated that New Delhi is tracking the progress of the measure in Washington. ""We are closely monitoring the developments,"" Jaiswal said. Reaffirming India's strategic approach towards fulfilling its domestic power and fuel requirements, the spokesperson emphasised that national interest remains the core pillar of the country's energy policy. ""On energy security, our position has been clarified and very well articulated on several occasions. It is something which is predicated on our national priorities and on securing the energy needs of our 1.4 billion people through diversified sources, which includes the US,"" he said. Jaiswal further highlighted that New Delhi maintains continuous dialogue with key official channels across the Atlantic regarding the proposed measures. ""We remain engaged with relevant stakeholders in the US at various levels on this particular matter,"" he said. The official response follows the US Senate passing the Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act of 2026 with a decisive 86-12 vote, paving the way for the measure to be taken up by the House of Representatives for further legislative review. If","Sat, 01 Aug 2026 07:35:29 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/closely-monitoring-india-on-us-bill-seeking-upto-100-tariffs-on-russian-oil-buyers-2026-08-01-133813,2026-08-03 01:31:28
