Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,Hungary shut its only nuclear plant for the first time in 44 years,Hungary shut its only nuclear plant for the first time in 44 years,"Hungary shut its only nuclear plant for the first time in 44 years <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132809525.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />Hungary's sole nuclear facility has been offline due to unprecedentedly low levels of the Danube River. This shutdown exacerbates power shortages amid a fierce summer heatwave, prompting the government to urge both households and businesses to conserve energy. Consequently, Hungary must depend on costly electricity imports from neighboring countries, highlighting the fragility of energy systems in the face of severe weather changes. At TOI World Desk, our dedicated team of seasoned journalists and passionate writers tirelessly sifts through the vast tapestry of global events to bring you the latest news and diverse perspectives round the clock. With an unwavering commitment to accuracy, depth, and timeliness, we strive to keep you informed about the ever-evolving world, delivering a nuanced understanding of international affairs to our readers. Join us on a journey across continents as we unravel the stories that shape our interconnected world.Read More",2026-08-02T21:41:53+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/hungary-shut-its-only-nuclear-plant-for-the-first-time-in-44-years-after-the-danube-fell-too-low-to-cool-its-reactors-nearly-half-its-electricity-supply-is-now-affected/articleshow/132809525.cms,2026-08-03 01:31:34
Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,"9,000 discarded Christmas trees help restore New Orleans wetlands","9,000 discarded Christmas trees help restore New Orleans wetlands","9,000 discarded Christmas trees help restore New Orleans wetlands <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132807056.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />New Orleans is giving used Christmas trees a second life by dropping them into coastal marshes to help slow land loss. The bundled trees trap sediment, reduce wave energy and support marsh grass growth. Scientists say the method helps restore wetlands in selected areas but is only one part of Louisiana's broader coastal protection efforts. At TOI World Desk, our dedicated team of seasoned journalists and passionate writers tirelessly sifts through the vast tapestry of global events to bring you the latest news and diverse perspectives round the clock. With an unwavering commitment to accuracy, depth, and timeliness, we strive to keep you informed about the ever-evolving world, delivering a nuanced understanding of international affairs to our readers. Join us on a journey across continents as we unravel the stories that shape our interconnected world.Read More",2026-08-02T21:00:00+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-orleans-collected-9000-discarded-christmas-trees-and-airlifted-them-into-coastal-wetlands-the-programme-has-restored-marsh-equal-to-nearly-200-football-fields/articleshow/132807056.cms,2026-08-03 01:31:34
Times of India,India (Mainstream),en,Ex-nurse revives baby who stopped breathing during Arizona post-office visit,Ex-nurse revives baby who stopped breathing during Arizona post-office visit,"Ex-nurse revives baby who stopped breathing during Arizona post-office visit <img align=""left"" border=""0"" hspace=""10"" src=""https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132809175.cms"" style=""margin-top: 3px; margin-right: 5px;"" />A former nurse's quick actions saved an infant's life at an Arizona post office. Mary Schwarz performed CPR and airway clearing on baby Nova who stopped breathing. Police Lieutenant Shari Aguilar then transported the infant to a nearby clinic for immediate medical attention. Nova, who had prior heart issues, began breathing again during the car ride. This incident highlights the critical importance of CPR training in everyday situations. At TOI World Desk, our dedicated team of seasoned journalists and passionate writers tirelessly sifts through the vast tapestry of global events to bring you the latest news and diverse perspectives round the clock. With an unwavering commitment to accuracy, depth, and timeliness, we strive to keep you informed about the ever-evolving world, delivering a nuanced understanding of international affairs to our readers. Join us on a journey across continents as we unravel the stories that shape our interconnected world.Read More",2026-08-02T21:05:44+05:30,https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arizona-baby-stopped-breathing-during-a-post-office-visit-former-nurse-mary-schwarz-performed-cpr-and-helped-restore-her-breathing-on-the-way-to-hospital/articleshow/132809175.cms,2026-08-03 01:31:34
