Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Sheikh Hasina may detail ‘homecoming’ plans, her visions for Bangladesh at presser in India on August 5","Sheikh Hasina may detail ‘homecoming’ plans, her visions for Bangladesh at presser in India on August 5","Sheikh Hasina may detail ‘homecoming’ plans, her visions for Bangladesh at presser in India on August 5 A 78-year-old Sheikh Hasina is set to address the virtual news conference at the Foreign Correspondents’ Club in the evening on August 5, event organisers said. Former Bangladesh prime minister Sheikh Hasina is expected to detail her plans to return home at her first virtual interaction with the media in New Delhi on Wednesday, exactly two years after she fled Dhaka following the fall of her government. Hasinahas lived in self-exile in India since she left Bangladesh on August 5, 2024, when the Awami League regime dramatically collapsed in the face of massive student-led protests. Her plans to virtually address the media are unlikely to go down well with the Bangladesh Nationalist Party (BNP) government, which has sought her extradition. The deposed 78-year-old is set to address the virtual news conference at the Foreign Correspondents’ Club in the evening on August 5, when she will “announce her homecoming and outline her vision for Bangladesh”, according to the organisers of the event. ALSO READ |No change in India's stance, clarifies MEA as Hasina plans return to Bangladesh The event will also feature an address by Hasina’s son Sajeeb Wazed Joy, and other Awami League leaders such as former education Mohibul Hasan Chowdhury Nowfel and former cricketer and MP Shakib Al Hasan. Mahammad Ali Siddique, general secretary of Bangladesh Human Rights Watch, Shah Mohammad Bakhtiar, director of Bangladesh Human Rights Watch USA, security analyst Aminul Hoque Polash, and counter-terrorism analyst Abu Obaidha Arin are also expected to join the event. Some of them will participate in person and others will appear virtually. ALSO READ |'Sheikh H","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 06:44:43 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/sheikh-hasina-return-to-bangladesh-homecoming-plans-vision-dhaka-press-conference-india-new-delhi-august-5-101785718948095.html,2026-08-03 01:31:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Twin Falls PD issues emotional statement after Idaho In-N-Out shooting, ‘Yesterday challenged our department in ways…’","Twin Falls PD issues emotional statement after Idaho In-N-Out shooting, ‘Yesterday challenged our department in ways…’","Twin Falls PD issues emotional statement after Idaho In-N-Out shooting, ‘Yesterday challenged our department in ways…’ The Twin Falls Police Department shared an emotional statement, thanking those who helped them deal with a deadly mass shooting at an In-N-Out in Idaho. The Twin Falls Police Department shared an emotional statement on Facebook, thanking those who helped them deal with a deadly mass shooting at anIn-N-Outin Idaho.The gunmanwas identified asChad Williams, 24, who killed himself with a self-inflicted gunshot wound, Twin Falls Police Chief Matthew Hicks said at a press conference Sunday, August 2. “Yesterday challenged our department in ways that no agency hopes to face. Today, we were reminded that we never face those challenges alone. We extend our heartfelt thanks to the officer from the Nampa Police Department, Caldwell Police Department, Meridian Police Department - Idaho and Idaho State Police who answered the call and helped patrol our streets today,” the Twin Falls Police Department wrote on Facebook. It added, “While we may wear different uniforms, we serve as one. In moments like these, badges, patches, and agency names take a back seat to our shared commitment to protecting our communities. We are one team with one mission. To our community, thank you. Your thoughts, kindness, and support have meant more than words can express. We are grateful to serve a community that stands with us.” Also Read |Who is Jordan Salinas? 5 things to know about the 'hero' bystander who confronted Idaho shooter Chad Williams Police have now confirmed that the three people who died did not include the shooter. Including Williams, four people lost their lives. Williams appeared to be armed with an AR-style rifle. He opened fire at the resta","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 06:44:43 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/twin-falls-pd-issues-emotional-statement-after-idaho-in-n-out-shooting-yesterday-challenged-our-department-in-ways-101785719294700.html,2026-08-03 01:31:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Twin Falls, Idaho shooting death toll: Was Chad Williams among 3 killed? Police provide ‘most accurate information’","Twin Falls, Idaho shooting death toll: Was Chad Williams among 3 killed? Police provide ‘most accurate information’","Twin Falls, Idaho shooting death toll: Was Chad Williams among 3 killed? Police provide ‘most accurate information’ The Twin Falls Police Department has shared an update on the death toll and victims following a deadly mass shooting at an In-N-Out in Idaho. The Twin Falls Police Department has shared an update on the death toll following a deadly mass shooting at anIn-N-Outin Idaho. The gunman was identified asChad Williams, 24, who killed himself with a self-inflicted gunshot wound, Twin Falls Police Chief Matthew Hicks said at a press conference Sunday, August 2. Police have now confirmed that the three people who died did not include the shooter. Including Williams, four people lost their lives. “The Twin Falls Police Department is providing an update on the tragic shooting that occurred Saturday, August 1, 2026, near In-N-Out. Our priority is to provide the most accurate information available, correct misinformation, and direct victims, families, witnesses, and community members to the proper resources,” the Twin Falls Police Department wrote on Facebook. “Our thoughts are with the victims, their families, and everyone impacted. We understand the fear, grief, and concern this has caused in our community.” Also Read |Twin Falls In-N-Out mass shooting: Gov. Brad Little under fire for saying Idaho is ‘one of the safest places live’ “At approximately 2:29 p.m., the Twin Falls City Communications Center received 911 calls reporting shots fired. Officers, along with local, state, and federal law enforcement partners, responded. The Twin Falls Fire Department and Magic Valley Paramedics also responded, provided aid, and transported victims,” the post added. At this time, the police department can confirm: “These numbers are prelimi","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 06:22:51 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/twin-falls-idaho-shooting-death-toll-was-chad-williams-among-3-killed-police-provide-most-accurate-information-101785718077029.html,2026-08-03 01:31:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Naked man jumps from Brooklyn Bridge after affixing multiple flags, miraculously survives; wild video surfaces","Naked man jumps from Brooklyn Bridge after affixing multiple flags, miraculously survives; wild video surfaces","Naked man jumps from Brooklyn Bridge after affixing multiple flags, miraculously survives; wild video surfaces A 44-year-old naked man jumped off the top of the Brooklyn Bridge Sunday afternoon and survived as onlookers watched in horror. A 44-year-old naked man jumped off the top of theBrooklyn BridgeSunday afternoon, August 2, the New York Post reported. Shockedonlookerswatched as the man jumped and miraculously survived, a shocking video shows. “Images from the Brooklyn bridge just moments Ago, a guy jumped out of the top after getting naked,”an X user wrote, sharing the video. Police sources said that the man erected several flags at the top of the bridge and “took off clothing” after scaling the north tower on the Manhattan side of the bridge around 2:30 pm, the outlet reported. Also Read |Haunting posts NY mom wrote before jumping to death at Niagara Falls with 2 kids revealed, ‘I want my family back’ The NYPD’s Emergency Services Unit tried to convince the man to come down. However, he jumped. Harbor Unit cops ultimately rescued him from the East River. The man was rushed to NYC Health+Hospitals Bellevue, where he was listed in stable condition. It remains unclear what was written on the flags. A few weeks ago, New York police rescued a woman who climbed onto the Brooklyn Bridge and threatened to jump, according toNYPDCommissioner Jessica Tisch. Body camera videoshared on social mediashowed members of the NYPD Emergency Services Unit climbing atop the bridge talking to the woman for almost an hour as they waited for a chance to safely pull her back from the edge. Also Read |Woman jumps into Niagara Falls days after New York mom and her 2 kids' fatal leap “This video of a rescue last night on the Brookly","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 05:34:11 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/naked-man-jumps-from-brooklyn-bridge-after-affixing-multiple-flags-miraculously-survives-wild-video-surfaces-101785714922194.html,2026-08-03 01:31:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Portland fire: Videos show blaze at vacant warehouse on Naito Parkway, smoke visible across downtown","Portland fire: Videos show blaze at vacant warehouse on Naito Parkway, smoke visible across downtown","Portland fire: Videos show blaze at vacant warehouse on Naito Parkway, smoke visible across downtown A large fire tore through the abandoned Centennial Mills warehouse in downtown Portland, sending heavy brown smoke across the city as crews fought it. A largefireerupted at the Centennial Mills warehouse on Naito Parkway in downtown Portland,Oregonon Sunday afternoon. The blaze tore through the abandoned structure that has been standing at the heart of downtown Portland for ages, sparking a massive response by the Portland Fire Department. ThePortland Fire Department saidin a post on social media that they are responding at the location on Naito parkway near Fremont Bridge. The department said that there is a ""heavy fire"" on the first floor which is now extending into the second floor. ""Thus is an unsafe building meaning no interior firefighting activity will occur,"" the department said. ""Only exterior defensive actions."" The smoke was seen by residents across Portland as the Fire Department also confirmed that ""significant brown smoke is pushing out under pressure on all sides."" Also read:Who was Chad Williams? Idaho Twin Falls shooting suspect identified Residents shared videos of the incident on social media. In a follow-up update, the Portland Fire Department said that there is a threat that the fire might spread to the other structures on the compound of the Centennial Mills building. They added that they are making special arrangements tolimit the spreadof the fire. Here's another set of videos of the incident recorded from up close. It was shared on social media by a resident. Here's another video of the incident recorded by a resident while driving from a highway near the site of the fire. Alongside structural damag","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 05:04:55 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/portland-fire-videos-downtown-show-blaze-at-vacant-centennial-mills-warehouse-on-naito-parkway-smoke-visible-101785713372806.html,2026-08-03 01:31:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Bryan Kohberger's own defense expert now wants him on death row,Bryan Kohberger's own defense expert now wants him on death row,"Bryan Kohberger's own defense expert now wants him on death row Bryan Kohberger is seeking a new trial, claiming his defense attorneys misled him into pleading guilty. Bryan Kohberger, who is serving fourlife sentenceswithout parole for the murders of four University ofIdahostudents, is seeking to withdraw his guilty plea through a post-conviction petition. If successful, the case could go back to trial and the death penalty could once again be an option. Sy Ray, a formerArizonahomicide investigator and digital forensics expert hired by Kohberger's defense team, has said investigators missed damning evidence against him. ""Bring back the death penalty. I am all for this,"" Ray told journalistBrian Entinon a podcast. Ray claimed Kohberger's smartphone data is far more incriminating than what was previously revealed. “I 100% believe that the offender, who is Bryan Kohberger- there's no alternative theory in my head at this point. I 100% believe he's been in the house before,” he said. He also claimed the data shows repeated ""collisions"" between Kohberger's phone and victim Madison Mogen's phone, adding, “I believe Maddie was the target.” However, Ray's recent statements appear to contradict his own expert report from January 2025. In that report, he wrote, ""It is my opinion that the geolocation data I have been provided as of the writing this report does not provide any evidence of association between Mr. Kohberger and any of the decedents and/or Mr. Kohberger's or decedent's residence,"" according toFox News. He had also written, “I am unable to locate any period of time between June 23, 2022 and November 13, 2022 where Mr. Kohberger's mobile d","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 03:07:00 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/bryan-kohbergers-own-defense-expert-now-wants-him-on-death-row-101785695967295.html,2026-08-03 01:31:41
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Chad Williams motive: What we know so far as police say Idaho Twin Falls mass shooting suspect 'acted alone',Chad Williams motive: What we know so far as police say Idaho Twin Falls mass shooting suspect 'acted alone',"Chad Williams motive: What we know so far as police say Idaho Twin Falls mass shooting suspect 'acted alone' Twin Falls police identified 24-year-old Chad Williams as the suspect in Saturday's mass shooting Police said he acted alone; motive remains under probe. On Sunday afternoon, amid a slew of misinformation about the deceased suspect of the Twin Falls, Idahomass shooting, authorities identified him as 24-year-oldChad Williams. Twin Falls Police Chief Matthew Hicks said at a press conference confirmed that Williams ""acted alone."" The mass shooting took place at an In-N-Out restaurant in Twin Falls, in Idaho's Magic Valley region, on Saturday afternoon around 2:29pm MDT. Three people were killed, and at least seven others were injured. Even as the suspect's identity is out, questions over his background and motive behind the shooting remain. The Twin Falls Police Department has not confirmed the motive, saying that it is under investigation. Chad Williams' family is also cooperating in the investigation, the police said. Chief Hicks added that the detectives are investigating the case and the unidentified parents have a huge role to play in the probe. It was not immediately clear from the press conference if 24-year-old Chad Williams was from Idaho. Also read:Idaho Twin Falls shooting: Viral videos show man engaging shooter with pistol; internet hails 'Jordan Salinas' as ‘hero’ TheFBIis also investigating Saturday afternoon's mass shooting. On Sunday, the agency requested bystanders and witnesses to share videos of the incident to aid in the investigation. Police Chief Matthew Hicks said at Sunday's press conference that Chad Williams was confronted by an active-duty state trooper and an armed citizen, identified in some reports a","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 02:53:27 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/chad-williams-motive-what-we-know-so-far-as-police-say-idaho-twin-falls-mass-shooting-suspect-acted-alone-101785693333818.html,2026-08-03 01:31:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Trump frequently announces he's halting strikes in Iran. But they keep happening,Trump frequently announces he's halting strikes in Iran. But they keep happening,"Trump frequently announces he's halting strikes in Iran. But they keep happening Trump frequently announces he's halting strikes in Iran. But they keep happening TEL AVIV, Israel — PresidentDonald Trumpsaid late Saturday that he would halt new planned attacks on Iran pending renewed talks towind down the warand revive stalled cargo traffic through theStrait of Hormuz. It was the latest in a pattern of announcements the U.S. president has made to first threaten massive strikes and then later call them off. The abrupt shifts have been a defining feature of the five-month conflict that hassent prices of oil and basic goods soaring— and the announcements to date have been upended by renewed attacks days or even hours afterward. Here is a look at some of Trump’s past major announcements about pausing strikes against Iran: The United States and Iranagree to a two-week ceasefireto end the intense fighting that began on Feb. 28with Israeli and U.S. attacks. Trump makes the announcement less than two hours before adeadline he had setfor Tehran to capitulate or faceattackson bridges and power plants — strikes he said would mean “a whole civilization will die.” Trump announces that the U.S. isindefinitely extending its ceasefirewith Iran a day before it was to expire. He adds that he has been asked by mediators to hold off on attacks to give Iranian leaders time to come up with additional proposals. The fragile ceasefire lastsuntil May 8, when the U.S. carried out strikes on Iranian tankers. After a weekend of dire threats against Iran,Trump says he is holding offon a major planned military strike because “serious negotiations” were underway. “T","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 01:40:12 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/trump-frequently-announces-he-s-halting-strikes-in-iran-but-they-keep-happening-101785701412805.html,2026-08-03 01:31:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Who was Chad Williams? Idaho Twin Falls shooting suspect identified,Who was Chad Williams? Idaho Twin Falls shooting suspect identified,"Who was Chad Williams? Idaho Twin Falls shooting suspect identified In a statement posted on social media early Sunday, In-N-Out owner Lynsi Snyder confirmed that one of the victims was an employee. Chad Williams, 24, has been identified as the suspect in Saturday’s mass shooting at an In-N-Out Burger in Twin Falls, Idaho, that left at least three people dead and seven others injured. Authorities confirmed during a Sunday press conference that Williams died from a self-inflicted gunshot wound after the attack. Authorities are confident he acted alone. Twin FallsPolice Chief Matthew Hicks said investigators are still working to determine a motive. ""Investigators are continuing to investigate the timeline, process evidence, and conduct interviews,” Hicks said. “The Williams family has been notified and they are fully cooperating with law enforcement. Their hearts are also broken during this time."" Hicks said an off-duty Idaho State Police trooper and a civilian returned fire on the suspect, helping end the attack. Victim identities were not released pending family notifications. Also Read:Idaho Twin Falls shooting: Viral videos show man engaging shooter with pistol; internet hails 'Jordan Salinas' as ‘hero’ In a statement posted on social media early Sunday, In-N-Out owner Lynsi Snyder confirmed that one of the victims was an employee. “My heart is broken, my chest is heavy, my eyes burn from the tears I've shed. We lost one of our beautiful Associates tonight,” Snyder said. “In-N-Out will be mourning with the families and praying for them as they tread through a very painful season.” Also Read:Twin Falls In-N-Out mass shooting: Gov. Brad Little under fire for saying Idaho","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 01:36:57 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/who-was-chad-williams-idaho-twin-falls-shooting-suspect-identified-101785700320374.html,2026-08-03 01:31:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Peru probes crash of tourist plane that killed 13,Peru probes crash of tourist plane that killed 13,"Peru probes crash of tourist plane that killed 13 Peru probes crash of tourist plane that killed 13 Peruvian authorities said Sunday they are investigating the crash of a small plane carrying tourists to view the famous Nazca Lines, which killed all 13 people on board. Seven Italians, two Germans and two Spaniards died, along with two Peruvian crew members, when their Cessna 208 Caravan aircraft crashed Saturday after it took off from the airport in Pisco, located about 240 kilometers south of the capital Lima. A grim recovery process carried on overnight, with police placing charred bodies in black bags for transport to the regional morgue. Once procedures at the crash site are completed, the investigation will be carried out ""in coordination with the relevant authorities to determine the causes of this tragic plane crash,"" the Public Prosecutor's Office said in a statement. Due to the condition in which the bodies were recovered, ""DNA tests will be conducted, which will allow for the scientific identification of the victims so their remains can be returned to their families."" It remained unclear why the plane went down, although Foreign Trade Minister Rogers Valencia told reporters that ""the pilot reported mechanical problems before the crash,"" adding it has yet to be determined whether there was an engine failure. ""The plane exploded, apparently as a result of the impact; it did not explode beforehand,"" said Carlos Cordero of the Transportation Ministry's aviation accident investigation commission. Early Sunday Italy's Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni offered her ""deepest c","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 01:16:56 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/peru-probes-crash-of-tourist-plane-that-killed-13-101785700017103.html,2026-08-03 01:31:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Eastern Washington fires have burned 600 structures and forced the evacuation of 5,000 homes","Eastern Washington fires have burned 600 structures and forced the evacuation of 5,000 homes","Eastern Washington fires have burned 600 structures and forced the evacuation of 5,000 homes Eastern Washington fires have burned 600 structures and forced the evacuation of 5,000 homes About 5,000 homes have been evacuated and about 600 homes, businesses and other buildings have been destroyed by wildfires that remained uncontained Sundayin eastern Washington state,authorities said. The fires burned more than 8.2 square miles around Spokane, the second largest city in Washington, and were among dozens across the western U.S. — stretching the ability of federal, state and local agencies to fight them. No deaths have yet been reported from the fires in the Spokane area. Meanwhile, crews using bulldozers and helicopters continued for the 10th day to fight a fire that has burned nearly 525 square miles of grassland in western Idaho and eastern Oregon. The area is home to cattle ranches, and authorities said the fire is threatening more than 600 homes and 800 other structures. The weather in the area was expected to remain sunny — and dry — well into the week, with temperatures rising to more than 90 degrees Fahrenheit on Wednesday. Officials say the fire was caused by lightning. The National Weather Service issued warnings about the air quality in eastern Washington, eastern Oregon, western and central Idaho and western Montana. It issued red flag fire warnings for parts of Utah and Montana and western Nebraska, and extreme heat warnings for the southern parts of Arizona, California and Nevada and northern Montana. While the high temperature Sunday in Spokane was forecast to remain below 80 F , wind gusts from 35 mph to 45 mph were expected later in the day, sa","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:58:41 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/eastern-washington-fires-have-burned-600-structures-and-forced-the-evacuation-of-5-000-homes-101785698922156.html,2026-08-03 01:31:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Hundreds flee Ethiopia's Tigray into Sudan after border fighting,Hundreds flee Ethiopia's Tigray into Sudan after border fighting,"Hundreds flee Ethiopia's Tigray into Sudan after border fighting Hundreds flee Ethiopia's Tigray into Sudan after border fighting Hundreds of Ethiopians from the northern Tigray region have crossed into neighbouring Sudan over the past two days, fleeing fighting near the border, Sudanese security and medical sources told AFP. The influx comes as Sudan itself remains engulfed in a brutal war between the army and the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces , which erupted in April 2023. A member of the Tigray People's Liberation Front said clashes involving heavy artillery and drones between the Ethiopian army and Tigray rebels broke out in the western Tigray area of Shererina, near the Sudanese border, early on Saturday and continued until around 5:00 pm . A Sudanese security source in the border town of Hamdayet said arrivals from Tigray included wounded fighters. A medical source at a border health centre said the injured received first aid before being transferred to al-Hashaba, 15 kilometres inside Sudan and home to thousands displaced by the 2020-2022 war between the Ethiopian army and Tigray rebels. The security source said al-Hashaba, also known as Village 8, serves as an ""administrative hub"" for Army 70, a TPLF-affiliated armed unit whose fighters fled to Sudan during the Tigray war and later fought alongside the Sudanese army against the RSF. - Explosions - Residents on the Sudanese side of the border reported hearing explosions and sustained gunfire throughout the fighting. A witness in Wad al-Hulaywah, about 40 kilometres from the frontier, said three powerful explosions were heard on Saturday morni","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:56:40 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/hundreds-flee-ethiopia-s-tigray-into-sudan-after-border-fighting-101785698800630.html,2026-08-03 01:31:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Retirement healthcare could cost $185,500 even with Medicare: How to prepare","Retirement healthcare could cost $185,500 even with Medicare: How to prepare","Retirement healthcare could cost $185,500 even with Medicare: How to prepare Retirement healthcare could cost $185,500 even with Medicare. Learn how to plan for medical costs, insurance, long-term care and rising healthcare expenses. Retirement does not mean your expenses suddenly disappear. Regular bills are still a huge part of your monthly expenditure even if you are someone who is healthy, has already paid off your home and does not plan to travel much. As a retiree, groceries, utilities, insurance, clothing, transportation and other everyday needs are still a drag. The bare minimum need to retire in today’s economy is still $1 million or more, considering all the above needs and a possible health fiasco even withMedicare. A recent Fidelity study estimated that a 65-year-old retiring in 2026 could spend about $185,500 on healthcare costs during retirement. This amount refers to healthcare expenses paid out of pocket and is part of the money a retiree may need during retirement. The Motley Fool said healthcare is difficult to avoid because medical expenses can continue throughout retirement. For someone who needs around $1 million or more to retire comfortably, healthcare could therefore take up a significant part of their retirement savings. Also read:Warren Buffett says most investors should buy an S&P 500 ETF. Here’s why he recommends it Having Medicare does not mean retirees will have all their healthcare bills covered. Seniors can still have to pay premiums, deductibles and co-pays even after enrolling in Medicare. Original Medicare also does not cover every type of medical service. If a service is not covered by Original Medicare and the retiree does not have additional insurance, they may have t","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:20:41 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/retirement-healthcare-could-cost-185-500-even-with-medicare-how-to-prepare-101785695058052.html,2026-08-03 01:31:42
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Hungary PM flags 'critical' days ahead with looming nuclear shutdown,Hungary PM flags 'critical' days ahead with looming nuclear shutdown,"Hungary PM flags 'critical' days ahead with looming nuclear shutdown EUROPE-WEATHER-HUNGARY:Hungary PM flags 'critical' days ahead with looming nuclear shutdown By Gergely Szakacs BUDEST, - Hungary faces a critical five days, Prime Minister Peter Magyar said on Sunday, as the drying out of the Danube forces the country's sole nuclear power plant to shut for the first time in over four decades, with a new heatwave looming. Large parts of Europe have been hit by prolonged heat and drought, lowering river levels and raising concerns about water supplies, river transport and power generation. As of 1837 GMT, Hungary's 2-gigawatt Paks power plant, which generates about half of the country's electricity, was running at just over 10% of its capacity after the Danube, whose waters it uses as a coolant, fell to a record low. The water authority was projecting that the level of the river, which flows from Germany to the Black Sea, would drop further in the coming days. PLANT COULD REMAIN IDLE FOR WEEKS ""We are facing the most critical five days ahead,"" Magyar said in a Facebook video. ""Tomorrow, the Paks power plant will not be generating, while the hottest, 40-degree days are ahead. ""The power grid, our public services and ourselves will all come under enormous strain,"" said Magyar, who has warned that Paks, which runs four Russian-built reactors, could remain idle for weeks. In a later video, he said the decision on when to shut down would be ""made by the plant's management observing a strict security protocol"". He said voluntary cuts in power usage by households and more than 300 companies, made after a government appeal, had reduced demand","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:12:16 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/hungary-pm-flags-critical-days-ahead-with-looming-nuclear-shutdown-101785696136999.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"In Ceuta, some migrants cling to hopes of someday reaching mainland Spain","In Ceuta, some migrants cling to hopes of someday reaching mainland Spain","In Ceuta, some migrants cling to hopes of someday reaching mainland Spain In Ceuta, some migrants cling to hopes of someday reaching mainland Spain CEUTA, Spain — Dikra, a 20-year-old migrant from Morocco, had spentfive days in Ceutaby Sunday after swimming tothe Spanish territorywith her younger sister and cousin. Since then, all her meals have come from local residents, and she isn't sure when her next one will come. Yet Dikra is certain she does not want to go back. “I want to stay. I want to go to Spain,” Dikra said, who asked that her last name be withheld for safety reasons. By Sunday afternoon, Dikra was among the last remaining migrants in the cityafter tens of thousandsof the 60,000 migrants that had breached the border with Morocco on Thursday and Friday walked back to that country. At least 72 people died in the crossing, and the humanitarian crisis the sudden rush of people caused reignited a debate around immigration in Europe and beyond. In Tangier, Dikra said she worked as a cleaner, but decided to leave alongside her sister and cousin, in part to escape her alcoholic father. She hopes to make use of a hairdressing diploma in continental Spain — from which she remains separated by the Strait of Gibraltar and the European Union's complex asylum system. Abdel Karim, 35, also from Morocco, waited outside Ceuta's official migration reception center on Sunday, asking for updates about what officials were saying they would do with the holdouts still in the city. Karim was unemployed in Morocco, and had lived in continental Spain years ago, before he was expelled from France where he was living on the streets. “I","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:06:09 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/in-ceuta-some-migrants-cling-to-hopes-of-someday-reaching-mainland-spain-101785695769701.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"14 dead as Ukraine, Russia exchange strikes: officials","14 dead as Ukraine, Russia exchange strikes: officials","14 dead as Ukraine, Russia exchange strikes: officials 14 dead as Ukraine, Russia exchange strikes: officials Ukrainian attacks on Russia killed at least nine people on Sunday, while Russian attacks on Ukraine killed at least five, according to officials in both countries. The exchange of strikes comes amid signs both Moscow and Kyiv are increasing the scale and intensity of attacks on each other, nearly four-and-a-half years into their grinding war. Civilian casualties in Ukraine have soared this year, as Russia has ramped up its use of hard-to-intercept long-range missiles, according to UN data. Kyiv has meanwhile launched waves of retaliatory strikes on Russia, including on energy facilities and retail warehouses, in an effort to pressure Moscow into negotiations on ending its offensive. Ukrainian strikes on Russia's Belgorod region bordering Ukraine killed four people earlier Sunday, including a 13-year-old girl near a playground, the region's acting governor Alexander Shuvaev said. ""The 13-year-old girl was gravely wounded. Medics who arrived at the scene took all possible measures to save her, but her injuries were not incompatible with life,"" he said. A separate drone attack on Russia's Saratov region bordering Kazakhstan killed two people, while three were killed in a Ukrainian drone strike on a car in Russia's Udmurtia region more than 1,000 kilometres from the front line, the region's acting governor Olga Abramova said. ""This act is monstrous in its senselessness. These people were definitely not a military target,"" she said. In Ukraine, Russian strikes killed two people in","Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:06:08 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/14-dead-as-ukraine-russia-exchange-strikes-officials-101785695769013.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Max Miller update: Bernie Moreno breaks silence, says ex-son-in-law ‘should not serve' as Congressman","Max Miller update: Bernie Moreno breaks silence, says ex-son-in-law ‘should not serve' as Congressman","Max Miller update: Bernie Moreno breaks silence, says ex-son-in-law ‘should not serve' as Congressman Sen Bernie Moreno has publicly slammed his former son-in-law, Rep Max Miller, saying he is unfit for Congress. RepublicanSenator Bernie Moreno has spoken out against his former son-in-law, RepresentativeMax Miller. Moreno, who has largely stayed quiet during the bitter custody battle between Miller and his daughter Emily, said in a long post that Miller ""fails"" basic standards of character needed to hold office and “should not serve in the House of Representatives.” Moreno also said Miller “needs serious psychological help,” adding, “He is a danger to my daughter, and I hold my breath every minute he has custody of my granddaughter.” Check his full statement: Despite the mounting pressure, Miller confirmed on Sunday that he will continue his re-election campaign ahead of Wednesday's deadline to replace him on the ballot. “I'm not dropping out of this race and I am winning in November,” Miller said, denying that he abused his ex-wife or daughter in his Sunday video. Check the full video: Also Read:Who is Max Miller's ex-wife Emily Moreno? Court filings detail abuse allegations; 'held a gun to her head' Theallegationshave put Miller's Republican colleagues in a difficult spot, especially after the GOP criticizedDemocratsover similar scandals involving Graham Platner and Eric Swalwell. Representative Anna Paulina Luna said she knows both Miller and Moreno personally and said, “I do not know Max to be a violent person and have only ever found him to be incredibly kind and honorable."" She added that she would ""not disparage Emily,"" saying, ""She comes from a wonderful family and Senator Mor","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 23:32:33 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/max-miller-update-bernie-moreno-breaks-silence-says-ex-son-in-law-should-not-serve-as-congressman-101785690594319.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Bay Bridge crash: Videos from San Francisco show cars overturned on I-80 as emergency crew respond,Bay Bridge crash: Videos from San Francisco show cars overturned on I-80 as emergency crew respond,"Bay Bridge crash: Videos from San Francisco show cars overturned on I-80 as emergency crew respond A crash on San Francisco-Oakland’s Bay Bridge closed part of the span Sunday, causing traffic delays. An overturned car was seen at the scene. Anaccidenton the Bay Bridge, which connectsSan Franciscoand Oakland, in California via Interstate 80, on Sunday afternoon affected traffic. Part of the bridge has been closed as emergency crews responded to the crash, affecting traffic in some lanes. As of now, officials have not confirmed the details of the accident or if anyone was injured. A driver, however, shared a video on X which showed a car overturned right in the middle of Bay Bridge, while two more had halted at the spot likely to check the situation. Also read:Jakob Butturff cause of death update: What happened to pro bowler who died at 32; fans mourn demise - ‘lost a good one’ Here's a video shared by Carlos Colindres on X. According to SFGate, the crash occurred on the westbound I-80 just off Treasure Island Road. An alert for severe traffic was issued by the California Highway Patrol before 9:15am PDT, the report confirmed. Also read:Kanan Fire erupts near Thousand Oaks and Westlake Village; smoke chokes Conejo Valley as residents share videos “Motorists are advised to expect delays and to use alternate routes to avoid the area,” the alert read. “There is no estimated time to reopen the roadway.” However, by 11:30am PDT, the area was cleared off and traffic on all lanes on the Bay Bridge was moving smoothly. The San Francisco-Oakland Bay Bridge carries about 260,000 vehicles a day across its two decks, according to official data. Shamik is a journalist covering the United States for Hindustan Times. He has more","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:54:42 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/bay-bridge-crash-videos-from-san-francisco-show-cars-overturned-on-i-80-as-emergency-crew-respond-101785690874165.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Mitch McConnell: Gov. Andy Beshear slams Rand Paul over Fancy Farms criticism as 'autopen' row continues,Mitch McConnell: Gov. Andy Beshear slams Rand Paul over Fancy Farms criticism as 'autopen' row continues,"Mitch McConnell: Gov. Andy Beshear slams Rand Paul over Fancy Farms criticism as 'autopen' row continues Rand Paul attacked Andy Beshear for missing Fancy Farm. Beshear hit back over Mitch McConnell’s alleged autopen signature on a disaster letter. On Saturday,KentuckyGovernor Andy Beshear was subject to a vicious attack from Senator Rand Paul over the former's absence from Fancy Farm: Kentucky's annual political picnic and fundraiser. Sen. Paul, a Republican Senator from Kentucky, took a dig at the Governor for missing the event. Speaking from the stage at the picnic, theRepublicanSenator said: ""If Andy Beshear is remembered, it will be for being neutered at every turn by the Republican legislature.” It did not sit well with Gov. Beshear, a Democrat who was not at the Fancy Farms Picnic because he was attending his son's final travel baseball tournament. Shortly after Paul's comments, Gov. Beshear took a dig at him bringing up the issue of Kentucky's GOP Senator Mitch McConnell, who has been absent from the US Senate since a June 12 fall. The senator signed a letter in July from Gov. Andy Beshear requesting that Donald Trump approve a request for a major disaster declaration in the state after the recent floods. Along with McConnell, the letter was signed by other Kentucky lawmakers, Rep. Andy Barr and Senator Rand Paul. But the signature of Mitch McConnell, who is currently undergoing rehab at the George Washington Hospital inWashington DC, raised allegations that it was done using an ""autopen"" by McConnell's chief of staff, Terry Carmack. An autopen is a machine that automatically reproduces a person's handwritten signature using a real pen. It's designed to make signatures look like they were written by hand, even t","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:37:34 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/mitch-mcconnell-gov-andy-beshear-slams-rand-paul-over-fancy-farms-criticism-as-autopen-row-continues-101785688321226.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"'There is an enemy within': Ceuta returns to normal after migrant crisis, but questions haunt locals","'There is an enemy within': Ceuta returns to normal after migrant crisis, but questions haunt locals","'There is an enemy within': Ceuta returns to normal after migrant crisis, but questions haunt locals A migrant crisis was triggered in Ceuta after 60,000 people flowed in from Morocco into the Spanish territory. Following a border security crisis as 60,000 migrants, mostly young men, from Morocco poured into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta, conditions have now mostly returned to normal in the city of 84,000 as most migrants have departed. Remnants of the incident and a political battle, however, still lingers in the air. The death toll from the crisis has already risen to 72, as five more bodies were discovered along the city's coast line, Reuters reported. The government, on its part, put up acontainment barrierto prevent entry along the sea route. Ceuta, a city of 84,000 which is generally known as a cultural hub with a mixed population of Christians, Jews, Hindus and Muslims living in relatively harmony, has now opened up an essential discussion overSpain's open border policy. As Spanish police personnel amped up their efforts to escort migrants out of the city, multiple shops were shut down in order to cut their supply to food. These shops are now gradually reopening as most of the influx crowd has headed back. Also Read IA ruling, a rumour, a rush: What happened before thousands crossed into Spain’s Ceuta enclave from Morocco Despite the chaos created by the situation, some residents choose not to place the blame on the migrant crowds. “It's not the young men's fault,” Mohamad Abdelkader Driss, 44, a waiter at a fried fish restaurant in town told AP. “If you open the border, of course everyone comes in, but the young men aren't to blame. The authorities are responsible.” ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 22:09:17 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/ceuta-morocco-africa-spain-eu-european-union-migrant-crisis-interior-ministry-sea-containment-barrier-101785682304629.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Blast in Pakistan's Khyber Pakhtunkhwa kills 14, dozens injured","Blast in Pakistan's Khyber Pakhtunkhwa kills 14, dozens injured","Blast in Pakistan's Khyber Pakhtunkhwa kills 14, dozens injured The blast occurred when the Swat Peace Rally was in progress in Kabal Town in the Swat district At least fourteen people were killed and over dozens were injured in an explosion during a peace rally inKhyber Pakhtunkhwaprovince in northwestPakistanon Sunday. The blast occurred when the Swat Peace Rally was in progress in Kabal Town in the Swat district, district officials quoted in the PTI report said. At least 14 people were killed, and dozens of others were injured in the blast, the Associated Press reported. “The attacker... detonated his explosive vest. A suicide bomber attempted to enter the police station located at the chowk (intersection), but was stopped by police at the main gate,” Swat's Deputy Inspector General of Police, Fida Hussain, told AFP. No group immediately claimed responsibility. Rescue teams shifted the wounded to nearby hospitals as police and other law enforcement agencies cordoned off the area, officials quoted by PTI said. Pakistan's interior minister,Mohsin Naqvi, condemned the attack, issuing a statement extending condolences to the families of those killed and prayers for the speedy recovery of the wounded. Pakistan has previously blamed such attacks in border provinces on militancy emanating fromAfghanistan. TheTaliban governmentin Kabul denies Afghan involvement. The Swat Peace Rally was organised by the Swat Aman Jirga (local tribal council), with participants raising slogans and carrying placards to demand peace in the area, which has seen a deterioration in security over the past few months. A military spokesman said on Friday that mil","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:51:53 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/death-toll-injured-in-a-blast-during-a-peace-rally-in-pakistan-khyber-pakhtunkhwa-101785683883283.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Forget gold and copper. Africa’s latest boom is in blueberries and oranges,Forget gold and copper. Africa’s latest boom is in blueberries and oranges,"Forget gold and copper. Africa’s latest boom is in blueberries and oranges A surge in fruit exports shows how high-value agriculture can spur industrialisation “IT’S A HIVE of activity,” says Alistair Campbell, observing the scene at his blueberry farm 40km outside of Harare, the capital of Zimbabwe. Hundreds of workers pick the fruit from the bushes, before carrying the bounty to a cold-storage facility. After sorting, the berries are flown to east Asia, where demand is high for the largest globules, or shipped to Europe for sale in major supermarkets. “We’re flat out,” says Mr Campbell. “We could sell our crop five or six times over.” For once the colour associated with a boom in Zimbabwe is blue,not gold. This year Zimbabwean growers expect to export 12,000 tonnes of blueberries, 40 times more than in 2017. “Every man and his dog is planting blueberries,” says one of the country’s most prominent bankers. The tiny fruit contains a deeper parable. Manufacturing has struggled in sub-Saharan Africa: its share of output has been more or less flat for 15 years. That worries analysts who thinkAfrican growthdepends on Asian-style, export-oriented factories. Yet high-tech farms are in effect mini-factories. They are labour-intensive and linked to global supply chains. This “industrialisation of freshness”, in the words of Christopher Cramer, an academic, could be a boon for Africa—and force a rethink of what is meant by farming and manufacturing. Africa’s economic history has left policymakers with an ambivalent view of agricultural exports. Under colonial rule many countries exported just a single crop, a model that remained after indepe","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:14:23 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/forget-gold-and-copper-africa-s-latest-boom-is-in-blueberries-and-oranges-101785681654281.html,2026-08-03 01:31:43
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,How Gen Z is driving ‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ toward $875 million,How Gen Z is driving ‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ toward $875 million,"How Gen Z is driving ‘Spider-Man: Brand New Day’ toward $875 million Spider Man Brand New Day eyes a $325 million opening as Tom Holland’s superhero movie draws Gen Z fans and gives Hollywood a major box office boost. Hollywood’s superhero boom has slowed sharply in recent years, but Spider-Man is showing that audiences can still turn up in huge numbers for the right superhero movie.Sony Picturessaid on Saturday that “Spider-Man: Brand New Day” was on track to collect at least $325 million at the North American box office from Thursday through Sunday. If that estimate holds, it would give the movie one of the biggest domestic openings in Hollywood history. The movie would rank second only to Disney’s “Avengers: Endgame,” which opened to $357 million in 2019, according to The New York Times. After adjusting for inflation, “Endgame” made about $467 million in today’s money. Analysts expected “Brand New Day” to make around $550 million from international markets. That would give the movie an estimated global opening of roughly $875 million. Sony spent an estimated $225 million to produce the PG-13 film, before adding the cost of marketing. That means the movie needs a massive audience not only to cover its production budget but also to make a major profit after marketing and theater splits. “Brand New Day” was especially popular with Generation Z, which includes people born between 1997 and 2012. That puts Gen Z viewers at roughly 14 to 29 years old today. The movie has several young stars who are already hugely popular with this generation, including Tom Holland, Zendaya and Sadie Sink. But the cast is not the only reason Gen Z is connecting with the movie. Greg Durkin, founder of entertainm","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:05:01 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/how-gen-z-is-driving-spider-man-brand-new-day-toward-875-million-101785680118515.html,2026-08-03 01:31:44
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Iran wants to charge for Hormuz, Houthis for the Red Sea: How straits around the world are governed","Iran wants to charge for Hormuz, Houthis for the Red Sea: How straits around the world are governed","Iran wants to charge for Hormuz, Houthis for the Red Sea: How straits around the world are governed The story of maritime chokepoints is centuries old — from a papal line down the Atlantic to Iran's toll at the Strait of Hormuz. History and the rules today Countries, the United Nations says, have argued over waters for as long as ships have sailed – perhaps from the time Egyptians first plied the Mediterranean in papyrus rafts. In 1493, the year after Christopher Columbus reached America, Pope Alexander VI attempted to settle one such quarrel between Spain and Portugal, the great maritime powers of the day, by drawing a line down the Atlantic. In a public decree called the papal bullinter caetera, he gave Spain everything west of that line and Portugal everything east of it. On that reckoning, the Pacific and the Gulf of Mexico became Spain's, and the South Atlantic and the Indian Ocean, Portugal's. A follow-on treaty between the two powers, signed at Tordesillas in 1494, shifted the line further west. Despite that neat 'solution', the disputes never really ended. In its war with the US and Israel, now in its sixth month, Iran has repeatedly staked claim to the Strait of Hormuz, launching missile and drone strikes against vessels that it says did not take its permission to cross the waterway. Tehran has also said it will restart charging ships that want to transit Hormuz for ""navigation, security and environmental services"". With much of the Gulf reliant on the strait for trade, Oman – the strait's other bordering country – made another pitch. A Western diplomat and a source said Oman has presented Iran with a plan – backed by other West Asian countries – to manage the strait and collect voluntary fees for using it, Reuters rep","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:13:09 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/ht-explainers/us-iran-war-west-asia-strait-of-hormuz-red-sea-bab-al-mandeb-how-waterways-are-operated-united-nations-rules-101785674953258.html,2026-08-03 01:31:44
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Two firefighting helicopters collide while battling Greece wildfire,Two firefighting helicopters collide while battling Greece wildfire,"Two firefighting helicopters collide while battling Greece wildfire ""Search and rescue teams were immediately mobilised to locate and assist the crews,"" the fire service said. Two firefighting helicopters collided while battling a wildfire in the Psatha area west of Greece's capital, Athens, on Sunday, with the fire department saying that a rescue operation has been launched to locate the crew. ""Search and rescue teams were immediately mobilised to locate and assist the crews,"" the fire service said. State broadcaster ERT reported that one crewmember had been found safe, while rescuers were searching for the second. Television footage showed one of the helicopters exploding and plunging to the ground in flames after an apparent rotor collision. The incident comes as Greece faced multiple fronts and a growing toll of damage, with wildfires believed to have devastated swathes of forest and agricultural land, and the prime minister warned of ""extremely difficult"" days ahead. Prime Minister Kyriakos Mitsotakis said Greece was experiencing ""extreme weather conditions"" with winds reaching 100 kilometres (60 miles) an hour. ""When the winds blow with such force, even the dozens of aircraft we have at our disposal cannot operate safely,"" he wrote on Facebook. ""There are moments when nature and the intensity of weather phenomena surpass any human planning and any operational capability,"" he added. Nearly 500 firefighters were battling blazes around the popular coastal village of Porto Germeno, some 70 kilometres northwest of Athens, the fire department said. They were attempting to keep the fire from approaching the western outskirts of Athens after it scale","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:07:46 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/two-firefighting-helicopters-collide-while-battling-greece-wildfire-death-toll-injuries-101785677799842.html,2026-08-03 01:31:44
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Carney lauds Hindu community’s contributions to Canada at Dhanteras gala,Carney lauds Hindu community’s contributions to Canada at Dhanteras gala,"Carney lauds Hindu community’s contributions to Canada at Dhanteras gala PM Mark Carney praised Canada's Hindu community for their contributions across various sectors at the CHCC’s Dhanteras gala in Calgary. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney has highlighted the significant contributions by the country’s Hindu community. Those remarks were made by the PM in a message extending greetings to the Canadian Hindu Chamber of Commerce (CHCC) as it held its annual Dhanteras gala. That event was held for the first time in the city of Calgary in the province of Alberta. In his message, Carney said, “Across Canada, Hindu Canadians have made significant contributions to the growth of our communities. Their impact can be seen across numerous sectors, including information technology, software development, healthcare, engineering, and public service. Through their innovation, leadership, and service, they have strengthened Canada’s social, cultural, and economic fabric.” He said the gala was a recognition of the “remarkable contributions of this vibrant community” and the “values, traditions, and spirit of service” of Canadian Hindus “continue to strengthen Canada’s diverse and inclusive society.” He commended the chamber for their work in supporting businesses and contributing to the Canadian economy. Welcoming CHCC members to Alberta, the province’s Premier Danielle Smith said, “Entrepreneurs and job creators like you supply the innovative spirit, resilience and resolve that help keep Alberta - and Canada - growing strong.” “Your success in business, commitment to giving back and dedication to preserving a vibrant cultural heritage help build a stronger and more prosperous Canada,” Leader o","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 17:57:38 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/carney-lauds-hindu-community-s-contributions-to-canada-at-dhanteras-gala-101785673658637.html,2026-08-03 01:31:44
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Moscow mayor calls deadly restaurant blast that left 3 dead a 'terrorist act',Moscow mayor calls deadly restaurant blast that left 3 dead a 'terrorist act',"Moscow mayor calls deadly restaurant blast that left 3 dead a 'terrorist act' According to officials, three people, including the suspected bomber, were killed and 21 others were injured. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin on Sunday called the deadly explosion at a restaurant in centralMoscowas a ""terrorist act"", a day after the blast killed three people and injured 21 others. ""Yesterday, a brutal terrorist act was committed in Moscow that claimed human lives. The victims are currently in the city's hospitals, where they are receiving all necessary care,"" Sobyanin wrote on social media, according to the Associated Press (AP). Also Read:3 killed, at least 21 injured after blast at Moscow restaurant, probe on The blast occurred on Saturday at a restaurant on Kudrinskaya Square, Russia's National Anti-Terrorism Committee said, as quoted by state news agency RIA Novosti. Authorities said the explosion is being treated as a bombing and an investigation is underway. According to Russian officials, three people, including the suspected bomber, were killed and 21 others were injured. The restaurant was not open to the public at the time of the explosion, as it was hosting a private banquet, according to information available on its official website. According to RIA Novosti, an unidentified woman allegedly attempted to carry an explosive device into the restaurant. A security guard stopped her from entering, following which the device detonated. The woman carrying the explosive, the security guard and a restaurant patron were killed in the blast, the state news agency reported, citing local officials. ""The attack was still being investigated,"" the Moscow Investigative Commi","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 17:42:10 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/moscow-mayor-calls-deadly-restaurant-blast-that-left-3-dead-a-terrorist-act-101785669929482.html,2026-08-03 01:31:44
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Renowned climber Nirmal Purja's body recovered from Broad Peak days after fatal avalanche,Renowned climber Nirmal Purja's body recovered from Broad Peak days after fatal avalanche,"Renowned climber Nirmal Purja's body recovered from Broad Peak days after fatal avalanche The ground team will bring the recovered bodies down to the Japanese camp. The body of renowned Nepalese-British climber Nirmal Purja was recovered by rescuers on Sunday, three days after he and nine other climbers were swept away in an avalanche on Broad Peak in Pakistan-occupied Kashmir's Gilgit-Baltistan. The mountain is the world's 12th-highest and is considered one of the most challenging peaks to climb. The Alpine Club of Pakistan (ACP) said the 43-year-old mountaineer's body was found at an altitude of around 5,700 metres, PTI news agency reported. “The ground rescue team has reached Nims Dai (Purja) at approximately 5,700m on Broad Peak -- a mountain he loved, and a mountain that has now taken him from us,” the club said in a post on social media, adding that three additional bodies were found at the altitude. The ground team will bring the recovered bodies down to the Japanese camp, ACP said, adding that rescue efforts continue under extremely difficult terrain conditions, PTI reported. The ACP said that apart from the mountain terrain, the risk of avalanches and steep slopes are also posing challenges to the rescue efforts. Helicopters cannot be deployed owing to rough weather conditions, it added. Also Read | 'Just before setting off for Broad Peak...': Nirmal Purja's final Instagram post before he was killed by an avalanche Purja was leading the expedition with nine other climbers – five from Nepal, one Pakistani, one Omani, one American and one Chinese. ACP general secretary Ayaz Shigri said a ground rescue team was transporting four bo","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 16:42:17 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/renowned-mountaineer-climber-nirmal-purjas-body-recovered-from-broad-peak-days-after-fatal-pakistan-avalanche-101785668948451.html,2026-08-03 01:31:44
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"After Trump's pause on strikes, Iran says it won't be 'caught off guard' or 'passive', vows to strengthen military","After Trump's pause on strikes, Iran says it won't be 'caught off guard' or 'passive', vows to strengthen military","After Trump's pause on strikes, Iran says it won't be 'caught off guard' or 'passive', vows to strengthen military Speaking to state media, Iran's acting Defence Minister Majid Ibn al-Reza said Tehran would not take any threats lightly. Iran said on Sunday that it views every threat from its adversaries as ""real and credible"" and will continue strengthening its military preparedness. This statement comes amid US President Donald Trump's announcement that Washington would hold off on fresh strikes to allow negotiations over Tehran's nuclear programme and the reopening of the Strait of Hormuz. Speaking to state media, Iran's acting defence minister Majid Ibn al-Reza said Tehran would not take any threats lightly, even if they were intended as psychological warfare, according to a Reuters report. ""We will neither be caught off guard nor remain passive,"" he said, adding that Iran would use such threats to increase its military readiness, strengthen deterrence and enhance its military capabilities. The remarks came after Trump announced that the United States would suspend plans for a fresh attack while diplomatic efforts continued. Also Read |Oil, gas fields in Saudi, Qatar, Israel among Iran's targets if US attacks Late on Saturday, Trump said the United States would refrain from launching another strike on Iran as long as a deal could be reached quickly to halt Tehran's nuclear ambitions and reopen the Strait of Hormuz. In a post on Truth Social, Trump said Iran and several Middle Eastern countries had requested time to finalise an agreement that would ensure the ""Immediate, Complete and Total"" reopening of the strategic waterway and ""an end to Iran's nuclear threat."" He did not identify the countries involved","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 15:56:43 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/after-trumps-pause-on-strikes-iran-says-it-wont-be-caught-off-guard-or-passive-vows-to-strengthen-military-101785659444723.html,2026-08-03 01:31:45
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Five dead, 41 missing in Indonesia ferry fire","Five dead, 41 missing in Indonesia ferry fire","Five dead, 41 missing in Indonesia ferry fire The captain reported the fire as the vessel sailed from Surabaya, Indonesia's second-largest city in East Java, to Makassar in South Sulawesi. Five people have been found dead, and 41 are missing after an Indonesian ferry with 271 people on board caught fire while at sea on Sunday, news agency AFP reported, citing search and rescue officials. The ferry was carrying 271 passengers and crew members, 225 of whom had been rescued, according to agency data on Sunday afternoon, Reuters reported. The captain reported the fire as the vessel sailed from Surabaya,Indonesia's second-largest city in East Java, to Makassar in South Sulawesi, according to Basarnas, the National Search and Rescue Agency. Nanang Sigit, head of the Surabaya Search and Rescue Office, said several nearby vessels had joined the rescue effort. ""TB Hasnur 26 and the British Mentor are assisting in evacuating passengers who jumped from KMP Mutiara Sentosa 2. Four vessels are now alongside the ferry,"" Nanang was quoted by Jakarta Global as saying. He added that the search-and-rescue vessel SAR 249 Permadi was en route to the scene but had an estimated travel time of about six hours. Videos circulating on social media appeared to show thick black smoke billowing from the upper decks as flames spread through the ferry. Passengers wearing life jackets could be seen gathered on one side of the vessel. HT has not immediately verified the authenticity of the footage. ""Based on preliminary reports from the field, passengers are waiting to be evacuated by the vessels in the vicinity of the incident site,"" said Muhammad Masyhud, a senior official at the Ministry of","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 15:09:10 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/death-toll-missing-in-indonesia-ferry-fire-rescue-east-java-makassar-south-sulawesi-101785663403470.html,2026-08-03 01:31:45
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Nolan Wells case update: Ex-FBI agent explains ‘redness’ on back of head as autopsy leaves family seeking answers,Nolan Wells case update: Ex-FBI agent explains ‘redness’ on back of head as autopsy leaves family seeking answers,"Nolan Wells case update: Ex-FBI agent explains ‘redness’ on back of head as autopsy leaves family seeking answers Nolan Wells' death has left his family seeking answers and an ex-FBI agent sought to explain the ‘redness’ at the back of his head seen in the private autopsy.&nbsp; Nolan Wells' family has been left seeking answers about the deadMississippiteen even as the state autopsy was completed. Wells, 18, had gone missing while out with friends on Horn Island, on July 4, and his body was found on July 6. While authorities did not find foul play in their initial assessment, the family launched their own investigation and ordered a private autopsy as well. The results of the same were shared by Wells' family attorney Ben Crump. Among the findings of the autopsy, one aspect stood out. There was a‘redness’ at the back of Wells' head. At the time, Dr. Roger Mitchell, who conducted the autopsy had said there was a red discoloration on the tissue at the back of Wells' head by the occipital bone. Also Read |Nolan Wells update: Friends launch GiveSendGo campaign to fight 'lies' and defamation lawsuits; 'This must stop' “It is important to reiterate that this finding could not have been observed in the first autopsy because the posterior head and neck dissections were not performed,” he noted. Now, former FBI agent Jennifer Coffindaffer has explained the reason behind the ‘redness’. Coffindaffer shared a set of photos, among which were diagrams of the back of Wells' head. “This is an autopsy head support. They are made of stainless steel. Nolan would have have his head resting on this for an extended period of time,” the former FBI agent noted, claiming it to be the likely reason behind the ‘redness’ observed. “The redness was described as redness, Not blun","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:57:30 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/nolan-wells-case-update-ex-fbi-agent-explains-redness-on-back-of-head-as-autopsy-leaves-family-seeking-answers-101785659937237.html,2026-08-03 01:31:45
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Want to work in Germany? Here's everything Indian professionals need to know before applying for visa,Want to work in Germany? Here's everything Indian professionals need to know before applying for visa,"Want to work in Germany? Here's everything Indian professionals need to know before applying for visa Germany attracts skilled Indian professionals, requiring a work visa and a job offer.&nbsp; Germany continues to attract skilled professionals from India as employers across sectors seek workers to fill labor shortages. For Indian citizens planning to take up employment in the European country, obtaining a German work visa is a mandatory step before relocating. Applicants must secure a job offer from a German employer before applying for a national employment visa. Those who do not yet have an offer may instead considerGermany's Opportunity Card (Chancenkarte), which allows eligible foreign nationals to enter the country and look for work. Indian applicants can submit their work visa applications through the German diplomatic mission responsible for their region. Also read:'I work till 2 am, still feel alone': NRI husband's viral post sparks debate on marriage and parenting Applications are accepted at the German Embassy inNew Delhiand the Consulates General in Bengaluru, Chennai, Kolkata and Mumbai. Depending on the jurisdiction, applicants may also be required to submit their applications through an authorized visa application center such as VFS Global. The embassy and consulates serve different states and Union Territories, with applicants required to apply only at the mission responsible for their place of residence. The application process begins after an applicant receives a job offer from an employer in Germany. Applicants must first book a visa appointment with the relevant German mission. Appointments can generally be scheduled up to six months in advance. ","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:27:15 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/want-to-work-in-germany-heres-everything-indian-professionals-need-to-know-before-applying-for-visa-101785658963373.html,2026-08-03 01:31:45
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Candace Owens questions FBI over ‘agents list’ during Charlie Kirk shooting, ‘Who were the first agents to arrive?’","Candace Owens questions FBI over ‘agents list’ during Charlie Kirk shooting, ‘Who were the first agents to arrive?’","Candace Owens questions FBI over ‘agents list’ during Charlie Kirk shooting, ‘Who were the first agents to arrive?’ In fresh questions raised about Charlie Kirk’s murder, Candace Owens asked whether authorities ever shared a list of which FBI agents were on the ground at UVU. In fresh questions raised about Charlie Kirk’s fatal shooting, Candace Owens asked whether authorities ever shared a list of which FBI agents were on the ground at Utah Valley University (UVU) on the day of the crime. Charlie, 31, was allegedly shot dead by Tyler Robinson on September 10, 2025, during an appearance at a campus event in Utah. The shooting happened around 12:20 pm local time during a student Q&A at UVU in Orem, per a statement from Utah Valley University (UVU). “Were we ever provided a list of which FBI agent were on the ground at UVU within 16 minutes of the explosive going off?” Candacewrote on X. “That’s actually a fascinating admission given the fact that the FBI office is located in Salt Lake City— a 45 minute drive away. What were the agents doing so close to UVU that day? Who were the first agents to arrive?” One user slammed Candace in the comment section,writing, “It took me two seconds of research. The FBI does not maintain a resident agency office directly in Orem. Their nearest local office is the Provo Resident Agency, which operates under the FBI Salt Lake City Field Office. This Provo satellite office is responsible for federal law enforcement coverage across Utah County.” Candace replied, “You realize that’s a tiny little shared office, with 4-8 employees max right? And that it’s 15 minutes away from UVU, fastest route? Are you suggesting this is the team that had secured UVU 16 minutes after the shot went off?” Candace recently sharedwhat she c","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 13:58:45 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/candace-owens-questions-fbi-over-agents-list-during-charlie-kirk-shooting-who-were-the-first-agents-to-arrive-101785656252185.html,2026-08-03 01:31:45
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Six months after Nancy Guthrie's kidnapping another Pima County woman goes missing, sparks worries: ‘What is going on?’","Six months after Nancy Guthrie's kidnapping another Pima County woman goes missing, sparks worries: ‘What is going on?’","Six months after Nancy Guthrie's kidnapping another Pima County woman goes missing, sparks worries: ‘What is going on?’ A woman named Debra E Esarey has gone missing from Pima County, six months after Nancy Guthrie's kidnapping, sparking worries among netizens.&nbsp; A woman named Debra E Esarey has gone missing from Pima County, six months afterNancy Guthrie's kidnapping. The 84-year-old mother of TODAY show host Savannah Guthrie was reported missing on February 1, and authorities believe she was taken from her Catania Foothills home near Tucson,Arizona, the night before. The Pima County Sheriff's Department, which is working the Nancy Guthrie case, also put out a notice about Esarey, who was last seen on July 29. They also shared a photo where Esarey could be seen in a blue striped tee-shirt with a black cap on her head. Here's what the PCSD had to say about the missing woman. The Pima County Sheriff's Department noted that Esarey was 66 and 5 feet 5 inches tall. She reportedly weighs 120 lbs and has blonde hair and hazel-colored eyes. She was last seen at 6225 W. Ajo Way. Also Read |Nancy Guthrie update: ‘Investigator’ slams Annie Guthrie, Tommaso Cioni's actions after kidnapping “Ms. Esarey may have a medical condition that affects her cognitive ability,” the notice from the cops further said. An elderly woman with an underlying condition reminded many of the Nancy Guthrie case. The octogenarian reportedly had a pacemaker, suffered from cardiac conditions and high blood pressure. Now, with the notice on Esarey, many rushed to seek updates in the Nancy Guthrie case, while others sought to find a pattern in these cases. Also Read |Nancy Guthrie update: Sheriff Nanos says search is ‘very active’ after ransom notes, vows ‘we are still her","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 13:29:25 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/six-months-after-nancy-guthries-kidnapping-another-pima-county-woman-goes-missing-sparks-worries-what-is-going-on-101785656368710.html,2026-08-03 01:31:45
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,All 10 climbers swept away in avalanche in Pakistan are confirmed dead,All 10 climbers swept away in avalanche in Pakistan are confirmed dead,"All 10 climbers swept away in avalanche in Pakistan are confirmed dead “The world has lost one of mountaineering's greatest climbers,” Nirmal Purja's company, Elite Exped, said in a statement. Renowned British-Nepali climber Nirmal Purja and nine other climbers swept away by an avalanche in Pakistan are confirmed to have died, and search teams were trying to recover their bodies, Purja's expedition company said Saturday. “The world has lost one of mountaineering's greatest climbers,” thecompany, Elite Exped, said in a statement, adding that all the lives lost were being mourned. “No words can ease the pain of this unimaginable loss.” The 10-member expedition was swept away by an avalanche Thursday on Pakistan’s Broad Peak. Also Read | 'Just before setting off for Pakistan...': Nirmal Purja's final Instagram post before he was killed by an avalanche Rescuers found four bodies and recovered three of them Friday in harsh weather that hampered flights by search and rescue helicopters. Rescuers backed by military helicopters had resumed a search earlier on Saturday for the others. “The loss of these courageous climbers, who came from different nations united by their passion for the mountains, is an immeasurable loss to the global mountaineering fraternity,” said Irfan Arshad Khan, the president of the Alpine Club of Pakistan. Khan paid tribute to the military and civilian rescuers and sherpas who took part in the search mission. “The mountains inspire us with their beauty, but they also remind us of the immense risks faced by those who venture into the high Himalaya and Karakoram,” he said. Earlier on Saturday, a local police official, Tahir Khan, said the remains of O","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 13:11:14 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/pakistan-avalanche-all-10-climbers-swept-away-confirmed-dead-nirmal-purja-alpine-club-elite-exped-101785655820529.html,2026-08-03 01:31:45
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Lynsi Snyder, In-N-Out president, pens emotional message after Twin Falls, Idaho shooting: ‘Lost one of our associates’","Lynsi Snyder, In-N-Out president, pens emotional message after Twin Falls, Idaho shooting: ‘Lost one of our associates’","Lynsi Snyder, In-N-Out president, pens emotional message after Twin Falls, Idaho shooting: ‘Lost one of our associates’ Lynsi Snyder, the In-N-Out president, penned an emotional message on social media after the deadly shooting at the Twin Falls outlet in Idaho.&nbsp; Lynsi Snyder, the In-N-Out president, penned an emotional message on social media after the deadly shooting at theTwin Falls outlet in Idaho. The incident on August 1 left many including the shooter dead. Snyder confirmed that one of the In-N-Out Associates was avictim of the shooting. The identity of the shooter and the motive has not been made public yet. However, videos emerged online showing alone gunmanengage the shooter with a pistol, and the internet hailed his heroics. Here's what the In-N-Out president said about the shooting. Snyder wrote “To my dear IN-N-OUT Family, Customers, and Friends and Family to both, My heart is broken, my chest is heavy, my eyes burn from the tears I've shed.” She added “We lost one of our beautiful Associates tonight. She was taking care of our most important asset - our Customers, and her life was taken by a disgusting human who doesn't value the lives of others or his own. He shot both on our property and off, and ended his life shortly after he took the precious lives of our Associate and Customers, innocent people who never saw it coming.” A post shared by Lynsi Snyder (@lynsi_snyder) Snyder noted the Associate was looking after customers when the gunman opened fire. “IN-N-OUT will be mourning with the families and praying for them as they tread through a very painful season,” Snyder added. Also Read |Twin Falls drive-by shooting: Gunfire erupts at Trotter Drive home; is it connected to Idaho In-N-Out shooting? “I am no stranger to lo","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:58:32 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/lynsi-snyder-in-n-out-president-pens-emotional-message-after-twin-falls-idaho-shooting-lost-one-of-our-associates-101785654614570.html,2026-08-03 01:31:46
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,Twin Falls drive-by shooting: Gunfire erupts at Trotter Drive home; is it connected to Idaho In-N-Out shooting?,Twin Falls drive-by shooting: Gunfire erupts at Trotter Drive home; is it connected to Idaho In-N-Out shooting?,"Twin Falls drive-by shooting: Gunfire erupts at Trotter Drive home; is it connected to Idaho In-N-Out shooting? The Twin Falls Police Department said that the drive-by shooting was reported at a home in the 300 block of Trotter Drive, near 4th Ave. E and Meadowview Lane. Twin Falls police are investigating a drive-by shooting that took place late Saturday night, August 1. The Twin Falls Police Department said that the shooting was reported around 8:45 pm at a home in the 300 block of Trotter Drive, near 4th Ave. E and Meadowview Lane. Officers who are in the area are actively investigating the shooting. As of 10:50 pm Saturday, no injuries had been reported. The Twin Falls Police Department confirmed in a press release shared on Facebook that the drive-by shooting appears to be “an isolated incident” and is not connected to the In-N-Out shooting. Also Read |Twin Falls In-N-Out mass shooting: Shocking video shows Idaho gunman firing several shots into parked Tesla as 3 dead “At approximately 8:45 p.m., officers with the our department were dispatched to a residence in the 300 block of Trotter Drive following a report of shots fired,” reads the press release. “Officers responded to the scene and are actively investigating the incident. At this time, the investigation is ongoing, and additional information will be released as it becomes available. At this time there are no reported injuries. Based on the information currently available, this appears to be an isolated incident and is not related to the earlier incident at In-N-Out.” It adds, “We ask the public to avoid the area while officers conduct their investigation. Anyone with information related to this incident is encouraged to contact the police department at 208-735-4357. Further update","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:34:49 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/twin-falls-drive-by-shooting-gunfire-erupts-at-trotter-drive-home-is-it-connected-to-idaho-in-n-out-shooting-101785653766162.html,2026-08-03 01:31:46
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,South Korea issues heatwave alert as temperature hits record,South Korea issues heatwave alert as temperature hits record,"South Korea issues heatwave alert as temperature hits record The Korea Meteorological Administration issued a severe heat wave alert for the southern parts of the country as of 1 pm local time. South Korea issued emergency heat wave instructions as the country sweltered, with its highest temperature on record reported in the southeastern city of Yangsan. Also Read |South Korea issues first emergency heatwave warning under new rating system “Each ministry shall use all available channels, including public broadcasters, emergency text messages, electronic information boards and village broadcasts, to swiftly inform the public about heat wave conditions,” Prime Minister Han Seongsook said in a statement posted Sunday on a government Facebook page. Also Read |Europe heat wave: Why Paris banned drinking liquor and what alcohol does to the body The Korea Meteorological Administration issued a severe heat wave alert for southern parts of the country as of 1 p.m. local time. The temperature in the city of Yangsan surged to 42.5C (108.5F), the highest recorded since observations began in 1904, Yonhap reported. Also Read |Heat wave expected to bring record-breaking temps, heighten wildfire risk to parts of Western US Separately, the Interior Ministry plans to dispatch director general-level officials to oversee operations in the Seoul metropolitan area, South Gyeongsang Province and other southern regions, to assess local heat wave responses and identify areas requiring additional support, Yonhap reported.","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:32:18 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/south-korea-issues-heatwave-alert-as-temperature-hits-record-101785653405390.html,2026-08-03 01:31:46
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Twin Falls, Idaho mass shooting: Latest updates as number of injured rises to 7; death toll remains at 3","Twin Falls, Idaho mass shooting: Latest updates as number of injured rises to 7; death toll remains at 3","Twin Falls, Idaho mass shooting: Latest updates as number of injured rises to 7; death toll remains at 3 A gunman opened fire at an In-N-Out in Twin Falls, Idaho. Here's the latest on the shooting. A mass shooting inTwin Falls, Idaho has left three people dead and many injured. A gunmanopened fireat anIn-N-Out, with videos of the shooter going viral on social media. While initial reports claimed that two people were injured in the shooting,AZ Intel shared in an X postthat the number of injured has risen to seven, a city spokesman told AP. While the death toll remained at three, it is unclear if the suspect was among the 3 dead. Terry Dudleyhas been identified by his son and his employer as one of the injured. North Star Taxiwrote on Facebookthat Terry is one of its drivers. It confirmed that he is alive but has a “long road ahead of him.” Also Read |Twin Falls In-N-Out mass shooting: Gov. Brad Little under fire for saying Idaho is ‘one of the safest places live’ At 2:29 pm, an “active shooter incident” was first reported, and shortly afterwards, police urged people to avoid the area. Cops noted that roads in the area would be closed, as officers responded. The suspected shooter, whose identity has yet to be revealed, is dead, Twin Falls Police Chief Matthew Hicks said during a press conference. Joshua Palmer, a public information coordinator for the city, told The Independent that the number of victims could increase. “We want to emphasize that that number may change,” Palmer said. “That was just the first number we got.” Also Read |Twin Falls In-N-Out mass shooting: Shocking video shows Idaho gunman firing several shots into parked Tesla as 3 dead The In-N-Out where th","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:11:51 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/twin-falls-idaho-mass-shooting-latest-updates-as-number-of-injured-rises-to-7-death-toll-remains-at-3-101785652654770.html,2026-08-03 01:31:46
Hindustan Times,India (Mainstream),en,"Nancy Guthrie update: ‘Investigator’ slams Annie Guthrie, Tommaso Cioni's actions after kidnapping","Nancy Guthrie update: ‘Investigator’ slams Annie Guthrie, Tommaso Cioni's actions after kidnapping","Nancy Guthrie update: ‘Investigator’ slams Annie Guthrie, Tommaso Cioni's actions after kidnapping A self-styled investigator slammed Annie Guthrie and Tommaso Cioni for their actions after Nancy Guthrie's kidnapping, implying they were not doing enough. A self-styled investigator has slammedAnnie GuthrieandTommaso Cionifor their actions afterNancy Guthrie's kidnapping. Jonathan Lee Riches, or JLR, put out posts alleging that the two were not doing enough to help find the 84-year-old. Nancy Guthrie was reported missing by her family on February 1, and authorities believe TODAY show host Savannah Guthrie's mother was taken from her home the night before. JLR's allegations come amid his numerous posts on Annie and Tommaso, which have served to fuel public speculation. The couple has captured public interest because they were among the last people to see Nancy Guthrie before she went missing. The octogenarian is believed to have had dinner with her daughter the night she was taken and Tommaso reportedly dropped her home after that. Notably, the Pima County Sheriff had earlier clarified that the Guthrie family members are not suspects in the case. Also Read |Nancy Guthrie update: ‘Investigator’ says Annie Guthrie sold car; sparks questions - ‘Car they took Nancy home in?’ However, JLR has questioned their actions, alleging more could be done to help find Nancy Guthrie. Notably, Annie and Tommaso keep their personal lives private, so it is not possible to know the extent to which the two have gone to help find the octogenarian. Savannah, in a past instance, had backed both Annie and Tommaso, slamming all speculations against the duo. Meanwhile, here's what JLR said about Annie Guthrie. JLR shared a screenshot of Annie Guthrie's Fa","Sun, 02 Aug 2026 11:37:45 +0530",https://www.hindustantimes.com/world-news/us-news/nancy-guthrie-update-investigator-slams-annie-guthrie-tommaso-cionis-actions-after-kidnapping-101785647523699.html,2026-08-03 01:31:46
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Sudan drone strike on Darfur court kills 35, rights group blames army","Sudan drone strike on Darfur court kills 35, rights group blames army","Sudan drone strike on Darfur court kills 35, rights group blames army A drone strike on a traditional court in Sudan's North Darfur killed at least 35 people, according to a rights group, as fighting between the army and the RSF continued A drone strike on a traditional court in Sudan's North Darfur killed at least 35 people, according to a rights group, as fighting between the army and the RSF continued At least 35 people were killed after a drone strike hit a traditional court in Garra al-Zawaya village in North Darfur on Sunday, according to a Sudanese rights group, which blamed the attack on the Sudanese army. The strike targeted a gathering where civilians had assembled to attend local hearings, as fighting between the army and the paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF) continued into its third year. The Emergency Lawyers group, which has documented abuses by both the Sudanese army and the RSF throughout the conflict, said the strike took place at around 1:00 pm local time (1100 GMT). According to the organisation, the court in Garra al-Zawaya was hearing local disputes when it was struck. A witness from the area toldAFP, on condition of anonymity for safety reasons, ""The court session was being held under a tree with the participation of local community leaders."" The witness said those killed included ""four tribal leaders and two RSF commanders"". The village is under the control of the Rapid Support Forces, which have been fighting the Sudanese army since April 2023. There was no immediate response from the army. The RSF's self-declared government condemned the attack as ""a horrific crime"", claiming 37 people were killed and 50 others were injured. Garra al-Zawaya is located near Kabkabiya in North Darf","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 06:56:40 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/sudan-drone-strike-on-darfur-court-kills-35-rights-group-blames-army-14035513.html,2026-08-03 01:31:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,US Senate unveils stopgap spending bill to avert government shutdown until December 11,US Senate unveils stopgap spending bill to avert government shutdown until December 11,"US Senate unveils stopgap spending bill to avert government shutdown until December 11 The bipartisan proposal would keep federal agencies running through December 11, pushing a potential funding crisis until after the elections while delaying a controversial grants rule and resolving key disputes between Congress and the White House The bipartisan proposal would keep federal agencies running through December 11, pushing a potential funding crisis until after the elections while delaying a controversial grants rule and resolving key disputes between Congress and the White House In a bid to prevent another disruptive federal government shutdown ahead of the upcoming elections, key US senators have introduced a bipartisan stopgap spending bill that would fund federal agencies through December 11. The continuing resolution (CR), unveiled after days of negotiations between congressional leaders and the White House, is expected to be voted on later this week before lawmakers leave Washington for the traditional August recess. If approved by both chambers of Congress and signed into law by the President, the measure would delay a potentially contentious funding battle until after the election season. Government funding disputes in Washington are typically resolved at the last minute, often bringing the country close to a shutdown. This time, however, lawmakers have acted nearly two months before the current fiscal year ends on September 30. The move reflects growing concern among both Democrats and Republicans over the political and economic fallout of another government closure. The United States has already witnessed two record-breaking shutdowns within the past 10 months. Senate Majority LeaderJohn Thunesaid preventing another shutdown before Congress leaves for its August recess is his top priority. While t","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 06:49:38 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-senate-unveils-stopgap-spending-bill-to-avert-government-shutdown-until-december-11-14035512.html,2026-08-03 01:31:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,'You'll find out': Trump threatens to 'punish' Canada over the wildfires fiasco,'You'll find out': Trump threatens to 'punish' Canada over the wildfires fiasco,"'You'll find out': Trump threatens to 'punish' Canada over the wildfires fiasco US President Donald Trump once again repeated his threat against Canada over the wildfires fiasco that impacted parts of the United States as well. US President Donald Trump once again repeated his threat against Canada over the wildfires fiasco that impacted parts of the United States as well. US President Donald Trump once again repeated his threat against Canada over the wildfires fiasco that impacted parts of the United States as well. The American president on Sunday said that he has decided to ""punish"" Canada for the wildfires, and the punishment will be revealed soon. The remarks from the American leader came after a journalist on boardAir Force Oneasked Trump what measures he will take against Canada over the wildfire issue and if he has planned any punishment. ""I have. You'll find out,"" Trump responded, repeating his assertion that ""Canada must pay"". It is pertinent to note that for the longest time, Trump has beenthreatening to impose new tariffs on Canadaafter hundreds of wildfires have left much of the northern US covered by a blanket of smoke. The threats came after US lawmakers complained about the wildfires. ""The United States is being unnecessarily invaded by filthy, polluted, and unhealthy air,"" Trump said last month, threatening to impose new levies over Canada's ""willful negligence"". At that time, Trump said in his post on TruthSocial that he would call Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney to demand an explanation over his country's ""willful negligence,"" accusing the country of ""not properly maintaining"" their forests and brush. Amid the constant threats from the US, Canada's International Trade Ministe","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 06:45:24 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/youll-find-out-trump-threatens-to-punish-canada-over-the-wildfires-fiasco-14035506.html,2026-08-03 01:31:47
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Globe at a glance: From US-Iran talks to India receiving the 2030 Commonwealth Games baton,Globe at a glance: From US-Iran talks to India receiving the 2030 Commonwealth Games baton,"Globe at a glance: From US-Iran talks to India receiving the 2030 Commonwealth Games baton US-Iran peace talks and Washington's bid to avert a shutdown to Spain's migrant tragedy, Canada's airline strike, Venezuela's political reset and India taking the Commonwealth Games baton for Ahmedabad 2030—here are the top global developments you need to know today US-Iran peace talks and Washington's bid to avert a shutdown to Spain's migrant tragedy, Canada's airline strike, Venezuela's political reset and India taking the Commonwealth Games baton for Ahmedabad 2030—here are the top global developments you need to know today Trump to begin Iran talks amid Gulf tensions:US President Donald Trump said negotiations with Iran will begin Monday after shelving planned military strikes. The talks aim to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and curb Tehran's nuclear ambitions, even as Israel remains on alert and Gulf nations warn against renewed regional escalation. US Senate moves to avert government shutdown:US senators have unveiled a stopgap spending bill to keep federal agencies funded through December 11, aiming to avoid a pre-election government shutdown. The measure buys Congress more time to resolve spending disputes while delaying a controversial federal grants rule. WestJet strike disrupts Canada holiday travel:A pay dispute has triggered a strike by WestJet flight attendants, forcing the cancellation of hundreds of flights and disrupting travel for around 250,000 passengers during Canada's long weekend. Cabin crew are demanding pay for all hours worked, including pre- and post-flight duties. Trump bets on tech to counter drone terror:The Trump administration is launching private-sector “incubators” to accelerate anti-drone technologies as unmanned aerial threats grow worldwide. Officials say the initiative will fast-track innovation to det","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 06:29:46 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/globe-at-a-glance-from-us-iran-talks-to-india-receiving-the-2030-commonwealth-games-baton-14035509.html,2026-08-03 01:31:48
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Turkey slams Netanyahu's 'expansionist approach'; condemns Israel's latest strikes on Gaza,Turkey slams Netanyahu's 'expansionist approach'; condemns Israel's latest strikes on Gaza,"Turkey slams Netanyahu's 'expansionist approach'; condemns Israel's latest strikes on Gaza Amid the growing tensions in West Asia, Turkey on Sunday slammed Israel's latest strikes on Gaza that killed 17 people in the coastal enclave. Amid the growing tensions in West Asia, Turkey on Sunday slammed Israel's latest strikes on Gaza that killed 17 people in the coastal enclave. Amid the growing tensions in West Asia, Turkey on Sunday slammed Israel's latest strikes on Gaza that killed 17 people in the coastal enclave. Ankara's condemnation was directed towards Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, as it insisted that the government of the Jewish nation has ""no intention of making peace with Palestinians"". ""Netanyahu's sole objective is to displacePalestinians from their homelandand prevent the establishment of peace and stability in the region,"" the Foreign Ministry said in a statement on its official website. It also maintained that the Israeli premier continues to take all steps that undermine the fragile regional balance and sabotage mediation efforts. ""It has become imperative for the international community to adopt a more determined, consistent and robust stance against Netanyahu's expansionist and militarist approach, which seeks to turn the entire Middle East into a zone of conflict,"" the statement said. Turkey went on to call on countries around the world to support peace and prosperity for the Palestinians and wider West Asia. The Turkish foreign ministry urged the international community to act responsibly and uphold international law and humanitarian values. It is pertinent to note that the remarks from the Turkish foreign ministry came just hours after theIsraeli strikes killed at least 17 ","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 05:52:53 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/turkey-slams-netanyahus-expansionist-approach-condemns-israels-latest-strikes-on-gaza-14035501.html,2026-08-03 01:31:48
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Japan, US intervene to prop up yen after 40-year lows; Trump says it's a 'signal of friendship'","Japan, US intervene to prop up yen after 40-year lows; Trump says it's a 'signal of friendship'","Japan, US intervene to prop up yen after 40-year lows; Trump says it's a 'signal of friendship' Japan and the United States have carried out a rare coordinated intervention to support the yen after it hit 40-year lows. President Donald Trump called the move a ""signal of friendship"", while Tokyo warned it was prepared to take further action to stabilise the currency Japan and the United States have carried out a rare coordinated intervention to support the yen after it hit 40-year lows. President Donald Trump called the move a ""signal of friendship"", while Tokyo warned it was prepared to take further action to stabilise the currency Japan on Monday confirmed it had carried out a rare coordinated intervention with the United States to support the battered yen, marking the first such joint action in nearly 15 years as the Japanese currency came under intense pressure after falling to its weakest level in about four decades. The confirmation came after US President Donald Trump publicly acknowledged Washington's role, describing the move as a ""signal of friendship"" towards one of America's closest allies. ""They have a weakening yen, and they wanted a little bit of help. And we're always there for Japan,"" Trump told reporters aboard Air Force One. ""It was a signal of friendship,"" he added, saying the intervention would also help the global economy. In a statement issued on Monday, Japan's Finance Ministry said it conducted coordinated yen-buying intervention with the US Treasury on Friday to counter what it called ""excessive volatility and disorderly movements"" in the Japanese currency. Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama said Tokyo remained in close contact with Washington and was prepared to act again if market conditions warranted. ""The Japanese Ministry of Finance remains attentive and in close communication with our counterparts at the US","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 05:32:57 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/business/japan-us-intervene-prop-up-yen-40-year-lows-trump-signal-of-friendship-14035502.html,2026-08-03 01:31:48
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Trump says negotiations with Iran will begin on Monday after calling off massive attack,Trump says negotiations with Iran will begin on Monday after calling off massive attack,"Trump says negotiations with Iran will begin on Monday after calling off massive attack US President Donald Trump said that new negotiations with Iran will begin Monday after he decided to hold off on striking the Islamic republic to pursue a deal to end the war entering its sixth month. US President Donald Trump said that new negotiations with Iran will begin Monday after he decided to hold off on striking the Islamic republic to pursue a deal to end the war entering its sixth month. US President Donald Trump said that new negotiations with Iran will begin Monday after he decided to hold off on striking the Islamic republic to pursue a deal to end the war entering its sixth month. Trump told reporters on Sunday that the talks would cover the Strait of Hormuz –- a route for global energy supplies that has become a key sticking point in the conflict -- and ultimately, the denuclearization of Iran. For its part, Iran said it was nearing a deal with Oman over a new route through the strait, where a tanker reported an explosion nearby on Sunday, underscoring the continued volatility of the strategic waterway. Oil prices fell on Monday at the opening of Asian trade after Trump announced the new negotiations, with West Texas Intermediate dropping 4.7 percent to $80.72 per barrel. Washington and Tehran have been at war since February 28, when the US and Israel launched surprise strikes against Iran, though months of on-off diplomacy have led to periods of relative calm. Following a return to strikes last month, fears had mounted that the fighting could escalate once again. Trump had threatened to hit Iran ""very hard"" and was reportedly considering renewed attacks including against energy infrastructure, with US embassies across the region on alert. Trump pulled back","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 05:24:58 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/trump-says-negotiations-with-iran-will-begin-on-monday-after-calling-off-massive-attack-14035500.html,2026-08-03 01:31:48
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Israel, CentCom caught off guard as Trump announced Iran strike cancellation on Truth Social: Report","Israel, CentCom caught off guard as Trump announced Iran strike cancellation on Truth Social: Report","Israel, CentCom caught off guard as Trump announced Iran strike cancellation on Truth Social: Report Israeli officials and the US military’s Central Command (CentCom) were reportedly not informed in advance about President Donald Trump’s decision to call off a planned major strike on Iran, with Israeli officials learning of the move through his Truth Social post, according to Israeli media. Israeli officials and the US military’s Central Command (CentCom) were reportedly not informed in advance about President Donald Trump’s decision to call off a planned major strike on Iran, with Israeli officials learning of the move through his Truth Social post, according to Israeli media. Israeli officials and the US military’s Central Command (CentCom) were reportedly not given advance notice of US President Donald Trump’s decision to call off a planned major strike on Iran, according to Israeli media. Israel’sChannel 12reported that Israeli officials first became aware of Trump’s decision through his post on Truth Social. CentCom was also reportedly not informed beforehand. The development came despite Trump saying in his post that Israel had joined the US in a commitment to pursue a possible agreement with Iran. Trump said on Saturday that he had called off the planned attack after Iran and other Middle Eastern countries asked Washington to hold off, claiming that the broad outlines of a deal had been agreed. He said the proposed arrangement would include the “Immediate, complete, and total OPENING OF THE HORMUZ STRAIT” and an end to Iran’s nuclear threat. Trump also claimed that Israel had agreed to the move and called for a rapid conclusion to the negotiations. Iranian officials have rejected Trump’s account, calling his claim that Tehran sought a halt to the planned attacks a “lie”. Iranian military sources said the country’s armed forces remained at the highest leve","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 00:45:06 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/israel-centcom-caught-off-guard-as-trump-announced-iran-strike-cancellation-on-truth-social-report-14035498.html,2026-08-03 01:31:48
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Sheikh Hasina to make first major public appearance in India since 2024 Bangladesh ouster,Sheikh Hasina to make first major public appearance in India since 2024 Bangladesh ouster,"Sheikh Hasina to make first major public appearance in India since 2024 Bangladesh ouster Former Bangladesh Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina is set to make her first major public appearance in India since leaving Bangladesh in August 2024 after a student-led uprising ended her nearly 16-year rule. Former Bangladesh Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina is set to make her first major public appearance in India since leaving Bangladesh in August 2024 after a student-led uprising ended her nearly 16-year rule. Former Bangladesh Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina is set to make her first major public appearance in India since fleeing Bangladesh in August 2024 following a student-led uprising that ended her nearly 16-year rule. Hasina, who has continued to issue statements, give interviews and participate in virtual events since leaving office, is expected to address a virtual programme hosted by the Foreign Correspondents’ Club of South Asia (FCC South Asia) in New Delhi. The event is scheduled for 6 pm on August 5, exactly two years after she left Bangladesh. It will be held at the Sir Mark Tully Auditorium on Mathura Road and streamed live on the FCC South Asia’s social media platforms. During the event, Hasina is expected to discuss her political future and plans to return to Bangladesh. Her appearance would mark her most prominent public engagement since she left the country after protests over a controversial government jobs quota system expanded into a nationwide movement against her administration. On August 5, 2024, protesters entered and vandalised government buildings in Dhaka, forcing Hasina to step down and leave the country for India. Since then, she has remained in India while occasionally speaking through interviews, statements and online appearances. Several Bangladeshi p","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 00:33:44 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/sheikh-hasina-to-make-first-major-public-appearance-in-india-since-2024-bangladesh-ouster-14035496.html,2026-08-03 01:31:48
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Israel raises 'serious security concerns' over Hamas disarmament deal with White House,Israel raises 'serious security concerns' over Hamas disarmament deal with White House,"Israel raises 'serious security concerns' over Hamas disarmament deal with White House Israel has conveyed ""serious security concerns"" to the White House over the proposed US-backed Hamas disarmament agreement, saying it will not withdraw troops from Gaza until the militant group fully surrenders its weapons. Israel has conveyed ""serious security concerns"" to the White House over the proposed US-backed Hamas disarmament agreement, saying it will not withdraw troops from Gaza until the militant group fully surrenders its weapons. Israel has informed the White House that it has ""serious security concerns"" about the proposed US-backed Hamas disarmament agreement, arguing that the militant group could rebuild its military capabilities if Israeli forces withdraw from Gaza too soon. The comments, made by Doron Spielman, spokesperson for Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office, are among Israel's first public remarks since US President Donald Trump announced the agreement. Speaking to the Associated Press, Spielman said Israeli intelligence believes Hamas remains focused on rebuilding its military infrastructure rather than genuinely disarming. ""Our assessment is that if we redeploy before Hamas is truly disarmed, it will quickly expand its presence throughout Gaza, rebuild its terrorist infrastructure, once again threaten Israeli communities, and seek to carry out another Oct. 7-style attack,"" he said. He added that Israel would not withdraw from areas under its control in Gaza until Hamas physically surrendered its weapons, saying, ""Disarming means physically giving up the weapons. Nothing less."" The proposed agreement follows Hamas' announcement earlier this week that it was prepared to begin disarming under a US-brokered ceasefire framework agreed last October. According to a copy","Mon, 3 Aug 2026 00:25:54 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/israel-raises-serious-security-concerns-over-hamas-disarmament-deal-with-white-house-14035494.html,2026-08-03 01:31:48
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Brazil's Lula confirms fourth-term bid as concern over foreign interference looms ahead of election,Brazil's Lula confirms fourth-term bid as concern over foreign interference looms ahead of election,"Brazil's Lula confirms fourth-term bid as concern over foreign interference looms ahead of election What is very likely to be the last reelection bid of Brazil’s President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva was confirmed on Sunday by his Workers' Party as the 80yearold leader faces increasing pressure from foreign leaders ahead of October's elections. It will be his seventh race for the top job. What is very likely to be the last reelection bid of Brazil’s President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva was confirmed on Sunday by his Workers' Party as the 80yearold leader faces increasing pressure from foreign leaders ahead of October's elections. It will be his seventh race for the top job. Brazil's Workers' Party on Sunday officially confirmed that President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva will seek another term in October's presidential election, setting the stage for what is widely expected to be the 80-year-old leader's final campaign for the country's highest office. The election will mark Lula's seventh presidential contest. Speaking at the party convention, Lula pledged to strengthen Brazil's defence industry, safeguard the country's strategic mineral resources and protect national sovereignty. ""No Chinese, no American, no French will touch these resources without respecting Brazil's sovereignty,"" he said, adding that his government would need to be ""much more daring"" to deliver further changes. Lula enters the campaign facing growing political pressure from abroad. His main challenger, Senator Flávio Bolsonaro, has received public backing from figures including members of US President Donald Trump's administration, Argentine President Javier Milei and Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Senior Workers' Party leaders warned that Brazil's election could be influenced by foreign actors. Party chairman Edinho Silva described the vote as pivotal for Latin America's future a","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 23:58:43 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/brazils-lula-confirms-fourth-term-bid-as-concern-over-foreign-interference-looms-ahead-of-election-14035492.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,UK's migrant crisis: Andy Burnham vows to be 'relentless' on small boat crossings after Dover visit,UK's migrant crisis: Andy Burnham vows to be 'relentless' on small boat crossings after Dover visit,"UK's migrant crisis: Andy Burnham vows to be 'relentless' on small boat crossings after Dover visit Andy Burnham has pledged tougher action against people-smuggling gangs behind small-boat crossings in the English Channel, with the government increasing efforts to tackle organised immigration crime. Andy Burnham has pledged tougher action against people-smuggling gangs behind small-boat crossings in the English Channel, with the government increasing efforts to tackle organised immigration crime. UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham has pledged to intensify the crackdown on people-smuggling gangs behind small-boat crossings in the English Channel, as the government deploys hundreds more officers to tackle organised immigration crime. The Labour government said the National Crime Agency (NCA) now has a record 791 officers working on organised immigration crime, more than double the number at the start of 2025. During a visit to Dover, Burnham said his government would be “relentless” in tackling Channel crossings, while arguing that enforcement must be combined with safe and legal routes for people seeking to enter the UK. “Clearly, progress is being made, but we’re not complacent. We’re just going to be relentless,” Burnham said. He added that the government also needed to create safe routes, arguing that doing so would weaken the business model of people-smuggling gangs. The government says the number of Channel arrivals so far this year is significantly lower than last year, although crossings have risen sharply during periods of favourable weather. Burnham said enforcement activity against people-smuggling networks had been strengthened on both sides of the Channel. The government has also increased the NCA’s resources to target organised immigration crime, including the fi","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 23:18:41 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/uks-migrant-crisis-andy-burnham-vows-to-be-relentless-on-small-boat-crossings-after-dover-visit-14035490.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Ceuta migrant crisis death toll rises to 72 as Spain tightens border security,Ceuta migrant crisis death toll rises to 72 as Spain tightens border security,"Ceuta migrant crisis death toll rises to 72 as Spain tightens border security Spanish authorities said at least 72 people have died following the mass influx of migrants into the North African enclave of Ceuta, as Madrid stepped up border security and European nations called for stronger protection of the bloc's external frontiers. Spanish authorities said at least 72 people have died following the mass influx of migrants into the North African enclave of Ceuta, as Madrid stepped up border security and European nations called for stronger protection of the bloc's external frontiers. The death toll from the mass migrant influx into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta has risen to 72, local authorities said on Sunday, days after tens of thousands of people crossed from Morocco in the territory's largest-ever migrant surge. Most of the estimated 60,000 migrants, many of whom swam around the border post or crossed by sea, have since returned to Morocco following the unprecedented influx. Miguel Angel Perez Triano, the Spanish government's delegate to Ceuta, said the latest confirmed death toll stood at 72, up from the previously reported 67. He added that more than 1,000 people had received medical treatment since Thursday. While the situation in Ceuta had improved significantly, officials said efforts to restore normality were still ongoing. Authorities said many migrants drowned while attempting to swim across the sea, while others were crushed trying to climb the breakwater and border fence. Officials said economic hardship and social media rumours encouraging people to make the crossing had contributed to the mass movement. Expressing grief over the tragedy, Karima Abenaz, a French national with family in Morocco, said it was heartbreaking to see young people and even infants dying during the dangero","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:19:55 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/ceuta-migrant-crisis-death-toll-rises-to-72-as-spain-tightens-border-security-14035480.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Personal loans without collateral: How unsecured loans actually work,Personal loans without collateral: How unsecured loans actually work,"Personal loans without collateral: How unsecured loans actually work An unsecured personal loan lets you borrow without pledging property, gold or other assets as collateral. Understand how lenders assess your credit profile, income, repayment capacity and financial stability before approval. An unsecured personal loan lets you borrow without pledging property, gold or other assets as collateral. Understand how lenders assess your credit profile, income, repayment capacity and financial stability before approval. Many people assume that borrowing money requires pledging an asset such as property, gold or investments. However, an unsecured personal loan works differently. Eligible borrowers can access funds without providing collateral because lenders evaluate their financial profile instead of relying on a pledged asset. Understanding how an unsecured personal loan works helps borrowers know what lenders assess before approving an application. The defining feature of an unsecured personal loan is that it does not require the borrower to provide an asset as security. Unlike secured loans, where property or other valuable assets act as collateral, unsecured loans are approved primarily on the basis of the applicant's financial profile. This means lenders focus on whether a borrower has the ability and willingness to repay the loan. Factors such as income, employment stability, repayment history, and existing financial obligations become central to the assessment process. For borrowers, this offers the advantage of accessing funds without placing personal assets at risk. At the same time, it also means maintaining a healthy financial profile becomes particularly important. Since there is no collateral to support the borrowing decision, lenders conduct a detailed asse","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 21:59:01 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/brand-connect/personal-loans-without-collateral-how-unsecured-loans-actually-work-14035486.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"14 killed, dozens injured in suicide blast at peace rally in Pakistan’s Swat","14 killed, dozens injured in suicide blast at peace rally in Pakistan’s Swat","14 killed, dozens injured in suicide blast at peace rally in Pakistan’s Swat A suicide bombing at a peace rally in Pakistan’s Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province killed at least 14 people and injured more than two dozen others on Sunday. The blast took place in Kabal town in the Swat Valley, where protesters had gathered to demand an end to militancy. A suicide bombing at a peace rally in Pakistan’s Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province killed at least 14 people and injured more than two dozen others on Sunday. The blast took place in Kabal town in the Swat Valley, where protesters had gathered to demand an end to militancy. A suicide bombing at a peace rally in Pakistan’s northwestern Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province killed at least 14 people, including police personnel, and injured more than two dozen others on Sunday, news agencyPTIreported citing officials. The explosion took place in Kabal town in the Swat Valley, where protesters had gathered near a police station to demand peace and raise slogans against militancy, officials said. Swat Deputy Inspector General of Police Fida Hussain said the attacker attempted to enter the police station but was stopped by officers at the main gate before detonating his explosive vest. “A suicide bomber attempted to enter the police station located at the chowk, but was stopped by police at the main gate,” Hussain told AFP. No militant group immediately claimed responsibility for the attack. Emergency teams rushed the injured to nearby hospitals as police and other security agencies sealed off the area, officials said. Pakistan’s Interior Minister Mohsin Naqvi condemned the bombing and expressed condolences to the families of those killed, while praying for the recovery of those injured. The bombing comes as security conditions in Swat have deteriorated in recent months. The Swat Peace Rally was o","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 21:44:55 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/14-killed-dozens-injured-in-suicide-blast-at-peace-rally-in-pakistans-swat-14035484.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,‘There is no agreement’: Iran rejects Trump claim of Strait of Hormuz reopening deal,‘There is no agreement’: Iran rejects Trump claim of Strait of Hormuz reopening deal,"‘There is no agreement’: Iran rejects Trump claim of Strait of Hormuz reopening deal Iran has denied Trump’s claim that Tehran agreed to reopen the Strait of Hormuz as part of a possible deal, saying no such agreement has been reached. Iranian officials also warned that the strategic waterway would remain closed as long as US “hostile actions” continue. Iran has denied Trump’s claim that Tehran agreed to reopen the Strait of Hormuz as part of a possible deal, saying no such agreement has been reached. Iranian officials also warned that the strategic waterway would remain closed as long as US “hostile actions” continue. Iran on Sunday denied reports that it had agreed to reopen the Strait of Hormuz, rejecting US President Donald Trump’s claim that an outline of a deal with Tehran included the “immediate, complete, and total” reopening of the strategic waterway. Iranian state media also dismissed reports of an agreement as false, while officials warned that the strait would remain closed as long as the United States continued what Tehran described as hostile actions. The semi-official Fars news agency, citing sources close to Iran’s negotiating team and military, said there was no agreement to reopen the Strait of Hormuz. “There is no agreement on reopening the Strait of Hormuz,” Fars reported, quoting an informed source. The source said the waterway would remain closed while US “hostile actions” continued. Iranian officials also rejected reports that Tehran had approved any plan to change its policy on the strategically important shipping route. According to Fars, vessels would only be permitted to pass through a designated route after coordinating with and receiving approval from the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps Navy. The agency quoted a military source as warning that vessels attempting to use other routes could face “","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 21:04:48 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/there-is-no-agreement-iran-rejects-trump-claim-of-strait-of-hormuz-reopening-deal-14035482.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Renowned climber Nirmal Purja’s body recovered days after deadly Broad Peak avalanche,Renowned climber Nirmal Purja’s body recovered days after deadly Broad Peak avalanche,"Renowned climber Nirmal Purja’s body recovered days after deadly Broad Peak avalanche Rescuers on Sunday recovered the body of renowned climber Nirmal Purja from Broad Peak in northern Pakistan, days after an avalanche killed him and nine other members of his expedition. The deadly avalanche struck on Thursday, cutting off contact with the team. Rescuers on Sunday recovered the body of renowned climber Nirmal Purja from Broad Peak in northern Pakistan, days after an avalanche killed him and nine other members of his expedition. The deadly avalanche struck on Thursday, cutting off contact with the team. Rescuers on Sunday recovered the body of renowned climber Nirmal Purja, days after an avalanche killed him and nine other members of an international expedition on Broad Peak in northern Pakistan, the Alpine Club of Pakistan said. The avalanche struck on Thursday, cutting off contact with the expedition led by Purja, a 43-year-old British-Nepali mountaineer and former British military serviceman. The Alpine Club said a ground rescue team reached Purja at an altitude of around 5,700 metres on Broad Peak. “The ground rescue team has reached Nims Dai (Purja) at approximately 5,700m on Broad Peak,” the club said in a social media post. Ayaz Shigri, general secretary of the Alpine Club of Pakistan, said rescuers were bringing down four bodies — those of Purja, two other Nepali climbers and a Chinese national. Rescuers also located another body at a significantly higher altitude. However, Shigri said the extreme terrain and weather conditions made it unlikely that an attempt would be made to recover it immediately. Purja’s expedition company confirmed on Saturday that none of the team members had survived the avalanche. Authorities in the region said the remains of three other climbers — an Omani woman, a Nepali man and an A","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 20:21:04 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/renowned-climber-nirmal-purjas-body-recovered-days-after-deadly-broad-peak-avalanche-14035479.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Second phase of PoK elections held under shadow of rigging allegations, protests and military scrutiny","Second phase of PoK elections held under shadow of rigging allegations, protests and military scrutiny","Second phase of PoK elections held under shadow of rigging allegations, protests and military scrutiny The second phase of elections to the Legislative Assembly in Pakistan-occupied Kashmir (PoK) concluded on Sunday, with voting held in eight of the nine constituencies in the Muzaffarabad division and all 12 refugee constituencies The second phase of elections to the Legislative Assembly in Pakistan-occupied Kashmir (PoK) concluded on Sunday, with voting held in eight of the nine constituencies in the Muzaffarabad division and all 12 refugee constituencies The second phase of elections to the Legislative Assembly in Pakistan-occupied Kashmir (PoK) concluded on Sunday, with voting held in eight of the nine constituencies in the Muzaffarabad division and all 12 refugee constituencies. Polling began at 8 am and continued until 5 pm for the refugee seats, while voting in the Muzaffarabad division was extended by an hour and concluded at 6 pm. More than 300 candidates contested the eight Muzaffarabad seats and the 12 constituencies reserved for refugees settled in different parts of Pakistan. The voting took place amid renewed allegations of electoral malpractice, with the Pakistan Peoples Party (PPP) accusing the ruling Pakistan Muslim League-Nawaz (PML-N) of using violence and intimidation to influence the outcome. PPP Chairman Bilawal Bhutto-Zardari alleged that the PML-N had once again attempted to manipulate the election through force. According to a report by Pakistani newspaperDawn, Bilawal condemned what he described as an attack on PPP's regional president Chaudhry Latif Akbar, who is also the party's candidate from LA-31 (Muzaffarabad-V). He further claimed that PPP worker Mushtaq Shah was killed in the same constituency. ""The PML-N is robbing the votes of the people through bullets, batons and co","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 19:52:04 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/second-phase-of-pok-elections-held-under-shadow-of-rigging-allegations-protests-and-military-scrutiny-14035478.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,8 killed in Ukrainian strikes across Russia as Kyiv-Moscow attacks intensify,8 killed in Ukrainian strikes across Russia as Kyiv-Moscow attacks intensify,"8 killed in Ukrainian strikes across Russia as Kyiv-Moscow attacks intensify Ukraine launched attacks on several Russian regions on Sunday, killing at least eight people, according to Russian officials. The strikes came as Moscow and Kyiv continue to intensify attacks on each other amid stalled efforts to revive peace talks. Ukraine launched attacks on several Russian regions on Sunday, killing at least eight people, according to Russian officials. The strikes came as Moscow and Kyiv continue to intensify attacks on each other amid stalled efforts to revive peace talks. Ukraine launched attacks across several Russian regions on Sunday, killing at least eight people, Russian officials said, as strikes between Moscow and Kyiv continue to intensify amid stalled efforts to revive peace talks. Three people were killed in Ukrainian shelling in Russia’s Belgorod region, which borders Ukraine, while two others died in a separate drone attack in the Saratov region, authorities said. Another three people were killed when a drone struck a car in Udmurtia, more than 1,000 km from the front line, acting regional governor Olga Abramova said. “ This act is monstrous in its senselessness. These people were definitely not a military target,” Abramova said in a post on Telegram. Russia’s Defence Ministry said its air defence systems intercepted 635 Ukrainian drones overnight. Moscow and Kyiv have stepped up attacks on each other in recent months, even as US-led efforts to broker an end to the war remain largely stalled. Ukraine, which denies deliberately targeting civilians, has described its strikes inside Russia as retaliation for Russian attacks on Ukrainian territory and an effort to pressure Moscow into negotiations. Meanwhile, Russian forces carried out an airstrike on the frontline Ukrainian city of Slovian","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 19:47:14 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/8-killed-in-ukrainian-strikes-across-russia-as-kyiv-moscow-attacks-intensify-14035470.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Two firefighting helicopters collide as Greece battles devastating wildfires near Athens,Two firefighting helicopters collide as Greece battles devastating wildfires near Athens,"Two firefighting helicopters collide as Greece battles devastating wildfires near Athens Two firefighting helicopters collided while battling a wildfire west of Athens as Greece struggled to contain multiple blazes fuelled by strong winds, with thousands of hectares of forest and farmland already destroyed. Two firefighting helicopters collided while battling a wildfire west of Athens as Greece struggled to contain multiple blazes fuelled by strong winds, with thousands of hectares of forest and farmland already destroyed. Two firefighting helicopters collided on Sunday while battling a wildfire in the Psatha area west of Athens, as Greece continued to battle multiple blazes that have scorched vast stretches of forest and farmland across the country. The crew members aboard the helicopters were killed in the collision, a fire service spokesperson confirmed. The Greek fire service said search and rescue teams were immediately deployed to locate and assist the crews involved in the mid-air collision. No immediate information was released on casualties or the cause of the crash. The accident came as Prime Minister Kyriakos Mitsotakis warned that Greece was facing ""extremely difficult"" days, with powerful winds and extreme weather hampering firefighting efforts. Writing on Facebook, Mitsotakis said wind speeds had reached 100 kmph, making it unsafe for firefighting aircraft to operate in some areas. ""There are moments when nature and the intensity of weather phenomena surpass any human planning and any operational capability,"" he said. Nearly 500 firefighters were deployed to tackle a major blaze near the coastal village of Porto Germeno, about 70 kilometres northwest of Athens, where flames spread over a mountain overnight and threatened the capital's western outskirts. Another 100","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 22:25:34 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/two-firefighting-helicopters-collide-as-greece-battles-devastating-wildfires-near-athens-14035469.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,US missile stockpiles under strain as Iran conflict raises defence concerns: Report,US missile stockpiles under strain as Iran conflict raises defence concerns: Report,"US missile stockpiles under strain as Iran conflict raises defence concerns: Report A senior US military commander has reportedly warned the Pentagon that continued operations against Iran are straining America's missile defence resources, raising concerns over the sustainability of support for Israel and future military readiness. A senior US military commander has reportedly warned the Pentagon that continued operations against Iran are straining America's missile defence resources, raising concerns over the sustainability of support for Israel and future military readiness. A top American military commander stationed in Europe has cautioned the Pentagon that Washington may soon confront hard decisions on missile defence resources as the ongoing conflict with Iran continues to place heavy pressure on American military stockpiles. The development was reported by The Washington Post, which noted that the chief of US European Command, Gen. Alexus Grynkewich, informed Pentagon officials earlier this week that the United States lacks adequate naval assets to continue intercepting Iranian ballistic missile strikes on Israel. The account emerges against a backdrop of mounting concerns about the depletion of advanced US interceptor missiles after months of military activity in the West Asia. According to The Washington Post, Gen. Grynkewich cautioned that, without the deployment of another US Navy destroyer to the region, European Command would eventually be forced to decide between protecting American interests and sustaining missile defence operations for Israel against Iranian attacks. The Pentagon declined to comment on the report. US European Command did not respond to requests for comment, while an Israeli embassy spokesperson in Washington could not immediately be reached, the publication reported. Con","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 19:18:59 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-missile-stockpiles-under-strain-as-iran-conflict-raises-defence-concerns-report-14035467.html,2026-08-03 01:31:49
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Moscow mayor calls deadly restaurant bombing a 'brutal terrorist act',Moscow mayor calls deadly restaurant bombing a 'brutal terrorist act',"Moscow mayor calls deadly restaurant bombing a 'brutal terrorist act' The bombing at an upscale Moscow restaurant killed three people, including the suspected female attacker, and injured at least 21 others. Russian authorities have not identified those responsible. The bombing at an upscale Moscow restaurant killed three people, including the suspected female attacker, and injured at least 21 others. Russian authorities have not identified those responsible. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin on Sunday described the deadly bombing at a restaurant in the Russian capital as a ""brutal terrorist act"", a day after the explosion killed three people and injured at least 21 others. In a post on social media, Sobyanin expressed condolences to the victims and said those injured were receiving medical treatment. However, he did not identify who was responsible for the attack. The explosion occurred on Saturday evening at Balzi Rossi, an upscale Italian restaurant in central Moscow. According to Russian state media, three people, including the suspected female bomber, were killed in the blast. Russia's National Anti-Terrorism Committee said at least 21 people were injured when the explosive device detonated inside or near the restaurant on Kudrinskaya Square. According to RIA Novosti, the woman allegedly attempted to carry the bomb into the restaurant but was stopped by a security guard before the device exploded. The restaurant had reportedly been closed for a private function at the time. Russia's Investigative Committee said the incident remains under investigation. As of Sunday afternoon, authorities had not disclosed the cause of the explosion or identified any suspects, and no group had claimed responsibility. Images released by Russian state media","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:56:58 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/moscow-mayor-calls-deadly-restaurant-bombing-a-brutal-terrorist-act-14035460.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Taslima Nasreen calls for Sheikh Hasina's return to Bangladesh, criticises Awami League ban","Taslima Nasreen calls for Sheikh Hasina's return to Bangladesh, criticises Awami League ban","Taslima Nasreen calls for Sheikh Hasina's return to Bangladesh, criticises Awami League ban Exiled Bangladeshi writer and activist Taslima Nasreen has called for former Bangladesh prime minister Sheikh Hasina to return to her country and lead the Awami League in future elections Exiled Bangladeshi writer and activist Taslima Nasreen has called for former Bangladesh prime minister Sheikh Hasina to return to her country and lead the Awami League in future elections Exiled Bangladeshi writer and activist Taslima Nasreen has called for former Bangladesh prime minister Sheikh Hasina to return to her country and lead the Awami League in future elections, saying both Hasina's ouster and the ban on her party were ""undemocratic."" Speaking to reporters in Kolkata during her first visit to the city in nearly two decades, Nasreen said Bangladesh should allow the Awami League to participate in elections and let voters decide its future. Her remarks come at a time when Hasina has alsoexpressed a desire to return to Bangladeshdespite facing legal cases and the possibility of arrest. Nasreen, who has lived in exile for years because of threats from Islamist groups over her writings, also criticised religious extremism and voiced support for free thinkers facing persecution in Bangladesh. ""The ouster of Awami League leader Sheikh Hasina in the way it happened was wrong. It was anti-democratic. Banning the party was absolutely undemocratic. They should be allowed to participate in elections. I want Hasina to return to Bangladesh,"" Nasreen said. She also made strong remarks against religious seminaries, alleging that radical Islamist groups use some madrasas to spread extremism. ""I feel there is no need for any madrasa. It only produces jihadis. All madrasas should be ","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:53:15 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/india/taslima-nasreen-calls-for-sheikh-hasinas-return-to-bangladesh-criticises-awami-league-ban-14035465.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,‘New lie’: Iranian media rejects Trump’s claim Tehran asked US to halt fresh strikes,‘New lie’: Iranian media rejects Trump’s claim Tehran asked US to halt fresh strikes,"‘New lie’: Iranian media rejects Trump’s claim Tehran asked US to halt fresh strikes The denial comes as tensions remain high over the Strait of Hormuz and the possibility of renewed US military action. The denial comes as tensions remain high over the Strait of Hormuz and the possibility of renewed US military action. Iran’s Mehr news agency on Sunday rejected US President Donald Trump’s claim that Tehran had asked Washington to refrain from launching new strikes, calling the allegation a “new lie”. The agency, citing military officials, said Iran’s armed forces remained on high alert and were prepared for any possible developments. Trump said on Saturday that the US was prepared to take further military action against Iran but claimed that Tehran and other countries in the region had asked him to hold off on new strikes. He said he had agreed to pause the attacks while pursuing a potential deal with Iran. Trump said any agreement would require the “Immediate, Complete and Total OPENING” of the Strait of Hormuz, along with an end to what he described as Iran’s nuclear threat. Iran’s Fars news agency, citing a source close to Iranian negotiators, said on Sunday that Tehran would not reopen the strategic waterway while the US continued what it called hostile actions. “As long as the United States maintains its hostile actions, the Strait of Hormuz will remain closed,” the source said. Iran has restricted passage through the Strait of Hormuz since the start of the conflict, requiring vessels to obtain permission and pay transit fees before using the route. Trump’s comments came after Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman reportedly pushed for efforts to de-escalate tensions i","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:01:49 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/new-lie-iranian-media-rejects-trumps-claim-tehran-asked-us-to-halt-fresh-strikes-14035463.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,IDF eliminates Hamas commanders as Gaza ceasefire talks hit troop withdrawal hurdle,IDF eliminates Hamas commanders as Gaza ceasefire talks hit troop withdrawal hurdle,"IDF eliminates Hamas commanders as Gaza ceasefire talks hit troop withdrawal hurdle The Israel Defense Forces (IDF) on Sunday claimed it had killed two Hamas commanders in separate operations in the Gaza Strip, including a commander from the group's elite Nukhba force whom it accused of taking part in the October 7 attack The Israel Defense Forces (IDF) on Sunday claimed it had killed two Hamas commanders in separate operations in the Gaza Strip, including a commander from the group's elite Nukhba force whom it accused of taking part in the October 7 attack The Israel Defense Forces (IDF) on Sunday claimed it had killed two Hamas commanders in separate operations in the Gaza Strip, including a commander from the group's elite Nukhba force whom it accused of taking part in the October 7, 2023, attack on Kibbutz Nir Oz. In a statement posted on X, the Israeli military identified the commander as Salem Jamal Abd al-Rahman Abu Labad, alleging that he infiltrated Kibbutz Nir Oz during the Hamas-led assault on southern Israel. The IDF also announced the killing of Muhammad Abd al-Nasser Muhammad Khatib, whom it identified as a commander in Hamas' Maghazi Battalion. The military did not say when or where the operations took place and provided no further details. Hamas had not immediately commented on the Israeli claims. According to the Israeli military, Abu Labad served as a commander in Hamas' elite Nukhba force, which Israel says spearheaded the cross-border attacks on October 7, 2023. The IDF said Khatib operated under Hamas' military wing and was involved in planning and attempting attacks against Israeli troops operating inside Gaza. In its statement, the military said the two commanders were ""eliminated"" during separate operations, adding that they had been involved in advancing attacks agains","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 17:59:29 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/idf-eliminates-hamas-commanders-as-gaza-ceasefire-talks-hit-troop-withdrawal-hurdle-14035462.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Hungary braces for critical days as Danube drought forces nuclear plant shutdown,Hungary braces for critical days as Danube drought forces nuclear plant shutdown,"Hungary braces for critical days as Danube drought forces nuclear plant shutdown Hungary's only nuclear power plant is set to shut down for the first time in more than four decades after record-low water levels in the Danube disrupted reactor cooling, as the country braces for another intense heatwave. Hungary's only nuclear power plant is set to shut down for the first time in more than four decades after record-low water levels in the Danube disrupted reactor cooling, as the country braces for another intense heatwave. Hungary is preparing for what Prime Minister Peter Magyar described as a ""critical"" five-day period after record-low water levels in the Danube River forced the country's only nuclear power plant to shut down for the first time in more than 40 years, with another severe heatwave expected this week. Large parts of Europe are grappling with prolonged drought and extreme temperatures that have lowered river levels, disrupted shipping and raised concerns over water supplies and electricity generation. Hungary's 2-gigawatt Paks nuclear power plant, which operates four Russian-built reactors, was running at just over 10 per cent of its capacity on Sunday as the Danube — its primary source of cooling water — fell to a record low. Water authorities warned that river levels are expected to decline even further over the coming days. ”We are facing the most critical five days ahead,” Magyar said in a Facebook video. ”Tomorrow, the Paks power plant will not be generating, while the hottest, 40-degree (Celsius, 104 Fahrenheit) days are ahead. ”The power grid, our public services and ourselves will all come under enormous strain,” said Magyar, who has warned that Paks could remain idle for weeks. Falls in water levels have also disrupted shipping and tourism in Hungary a","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 17:38:32 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/hungary-braces-for-critical-days-as-danube-drought-forces-nuclear-plant-shutdown-ws-e-14035454.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Indonesia ferry tragedy: 5 killed, 41 missing after vessel catches fire","Indonesia ferry tragedy: 5 killed, 41 missing after vessel catches fire","Indonesia ferry tragedy: 5 killed, 41 missing after vessel catches fire At least five people have died and 41 are missing after a ferry carrying 271 people caught fire off Indonesia on Sunday. Rescue teams and nearby vessels have so far saved 225 passengers and crew members, officials said. At least five people have died and 41 are missing after a ferry carrying 271 people caught fire off Indonesia on Sunday. Rescue teams and nearby vessels have so far saved 225 passengers and crew members, officials said. At least five people have died and 41 remain missing after a ferry carrying 271 passengers and crew caught fire while sailing off Indonesia on Sunday, according to search and rescue officials cited by AFP. The ferry, KMP Mutiara Sentosa 2, was travelling from Surabaya in East Java to Makassar in South Sulawesi when its captain reported the fire, Indonesia’s National Search and Rescue Agency (Basarnas) said. Of the 271 people aboard, 225 had been rescued by Sunday afternoon, according to agency data cited byReuters. Several nearby vessels joined the rescue operation as passengers were evacuated from the burning ferry. Nanang Sigit, head of the Surabaya Search and Rescue Office, said vessels including TB Hasnur 26 and British Mentor were helping rescue passengers who had jumped into the sea. “Four vessels are now alongside the ferry,” Nanang was quoted as saying by Jakarta Global. The search-and-rescue vessel SAR 249 Permadi was also heading to the site, although officials estimated it would take around six hours to reach the ferry. Videos circulating on social media appeared to show thick black smoke rising from the ferry’s upper decks as flames spread across the vessel. Passengers wearing life jackets could be seen gathered on one side of the ferry as rescue e","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:59:00 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/indonesia-ferry-tragedy-5-killed-41-missing-after-vessel-catches-fire-14035455.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"South Korea records highest-ever temperature of 42.5°C, issues emergency heatwave warnings","South Korea records highest-ever temperature of 42.5°C, issues emergency heatwave warnings","South Korea records highest-ever temperature of 42.5°C, issues emergency heatwave warnings South Korea recorded its highest temperature since weather records began more than a century ago on Sunday, as an intense heatwave swept across the country, prompting authorities to issue emergency warnings South Korea recorded its highest temperature since weather records began more than a century ago on Sunday, as an intense heatwave swept across the country, prompting authorities to issue emergency warnings South Korea recorded its highest temperature since weather records began more than a century ago on Sunday, as an intense heatwave swept across the country, prompting authorities to issue emergency warnings and urge people to avoid all outdoor activities. The Korea Meteorological Administration (KMA) said the southeastern city of Yangsan recorded a temperature of 42.5 degrees Celsius at 1:26 PM local time, the highest ever measured in the country. The city has remained at the centre of the ongoing heatwave, with temperatures crossing 40°C for the fifth straight day. The scorching weather has disrupted daily life across South Korea, with residents seeking shelter in air-conditioned shopping malls, cafés and public cooling centres as authorities warned that prolonged exposure to the heat could be dangerous. More than 20 regions across South Korea were placed under emergency heatwave alerts on Sunday, a warning category introduced this year to respond more effectively to rising temperatures. The emergency alert is issued when the perceived temperature is expected to reach 38°C or the actual temperature touches 39°C during the day. Issuing an advisory, the KMA urged people to ""immediately stop all outdoor activities"", warning that indoor spaces without air conditioning could a","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:11:20 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/south-korea-records-highest-ever-temperature-of-42-5c-issues-emergency-heatwave-warnings-14035447.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,22 EU leaders slam Sanchez's handling of Ceuta crisis; Spain defends itself,22 EU leaders slam Sanchez's handling of Ceuta crisis; Spain defends itself,"22 EU leaders slam Sanchez's handling of Ceuta crisis; Spain defends itself Twenty-two European Union leaders, including German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni, slammed Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez on Saturday following the Ceuta crisis Twenty-two European Union leaders, including German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni, slammed Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez on Saturday following the Ceuta crisis Twenty-two European Union leaders, including German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni, slammed Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez on Saturday following the Ceuta crisis, which they said undermined the security of the regional bloc. Amid the backlash, the Spanish premier hit back against his EU partners, calling them ""selfish"" when addressing the sudden influx of around 50,000 unauthorised migrants from Morocco into the Spanish exclave of Ceuta in North Africa. While almost all of the migrants have now returned to Morocco, the 22 leaders still raised “serious concern” over the threat to the EU’s frontier, and zeroed in on Sánchez’s move to grant legal status to up to 1.2 million unauthorised migrants as a “pull factor” that fueled the crisis. In a letter to the European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen, European Council President António Costa and Irish Prime Minister Micheál Martin, the 22 leaders made direct reference to the need for EU-level cooperation on policies such as Madrid’s migrant regularisation scheme. “We have a duty to effectively deter and relentlessly combat illegal migration, by coordinating our action, strengthening our external borders and addressing all policies that can serve as pull factors, such as the regul","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:00:47 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/22-eu-leaders-slam-sanchezs-handling-of-ceuta-crisis-spain-defends-itself-14035446.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Baffled by India-Afghanistan ties, Pak Army invokes Quran, says Muslims shouldn't befriend 'kaafirs'","Baffled by India-Afghanistan ties, Pak Army invokes Quran, says Muslims shouldn't befriend 'kaafirs'","Baffled by India-Afghanistan ties, Pak Army invokes Quran, says Muslims shouldn't befriend 'kaafirs' Pakistan Army has triggered a fresh controversy after invoking a Quranic verse while responding to recent remarks by an Afghan Taliban minister who said India and Afghanistan ""share the same DNA"" Pakistan Army has triggered a fresh controversy after invoking a Quranic verse while responding to recent remarks by an Afghan Taliban minister who said India and Afghanistan ""share the same DNA"" Pakistan Army's chief military spokesperson, Lieutenant General Ahmed Sharif Chaudhry, has triggered a fresh controversy after invoking a Quranic verse while responding to recent remarks by an Afghan Taliban minister who saidIndia and Afghanistan ""share the same DNA""because of their historical and cultural ties. Speaking at an official press conference in Rawalpindi, Chaudhry referred to a Quranic verse which, according to his interpretation, says Muslims should not befriendkaafirs(disbelievers). His comments, made while discussing the Afghan minister's statement, quickly gained traction on social media, where a clip of the exchange was widely shared. The remarks came during a broader media briefing on Pakistan's counter-terrorism operations, the security situation in Balochistan, ties with Afghanistan and Islamabad's repeated allegations that India supports militant violence inside Pakistan. India has consistently rejected those allegations. Responding to the Afghan minister's remarks on India-Afghanistan ties, Chaudhry said people claiming such closeness with India and Hindus raised questions, in his view, about adherence to Islamic principles. He sought to distinguish between the Afghan people and the Taliban administration, saying ordinary Afghans were suffering under Taliban rul","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:05:25 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/india/baffled-by-india-afghanistan-ties-pak-army-invokes-quran-says-muslims-shouldnt-befriend-kaafirs-14035440.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Indian diaspora in China seeks action on anti-India content, declining work visas","Indian diaspora in China seeks action on anti-India content, declining work visas","Indian diaspora in China seeks action on anti-India content, declining work visas The interaction comes at a time when New Delhi and Beijing are gradually rebuilding ties after relations remained frozen for nearly four years following the military stand-off in eastern Ladakh The interaction comes at a time when New Delhi and Beijing are gradually rebuilding ties after relations remained frozen for nearly four years following the military stand-off in eastern Ladakh Indian diaspora in China has raised concerns over a rise in abusive anti-India content on Chinese social media platforms, declining work visas for Indian professionals and restrictions on employment for spouses during the Indian Embassy's first Open House interaction in recent years. According to aPTIreport, the outreach programme, held on Friday, brought together a large number of Indian professionals working across different sectors in Beijing. Indian Ambassador Vikram Doraiswami, along with Counsellor (Consular, Education and Community Affairs) Nitinjeet Singh and Counsellor (Visa) Ramesh Singh, interacted with members of the community and discussed issues affecting Indians living and working in China. The interaction comes at a time when New Delhi and Beijing are gradually rebuilding ties after relations remained frozen for nearly four years following the military stand-off in eastern Ladakh. Since the October 2024 patrolling agreement, both countries have taken steps to restore people-to-people exchanges, business links and travel. According to the report, members of the diaspora highlighted a growing number of abusive posts targeting Indians, their food habits and culture on Chinese social media platforms. They also expressed concern over the decline in work visas issued to India","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 14:00:31 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/india/indian-diaspora-in-china-seeks-action-on-anti-india-content-declining-work-visas-14035436.html,2026-08-03 01:31:50
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Greece wildfires scorch over 12,000 hectares as firefighters battle multiple blazes","Greece wildfires scorch over 12,000 hectares as firefighters battle multiple blazes","Greece wildfires scorch over 12,000 hectares as firefighters battle multiple blazes Wildfires have burned more than 12,000 hectares across Greece, with authorities battling multiple blazes and experts warning that the Porto Germeno fire could be classified as a megafire Wildfires have burned more than 12,000 hectares across Greece, with authorities battling multiple blazes and experts warning that the Porto Germeno fire could be classified as a megafire Greece on Sunday faced multiple fronts and a growing damage toll after a week of wildfires devastated over 12,000 hectares of forest and agricultural land, experts said. The National Observatory's climate tracker meteo.gr said early estimates indicated that over 6,500 hectares (16,000 acres) had been burned in separate fires on the Gulf of Corinth which also swept through the popular coastal village of Porto Germeno near Athens. Porto Germeno and other villages were evacuated when the fire broke out on Friday but local authorities say scores of homes were damaged or destroyed. Earlier this week, fires on the islands of Crete and Paros affected another 6,000 hectares according to meteo. But Theodore Giannaros, a wildfire meteorologist and senior researcher at the National Observatory, said the fires around Porto Germeno appear to have affected an area of over 10,000 hectares -- almost double the original estimate. ""Unfortunately, it is highly likely (if not almost certain) that this particular wildfire will be classified as a megafire,"" Giannaros wrote on Facebook. Firefighters have faced dozens of fires daily and Greece's Civil Protection Minister Evangelos Tournas on Saturday said the fire department had been ""pushed to its limits"". Three firefighters died this week in the line of duty, two ","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 13:35:44 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/greece-wildfires-scorch-over-12000-hectares-as-firefighters-battle-multiple-blazes-14035434.html,2026-08-03 01:31:51
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,'Don't let them forget me': Iran executes 20-year-old protester after January unrest,'Don't let them forget me': Iran executes 20-year-old protester after January unrest,"'Don't let them forget me': Iran executes 20-year-old protester after January unrest Iran has executed 20-year-old protester Arvin Kheirkhah in the latest execution linked to the country's January anti-government protests Iran has executed 20-year-old protester Arvin Kheirkhah in the latest execution linked to the country's January anti-government protests Iran has executed a 20-year-old protester, Arvin Kheirkhah, in the latest execution linked to the country's January anti-government protests. His death has raised fresh concerns that several other protesters arrested during the same unrest could soon face the death penalty. According to a report byIran International, Kheirkhah was arrested during the January demonstrations and sentenced to death by a Revolutionary Court on charges including moharebeh, or ""waging war against God""—a charge often used in Iran for offences considered to threaten the state. He was reportedly moved to solitary confinement on Wednesday before being executed at Shahroud prison. According to the report, Kheirkhah's family gathered outside the prison on Friday night in a final attempt to stop the execution. In what was reported to be his last conversation with them, he said: ""Don't let them forget me. We stood up for the liberation of our homeland. Don't let the path we chose be silenced."" According to the report, Iran's former Crown Prince Reza Pahlavi condemned the execution and warned that several other detainees could soon meet the same fate. He identified Javad Ajam, Morteza Zamani, Mehdi Ranjar, Farshid Rahmani, Alireza Sagheri and Pouya Sagheri as among those believed to be at risk of execution. Kheirkhah's execution came just days after Iran publicly hanged tw","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 13:10:38 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/dont-let-them-forget-me-iran-executes-20-year-old-protester-after-january-unrest-14035430.html,2026-08-03 01:31:51
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Jay Clayton will take over as US intelligence chief as Bill Pulte exits on Monday, but there is a catch","Jay Clayton will take over as US intelligence chief as Bill Pulte exits on Monday, but there is a catch","Jay Clayton will take over as US intelligence chief as Bill Pulte exits on Monday, but there is a catch Acting Director of National Intelligence Bill ​Pulte announced on Saturday that his two-month stint in the office is formally coming to an end on Monday, and Jay Clayton will take charge after his confirmation by the US Senate this week. Acting Director of National Intelligence Bill ​Pulte announced on Saturday that his two-month stint in the office is formally coming to an end on Monday, and Jay Clayton will take charge after his confirmation by the US Senate this week. Acting Director of National Intelligence Bill ​Pulte announced on Saturday that his two-month stint in the office is formally coming to an end on Monday, and Jay Clayton will take charge after his confirmation by the US Senate this week. In a social media post, Pulte said that he has discussed the handover with both US President Donald Trump and Clayton. It is pertinent to note that Trump had chosen Pulte as the interim director after his predecessor Tulsi Gabbard resigned. However, his appointment garnered backlash from Republican lawmakers who said the head of the Federal Housing Finance Agency did not have the national security background for the post. Clayton, a former US attorney for the Southern District of New York, also served as the former chairman of the Securities and Exchange Commission. He was confirmed along party lines on Tuesday. The Republican-led Senate was expected to confirm him in June. However, Trump delayed the hearing. Gabbard, who was appointed by Trump right after he took office, faced clashes with congressional Democrats, who accused her of advancing US President Donald Trump's political agenda and promoting debunked election claims. During Pulte's time in office, Trump delivered a speech from White House in which h","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 11:57:00 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/jay-clayton-will-take-over-as-us-intelligence-chief-as-bill-pulte-exits-on-monday-but-there-is-a-catch-14035409.html,2026-08-03 01:31:51
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,"Gansu flash floods kill 25, injure 23 as China braces for more heavy rain","Gansu flash floods kill 25, injure 23 as China braces for more heavy rain","Gansu flash floods kill 25, injure 23 as China braces for more heavy rain Flash floods in China's Gansu province have killed 25 people and injured 23, while authorities warn of continued heavy rain and landslide risks Flash floods in China's Gansu province have killed 25 people and injured 23, while authorities warn of continued heavy rain and landslide risks The death toll from last week's flash floods in Gansu Province in northwestern China has risen to 25, with 23 people injured, according to state-runXinhuaon Sunday. The updated figures come as authorities warn of continued heavy rainfall, renewed landslide threats and worsening flood conditions in several parts of the country. The flooding struck Weiyuan County in Dingxi City on July 26, after torrential rain battered the region. Initial reports had said 10 people were killed, butXinhuasaid the latest official toll now stands at 25 dead and 23 injured. The National Commission for Disaster Prevention, Reduction and Relief has directed Gansu provincial authorities to carry out investigations and damage assessments following the disaster. Officials in Gansu have warned that continued rainfall during China's annual flood season could trigger more landslides, particularly in Dingxi. Meanwhile, Beijing and Inner Mongolia also issued weather alerts on Sunday as adverse weather conditions persisted. Severe rainfall is also affecting large parts of Sichuan Province, where state broadcasterCCTVreported that 64,609 people have been evacuated. The broadcaster added that more than 881,000 residents have been relocated since the beginning of the annual flood season. The latest update comes as authorities continue to monitor multiple flood-hit regio","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 11:38:37 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/gansu-flash-floods-kill-25-injure-23-as-china-braces-for-more-heavy-rain-14035419.html,2026-08-03 01:31:51
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Word of the Week is Wildfire: How these blazes are becoming more dangerous across the world,Word of the Week is Wildfire: How these blazes are becoming more dangerous across the world,"Word of the Week is Wildfire: How these blazes are becoming more dangerous across the world Wildfires are growing larger, faster, and more destructive as climate change, prolonged heatwaves, and drought fuel unprecedented blazes across Europe, North America, and North Africa. Firstpost looks at why modern megafires are becoming harder to contain and what terms like PyroCb and sixth-generation fires really mean Wildfires are growing larger, faster, and more destructive as climate change, prolonged heatwaves, and drought fuel unprecedented blazes across Europe, North America, and North Africa. Firstpost looks at why modern megafires are becoming harder to contain and what terms like PyroCb and sixth-generation fires really mean Welcome toFirstpost’sweeklyWord of the Weeksegment, where we unpack a single word or phrase dominating headlines, dissect its linguistic roots, and examine the geopolitical, environmental, and socio-economic realities driving its currency. For this week's edition, our chosen term isWildfire. Over the past fortnight, satellite sensors and atmospheric monitors have painted a grim picture: vast swathes of the Northern Hemisphere — from the pine forests of southwestern France and the sun-baked plateaus of central Spain to the dense boreal wilderness of Canada and the Mediterranean coastlines of North Africa — are ablaze. Billions of people are breathing air tainted by distant infernos, while emergency services across multiple continents are pushed past their operational limits. The word ""wildfire"" is no longer just a descriptor for a seasonal ecological hazard. it has transformed into a symbol of our planet's shifting climate regime. To understand how a word captures the global zeitgeist,Firstpostlooks at its origins. The word wildfire traces its roots to the Old English wilde fȳr, a combination of wilde (wild, untamed, or uncontrolled) and fȳr (fire). Historicall","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 11:27:50 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/explainers/word-of-the-week-is-wildfire-how-these-blazes-are-becoming-more-dangerous-across-the-world-14035185.html,2026-08-03 01:31:51
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Israeli strikes kill seven in Gaza as Hamas backs next phase of ceasefire deal,Israeli strikes kill seven in Gaza as Hamas backs next phase of ceasefire deal,"Israeli strikes kill seven in Gaza as Hamas backs next phase of ceasefire deal Seven people were killed in Israeli strikes across Gaza as Hamas said it had accepted the latest phase of a ceasefire deal, while Israel continued military operations and demanded the group's disarmament Seven people were killed in Israeli strikes across Gaza as Hamas said it had accepted the latest phase of a ceasefire deal, while Israel continued military operations and demanded the group's disarmament Israeli strikes across the Gaza Strip killed seven people and damaged medical supply warehouses on Saturday, according to Gaza authorities, a day after Hamas announced it had accepted the latest phase of a proposed agreement aimed at ending the war. While the group said it had agreed to the next stage of the deal, Israel continued military operations and reiterated that any withdrawal would depend on Hamas being disarmed. The Israeli military said it had targeted Hamas weapons depots as part of ongoing operations, maintaining that it must verify thegroup's disarmament before any broader agreementcan move forward. The latest attacks came a day after Hamas said it had accepted the next phase of a proposal championed by US President Donald Trump, which includes provisions for handing over its weapons and the gradual withdrawal of Israeli forces from the Gaza Strip. Israel has not officially commented on the agreement. However, a political source toldAFP""that there will be no withdrawal whatsoever"" without Hamas's ""genuine disarmament"". Mahmoud Basal, spokesperson for Gaza's civil defence agency, toldAFPthat seven people had been killed and several others injured across the enclave since dawn on Saturday. According to Basal, an Israeli air strike on a rooftop southwest of Gaza Ci","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 10:00:46 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/israeli-strikes-kill-seven-in-gaza-as-hamas-backs-next-phase-of-ceasefire-deal-14035410.html,2026-08-03 01:31:51
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Hungary to shut down its only nuclear power plant amid record-low water levels,Hungary to shut down its only nuclear power plant amid record-low water levels,"Hungary to shut down its only nuclear power plant amid record-low water levels Hungary on Saturday announced that it will shut down its only nuclear power plant after record-low levels on the Danube River, which has created a drought-like situation in the area and significantly reduced the water available for cooling its reactors. Hungary on Saturday announced that it will shut down its only nuclear power plant after record-low levels on the Danube River, which has created a drought-like situation in the area and significantly reduced the water available for cooling its reactors. Hungary on Saturday announced that it will shut down its only nuclear power plant after record-low levels on the Danube River, which has created a drought-like situation in the area and significantly reduced the water available for cooling its reactors. The country's new Prime Minister, Peter Magyar, said the Paks Nuclear Power Plant in central Hungary would be powered down on Sunday. This will be the first full shutdown of the plant in its 44-year history. It is pertinent to note that the plant has been important for Hungary since it has supplied nearly half of the country's electricity. While announcing the move, Magyar said output had fallen to 965 megawatts on Friday and to 240 overnight, far below the normal 2,000. The plant was built during the Soviet era and comprises four reactors located in the South of Budapest. For years, the plant has siphoned water from the Danube for cooling, but low river levels have impacted its pumps’ ability to draw in enough water. A river level of minus 134cm at Paks forces a full shutdown, and the level is expected to fall as low as 144cm, far below the previous 98cm record set in 2018. It is pertinent to note that the Danube, which flows from Germany to the Black Sea, is one of several Eu","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 09:27:03 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/hungary-to-shut-down-its-only-nuclear-power-plant-amid-record-low-water-levels-14035401.html,2026-08-03 01:31:52
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,This Week in Explainers: A guide to the influx of migrants from Morocco into Spain’s Ceuta,This Week in Explainers: A guide to the influx of migrants from Morocco into Spain’s Ceuta,"This Week in Explainers: A guide to the influx of migrants from Morocco into Spain’s Ceuta Over 60,000 migrants from Morocco swam, climbed fences, and forced themselves into the North African Spanish enclave of Ceuta, resulting in at least 57 deaths and Madrid deploying troops. Here’s more on this and other big news in our weekly wrap Over 60,000 migrants from Morocco swam, climbed fences, and forced themselves into the North African Spanish enclave of Ceuta, resulting in at least 57 deaths and Madrid deploying troops. Here’s more on this and other big news in our weekly wrap A restart of a war, a possible end to another war, natural disasters and a landmark settlement. The world has seen it all this week. This week, the brief pause in the US-Iran war came to an end. US President Trump launched new “powerful” strikes at Iran in response to new attacks on a US base in Jordan. The war also appears have spread this week, with a new explosion reported in Egypt, and joint US-Saudi strikes in Iraq. While Trump renewed fighting against Tehran, he declared a breakthrough on the Gaza war. The US president announced on Truth Social that the Board of Peace reached an agreement for the “complete disarmament” of Hamas and other armed groups in Gaza. This sparked speculation that the fighting in Gaza would finally end, providing Gazans much-needed relief. The other big story of the week was the mass migration that took place from Morocco to Ceuta, a Spanish enclave in North Africa. Thousands of people were seen swimming and climbing over fences to gain access to the territory. The surge of people also resulted in 18 deaths. Meanwhile, parts of Europe have also had to contend with deadly wildfires. Ferocious flames continue to rage in parts of France and Spain, reducing everything in their path to ash. We discuss all of ","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 09:24:51 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/explainers/this-week-in-explainers-a-guide-to-the-influx-of-migrants-from-morocco-into-spains-ceuta-14035187.html,2026-08-03 01:31:52
Firstpost,India (Center-Right),en,Pashmina to spices: What India and China are trading through the reopened Shipki La pass,Pashmina to spices: What India and China are trading through the reopened Shipki La pass,"Pashmina to spices: What India and China are trading through the reopened Shipki La pass The reopening of the Shipki La pass has revived centuries-old barter trade between India and China, allowing the exchange of approved goods ranging from spices and tea to pashmina and yak hair. The reopening of the Shipki La pass has revived centuries-old barter trade between India and China, allowing the exchange of approved goods ranging from spices and tea to pashmina and yak hair. From pashmina, raw wool and yak hair to spices, tea and medicinal herbs, the centuries-old barter trade between India and China is back in business. The reopening of the historic Shipki La pass on Saturday has revived one of the ancient Silk Route's oldest commercial links after a nearly six-year suspension. The border trade corridor had remained shut since 2020 following the Covid-19 pandemic and the subsequent deterioration in bilateral ties after tensions along the India-China border. The reopening of the traditional Silk Route corridor is expected to strengthen economic activity, create local employment opportunities and boost tourism in the border region. Situated at an altitude of 3,930 metres in the Sutlej valley, Shipki La connects Kinnaur with China's Tibet Autonomous Region. The seasonal trade route will remain operational until November 30. Unlike most internationaltrade corridors, commercial exchanges at Shipki La continue under a centuries-old barter system instead of monetary transactions. Goods are transported by road to the frontier before being shifted by pack animals to a designated exchange point around two kilometres inside Tibetan territory. To support customs procedures and trader registration, authorities inaugurated the newly built Chhuppan Trade Mart. Trade ope","Sun, 2 Aug 2026 08:47:37 +0530",https://www.firstpost.com/world/pashmina-to-spices-what-india-and-china-are-trading-through-the-reopened-shipki-la-pass-ws-e-14035398.html,2026-08-03 01:31:52
